{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015TE3zuKGx7VnSD9c8GeD4p","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PROJECT_MAP.md — Directory Layout\n2\t\n3\t```\n4\tAGENTS.md          — Workspace orientation and rules\n5\tPROJECT_MAP.md     — This file; directory summary\n6\tRULEBOOK.txt       — The entire MTG comprehensive rules. Grep — do not read whole.\n7\tprompt.md          — Per-run task prompt (written at stage time)\n8\trun_manifest.json  — Per-run manifest written by the harness: `{timeout_seconds, deadline_utc}`. Harness-owned — do not edit.\n9\tpytest.ini         — Pytest configuration for the workspace\n10\tconftest.py        — Pytest fixtures shared across the workspace\n11\ttest_utils.py      — Shared test helpers (`create_game`, `set_board_state`, …)\n12\ttest_utils.md      — API reference for `test_utils.py`\n13\t.gitignore         — Git ignore rules\n14\tengine/            — Canonical game engine source. Imported as `engine`.\n15\tengine_tests/      — Engine regression tests (do not modify).\n16\tcards/             — Card implementations.\n17\t  cards/fdn/       — Completed FDN reference cards (do not modify their tests).\n18\t  cards/sos/       — SOS card stubs to implement.\n19\tskills/            — Workspace-local skills (e.g. `grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n20\t```\n21\t\n22\t## Card paths\n23\t\n24\tFor an SOS card with collector number `N`:\n25\t\n26\t```\n27\tcards/sos/sos_<N>/card_spec.json   — card metadata (name, mana_cost, oracle_text, P/T, keywords, …)\n28\tcards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py     — implementation stub you complete\n29\tcards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py         — your tests for this card (you create this)\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\tFor an FDN reference card:\n33\t\n34\t```\n35\tcards/fdn/fdn_<N>/card_spec.json   — card metadata\n36\tcards/fdn/fdn_<N>/card_impl.py     — completed reference implementation (read for examples)\n37\tcards/fdn/fdn_<N>/tests.py         — only present for the cards listed below; read as test examples\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t### FDN cards that ship with a `tests.py`\n41\t\n42\tThis is the canonical list — agent prompts refer back here instead of duplicating it.\n43\tDiscover the current set at any time with:\n44\t\n45\t```bash\n46\tfind cards/fdn -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -name tests.py -printf '%h\\n' | sort -V\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tAs of the latest workspace stage, the list is: `fdn_13`, `fdn_142`, `fdn_205`, `fdn_215`, `fdn_244`. If you suspect the list has grown, re-run the `find` command above — it is authoritative.\n50\t\n51\t## Imports\n52\t\n53\tThe workspace root is on `sys.path`, so use bare package imports:\n54\t\n55\t```python\n56\tfrom cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl import TheDawningArchaic\n57\tfrom engine.card import CardImpl, Creature, Instant\n58\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone\n59\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n60\t```\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"2b26e400-6a58-4ae5-9a2e-4c149fc78109","timestamp":"2026-06-02T07:34:05.709Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md","content":"# PROJECT_MAP.md — Directory Layout\n\n```\nAGENTS.md          — Workspace orientation and rules\nPROJECT_MAP.md     — This file; directory summary\nRULEBOOK.txt       — The entire MTG comprehensive rules. Grep — do not read whole.\nprompt.md          — Per-run task prompt (written at stage time)\nrun_manifest.json  — Per-run manifest written by the harness: `{timeout_seconds, deadline_utc}`. Harness-owned — do not edit.\npytest.ini         — Pytest configuration for the workspace\nconftest.py        — Pytest fixtures shared across the workspace\ntest_utils.py      — Shared test helpers (`create_game`, `set_board_state`, …)\ntest_utils.md      — API reference for `test_utils.py`\n.gitignore         — Git ignore rules\nengine/            — Canonical game engine source. Imported as `engine`.\nengine_tests/      — Engine regression tests (do not modify).\ncards/             — Card implementations.\n  cards/fdn/       — Completed FDN reference cards (do not modify their tests).\n  cards/sos/       — SOS card stubs to implement.\nskills/            — Workspace-local skills (e.g. `grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n```\n\n## Card paths\n\nFor an SOS card with collector number `N`:\n\n```\ncards/sos/sos_<N>/card_spec.json   — card metadata (name, mana_cost, oracle_text, P/T, keywords, …)\ncards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py     — implementation stub you complete\ncards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py         — your tests for this card (you create this)\n```\n\nFor an FDN reference card:\n\n```\ncards/fdn/fdn_<N>/card_spec.json   — card metadata\ncards/fdn/fdn_<N>/card_impl.py     — completed reference implementation (read for examples)\ncards/fdn/fdn_<N>/tests.py         — only present for the cards listed below; read as test examples\n```\n\n### FDN cards that ship with a `tests.py`\n\nThis is the canonical list — agent prompts refer back here instead of duplicating it.\nDiscover the current set at any time with:\n\n```bash\nfind cards/fdn -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -name tests.py -printf '%h\\n' | sort -V\n```\n\nAs of the latest workspace stage, the list is: `fdn_13`, `fdn_142`, `fdn_205`, `fdn_215`, `fdn_244`. If you suspect the list has grown, re-run the `find` command above — it is authoritative.\n\n## Imports\n\nThe workspace root is on `sys.path`, so use bare package imports:\n\n```python\nfrom cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl import TheDawningArchaic\nfrom engine.card import CardImpl, Creature, Instant\nfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone\nfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n```\n","numLines":61,"startLine":1,"totalLines":61}}}
