rite `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`.\n4. Confirm the tests are well-formed by running them (they should fail/error because the card is unimplemented — that is expected). Do not try to make them pass.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py` — your tests.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-rationale.md` — what each test covers and the behavior contract you derived from the spec.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-files.txt` — list of test file path(s) you created (one per line).\n- If any spec requirement cannot be tested with the current engine/test API, write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/untestable.json` — a JSON array of `{\"requirement\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\", \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"...\"}`. Omit the file entirely if everything is testable.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn a short summary: number of tests written, the test file path, and `untestable_count: <N>` (0 if none). Do not paste the full test code."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011iK149NzDQc9T1HBggYLU2","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b268e902-ae31-4871-a754-266ecbf296ea","timestamp":"2026-06-02T07:34:42.860Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_1"}
