{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014HdEqhSeRgCo4WEkbHRLmF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HfvFCcp8P8bbrRxDFLTnJ8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — SOS 1: The Dawning Archaic\n\n## Card under test\n\n```\nThe Dawning Archaic — {10} — Legendary Creature — Avatar — 7/7 — colorless\nThis spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard.\nReach\nWhenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery card\nfrom your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into\nyour graveyard, exile it instead.\n```\n\n## Behavior contract derived from the spec\n\n1. **Static data** — Legendary Creature with the Avatar subtype, 7/7, mana cost\n   `{10}` (all generic ⇒ colorless), keyword Reach.\n2. **Cost reduction** — `cost_reduction(game)` returns the count of cards in the\n   *controller's* graveyard whose card types include `INSTANT` or `SORCERY`.\n   Creatures/lands/etc. do not count, and the opponent's graveyard does not count.\n   The engine's `get_cost_reduction()` clamps the reduction to the generic\n   portion (10), so generic mana can never go below 0.\n3. **Attack trigger** — `register_triggers(game)` registers exactly one\n   `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger sourced on this card. It fires only when *this*\n   card attacks (not when another creature attacks).\n4. **Optional free recast** — On resolution the controller *may* cast a target\n   instant/sorcery from their graveyard for free. Declining (or an empty\n   graveyard) is a no-op.\n5. **Exile replacement** — If the recast spell would be put into the graveyard,\n   it is exiled instead. After the free cast resolves the spell card is in the\n   exile zone and not in the graveyard.\n\n## Test file\n\n`cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`\n\n### `TestTheDawningArchaicProperties`\nStatic-data checks against the spec.\n- `test_is_creature` — the class is a `Creature`.\n- `test_name` — name is \"The Dawning Archaic\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — cost parses to `{10}`.\n- `test_power_toughness` — 7/7 base.\n- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` present.\n- `test_is_avatar` — \"Avatar\" subtype present.\n- `test_has_reach` — `Keyword.REACH` present.\n- `test_is_colorless_all_generic` — cmc/generic are both 10 with no colored pips\n  (strengthened so it cannot pass against the empty stub's default empty cost).\n\n### `TestTheDawningArchaicCostReduction`\nValidates the \"{1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard\" clause.\n- `test_no_reduction_with_empty_graveyard` — 0 with empty graveyard.\n- `test_one_instant_reduces_by_one` / `test_one_sorcery_reduces_by_one` — each\n  spell type counts.\n- `test_instants_and_sorceries_both_count` — mixed graveyard sums correctly (3).\n- `test_non_instant_sorcery_cards_do_not_count` — creatures don't count (edge:\n  guards against counting all graveyard cards).\n- `test_only_controllers_graveyard_counts` — opponent's spells don't count (edge:\n  enforces \"your graveyard\").\n- `test_effective_reduction_clamped_to_generic` — 13 spells ⇒ clamped to 10 via\n  the engine's `get_cost_reduction` (edge: cost cannot underflow).\n- `test_partial_reduction_value_through_engine` — 4 spells ⇒ effective reduction 4.\n\n### `TestTheDawningArchaicAttackTriggerRegistration`\nValidates trigger wiring.\n- `test_registers_one_trigger` — exactly one trigger added.\n- `test_trigger_watches_attacks_event` — its `event_type` is `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.\n- `test_trigger_only_fires_when_this_card_attacks` — a different attacker does not\n  fire it (edge: condition must check the attacking creature).\n- `test_trigger_fires_when_this_card_attacks` — firing the event with this card as\n  the attacker pushes a StackObject sourced on the card.\n\n### `TestTheDawningArchaicRecast`\nValidates the optional free-cast and the exile replacement. A shared\n`_setup_attack` helper puts the card on the battlefield with a target spell in the\ngraveyard, scripts the controller's optional/target choices, and fires the attack\ntrigger. `_resolve_full_stack` then drains the stack (including the nested free\ncast the trigger pushes).\n- `test_chosen_spell_resolves_for_free` — with the mana pool emptied, the chosen\n  marker instant still resolves (gains 5 life), proving the cast was free.\n- `test_recast_spell_is_exiled_not_in_graveyard` — after resolution the spell is in\n  exile and not in the graveyard (the \"exile it instead\" clause).\n- `test_spell_leaves_graveyard_when_cast` — the spell no longer occupies the\n  graveyard it was cast from.\n- `test_optional_decline_leaves_spell_in_graveyard` — saying \"no\" leaves the spell\n  in the graveyard and does not resolve it (edge: the ability is optional).\n- `test_empty_graveyard_is_noop` — no instant/sorcery to cast ⇒ resolving the\n  trigger does nothing and does not raise (edge: empty-target no-op).\n- `test_can_target_a_sorcery` — a sorcery (not just an instant) is a legal target\n  and is likewise exiled on resolution.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately covered\n- Opponent-graveyard exclusion and non-spell exclusion for cost reduction.\n- Cost-reduction clamping so generic mana can't go negative.\n- Trigger fires only for this creature's attack.\n- Optional (\"you may\") decline path and empty-graveyard no-op.\n- Both instant and sorcery targets.\n\n## Edge cases NOT covered (out of scope for this card / engine surface)\n- **Mana actually saved during a real hard-cast.** The cost reduction is asserted\n  via the `cost_reduction` hook and the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamp rather\n  than by hard-casting `{10}` through the full mana-payment pipeline, because the\n  reduction value itself is the observable contract and the full payment path adds\n  no card-specific signal.\n- **Targeting legality enforcement at cast time** (e.g. rejecting a creature card\n  as a target). The card's targeting filter, if any, is an implementation choice;\n  the tests assert the positive recast behavior (instant/sorcery target works) and\n  the no-op for an empty pool of legal targets rather than pinning a specific\n  target-validation API the implementer hasn't committed to yet.\n- **APNAP / multi-trigger ordering and legend-rule interactions** — generic engine\n  behavior already covered by `engine_tests/`; not card-specific here.\n\n## Engine-limitation note (see untestable.json)\nThe \"exile it instead\" clause is fully tested, but the *natural* implementation\npath does not satisfy it: `engine.zones.move_to_zone` only consults the\nreplacement manager when a card is leaving the **battlefield**. A spell cast via\nthe trigger resolves from the **stack** to the graveyard (`_resolve_spell`) with no\nreplacement event supplied, so a `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` redirect never\nfires. A throwaway reference implementation using that approach passed 23/26 tests\nbut failed exactly the 3 exile-instead assertions, confirming the implementer must\neither add an additive engine hook (consult replacements / accept a redirect on\nstack→graveyard resolution) or route the recast spell to exile through a custom\nresolution path. The requirement is testable and correct as written — this note is\nrecorded so the Coordinator knows the clause needs more than the off-the-shelf\nreplacement pathway.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":374,"cache_read_input_tokens":104434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":374,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":66,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011iK149NzDQc9T1HBggYLU2","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b534f153-1ade-4857-92c6-95b662070b1d","request_id":"req_011Cbe3zvMgFWkwDgnDyNDqW","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_1"}
