{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011iK149NzDQc9T1HBggYLU2","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is in place. Here is my summary.\n\n## Summary\n\nI wrote **26 pytest tests** for SOS 1 — The Dawning Archaic at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`, covering its full oracle text:\n\n- **Static data (8 tests)**: Legendary Creature — Avatar, 7/7, `{10}` (all-generic ⇒ colorless), Reach.\n- **Cost reduction (8 tests)**: `{1}` less per instant/sorcery in *your* graveyard — verifies counting, that creatures/lands and the opponent's graveyard are excluded, and that the engine clamps the reduction to the generic 10.\n- **Attack-trigger registration (4 tests)**: one `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger that fires only when this card attacks.\n- **Optional free recast + exile replacement (6 tests)**: the \"you may cast target instant/sorcery from your graveyard without paying its mana cost; if it would go to the graveyard, exile it instead\" clause, including the decline path and empty-graveyard no-op.\n\nRed phase confirmed: **20 fail / 6 pass** against the empty stub (the 6 passing are legitimate negative/no-op assertions the stub coincidentally satisfies). I validated the contract is satisfiable by running a throwaway reference implementation (then discarded it, stub restored): it passed 23/26.\n\n**Key finding flagged in `untestable.json`**: the \"exile it instead\" clause is tested and correct, but the natural implementation path cannot satisfy it — `engine.zones.move_to_zone` only consults the replacement manager when a card leaves the *battlefield*, whereas a recast spell resolves from the *stack* to the graveyard with no replacement event. The 3 exile-instead tests failed even against an otherwise-correct reference impl, confirming the implementer needs an additive engine hook or a custom resolution path that routes the spell to exile.\n\n```markdown\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 26\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-rationale.md\nfiles_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-files.txt\nuntestable_count: 1\nuntestable_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/untestable.json\nnotes: wrote 26 tests for sos_1 The Dawning Archaic; exile-instead clause is tested but needs an additive engine hook (move_to_zone only consults replacements when leaving the battlefield)\n```\n\nRelevant paths:\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-rationale.md`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-files.txt`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/untestable.json`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a49ae89e43421d2d0 (use SendMessage with to: 'a49ae89e43421d2d0' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 109964\ntool_uses: 54\nduration_ms: 310089</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"70d239f8-9513-4890-9eec-c2dcc875cdc0","timestamp":"2026-06-02T07:39:52.948Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are writing pytest tests for a single Magic: The Gathering card implementation (TDD red phase). The card is **sos_1**.\n\n## Inputs\n- Card spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_spec.json` (read this for name, mana cost, oracle text, P/T, keywords).\n- Implementation stub you are testing against: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py`.\n- Test conventions: study existing tests under `/workspace/engine_tests/` (e.g. `/workspace/engine_tests/test_casting.py`, `/workspace/engine_tests/test_triggers.py`, `/workspace/engine_tests/test_combat.py`) and the FDN reference card tests that ship with a `tests.py`: `cards/fdn/fdn_13/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_142/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_205/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_215/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_244/tests.py`.\n- Test helpers: `/workspace/test_utils.py` and its reference `/workspace/test_utils.md` (`create_game`, `set_board_state`, etc.).\n- Reference card implementations: `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_*/card_impl.py`.\n- Engine source with