{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rt3R12WRW9d6D936FaS8yW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives — sos_1\n2\t\n3\t## Engine gap to close (from Tester's untestable.json)\n4\t\n5\tThe card's \"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\"\n6\tclause IS already covered by tests in `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`\n7\t(`test_recast_spell_is_exiled_not_in_graveyard`,\n8\t`test_spell_leaves_graveyard_when_cast`, `test_can_target_a_sorcery`).\n9\t\n10\tThe Tester found that the natural path does not satisfy it: `engine.zones.move_to_zone`\n11\tonly consults the replacement manager when `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`. A spell cast\n12\tfor free via the attack trigger resolves STACK -> GRAVEYARD through\n13\t`engine.casting._resolve_spell`, which calls `move_to_zone(STACK -> GRAVEYARD)` with\n14\tno `replacement_event`, so a registered redirect-to-exile never fires.\n15\t\n16\t### Directive\n17\tYou ARE permitted (and expected) to make an **additive** engine change to close this gap.\n18\tAGENTS.md allows adding methods/helpers and modifying existing function bodies; you must\n19\tNOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Choose whichever is cleaner:\n20\t\n21\t- (preferred) Make stack->graveyard resolution consult replacement effects, so a\n22\t  registered MoveToGraveyard-style redirect to exile fires when the recast spell would\n23\t  hit the graveyard; OR\n24\t- a card-side custom resolution path that routes the recast instant/sorcery to exile\n25\t  directly instead of the graveyard.\n26\t\n27\tEither approach must make the 3 exile-instead tests pass **without modifying any test file**.\n28\tDo not break existing engine regression tests — verify with the full suite.\n29\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01V47x35JN2jnvC54S4NFizo","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"a1c9dc83-399d-40ea-8b8f-e2b7574f94e1","timestamp":"2026-06-02T07:40:45.385Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_1"}
