p/coordinator-run/sos_1/coordinator-directives.md` — describes an additive engine change you must make for the \"exile it instead\" clause.\n- Reference implementations: `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_*/card_impl.py`.\n- Engine source with rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/types.py`.\n- Workspace rules: `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`, `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md`, `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n- Rules reference: `/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt` (grep; see `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n\n## Constraints\n- You MUST NOT modify any test file listed in test-files.txt, nor anything under `engine_tests/`, nor any FDN `tests.py`.\n- Engine changes must be ADDITIVE per AGENTS.md: you may add methods/classes/helpers and modify existing function bodies, but you MUST NOT rename, move, or delete existing engine symbols.\n- Make ALL tests for sos_1 pass. Also run the FULL test suite (`pytest` from `/workspace`) and ensure you do not break any existing engine regression tests.\n- If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible (not just hard), do NOT edit it — instead return DISPUTE with details.\n\n## Your task\n1. Read the spec, the tests, and the coordinator directives.\n2. Implement `cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` and make whatever additive engine changes are needed (especially the stack->graveyard replacement/exile hook described in the directives).\n3. Verify: run `pytest cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py` then the full `pytest` suite from `/workspace`.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- Completed `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` (and any engine source changes).\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl.diff` — `git diff` of all your changes (run `git diff > /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl.diff` from `/workspace`, including staged+unstaged; use `git add -N` for new files first so they appear in the diff).\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-rationale.m