{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gvo6PGhJ6gyyXseKruD6tG","type":"tool_result","content":"engine/casting.py:89:def get_cost_reduction(game: GameState, card: CardImpl, controller: Player) -> int:\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-90-    \"\"\"Return the generic mana reduction for casting *card*.\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-91-\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-92-    Queries ``card.cost_reduction(game)`` and clamps the result so that\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-93-    the generic portion of the mana cost cannot go below 0.\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-94-\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-95-    This is a simplified single-card self-reduction model.  Full MTG\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-96-    cost-reduction interactions (Trinisphere, multiple reductions from\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-97-    different sources) are deferred.\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-98-    \"\"\"\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-99-    # Ensure card.controller is set so the hook can reference \"you\" / the\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-100-    # casting player even when the card was never explicitly assigned one.\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-101-    prev_controller = card.controller\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-102-    card.controller = controller\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-103-    raw = card.cost_reduction(game)\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-104-    # Restore previous controller in case the caller doesn't want a\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-105-    # side-effect (get_cost_reduction is a query, not a mutation).\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-106-    card.controller = prev_controller\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-107-    generic = card.mana_cost.generic if card.mana_cost else 0\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-108-    return max(0, min(raw, generic))\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-109-\n/workspace/engine/casting.py-110-\nengine/casting.py-111-def _apply_cost_reduction(cost: ManaCost, reduction: int) -> ManaCost:\nengine/casting.py-112-    \"\"\"Return a new :c