{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016vT2jg8HPMuWbJdrm89h1Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VywsFYsvL2Wois2AbXhfRT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/review.json","content":"[\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"engine/casting.py\", \"line\": 469, \"comment\": \"The stack->graveyard redirect entry is only consumed in _resolve_spell. If the free-cast spell leaves the stack without resolving normally (e.g. it is countered or otherwise removed), the id(card)->destination entry is never popped and leaks in the per-game registry. Because the key is id(card), a future card object that reuses that CPython id could in principle be wrongly redirected to exile. The common path (resolve / cast-failure clear) is clean and defaults to graveyard correctly, so this is a low-risk edge case in the current simplified engine, but consider clearing the entry on any STACK exit (or keying on the card object itself / a per-resolution token) to fully avoid cross-spell state leakage.\"},\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 106, \"comment\": \"The trigger effect wraps choose_yes_no, choose_card, and cast_spell_free in bare `except Exception` blocks. Swallowing all exceptions can mask genuine implementation bugs (e.g. a real error inside cast_spell_free) by silently turning them into a no-op. The MTG-correct outcome (do nothing if the spell can't be cast) is fine, but consider narrowing these to the specific expected exception type(s) so unexpected errors still surface.\"},\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 118, \"comment\": \"The oracle text says 'target instant or sorcery card', but the chosen spell is selected via choose_card rather than the engine's targeting system (get_targets/choose_target). In this simplified engine that is acceptable since the card comes from the controller's own graveyard, but it means the choice is not a true 'target' and won't interact with targeting restrictions/redirection. Worth noting if a future card needs the chosen spell to be a legal, trackable target.\"},\n  {\"severity\": \"advisory\", \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\", \"line\": 85, \"comment\": \"`controller = getattr(self, 'controller', None) or game.active_player` captures the controller at registration time only for APNAP ordering, which is fine. The effect body re-reads `source.controller` at resolution, so behaviour is correct; just flagging that the registration-time fallback to active_player is purely an ordering hint and not the controller used for the actual effect.\"}\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_read_input_tokens":49016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":969,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01V4UV3nu5k25iEqvDPF1Kdu","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"781ba885-faf5-4dea-89bc-d337bd188c25","request_id":"req_011Cbe4VAYjcHVL2esNpPcWV","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_1 implementation"}
