{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WYgy5ZZjF6fAUhaa5KtsB4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent, append-only log of conventions and design decisions across runs.\n4\t\n5\t## Engine: stack->graveyard exile redirect (from sos_1)\n6\t- For \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" free-cast effects:\n7\t  `engine.casting` now has an additive per-game redirect registry:\n8\t  - `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card, destination)` — one-shot, identity-keyed by `id(card)`.\n9\t  - `clear_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card)`.\n10\t  - `_redirect_registry(game)` lazily attaches `game._stack_to_graveyard_redirects` (no GameState.__init__ change).\n11\t  - `_resolve_spell` pops any registered redirect for a non-permanent spell and routes it there instead of the graveyard; with no redirect registered, behavior is unchanged (defaults to GRAVEYARD).\n12\t- Usage in a card: call `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, chosen_card, \"exile\")` before `cast_spell_free(...)`. Clear it if the cast raises.\n13\t- Rationale: `engine.zones.move_to_zone` only consults replacement effects when `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`, so STACK->GRAVEYARD resolution would otherwise bypass an exile-instead replacement.\n14\t\n15\t## Convention: cost_reduction counts (from sos_1)\n16\t- Card `cost_reduction` returns the raw count (e.g. instants+sorceries in controller's graveyard); the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the generic portion of the cost. Mirrors fdn_167 (Tolarian Terror). Count only the controller's graveyard unless the card says otherwise.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017XnfBsLBoqcc16puCrNhTD","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"ccf4bb7c-bf14-453a-a4b2-69c6233382b7","timestamp":"2026-06-02T07:46:27.980Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_4"}
