{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Wk5WnnFVcYcYXkkrqByR2k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MUZRpdYTUSQt65WtCbqTHt","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_4 \"Together as One\"\n\nCard: **Together as One** — `{6}` Sorcery (Converge).\n\n> Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to\n> any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana\n> spent to cast this spell.\n\nTest file: `cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` (20 tests).\n\n## Behavior contract derived from the spec + engine\n\n- **X = number of distinct colors of mana spent.** The engine's cast pipeline\n  (`engine/casting.py`) records this on the card as\n  `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` — a list of\n  `engine.types.Color` (colorless excluded, de-duplicated). Therefore\n  `X == len(self.colors_spent)`. This is the realistic engine-produced format\n  (the FDN 205 reference card defaults the attribute to `0` and overrides it,\n  but the live pipeline always assigns a list). Tests set `colors_spent` to a\n  list of `Color` values; the full-cast test lets the engine populate it.\n- **Two targets**, in oracle order: (1) a *target player* (for the draw) and\n  (2) an *any target* — a player or creature (for the damage). `chosen_targets`\n  is `[target_player, any_target]`. This mirrors the FDN target convention\n  (`get_targets()` returns `TargetRequirement`s; the cast pipeline / tests\n  populate `chosen_targets`).\n- **Resolution** applies all three clauses scaled by the same X:\n  the target player draws X, the any-target takes X damage, and the controller\n  (\"you\") gains X life. X == 0 is a no-op for every clause.\n\n## Tests and what each validates\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneProperties` (static data)\n- `test_name` — name is \"Together as One\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost parses to `{6}`.\n- `test_is_sorcery` — is a `Sorcery` / has `CardType.SORCERY`.\n- `test_not_a_creature` — not a creature; has no P/T. (Passes against the empty\n  stub too — it is a static negative property, kept as a contract guard.)\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneTargeting`\n- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — `get_targets` returns exactly two\n  `TargetRequirement`s.\n- `test_player_target_accepts_a_player` / `test_player_target_rejects_a_creature`\n  — the first requirement (target player) accepts players, rejects creatures.\n- `test_any_target_accepts_player_and_creature` — the second requirement\n  (\"any target\") accepts both a player and a creature.\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneConvergeValue`\n- `test_zero_colors_is_a_noop` — X == 0 (all generic mana) → no draw, no damage,\n  no life gain. (Passes against the empty stub as well — it asserts the\n  no-effect case, kept as the lower-bound contract.)\n- `test_two_colors_yields_x_equals_two` — two colors → draw 2 / 2 damage / +2 life.\n- `test_five_colors_yields_x_equals_five` — five colors (WUBRG) → 5 / 5 / +5.\n- `test_duplicate_color_pips_count_once` — distinct colors, not pips: one color\n  → X == 1. (Engine de-dupes `last_payment_colors`; the card must use the\n  distinct-color count it is handed.)\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneDraw`\n- `test_target_player_draws_x_cards` — the chosen target player (here the\n  opponent) draws exactly X cards off the top of their library; library shrinks\n  by X and those specific cards land in hand.\n- `test_controller_can_be_the_drawing_player` — the target player may be the\n  controller; they both draw X and (as \"you\") gain X life.\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneDamage`\n- `test_damage_to_player_reduces_life` — X damage to a player target reduces\n  that player's life by X.\n- `test_damage_to_creature_marks_damage` — X damage to a creature target marks\n  X damage on it (`damage_marked`).\n- `test_lethal_damage_to_creature_kills_it_via_sba` — X >= toughness destroys\n  the creature once state-based actions run (moves to graveyard).\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneLifeGain`\n- `test_controller_gains_x_life` — the controller gains X life even when the\n  target player / damage target is the opponent.\n- `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` — isolates the lifegain\n  clause (damage aimed at an opponent creature): only the controller gains\n  life; the opponent target player does not.\n\n### `TestTogetherAsOneFullCast`\n- `test_cast_with_three_colors_drives_x_equals_three` — end-to-end through the\n  real `engine.casting.cast_spell`: pays `{6}` with three distinct colors + three\n  colorless, scripts both target choices, resolves the spell, and asserts\n  X == 3 (draw 3 / 3 damage / +3 life). This is the authoritative check that the\n  card reads the engine-populated `colors_spent` correctly.\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- X == 0 no-op (lower bound).\n- Distinct-color counting vs. raw pip counting.\n- Damage routed to a player vs. a creature; lethal damage + SBA destruction.\n- Controller vs. target-player separation for both the draw and the lifegain.\n- Full mixed-mana cast (colored + colorless) through the real pipeline.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope)\n- Choosing/optimizing the generic-mana split to maximize colors — the engine\n  notes this is deferred (`# TODO: Phase 3` in `engine/casting.py`); the card\n  consumes whatever colors the engine reports, so this is an engine concern.\n- Protection / hexproof / ward target legality — handled generically by the\n  engine's targeting/protection layer, not by this card.\n- Drawing from an empty library (deck-out loss) — engine SBA behavior, not\n  specific to this card.\n- Replacement effects on damage/lifegain/draw — generic engine behavior.\n\n## Notes on red phase\n18 of 20 tests fail against the empty stub (the real behavior is unimplemented).\nThe 2 that pass (`test_not_a_creature`, `test_zero_colors_is_a_noop`) assert\nstatic/negative-case contract that a correct implementation must also satisfy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":546,"cache_read_input_tokens":86314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":546,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017XnfBsLBoqcc16puCrNhTD","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"e5bd6239-5c36-42a7-973e-daed3fc9957c","request_id":"req_011Cbe4py1WhnGprpewyKuCC","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_4"}
