.\n- If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible (not just hard), do NOT edit it — return DISPUTE with details.\n\n## Your task\n1. Read the spec, the tests, the rationale, and KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n2. Implement `cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` (Converge: X = distinct colors of mana spent; target player draws X; any target takes X damage; you gain X life). Make whatever additive engine changes are needed if Converge / `colors_spent` is not already supported.\n3. Verify: run `pytest cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` then the full `pytest` suite from `/workspace`.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- Completed `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` (and any engine source changes).\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl.diff` — `git diff` of all changes (`git add -N` new files first, then `git diff > /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl.diff` from `/workspace`).\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl-rationale.md` — what you implemented, key design decisions, engine changes and why, any spec deviations.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl-files.txt` — list of all files you changed (one per line).\n- Upsert this card's entry into `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` (match by `card: \"sos_4\"`; replace in place if present). Shape:\n  ```json\n  { \"card\": \"sos_4\",\n    \"tests\":          [{\"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py\", \"summary\": \"<one-line>\"}],\n    \"implementation\": [{\"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py\", \"summary\": \"<one-line>\"}] }\n  ```\n  (add engine file entries to `implementation` if you changed engine source.)\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nIf all tests pass:\n```\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: <N>\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: <one-line>\n```\nIf you must dispute a test (write reasoning to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-dispute.md`):\n```\nDISPUTE\ntests_failing: <N>\ndisputed_tests: <list>\ndispute_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-dispute.md\nnotes: