{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TDpFhm728x2aR5HLbaZHys","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_4 \"Together as One\"\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Together as One** — `{6}` Sorcery (Converge).\n4\t\n5\t> Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to\n6\t> any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana\n7\t> spent to cast this spell.\n8\t\n9\tTest file: `cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` (20 tests).\n10\t\n11\t## Behavior contract derived from the spec + engine\n12\t\n13\t- **X = number of distinct colors of mana spent.** The engine's cast pipeline\n14\t  (`engine/casting.py`) records this on the card as\n15\t  `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` — a list of\n16\t  `engine.types.Color` (colorless excluded, de-duplicated). Therefore\n17\t  `X == len(self.colors_spent)`. This is the realistic engine-produced format\n18\t  (the FDN 205 reference card defaults the attribute to `0` and overrides it,\n19\t  but the live pipeline always assigns a list). Tests set `colors_spent` to a\n20\t  list of `Color` values; the full-cast test lets the engine populate it.\n21\t- **Two targets**, in oracle order: (1) a *target player* (for the draw) and\n22\t  (2) an *any target* — a player or creature (for the damage). `chosen_targets`\n23\t  is `[target_player, any_target]`. This mirrors the FDN target convention\n24\t  (`get_targets()` returns `TargetRequirement`s; the cast pipeline / tests\n25\t  populate `chosen_targets`).\n26\t- **Resolution** applies all three clauses scaled by the same X:\n27\t  the target player draws X, the any-target takes X damage, and the controller\n28\t  (\"you\") gains X life. X == 0 is a no-op for every clause.\n29\t\n30\t## Tests and what each validates\n31\t\n32\t### `TestTogetherAsOneProperties` (static data)\n33\t- `test_name` — name is \"Together as One\".\n34\t- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost parses to `{6}`.\n35\t- `test_is_sorcery` — is a `Sorcery` / has `CardType.SORCERY`.\n36\t- `test_not_a_creature` — not a creature; has no P/T. (Passes against the empty\n37\t  stub too — it is a static negative property, kept as a contract guard.)\n38\t\n39\t### `TestTogetherAsOneTargeting`\n40\t- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — `get_targets` returns exactly two\n41\t  `TargetRequirement`s.\n42\t- `test_player_target_accepts_a_player` / `test_player_target_rejects_a_creature`\n43\t  — the first requirement (target player) accepts players, rejects creatures.\n44\t- `test_any_target_accepts_player_and_creature` — the second requirement\n45\t  (\"any target\") accepts both a player and a creature.\n46\t\n47\t### `TestTogetherAsOneConvergeValue`\n48\t- `test_zero_colors_is_a_noop` — X == 0 (all generic mana) → no draw, no damage,\n49\t  no life gain. (Passes against the empty stub as well — it asserts the\n50\t  no-effect case, kept as the lower-bound contract.)\n51\t- `test_two_colors_yields_x_equals_two` — two colors → draw 2 / 2 damage / +2 life.\n52\t- `test_five_colors_yields_x_equals_five` — five colors (WUBRG) → 5 / 5 / +5.\n53\t- `test_duplicate_color_pips_count_once` — distinct colors, not pips: one color\n54\t  → X == 1. (Engine de-dupes `last_payment_colors`; the card must use the\n55\t  distinct-color count it is handed.)\n56\t\n57\t### `TestTogetherAsOneDraw`\n58\t- `test_target_player_draws_x_cards` — the chosen target player (here the\n59\t  opponent) draws exactly X cards off the top of their library; library shrinks\n60\t  by X and those specific cards land in hand.\n61\t- `test_controller_can_be_the_drawing_player` — the target player may be the\n62\t  controller; they both draw X and (as \"you\") gain X life.\n63\t\n64\t### `TestTogetherAsOneDamage`\n65\t- `test_damage_to_player_reduces_life` — X damage to a player target reduces\n66\t  that player's life by X.\n67\t- `test_damage_to_creature_marks_damage` — X damage to a creature target marks\n68\t  X damage on it (`damage_marked`).\n69\t- `test_lethal_damage_to_creature_kills_it_via_sba` — X >= toughness destroys\n70\t  the creature once state-based actions run (moves to graveyard).\n71\t\n72\t### `TestTogetherAsOneLifeGain`\n73\t- `test_controller_gains_x_life` — the controller gains X life even when the\n74\t  target player / damage target is the opponent.\n75\t- `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` — isolates the lifegain\n76\t  clause (damage aimed at an opponent creature): only the controller gains\n77\t  life; the opponent target player does not.\n78\t\n79\t### `TestTogetherAsOneFullCast`\n80\t- `test_cast_with_three_colors_drives_x_equals_three` — end-to-end through the\n81\t  real `engine.casting.cast_spell`: pays `{6}` with three distinct colors + three\n82\t  colorless, scripts both target choices, resolves the spell, and asserts\n83\t  X == 3 (draw 3 / 3 damage / +3 life). This is the authoritative check that the\n84\t  card reads the engine-populated `colors_spent` correctly.\n85\t\n86\t## Edge cases covered\n87\t- X == 0 no-op (lower bound).\n88\t- Distinct-color counting vs. raw pip counting.\n89\t- Damage routed to a player vs. a creature; lethal damage + SBA destruction.\n90\t- Controller vs. target-player separation for both the draw and the lifegain.\n91\t- Full mixed-mana cast (colored + colorless) through the real pipeline.\n92\t\n93\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope)\n94\t- Choosing/optimizing the generic-mana split to maximize colors — the engine\n95\t  notes this is deferred (`# TODO: Phase 3` in `engine/casting.py`); the card\n96\t  consumes whatever colors the engine reports, so this is an engine concern.\n97\t- Protection / hexproof / ward target legality — handled generically by the\n98\t  engine's targeting/protection layer, not by this card.\n99\t- Drawing from an empty library (deck-out loss) — engine SBA behavior, not\n100\t  specific to this card.\n101\t- Replacement effects on damage/lifegain/draw — generic engine behavior.\n102\t\n103\t## Notes on red phase\n104\t18 of 20 tests fail against the empty stub (the real behavior is unimplemented).\n105\tThe 2 that pass (`test_not_a_creature`, `test_zero_colors_is_a_noop`) assert\n106\tstatic/negative-case contract that a correct implementation must also satisfy.\n107\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GofJ6gwpGA4k6cyTLF6tM5","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"53ca899d-ef60-448b-8816-1fde7ef82779","timestamp":"2026-06-02T07:51:01.840Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_4"}
