onfirm the tests are well-formed by running them (they should fail/error because the card is unimplemented — that is expected). Do not try to make them pass.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` — your tests.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-rationale.md` — what each test covers and the behavior contract you derived from the spec.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-files.txt` — list of test file path(s) you created (one per line).\n- If any spec requirement cannot be tested with the current engine/test API, write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/untestable.json` — a JSON array of `{\"requirement\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\", \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"...\"}`. Omit the file entirely if everything is testable.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn a short summary: number of tests written, the test file path, and `untestable_count: <N>` (0 if none). Do not paste the full test code."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01X1Cjv5kQbWsufC3nuUDWwW","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"a4704f77-050a-4219-9c66-977376fabc1f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T07:55:16.344Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_13"}
