{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01HqHthV8anfp9BGFUwCuD5c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012pUHyLydZ27x57A9Cgny2x","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n\nThis is a \"complex\"-tier card with a brand-new **Prepared / Preparation Card** mechanic\n(keyword `\"Prepared\"`). The Tester wrote 21 tests for the directly-observable subset and\ndeferred 3 items (see `untestable.json`) because no engine support exists yet. You are\nexpected and required to build that support — ADDITIVELY per AGENTS.md (add new\nmethods/classes/helpers, modify existing function bodies; never rename/move/delete existing\nengine symbols).\n\n## Spec facts\n- Front face: **Emeritus of Truce** — `{1}{W}{W}` — Creature — Cat Cleric — 3/3 — white — keyword \"Prepared\".\n- ETB: \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling\n  creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this\n  creature becomes prepared.\"\n- Reminder: \"While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.\"\n- Back / prepare half: **Swords to Plowshares** — `{W}` — Instant.\n\n## Required: pass all 21 existing tests (DO NOT modify them)\nThe tests cover: front-face static data (name, `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3, white, Cat/Cleric),\nthe single self-referencing ETB trigger, Inkling token creation (1/1 white+black, flying,\ntoken, created under the *targeted* player's control — may be an opponent), the conditional\n\"becomes prepared\" (strictly more opponent creatures ⇒ prepared; equal/fewer ⇒ not), and a\n`{W}` cost surface for the prepare half. The tests read the prepared designation via probe\nattributes `is_prepared` / `prepared`, and read the prepare-half cost via\n`prepare_mana_cost` / `back_mana_cost` or a back-face object/factory — expose at least one\nof those shapes.\n\n## Required: build an additive engine Preparation framework\nModel the mechanic so it is observable and correct:\n1. A way to mark a permanent as **prepared** (e.g. a boolean designation / `is_prepared`\n   on the card, and ideally a `Keyword.PREPARED` if you add one additively to the enum —\n   additive enum members are allowed).\n2. On **becoming prepared**: create a castable **copy of the prepare spell** (the `{W}`\n   Swords to Plowshares instant) in the controller's **exile** zone, keyed to the prepared\n   permanent (CR 722.3c).\n3. The controller **may cast** that exiled copy (use/extend `cast_spell_free` or an\n   equivalent path to cast from exile). **Casting the copy clears the prepared designation**\n   (unprepares the source permanent).\n4. Keep it additive and do not break existing engine regression tests.\n\n## Required: implement the back-face Swords to Plowshares effect (coordinator ruling)\nThe card_spec.json omits the back-face rules text, but the name \"Swords to Plowshares\" is\nunambiguous. Implement the canonical effect for the prepare half:\n\n> **Swords to Plowshares** `{W}` Instant — Exile target creature. Its controller gains life\n> equal to its power.\n\nSo the back/prepare half is an Instant costing `{W}` that exiles a target creature and gives\nthat creature's controller life equal to its (last-known) power.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` → all pass.\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions.\n\nAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester once to add tests for the\ncopy-in-exile creation, cast-from-exile unprepare transition, and the Swords effect — build\nthe framework so those behaviours are real and observable, not just stubbed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3571,"cache_read_input_tokens":53176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3571},"output_tokens":54,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"75c116ab-7fe5-4e10-b33e-19c9886d0dfb","request_id":"req_011Cbe5qEghpkviqNmDXqiGv"}
