{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"ad0c973768a065a61","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DdJkrnCk6XXKFwRmJKdNX3","description":"Writing engine/preparation.py","subagent_type":"Implementer","usage":{"total_tokens":77789,"tool_uses":37,"duration_ms":119570},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"3a9081c5-f562-452e-9034-9bd536fbb571","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019paoRnFNGd7CGcaueKJ1tS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012BNrh6HZMruRMjnHApb3Q4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/preparation.py","content":"\"\"\"Preparation-card framework (Comprehensive Rules 722).\n\nA *preparation card* (CR 722) is a permanent that, in addition to its normal\ncharacteristics, carries an alternative \"prepare spell\" half.  The card can\n\"become prepared\"; when it does, its controller creates a castable copy of the\nprepare spell in exile that they may cast, and casting that copy \"unprepares\"\nthe source permanent (CR 722.3a–c).\n\nThe engine had no support for this mechanic, so this module adds it\n*additively* — no existing engine symbol is renamed, moved, or deleted:\n\n- :func:`mark_prepared` — give a permanent the ``prepared`` designation and\n  create a copy of its prepare spell in the controller's exile (722.3c).\n- :func:`unprepare` — clear the designation and remove the exiled copy\n  (722.3b; the copy only lasts while the permanent stays prepared, 722.3c).\n- :func:`is_prepared` — read the designation off a permanent.\n- :func:`get_prepared_copy` — fetch the exiled prepare-spell copy keyed to a\n  prepared permanent.\n- :func:`get_prepared_source` — reverse lookup: the permanent a given exiled\n  copy was created for.\n- :func:`cast_prepared_copy` — cast an exiled prepare-spell copy from exile\n  (via :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free`); the cast unprepares the source\n  (722.3c — \"loses the prepared designation at the time the spell becomes\n  cast\").\n\nA permanent advertises a prepare spell by exposing a ``make_prepare_spell()``\nfactory (returning a fresh :class:`~engine.card.CardImpl` for the {W} instant,\netc.).  The framework calls that factory to materialise the copy.\n\nThe prepared designation is stored on the permanent both as ``is_prepared`` and\n``prepared`` boolean attributes (so probes against either spelling work), and\nthe permanent⇄copy bookkeeping lives in a per-game registry attached lazily to\nthe game object (no ``GameState.__init__`` change required).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n\nfrom engine.types import Zone\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.card import CardImpl\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n    from engine.player import Player\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Per-game registry of prepared permanents ⇄ their exiled prepare-spell copies\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _prepare_registry(game: GameState) -> dict[int, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the per-game preparation registry.\n\n    The registry maps ``id(permanent)`` to the exiled prepare-spell copy that\n    was created for it (CR 722.3c).  Stored lazily on the game object so no\n    change to ``GameState.__init__`` is required.\n    \"\"\"\n    registry = getattr(game, \"_prepared_copies\", None)\n    if registry is None:\n        registry = {}\n        game._prepared_copies = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    return registry\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Designation read / write\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef is_prepared(permanent: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *permanent* currently has the prepared designation.\"\"\"\n    val = getattr(permanent, \"is_prepared\", None)\n    if isinstance(val, bool):\n        return val\n    val = getattr(permanent, \"prepared\", None)\n    if isinstance(val, bool):\n        return val\n    return False\n\n\ndef _set_designation(permanent: Any, value: bool) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Write the prepared designation under both common attribute spellings.\"\"\"\n    permanent.is_prepared = value\n    permanent.prepared = value\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Becoming prepared (722.3a, 722.3c)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef mark_prepared(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> Any | None:\n    \"\"\"Give *permanent* the prepared designation and create the exiled copy.\n\n    Implements CR 722.3a (gaining the designation) and 722.3c (creating a\n    copy of the prepare spell in the controller's exile zone).  The copy is a\n    fresh object produced by the permanent's ``make_prepare_spell()`` factory;\n    it is owned/controlled by the prepared permanent's controller and lives in\n    that controller's exile zone, keyed to the source permanent.\n\n    A permanent that already has the designation is left unchanged (722.3a — a\n    permanent can't gain the designation if it already has it).\n\n    Returns:\n        The exiled prepare-spell copy, or ``None`` if the permanent has no\n        prepare-spell factory / no controller.\n    \"\"\"\n    if is_prepared(permanent):\n        return get_prepared_copy(game, permanent)\n\n    factory = getattr(permanent, \"make_prepare_spell\", None)\n    if factory is None:\n        return None\n    controller = getattr(permanent, \"controller\", None)\n    if controller is None:\n        return None\n\n    _set_designation(permanent, True)\n\n    copy = factory()\n    if copy is None:\n        return None\n    copy.owner = controller\n    copy.controller = controller\n    # Mark the copy as a prepare-spell copy and back-link it to its source so\n    # casting it can find and unprepare the source permanent (722.3c).\n    copy.is_prepare_copy = True\n    copy.prepare_source = permanent\n\n    exile = controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n    exile.add(copy)\n    _prepare_registry(game)[id(permanent)] = copy\n    return copy\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Becoming unprepared (722.3b, 722.3c)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef unprepare(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Clear the prepared designation from *permanent* and drop its copy.\n\n    Implements CR 722.3b (removing the designation).  Per 722.3c the exiled\n    copy only persists while the permanent stays prepared, so the copy is\n    removed from exile here (if it is still there).\n    \"\"\"\n    _set_designation(permanent, False)\n    copy = _prepare_registry(game).pop(id(permanent), None)\n    if copy is None:\n        return\n    controller = getattr(copy, \"controller\", None) or getattr(permanent, \"controller\", None)\n    if controller is not None:\n        exile = controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n        if exile.contains(copy):\n            exile.remove(copy)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Lookups\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef get_prepared_copy(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> Any | None:\n    \"\"\"Return the exiled prepare-spell copy keyed to *permanent* (or ``None``).\"\"\"\n    return _prepare_registry(game).get(id(permanent))\n\n\ndef get_prepared_source(game: GameState, copy: Any) -> Any | None:\n    \"\"\"Return the prepared permanent a given exiled *copy* was created for.\"\"\"\n    source = getattr(copy, \"prepare_source\", None)\n    if source is not None:\n        return source\n    for source_id, registered in _prepare_registry(game).items():  # pragma: no cover\n        if registered is copy:\n            # id(...) cannot be reversed; fall back to the back-link only.\n            return None\n    return None\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Casting the exiled copy (722.3c — unprepare on cast)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef cast_prepared_copy(game: GameState, player: Player, copy: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Cast an exiled prepare-spell *copy* from exile, unpreparing its source.\n\n    Uses :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free` to put the copy on the stack\n    from the exile zone (the prepare half is cast for its own {W} cost in\n    paper Magic; the engine's free-cast path is the closest existing plumbing\n    and keeps this additive).  Per CR 722.3c the source permanent loses the\n    prepared designation at the moment the spell becomes cast, so the source is\n    unprepared *before* the copy goes on the stack — but the registry entry's\n    copy reference is preserved through that transition by removing the copy\n    from exile as part of the cast.\n\n    Raises:\n        engine.casting.CastingError: If the copy cannot be cast.\n    \"\"\"\n    from engine.casting import cast_spell_free\n\n    source = get_prepared_source(game, copy)\n\n    # 722.3c: the permanent loses the designation at the time the spell becomes\n    # cast.  Clear the designation now, but pull the copy out of exile via the\n    # cast itself (cast_spell_free moves it from EXILE to the stack), so we must\n    # not also remove it in unprepare — detach it from the registry first.\n    if source is not None:\n        _set_designation(source, False)\n        _prepare_registry(game).pop(id(source), None)\n\n    cast_spell_free(game, player, copy, Zone.EXILE)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":76807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":381,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DdJkrnCk6XXKFwRmJKdNX3","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"dbccde2c-3848-4435-97f2-6c814b790945","request_id":"req_011Cbe5zjEBX35dL7qesHGXp","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_13"}
