{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFb1gHoLxSGqc7bg91fWgF","type":"tool_result","content":"-rw-r--r-- 1 node node 2375 Jun  2 08:02 /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md\nd4ac78b feat: implement card sos_1\n---head---\n# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Untestable item: sos_1 — \"exile it instead\" clause\n- **Requirement**: recast spell that would go to graveyard is exiled instead.\n- **Tester finding**: clause is already tested; natural path fails because `move_to_zone` only consults replacements when leaving the battlefield (STACK->GRAVEYARD resolution skips replacements).\n- **Resolution**: case (a) — handed back to Implementer via coordinator-directives.md. Implementer must add an additive engine hook (consult replacements on stack->graveyard, or card-side custom resolution to exile). No test change. No Tester re-invocation needed (test already exists).\n## Untestable items: sos_13 — Preparation Card mechanic (3 items)\n- Card: \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\" — front face {1}{W}{W} Creature; keyword \"Prepared\"; back/prepare half {W} Instant. Complexity tier: complex.\n- Tester wrote 21 tests for the testable subset (front-face stats, ETB Inkling token, conditional becomes-prepared, {W} prepare-half cost). 3 items deferred for lack of engine support:\n  1. On \"becomes prepared\": create a castable copy of the prepare spell in exile (CR 722.3c).\n  2. Casting that copy unprepares the permanent.\n  3. The back-face Swords to Plowshares resolution effect (spec omits its rules text).\n- **Decision (a — hand to Implementer)**: direct the Implementer to build an ADDITIVE engine Preparation framework (a `prepared` designation on permanents; on becoming prepared, register/create a castable copy of the prepare spell in the controller's exile keyed to the permanent; casting it clears the prepared designation). Make all 21 existing tests pass.\n- **Decision on item 3 (coordinator ruling)**: the back-face oracle text is omitted from card_spec.json, but the name \"Swords to Plowshares\" is unambiguous. Implement the canonical effect: \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\" Logged here so it's grep-able. If the grader's authoritative back-face text differs, this is a best-effort match.\n- After the Implementer builds the framework, re-invoke the Tester ONCE to extend coverage of the now-testable mechanics (copy-in-exile, cast-from-exile unprepare, Swords effect), then re-invoke the Implementer if the extended tests fail.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DdJkrnCk6XXKFwRmJKdNX3","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"7e86db05-ca3d-4704-b786-144de4836a9c","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:07:53.633Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_13"}
