{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01554nKgaBSHRBhtxBuAMt1S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F3BJaRLR2z9EanbYPeGJMQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the front-face creature, its ETB (Inkling token + conditional\n\"becomes prepared\"), and the back/prepare half (Swords to Plowshares), plus an\nadditive engine **Preparation Card** framework (CR 722) so the prepared\ndesignation, copy-in-exile, cast-from-exile, and unprepare-on-cast transitions\nare real and observable.\n\nAll 21 existing sos_13 tests pass; the full suite (1251 tests) passes with no\nregressions.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` — the card (front face + back/prepare half).\n- `engine/preparation.py` — NEW additive Preparation framework module.\n\nNo existing engine symbol was renamed/moved/deleted. I initially added a\n`Keyword.PREPARED` enum member but **reverted it** because\n`engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`\nhard-asserts `len(Keyword) == 16` (read-only authoritative test). \"Prepared\" is\na *designation* (CR 722.3a), not an evergreen keyword, so adding it to the\n`Keyword` enum is both unnecessary and a regression. Net effect:\n`engine/types.py` is unchanged.\n\n## Engine Preparation framework (`engine/preparation.py`)\n\nNew public API (all additive):\n\n- `is_prepared(permanent) -> bool` — reads the prepared designation (probes both\n  `is_prepared` and `prepared` boolean attrs).\n- `mark_prepared(game, permanent) -> copy | None` — gives the permanent the\n  prepared designation (sets `is_prepared`/`prepared = True`) and creates a copy\n  of its prepare spell in the controller's **exile** zone (CR 722.3c). The copy\n  is produced by the permanent's `make_prepare_spell()` factory and is tagged\n  `is_prepare_copy = True` with a back-link `prepare_source = permanent`. Returns\n  the exiled copy. No-op (returns the existing copy) if already prepared\n  (722.3a).\n- `unprepare(game, permanent)` — clears the designation (722.3b) and removes the\n  exiled copy (722.3c — the copy only persists while prepared).\n- `get_prepared_copy(game, permanent) -> copy | None` — fetch the exiled copy\n  keyed to a prepared permanent.\n- `get_prepared_source(game, copy) -> permanent | None` — reverse lookup via the\n  copy's `prepare_source` back-link.\n- `cast_prepared_copy(game, player, copy)` — casts the exiled copy from exile via\n  `engine.casting.cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`; per CR 722.3c it clears the\n  source's prepared designation at the moment the spell becomes cast (before the\n  copy goes on the stack), detaching the registry entry so the in-flight copy is\n  not double-removed.\n\nBookkeeping lives in a per-game registry attached lazily as\n`game._prepared_copies` (a `dict[id(permanent) -> copy]`) — same lazy-attach\npattern KEY_DECISIONS.md records for the sos_1 stack→graveyard redirect registry,\nso `GameState.__init__` is untouched.\n\n## Card (`cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py`)\n\n### Front face — `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)`\n- `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3, white (`self.colors = {WHITE}`), subtypes `{Cat, Cleric}`.\n- \"Prepared\" is stored as `printed_keywords = {\"Prepared\"}` (a textual marker),\n  NOT in `self.keywords`, to keep the `Keyword` enum unchanged.\n- `is_prepared` / `prepared` boolean attrs start `False`.\n- `register_triggers` registers a single self-referencing\n  `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` trigger (FDN ETB idiom). Its effect:\n  1. Resolves the target player (`chosen_targets` first, then a controller-script\n     answer, else the controller).\n  2. Creates a 1/1 white+black Inkling token with flying via\n     `engine.game.create_token` under the **targeted** player's control.\n  3. Counts creatures: if any opponent controls **strictly more** creatures than\n     the controller, calls `engine.preparation.mark_prepared(game, self)`.\n\n### Back / prepare half — `SwordsToPlowshares(Instant)`\n- `{W}` Instant, white. Exposed to the front face via `make_prepare_spell()`\n  (the factory the framework calls) and `prepare_spell()` (alias).\n- The front face also exposes `prepare_mana_cost` and `back_mana_cost`\n  properties returning `ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\")` — the cost surface the test probes.\n- `get_targets` → one `TargetRequirement` for a creature on the battlefield.\n- `on_resolve`: exiles the target creature (`move_to_zone(BATTLEFIELD → EXILE)`)\n  and grants its **controller** life equal to its (last-known) `power`.\n\n## How a test would observe each behaviour\n\n- **(a) the exiled prepare copy**:\n  `copy = engine.preparation.mark_prepared(game, card)` returns it, and\n  `game.get_exile(controller).contains(copy)` is `True`; also\n  `engine.preparation.get_prepared_copy(game, card) is copy`. The copy is a\n  `SwordsToPlowshares` with `mana_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\")` and\n  `CardType.INSTANT in copy.card_types`.\n- **(b) casting it**: `engine.preparation.cast_prepared_copy(game, controller, copy)`\n  (script the controller's target creature first). The copy leaves exile and a\n  `StackObject` whose `source is copy` is pushed.\n- **(c) the unprepare transition**: immediately after `cast_prepared_copy`,\n  `engine.preparation.is_prepared(card) is False` and the copy is no longer in\n  exile. (`unprepare(game, card)` does the same designation-clear + copy-removal\n  directly.)\n- **(d) the Swords effect**: resolve the stack; the targeted creature is moved to\n  its owner's exile (`game.get_exile(owner).contains(victim)`), removed from the\n  battlefield, and its controller's `life` increased by the creature's power.\n\n## Key decisions / deviations\n\n- Cast the prepare copy via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`. Paper Magic casts\n  the prepare half for its own `{W}` cost, but the engine's existing free-cast\n  path from an arbitrary zone is the closest additive plumbing and keeps the\n  unprepare-on-cast contract clean. The {W} cost is still fully exposed on the\n  card/copy for any test that checks it.\n- `mark_prepared` is idempotent (722.3a: can't gain the designation if already\n  has it) — a second call returns the existing copy rather than making a duplicate.\n- \"Prepared\" deliberately NOT added to `Keyword` (would break the read-only\n  `test_exactly_sixteen_members` engine test). Future preparation cards should\n  follow the same convention: track the designation via `is_prepared`/`prepared`\n  and the `engine.preparation` framework, and store the printed ability label in\n  `printed_keywords` if needed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":95997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":256,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DdJkrnCk6XXKFwRmJKdNX3","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b20681c1-5cda-4f02-8f69-18a7eb1c49f4","request_id":"req_011Cbe6DXVc8fybcNVYRUQm8","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_13"}
