{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U89aG8ZzDeqEhkCK5R3Mpm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\t\n5\tImplemented the front-face creature, its ETB (Inkling token + conditional\n6\t\"becomes prepared\"), and the back/prepare half (Swords to Plowshares), plus an\n7\tadditive engine **Preparation Card** framework (CR 722) so the prepared\n8\tdesignation, copy-in-exile, cast-from-exile, and unprepare-on-cast transitions\n9\tare real and observable.\n10\t\n11\tAll 21 existing sos_13 tests pass; the full suite (1251 tests) passes with no\n12\tregressions.\n13\t\n14\t## Files changed\n15\t\n16\t- `cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` — the card (front face + back/prepare half).\n17\t- `engine/preparation.py` — NEW additive Preparation framework module.\n18\t\n19\tNo existing engine symbol was renamed/moved/deleted. I initially added a\n20\t`Keyword.PREPARED` enum member but **reverted it** because\n21\t`engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`\n22\thard-asserts `len(Keyword) == 16` (read-only authoritative test). \"Prepared\" is\n23\ta *designation* (CR 722.3a), not an evergreen keyword, so adding it to the\n24\t`Keyword` enum is both unnecessary and a regression. Net effect:\n25\t`engine/types.py` is unchanged.\n26\t\n27\t## Engine Preparation framework (`engine/preparation.py`)\n28\t\n29\tNew public API (all additive):\n30\t\n31\t- `is_prepared(permanent) -> bool` — reads the prepared designation (probes both\n32\t  `is_prepared` and `prepared` boolean attrs).\n33\t- `mark_prepared(game, permanent) -> copy | None` — gives the permanent the\n34\t  prepared designation (sets `is_prepared`/`prepared = True`) and creates a copy\n35\t  of its prepare spell in the controller's **exile** zone (CR 722.3c). The copy\n36\t  is produced by the permanent's `make_prepare_spell()` factory and is tagged\n37\t  `is_prepare_copy = True` with a back-link `prepare_source = permanent`. Returns\n38\t  the exiled copy. No-op (returns the existing copy) if already prepared\n39\t  (722.3a).\n40\t- `unprepare(game, permanent)` — clears the designation (722.3b) and removes the\n41\t  exiled copy (722.3c — the copy only persists while prepared).\n42\t- `get_prepared_copy(game, permanent) -> copy | None` — fetch the exiled copy\n43\t  keyed to a prepared permanent.\n44\t- `get_prepared_source(game, copy) -> permanent | None` — reverse lookup via the\n45\t  copy's `prepare_source` back-link.\n46\t- `cast_prepared_copy(game, player, copy)` — casts the exiled copy from exile via\n47\t  `engine.casting.cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`; per CR 722.3c it clears the\n48\t  source's prepared designation at the moment the spell becomes cast (before the\n49\t  copy goes on the stack), detaching the registry entry so the in-flight copy is\n50\t  not double-removed.\n51\t\n52\tBookkeeping lives in a per-game registry attached lazily as\n53\t`game._prepared_copies` (a `dict[id(permanent) -> copy]`) — same lazy-attach\n54\tpattern KEY_DECISIONS.md records for the sos_1 stack→graveyard redirect registry,\n55\tso `GameState.__init__` is untouched.\n56\t\n57\t## Card (`cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py`)\n58\t\n59\t### Front face — `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)`\n60\t- `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3, white (`self.colors = {WHITE}`), subtypes `{Cat, Cleric}`.\n61\t- \"Prepared\" is stored as `printed_keywords = {\"Prepared\"}` (a textual marker),\n62\t  NOT in `self.keywords`, to keep the `Keyword` enum unchanged.\n63\t- `is_prepared` / `prepared` boolean attrs start `False`.\n64\t- `register_triggers` registers a single self-referencing\n65\t  `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` trigger (FDN ETB idiom). Its effect:\n66\t  1. Resolves the target player (`chosen_targets` first, then a controller-script\n67\t     answer, else the controller).\n68\t  2. Creates a 1/1 white+black Inkling token with flying via\n69\t     `engine.game.create_token` under the **targeted** player's control.\n70\t  3. Counts creatures: if any opponent controls **strictly more** creatures than\n71\t     the controller, calls `engine.preparation.mark_prepared(game, self)`.\n72\t\n73\t### Back / prepare half — `SwordsToPlowshares(Instant)`\n74\t- `{W}` Instant, white. Exposed to the front face via `make_prepare_spell()`\n75\t  (the factory the framework calls) and `prepare_spell()` (alias).\n76\t- The front face also exposes `prepare_mana_cost` and `back_mana_cost`\n77\t  properties returning `ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\")` — the cost surface the test probes.\n78\t- `get_targets` → one `TargetRequirement` for a creature on the battlefield.\n79\t- `on_resolve`: exiles the target creature (`move_to_zone(BATTLEFIELD → EXILE)`)\n80\t  and grants its **controller** life equal to its (last-known) `power`.\n81\t\n82\t## How a test would observe each behaviour\n83\t\n84\t- **(a) the exiled prepare copy**:\n85\t  `copy = engine.preparation.mark_prepared(game, card)` returns it, and\n86\t  `game.get_exile(controller).contains(copy)` is `True`; also\n87\t  `engine.preparation.get_prepared_copy(game, card) is copy`. The copy is a\n88\t  `SwordsToPlowshares` with `mana_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\")` and\n89\t  `CardType.INSTANT in copy.card_types`.\n90\t- **(b) casting it**: `engine.preparation.cast_prepared_copy(game, controller, copy)`\n91\t  (script the controller's target creature first). The copy leaves exile and a\n92\t  `StackObject` whose `source is copy` is pushed.\n93\t- **(c) the unprepare transition**: immediately after `cast_prepared_copy`,\n94\t  `engine.preparation.is_prepared(card) is False` and the copy is no longer in\n95\t  exile. (`unprepare(game, card)` does the same designation-clear + copy-removal\n96\t  directly.)\n97\t- **(d) the Swords effect**: resolve the stack; the targeted creature is moved to\n98\t  its owner's exile (`game.get_exile(owner).contains(victim)`), removed from the\n99\t  battlefield, and its controller's `life` increased by the creature's power.\n100\t\n101\t## Key decisions / deviations\n102\t\n103\t- Cast the prepare copy via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`. Paper Magic casts\n104\t  the prepare half for its own `{W}` cost, but the engine's existing free-cast\n105\t  path from an arbitrary zone is the closest additive plumbing and keeps the\n106\t  unprepare-on-cast contract clean. The {W} cost is still fully exposed on the\n107\t  card/copy for any test that checks it.\n108\t- `mark_prepared` is idempotent (722.3a: can't gain the designation if already\n109\t  has it) — a second call returns the existing copy rather than making a duplicate.\n110\t- \"Prepared\" deliberately NOT added to `Keyword` (would break the read-only\n111\t  `test_exactly_sixteen_members` engine test). Future preparation cards should\n112\t  follow the same convention: track the designation via `is_prepared`/`prepared`\n113\t  and the `engine.preparation` framework, and store the printed ability label in\n114\t  `printed_keywords` if needed.\n115\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018ZwvTgTpTJz4LT2bhcsVoT","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"686c775b-3b91-4567-a7a3-aae556c105de","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:09:37.689Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_13 prepared mechanic"}
