{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01G5JDSxC86QnknY1B7jaD1Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HbENSo9eKV6ZTPJnPiN5jf","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-rationale.md","old_string":"- Casting timing / sorcery-vs-instant restrictions on the prepare copy.","new_string":"- Casting timing / sorcery-vs-instant restrictions on the prepare copy.\n\n## Extended coverage\n\nThe Implementer built the additive engine Preparation-card framework\n(`engine/preparation.py`), so the three items previously deferred in\n`untestable.json` are now real and observable. The test file was **extended**\n(all 21 original tests unchanged) with **16 new tests** across four classes,\ntesting the framework's public API as documented in the Implementer's rationale:\n`preparation.is_prepared`, `mark_prepared`, `get_prepared_copy`, `unprepare`,\n`cast_prepared_copy`, plus the `SwordsToPlowshares` back-face effect. New total:\n**37 tests**, all passing.\n\nA `_prepared_card_on_battlefield` helper places an Emeritus on a player's\nbattlefield with owner/controller set, so `mark_prepared` has a real controller\nwhose exile zone receives the copy.\n\n### TestPreparationCopyInExile — 7 tests (deferred item 1: copy-in-exile)\n- `test_mark_prepared_sets_designation` — `is_prepared` flips `False → True`.\n- `test_mark_prepared_returns_exiled_copy` — the returned copy is the object now\n  sitting in the controller's exile (`game.get_exile(p1).contains(copy)`).\n- `test_exiled_copy_is_swords_to_plowshares_instant` — the copy is a\n  `SwordsToPlowshares` with `CardType.INSTANT`.\n- `test_exiled_copy_costs_w` — the copy's `mana_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\")`.\n- `test_copy_keyed_to_prepared_permanent` — `get_prepared_copy(game, card) is\n  copy`, and the per-game registry `game._prepared_copies[id(card)] is copy`.\n- `test_copy_controlled_by_prepared_controller` — the copy is owned/controlled by\n  the prepared permanent's controller and lands in *that* player's exile (not the\n  opponent's). Guards against the copy going to the wrong exile.\n- `test_etb_prepared_branch_creates_exile_copy` — exercises the **real ETB\n  prepared branch** (opponent has strictly more creatures via `_fire_etb`), then\n  asserts the exile copy exists. Anchors the framework to the card's actual\n  trigger path, not just a direct `mark_prepared` call.\n\n### TestPreparationIdempotencyAndUnprepare — 3 tests (deferred edge cases, item 4)\n- `test_mark_prepared_is_idempotent` — a second `mark_prepared` returns the same\n  copy and does not create a duplicate in exile (CR 722.3a). Counts the\n  `SwordsToPlowshares` objects in exile to prove no duplication.\n- `test_unprepare_clears_designation` — `unprepare` flips `is_prepared` back to\n  `False`.\n- `test_unprepare_removes_exile_copy` — `unprepare` removes the copy from exile\n  and clears the registry entry (the copy only persists while prepared, 722.3c).\n\n### TestPreparationCastFromExile — 3 tests (deferred item 2: cast + unprepare)\n- `test_cast_from_exile_unprepares_source` — after `cast_prepared_copy`, the\n  source is no longer prepared (CR 722.3c — unprepare-on-cast).\n- `test_cast_from_exile_moves_copy_off_exile` — the copy leaves exile and a\n  `StackObject` whose `source is copy` is now on the stack.\n- `test_cast_from_exile_clears_registry_entry` — `get_prepared_copy` returns\n  `None` after the cast (registry detached).\n\nThese three script the controller's target creature (`scripts=([victim], [])`)\nso `cast_prepared_copy → choose_target` resolves to a legal creature.\n\n### TestSwordsToPlowsharesEffect — 3 tests (deferred item 3: back-face effect)\nImplements the coordinator's back-face ruling: \"Exile target creature. Its\ncontroller gains life equal to its power.\"\n- `test_resolved_swords_exiles_target_creature` — after casting + resolving, the\n  targeted creature is off the battlefield and in its owner's exile.\n- `test_resolved_swords_controller_gains_life_equal_to_power` — the target's\n  controller gains life equal to the creature's power (a 2/2 ⇒ +2 life).\n- `test_swords_life_goes_to_targets_controller_not_caster` — when the target is an\n  **opponent's** creature, the life goes to the target's controller (the\n  opponent), not the spell's caster, and the creature is exiled to its owner's\n  exile. Guards the \"its controller\" (not \"you\") wording.\n\n### Result\n`pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` → **37 passed** (21 original + 16 new). No new\nfailures; no implementation bugs surfaced. All deferred `untestable.json` items\nare now covered, so the deferral list is fully retired."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":135,"cache_read_input_tokens":64878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":135,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018ZwvTgTpTJz4LT2bhcsVoT","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"1601d5ab-4035-40a5-9f55-efd9e0be9740","request_id":"req_011Cbe6TDQZdRPippm9dUwfr","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_13 prepared mechanic"}
