{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ZwvTgTpTJz4LT2bhcsVoT","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 37 tests pass. The work is complete.\n\nTESTS_REWRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 37 (21 original, 16 added)\npytest_result: 37 passed (`pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`)\nnew_failures: 0\n\nSummary of what I did:\n\nExtended `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` with 16 new tests across four classes, covering the three previously-deferred `untestable.json` items now made testable by the additive `engine/preparation.py` framework. I kept all 21 original tests unchanged and added the framework import (`from engine import preparation`) plus a `SwordsToPlowshares` import.\n\n- `TestPreparationCopyInExile` (7 tests) — item 1: `mark_prepared` sets the designation and creates a `SwordsToPlowshares` `{W}` instant copy in the controller's exile, keyed to the permanent (`get_prepared_copy` + `game._prepared_copies[id(card)]`), owned/controlled by the prepared controller (not the opponent). One test routes through the real ETB prepared branch (opponent has strictly more creatures) rather than a direct `mark_prepared` call.\n- `TestPreparationIdempotencyAndUnprepare` (3 tests) — edge cases: `mark_prepared` idempotency (no duplicate exile copy), and `unprepare` clearing the designation and removing the exile copy.\n- `TestPreparationCastFromExile` (3 tests) — item 2: `cast_prepared_copy` unprepares the source, moves the copy off exile onto the stack (`stack.peek().source is copy`), and clears the registry entry.\n- `TestSwordsToPlowsharesEffect` (3 tests) — item 3: resolving the prepare spell exiles the target creature to its owner's exile and gives its controller life equal to its power; a dedicated test confirms the life goes to the target's controller (an opponent) and not the caster.\n\nNo implementation bugs surfaced — all new tests pass against the existing implementation as intended (the implementation already exists, so these confirm the contract). The deferral list in `untestable.json` is now fully retired.\n\nFiles:\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` (updated — 37 tests)\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-rationale.md` (appended \"## Extended coverage\" section)\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-files.txt` (unchanged — already lists the single file)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acb9cb72b3114ea8f (use SendMessage with to: 'acb9cb72b3114ea8f' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 68087\ntool_uses: 23\nduration_ms: 122152</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"4b368e66-599a-47c0-9172-c7a244e5c93e","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:11:36.736Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You previously wrote tests for card **sos_13** (\"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\"). The Implementer has now built an additive engine **Preparation Card** framework, so the 3 items you previously deferred in `untestable.json` are now testable. Extend your test file to cover them.\n\n## Context: your existing work\n- Your existing tests: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` (21 tests, all currently passing). EXTEND this file — keep all existing tests, ADD new ones.\n- Your prior rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-rationale.md`.\n- Your deferred items: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/untestable.json`.\n- Coordinator directives (back-face ruling): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/coordinator-directives.md`.\n- Implementer's rationale with the exact observable API: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-rationale.md` — READ THIS for the precise framework API.\n\n## The new engine framework (`engine/preparation.py`) — public API to test against\n- `engine.preparation.is_prepared(permanent) -> bool`\n- `engine.preparation.mark_prepared(game, permanent) -> copy | None` — marks prepared and creates a copy of the prepare spell ({W} Swords to Plowshares instant) in the controller's exile; returns the exiled copy; idempotent.\n- `engine.preparation.get_prepared_copy(game, permanent) -> copy | None`\n- `engine.preparation.unprepare(game, permanent)` — clears designation and removes the exiled copy.\n- `engine.preparation.cast_prepared_copy(game, player, copy)` — casts the exiled copy from exile and clears the source's prepared designation at cast time.\n- The exiled copy is a `SwordsToPlowshares` instant with `mana_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\")`. Its back-face effect (coordinator ruling): exile target creature; its controller gains life equal to its power.\n- Per-game registry is `game._prepared_copies`. Exile zone accessed via `game.get_exile(player)` (check the impl-rationale / `engine/zones.py` for exact accessor).\n\n## Your task — add tests covering the previously-untestable items\n1. **Copy-in-exile creation**: after `mark_prepared(game, card)` (or after the card's ETB makes it prepared in a board state where an opponent has strictly more creatures), assert a `SwordsToPlowshares` {W} instant copy exists in the controller's exile, keyed to the prepared permanent, and `is_prepared(card)` is True.\n2. **Cast-from-exile + unprepare transition**: cast the copy via `cast_prepared_copy`; assert the source is no longer prepared and the copy left exile.\n3. **Swords to Plowshares back-face effect**: resolve the prepare spell against a target creature; assert the creature is exiled (off the battlefield, in its owner's exile) and that creature's controller gained life equal to its power.\n4. Cover at least one edge case you find relevant (e.g. `mark_prepared` idempotency, or that `unprepare` removes the exile copy).\n\n## Constraints\n- DO NOT modify `engine_tests/`, FDN `tests.py`, or any engine source. Only edit `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`.\n- DO NOT change or weaken any of your existing 21 tests — only add new ones.\n- The implementation already exists, so your new tests should PASS. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` and confirm everything (old + new) passes. If a 