inize:\n- The ETB: target player creates one 1/1 white+black flying Inkling token under the *targeted* player's control; then \"becomes prepared\" iff an opponent controls STRICTLY MORE creatures than you.\n- The Preparation framework in `engine/preparation.py`: copy-in-exile creation keyed to the permanent, idempotency of `mark_prepared`, the unprepare-on-cast transition (does it clear the designation at the right moment and avoid double-removal?), and whether the lazy `game._prepared_copies` registry can leak/collide across permanents (it keys by `id(permanent)` — any stale-id reuse risk?).\n- The back-face Swords to Plowshares: exiles target creature and gives ITS CONTROLLER (not the caster) life equal to its (last-known) power.\n- Regression safety: confirm nothing existing in engine was renamed/removed (additive-only) and that the `Keyword` enum was left unchanged.\n\n## Important guardrails\n- DO NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards (see `FILES_MODIFIED.json`) or conventions in `KEY_DECISIONS.md` (e.g., the lazy per-game registry pattern, or \"Prepared\" not being a Keyword enum member — these are deliberate).\n- DO NOT demand test rewrites — tests were already arbitrated. Any test-quality concern is `advisory` only.\n- Focus on what is visible in the diff.\n\n## Output (write this)\nWrite `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/review.json` — a JSON array of:\n```json\n{\"severity\": \"strict\" | \"advisory\", \"file\": \"<path>\", \"line\": <int or null>, \"comment\": \"<actionable comment>\"}\n```\nUse `strict` only for must-fix issues (correctness bugs, spec/ruling violations, regression risks). Use `advisory` for style/clarity. Write `[]` if none.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\n```\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/review.json\n```"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1066,"cache_read