ICTLY MORE creatures than you.\n- The Preparation framework in `engine/preparation.py`: copy-in-exile creation keyed to the permanent, idempotency of `mark_prepared`, the unprepare-on-cast transition (does it clear the designation at the right moment and avoid double-removal?), and whether the lazy `game._prepared_copies` registry can leak/collide across permanents (it keys by `id(permanent)` — any stale-id reuse risk?).\n- The back-face Swords to Plowshares: exiles target creature and gives ITS CONTROLLER (not the caster) life equal to its (last-known) power.\n- Regression safety: confirm nothing existing in engine was renamed/removed (additive-only) and that the `Keyword` enum was left unchanged.\n\n## Important guardrails\n- DO NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards (see `FILES_MODIFIED.json`) or conventions in `KEY_DECISIONS.md` (e.g., the lazy per-game registry pattern, or \"Prepared\" not being a Keyword enum member — these are deliberate).\n- DO NOT demand test rewrites — tests were already arbitrated. Any test-quality concern is `advisory` only.\n- Focus on what is visible in the diff.\n\n## Output (write this)\nWrite `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/review.json` — a JSON array of:\n```json\n{\"severity\": \"strict\" | \"advisory\", \"file\": \"<path>\", \"line\": <int or null>, \"comment\": \"<actionable comment>\"}\n```\nUse `strict` only for must-fix issues (correctness bugs, spec/ruling violations, regression risks). Use `advisory` for style/clarity. Write `[]` if none.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\n```\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/review.json\n```","agentId":"a22d9dcf96202abe1","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 1\nadvisory_count: 5\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/review.json\n\nKey findings (full detail in the JSON):\n\n- **strict** — `engine/preparation.py` `cast_prepared_copy` (around line 515): it unprepares the source and pops the registry entry *before* `cast_spell_free`, which can raise `CastingError` and roll the copy back into exile. On that failure the permanent is wrongly unprepared and the surviving exile copy is orphaned. CR 722.3c only removes the designation when the spell \"becomes cast\" (success). Cast first, then unprepare/detach.\n\n- advisory — `id(permanent)` registry keying risks stale-id aliasing / copy leak (mirrors the sanctioned sos_1 pattern, so non-blocking; suggest `object_id`).\n- advisory — `get_prepared_source` dead `# pragma: no cover` loop that always returns None.\n- advisory — `cast_prepared_copy` silently skips unprepare when a copy has no `prepare_source` back-link.\n- advisory — `_get_target_player` script branch calls `choose_target` with mismatched argument shapes (unreached by tests).\n- advisory — `SwordsToPlowshares.on_resolve` computes unused `owner`/`from_bf` bookkeeping.\n\nRegression safety confirmed: no engine symbol renamed/moved/deleted, `engine/preparation.py` is new/additive, `engine/types.py` (Keyword enum, 16 members) unchanged, and the card class lives at the required `cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py`. The strictly-more-creatures comparison, token-under-targeted-player creation, and life-to-target's-controller back-face effect all match the spec/ruling."}],"totalDurationMs":78888,"totalTokens":83840,"totalToolUseCount":17,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2517,"cache_read_input_tokens":80712,"output_tokens":609,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2517},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":609,"cache_read_input_tokens":80712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2517,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2517,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":15,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":0,