{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are applying review feedback to your implementation of card **sos_13** (\"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\") and its engine Preparation framework.\n\n## Inputs\n- Your current implementation diff: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl.diff` (covers `cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` and `engine/preparation.py`).\n- Your rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-rationale.md`.\n- Review comments to address: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/review.json` (a JSON array; each has `severity`, `file`, `line`, `comment`).\n- Tests you must keep passing (DO NOT MODIFY): `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` (37 tests).\n- Workspace rules: `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md`, `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n- Engine source: `engine/preparation.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/zones.py`.\n\n## What to do\nApply every `strict` review comment. You may apply `advisory` comments if they are quick and safe (they are optional).\n\nThe key STRICT issue:\n- `engine/preparation.py` `cast_prepared_copy`: it currently unprepares the source and pops the registry entry BEFORE calling `cast_spell_free`. If the cast raises (e.g. `CastingError`), the permanent is left wrongly unprepared and the exiled copy is orphaned. Per CR 722.3c the designation is only removed when the spell actually \"becomes cast\" (succeeds). FIX: cast the copy first; only after the cast succeeds, clear the source's prepared designation and detach/remove the registry entry. Ensure no double-removal of the in-flight copy. On a cast failure, leave the source prepared and the copy in exile (propagate the error).\n\nConstraints:\n- DO NOT modify any test file, anything under `engine_tests/`, or any FDN `tests.py`.\n- Engine changes remain ADDITIVE: do not rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Keep the `Keyword` enum unchanged (16 members).\n- After changes, run `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` (all 37 must pass) and the FULL `pytest` suite from `/workspace` (no regressions).\n- If you DISAGREE with a strict comment (think it is wrong), do NOT silently ignore it — record the disagreement in the disagreements file with justification.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- Updated `engine/preparation.py` / `cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` as needed.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-revised.diff` — `git diff` of the implementation+engine files only (exclude the tests file): `git diff -- cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py engine/ > /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-revised.diff` from `/workspace`.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-revised-rationale.md` — what you changed for each addressed comment.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/disagreements.json` — a JSON array of `{\"review_comment_index\": <int>, \"reviewer_comment\": \"...\", \"implementer_justification\": \"...\"}` for any comment you chose NOT to apply (use `[]` if you applied everything).\n- Keep `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` accurate for `card: \"sos_13\"`.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\n```\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: <N>\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/disagreements.json\nnotes: <one-line>\n```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RVMC8pWzD1khWv5YamS13i","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"3aeb4d2b-108e-4e0b-8b68-9cea94dadd7c","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:13:45.854Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_13 per review"}
