{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01AoZYXUiAzHdKqzm4Yd1g5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WZNqVXpJQTMjStNhxBKC4x","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revision rationale — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n\nAll 37 sos_13 tests still pass and the full suite is green (1267 passed, no\nregressions).\n\n## STRICT — `engine/preparation.py` `cast_prepared_copy` (review line 515)\n\n**Reviewer concern:** the function unprepared the source and popped the registry\nentry *before* calling `cast_spell_free`. Since `cast_spell_free` can raise\n`CastingError` (no legal target / target has protection) and roll the copy back\ninto exile, the failure path left the permanent wrongly unprepared and the\nsurviving exile copy orphaned (`get_prepared_copy` would return `None` for a copy\nstill sitting in exile). CR 722.3c says the designation is lost only \"at the time\nthe spell becomes cast\" — i.e. on success.\n\n**Fix applied:** reordered so the cast happens first.\n\n- `cast_spell_free(game, player, copy, Zone.EXILE)` is now called *before* any\n  state mutation. I confirmed from `engine/casting.py` that `cast_spell_free`\n  only removes the copy from exile after legality/targeting succeed, and on any\n  failure it rolls the copy back into exile and raises `CastingError` (lines\n  300–354). So if the cast fails, the exception propagates *before* we touch the\n  designation or registry — the source stays prepared and the copy stays in\n  exile, exactly as CR 722.3c requires.\n- Only *after* `cast_spell_free` returns without error do we clear the source's\n  designation (`_set_designation(source, False)`) and `pop` the registry entry.\n- No double-removal of the in-flight copy: `cast_spell_free` already moved the\n  copy from exile onto the stack, so the cleanup only pops the registry *dict\n  key* (`id(source)`) and never re-touches the copy object.\n\n## ADVISORY (applied — quick and safe)\n\n**`get_prepared_source` dead loop (review line 480):** removed the\n`# pragma: no cover` loop that iterated the registry only to unconditionally\nreturn `None`. `get_prepared_source` now simply returns the `prepare_source`\nback-link (or `None`), with the docstring noting that `id()` keys can't be\nreversed.\n\n**External-copy unprepare fallback (review line 515, advisory variant):** added\na small helper `_registry_key_for_copy(game, copy)` that reverse-scans the\nregistry by value. In `cast_prepared_copy`, when a copy has no `prepare_source`\nback-link (e.g. an externally-supplied copy), we now still detach any matching\nregistry entry by that key so the source unprepares after a successful cast,\ninstead of silently leaving the entry in place.\n\n## ADVISORY (acknowledged, not applied)\n\n- **`id(permanent)` keying vs `GameObject.object_id` (line 357):** acknowledged.\n  The reviewer explicitly notes this mirrors the sanctioned sos_1 `id()`-keyed\n  registry pattern (per KEY_DECISIONS.md) and is \"not a blocker.\" Keeping the\n  established convention; switching keying schemes is out of scope for this\n  revision and would diverge from the sibling registry. (No disagreement\n  recorded — this is an explicitly-optional advisory.)\n- **`_get_target_player` script-fallback `choose_target` shape (line 281):** the\n  fallback branch is only reached when `chosen_targets` is empty; all tests set\n  `chosen_targets`, so it is never exercised. Left as-is to avoid touching a\n  passing path; noted for future hardening.\n- **`SwordsToPlowshares.on_resolve` dead bookkeeping (line 104):** the unused\n  `owner`/`from_bf` locals are harmless and the branch is covered by tests. Left\n  as-is to keep the revision focused on the strict correctness fix.\n\n## Disagreements\n\nNone. See `disagreements.json` (`[]`).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":184,"cache_read_input_tokens":52075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":184,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":56,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RVMC8pWzD1khWv5YamS13i","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"e25b71e1-d447-4676-a464-23c9c310d055","request_id":"req_011Cbe6mPWmqdPQU6S5zU8qt","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_13 per review"}
