{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NAdbD7d12j6VyM6XvNMgPz","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests are well-formed and in the expected TDD red phase (17 fail against the empty stub; the 4 that \"pass\" are no-op/negative assertions paired with failing positive tests, and they remain valid contracts the real implementation must satisfy).\n\nTESTS_WRITTEN\n\n- **test_files:** 1 — `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`\n- **test_cases:** 21\n- **rationale_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md`\n- **files_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-files.txt`\n- **untestable_count:** 2\n- **untestable_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/untestable.json`\n\n**Summary:** Wrote 21 pytest tests for sos_57 Mana Sculpt ({1}{U}{U} instant), covering static data, the \"counter target spell\" half (stack removal, owner's graveyard, creature-spell counter, self-target rejection, empty-stack uncastability, no-target fizzle), and the Wizard-conditional deferred {C} clause (registers exactly one \"you\"-controlled delayed trigger, scales colorless mana with the countered spell's cost, opponent's Wizard doesn't count, colorless-only, and end-to-end pool delivery). The card requires engine extensions the Implementer must add; the counter half follows the established `_counter_spell` pattern from fdn_48/fdn_153.\n\n**Two flagged ambiguities** (in `untestable.json`): (1) the engine tracks no literal \"amount of mana spent\" total, so tests assert against the countered spell's mana value (valid for normally-cast spells but not X/cost-reduced ones); (2) there's no main-phase-begin event in the engine, so the delivery test fires the registered delayed trigger's effect directly rather than asserting the engine-driven one-shot timing. All tests fail against the current empty stub as expected for TDD red phase."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: afbdf5e3b2c09114c (use SendMessage with to: 'afbdf5e3b2c09114c' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 109995\ntool_uses: 48\nduration_ms: 278919</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"a03821c9-2787-4d68-8332-e47f7b4e446f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:20:58.909Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are writing pytest tests for a single Magic: The Gathering card implementation (TDD red phase). The card is **sos_57**.\n\n## Inputs\n- Card spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_spec.json` (read this for name, mana cost, oracle text, P/T, keywords).\n- Implementation stub you are testing against: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`.\n- Test conventions: study existing tests under `/workspace/engine_tests/` (e.g. `test_casting.py`, `test_triggers.py`, `test_combat.py`, `test_abilities.py`, `test_replacement_effects.py`) and the FDN reference tests that ship with a `tests.py`: `cards/fdn/fdn_13/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_142/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_205/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_215/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_244/tests.py`.\n- Test helpers: `/workspace/test_utils.py` and `/workspace/test_utils.md` (`create_game`, `set_board_state`, etc.).\n- Reference card implementations: `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_*/card_impl.py`.\n- Engine source with rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`, `engine/types.py`.\n- Workspace rules: `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`, `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` (read — records engine conventions from earlier cards), `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n- Rules reference: `/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt` (grep, do not read whole; see `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n\n## Your task\n1. Read the card spec and understand the card's full behavior.\n2. Write thorough pytest tests at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` that verify the card's behavior per its oracle text. Cover main functionality plus relevant edge cases. Tests must follow existing engine/FDN test conventions and must FAIL against the current empty stub (TDD red) but PASS once the card is correctly implemented.\n3. Do NOT modify any files under `engine_tests/` or any FDN `tests.py`. Do NOT modify engine source. You only write `cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`.\n4. Confirm the tests are well-formed by running them (they should fail/error because the card is unimplemented — that is expected). Do not try to make them pass.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` — your tests.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md` — what each test covers and the behavior contract you derived from the spec.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-files.txt` — list of test file path(s) you created (one per line).\n- If any spec requirement cannot be tested with the current engine/test API, write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/untestable.json` — a JSON array of `{\"requirement\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\", \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"...\"}`. Omit the file entirely if everything is testable.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn a short summary: number of tests written, the test file path, and `untestable_count: <N>` (0 if none). Do not paste the full test code.","agentId":"afbdf5e3b2c09114c","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests are well-formed and in the expected TDD red phase (17 fail against the empty stub; the 4 that \"pass\" are no-op/negative assertions paired with failing positive tests, and they remain valid contracts the real implementation must satisfy).\n\nTESTS_WRITTEN\n\n- **test_files:** 1 — `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`\n- **test_cases:** 21\n- **rationale_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md`\n- **files_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-files.txt`\n- **untestable_count:** 2\n- **untestable_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/untestable.json`\n\n**Summary:** Wrote 21 pytest tests for sos_57 Mana Sculpt ({1}{U}{U} instant), covering static data, the \"counter target spell\" half (stack removal, owner's graveyard, creature-spell counter, self-target rejection, empty-stack uncastability, no-target fizzle), and the Wizard-conditional deferred {C} clause (registers exactly one \"you\"-controlled delayed trigger, scales colorless mana with the countered spell's cost, opponent's Wizard doesn't count, colorless-only, and end-to-end pool delivery). The card requires engine extensions the Implementer must add; the counter half follows the established `_counter_spell` pattern from fdn_48/fdn_153.\n\n**Two flagged ambiguities** (in `untestable.json`): (1) the engine tracks no literal \"amount of mana spent\" total, so tests assert against the countered spell's mana value (valid for normally-cast spells but not X/cost-reduced ones); (2) there's no main-phase-begin event in the engine, so the delivery test fires the registered delayed trigger's effect directly rather than asserting the engine-driven one-shot timing. All tests fail against the current empty stub as expected for TDD red phase."}],"totalDurationMs":278919,"totalTokens":109995,"totalToolUseCount":48,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":108961,"output_tokens":666,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":366},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":666,"cache_read_input_tokens":108961,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":366,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":26,"searchCount":11,"bashCount":7,"editFileCount":4,"linesAdded":590,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
