{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pk6F7p37woviM7aHQF1kkC","type":"tool_result","content":"=== test-files.txt ===\n/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py\n\n=== untestable.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell\",\n    \"reason\": \"The engine does not record the literal amount of mana a player spent to cast a spell. engine/mana.py only exposes last_payment_colors (the distinct colors of the last payment), not a total count, and the cast pipeline in engine/casting.py stores nothing equivalent. Tests therefore assert the deferred {C} equals the countered spell's mana value (mana_cost.cmc), which matches 'amount of mana spent' only for normally-cast spells with no X, no cost reduction, and no alternative/additional costs. Spells cast for {X}, with cost reductions, or via alternative costs cannot be distinguished from their printed mana value with the current API.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Have the engine track the actual total mana paid for each cast (e.g. record mana_pool.total() consumed during payment, or sum the paid pips/generic) and attach it to the cast spell (analogous to colors_spent). Tests could then assert the deferred {C} equals that recorded total even for X spells or reduced-cost spells.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"at the beginning of your next main phase (deferred trigger fires exactly once at the controller's next main phase and not before)\",\n    \"reason\": \"engine/turn.py fires only upkeep/combat/end-step events (engine/events.py has BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent / BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent / EndStep / EndOfTurn but no main-phase-begin event), so there is no existing hook to advance the game through run_turn and observe the {C} appear precisely at the controller's next main phase. The delivery test executes the registered delayed trigger's effect directly to assert the colorless mana lands in the pool, but it cannot assert the engine-driven one-shot timing (fires once, only at the controller's next main phase, then is removed).\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Add a BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (with the active/controlling player) and fire it from engine/turn.py at each main phase, and provide a delayed/one-shot trigger registration the card can use. A timing test could then run_turn() and assert the {C} appears exactly at the controller's next main phase and the trigger is consumed.\"\n  }\n]\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"a737562b-8c85-4d78-9c67-a9750edd24a2","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:21:04.183Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== test-files.txt ===\n/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py\n\n=== untestable.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell\",\n    \"reason\": \"The engine does not record the literal amount of mana a player spent to cast a spell. engine/mana.py only exposes last_payment_colors (the distinct colors of the last payment), not a total count, and the cast pipeline in engine/casting.py stores nothing equivalent. Tests therefore assert the deferred {C} equals the countered spell's mana value (mana_cost.cmc), which matches 'amount of mana spent' only for normally-cast spells with no X, no cost reduction, and no alternative/additional costs. Spells cast for {X}, with cost reductions, or via alternative costs cannot be distinguished from their printed mana value with the current API.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Have the engine track the actual total mana paid for each cast (e.g. record mana_pool.total() consumed during payment, or sum the paid pips/generic) and attach it to the cast spell (analogous to colors_spent). Tests could then assert the deferred {C} equals that recorded total even for X spells or reduced-cost spells.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"at the beginning of your next main phase (deferred trigger fires exactly once at the controller's next main phase and not before)\",\n    \"reason\": \"engine/turn.py fires only upkeep/combat/end-step events (engine/events.py has BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent / BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent / EndStep / EndOfTurn but no main-phase-begin event), so there is no existing hook to advance the game through run_turn and observe the {C} appear precisely at the controller's next main phase. The delivery test executes the registered delayed trigger's effect directly to assert the colorless mana lands in the pool, but it cannot assert the engine-driven one-shot timing (fires once, only at the controller's next main phase, then is removed).\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Add a BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (with the active/controlling player) and fire it from engine/turn.py at each main phase, and provide a delayed/one-shot trigger registration the card can use. A timing test could then run_turn() and assert the {C} appears exactly at the controller's next main phase and the trigger is consumed.\"\n  }\n]","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
