{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jq4XYzm9gPWe3gnuTtkcj3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_57 Mana Sculpt\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant.\n4\tOracle: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C}\n5\tequal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your\n6\tnext main phase.\"\n7\t\n8\tTest file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` (21 tests).\n9\t\n10\t## Behavior contract derived from the spec\n11\t\n12\t1. **Static data** — name `\"Mana Sculpt\"`, mana cost `{1}{U}{U}`, an `Instant`\n13\t   (and not a creature).\n14\t2. **Counter half** — targets another spell on the stack; on resolution removes\n15\t   that spell's `StackObject` from the stack and puts the countered card into\n16\t   its owner's graveyard. Follows the established engine pattern in\n17\t   `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) and `cards/fdn/fdn_153` (Essence Scatter):\n18\t   `can_cast` is gated on a counterable spell existing, `get_targets` returns one\n19\t   STACK-zone `TargetRequirement` excluding Mana Sculpt itself, and resolution\n20\t   uses the `_counter_spell` move-to-graveyard idiom.\n21\t3. **No-target fizzle** — with no legal target the spell does nothing.\n22\t4. **Wizard condition** — the deferred-mana clause applies only if the\n23\t   controller of Mana Sculpt controls a Wizard as the counter resolves. \"You\" is\n24\t   the controller, so an opponent's Wizard does not enable it.\n25\t5. **Deferred {C}** — when the controller controls a Wizard, a delayed effect is\n26\t   set up that, at the beginning of the controller's next main phase, adds an\n27\t   amount of `{C}` (colorless) to the controller's pool equal to the amount of\n28\t   mana spent to cast the countered spell.\n29\t\n30\tThe deferred-mana clause is verified through the public trigger system: a\n31\tWizard-conditional counter registers exactly one new (delayed) trigger\n32\tcontrolled by \"you\", and executing that trigger's `effect(game)` adds the\n33\tcorrect colorless mana to the controller's pool. This asserts the observable end\n34\tstate without pinning the Implementer to a specific event-class name.\n35\t\n36\t## Test-by-test\n37\t\n38\t### TestManaSculptProperties\n39\t- `test_name`, `test_mana_cost`, `test_is_instant`, `test_not_a_creature` —\n40\t  static-data contract (requirement 1).\n41\t\n42\t### TestManaSculptTargeting\n43\t- `test_cannot_cast_with_empty_stack` — `can_cast` is False when there is nothing\n44\t  to counter (requirement 2 gating).\n45\t- `test_can_cast_when_a_spell_is_on_the_stack` — `can_cast` is True when a spell\n46\t  is on the stack.\n47\t- `test_get_targets_offers_the_spell_on_the_stack` — `get_targets` returns one\n48\t  STACK-zone requirement whose filter accepts the spell's stack object.\n49\t- `test_get_targets_rejects_self` — the filter rejects Mana Sculpt's own stack\n50\t  object (a counter cannot target itself).\n51\t\n52\t### TestManaSculptCounter\n53\t- `test_counter_removes_spell_from_stack` — the targeted `StackObject` is removed\n54\t  on resolve (requirement 2).\n55\t- `test_countered_spell_goes_to_owners_graveyard` — the countered card lands in\n56\t  its *owner's* graveyard and leaves the stack zone.\n57\t- `test_counters_creature_spell_too` — \"counter target spell\" is not limited to\n58\t  noncreature spells (contrast with Essence Scatter's creature-only counter).\n59\t- `test_no_target_is_a_noop` — a counter with no legal target fizzles; an\n60\t  unrelated spell on the stack is untouched (requirement 3).\n61\t\n62\t### TestManaSculptWizardCondition\n63\t- `test_no_wizard_registers_no_delayed_trigger` — with only a non-Wizard creature,\n64\t  the spell is still countered but no deferred-mana trigger is registered.\n65\t- `test_no_wizard_adds_no_mana_now_or_via_pool` — without a Wizard the pool gains\n66\t  no colorless mana.\n67\t- `test_wizard_registers_a_delayed_trigger` — controlling a Wizard registers\n68\t  exactly one new delayed trigger (requirement 4 + 5).\n69\t- `test_delayed_trigger_is_controlled_by_caster` — the registered trigger is\n70\t  controlled by Mana Sculpt's controller (\"you\").\n71\t- `test_delayed_trigger_effect_adds_colorless_equal_to_mana_spent` — firing the\n72\t  delayed effect adds `{C}` equal to the countered spell's mana value\n73\t  ({2}{R} → 3 colorless).\n74\t- `test_deferred_amount_scales_with_a_more_expensive_spell` — a 5-mana spell\n75\t  yields 5 colorless (the amount scales with the spell's cost).\n76\t- `test_deferred_mana_is_colorless_not_colored` — the added mana is `{C}` only; no\n77\t  colored mana is added.\n78\t- `test_opponents_wizard_does_not_enable_the_clause` — only \"you\" controlling a\n79\t  Wizard counts; an opponent's Wizard does not register the deferred trigger.\n80\t\n81\t### TestManaSculptDeliveryTiming\n82\t- `test_mana_lands_in_pool_after_firing_delayed_trigger` — end-to-end: the {C} is\n83\t  not in the pool immediately after the counter resolves, but appears once the\n84\t  delayed trigger's effect runs (the observable outcome of \"add ... at the\n85\t  beginning of your next main phase\").\n86\t\n87\t## Edge cases covered\n88\t- Empty stack (uncastable), self-targeting rejection, creature-spell counter,\n89\t  no-target fizzle, opponent's Wizard not counting, colorless-only mana,\n90\t  amount scaling with spell cost, and pre-vs-post delivery timing.\n91\t\n92\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope / engine-limited)\n93\t- **Exact \"amount of mana spent\" vs mana value** — the engine does not track the\n94\t  literal amount of mana a player spent (only `last_payment_colors`, not a total\n95\t  count). The tests therefore assert against the countered spell's mana value\n96\t  (`mana_cost.cmc`), which equals the amount of mana spent for the normally-cast,\n97\t  no-X / no-cost-reduction spells used here. Spells cast for X, with cost\n98\t  reductions, or with alternative/additional costs would diverge — see\n99\t  `untestable.json`.\n100\t- **The precise engine event/step that fires the deferred trigger** — \"at the\n101\t  beginning of your next main phase\" requires a main-phase-begin event the\n102\t  engine does not currently fire (only upkeep/combat/end events exist in\n103\t  `engine/events.py` + `engine/turn.py`). The delivery test executes the\n104\t  registered trigger's effect directly instead of asserting on a specific new\n105\t  event class, so it stays robust to whatever hook the Implementer adds. The\n106\t  one-shot \"next main phase only\" timing (the trigger firing exactly once and\n107\t  then being removed) is left to the Implementer's engine wiring and is recorded\n108\t  in `untestable.json`.\n109\t- General engine mechanics (stack LIFO, mana-pool emptying on phase transitions,\n110\t  graveyard zone moves) — covered by `engine_tests/`, not re-tested here.\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b2a2f9af-cdbb-49d9-bff5-893c58b486ec","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:21:19.667Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_57 Mana Sculpt\n\nCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant.\nOracle: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C}\nequal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your\nnext main phase.\"\n\nTest file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` (21 tests).\n\n## Behavior contract derived from the spec\n\n1. **Static data** — name `\"Mana Sculpt\"`, mana cost `{1}{U}{U}`, an `Instant`\n   (and not a creature).\n2. **Counter half** — targets another spell on the stack; on resolution removes\n   that spell's `StackObject` from the stack and puts the countered card into\n   its owner's graveyard. Follows the established engine pattern in\n   `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) and `cards/fdn/fdn_153` (Essence Scatter):\n   `can_cast` is gated on a counterable spell existing, `get_targets` returns one\n   STACK-zone `TargetRequirement` excluding Mana Sculpt itself, and resolution\n   uses the `_counter_spell` move-to-graveyard idiom.\n3. **No-target fizzle** — with no legal target the spell does nothing.\n4. **Wizard condition** — the deferred-mana clause applies only if the\n   controller of Mana Sculpt controls a Wizard as the counter resolves. \"You\" is\n   the controller, so an opponent's Wizard does not enable it.\n5. **Deferred {C}** — when the controller controls a Wizard, a delayed effect is\n   set up that, at the beginning of the controller's next main phase, adds an\n   amount of `{C}` (colorless) to the controller's pool equal to the amount of\n   mana spent to cast the countered spell.\n\nThe deferred-mana clause is verified through the public trigger system: a\nWizard-conditional counter registers exactly one new (delayed) trigger\ncontrolled by \"you\", and executing that trigger's `effect(game)` adds the\ncorrect colorless mana to the controller's pool. This asserts the observable end\nstate without pinning the Implementer to a specific event-class name.\n\n## Test-by-test\n\n### TestManaSculptProperties\n- `test_name`, `test_mana_cost`, `test_is_instant`, `test_not_a_creature` —\n  static-data contract (requirement 1).\n\n### TestManaSculptTargeting\n- `test_cannot_cast_with_empty_stack` — `can_cast` is False when there is nothing\n  to counter (requirement 2 gating).\n- `test_can_cast_when_a_spell_is_on_the_stack` — `can_cast` is True when a spell\n  is on the stack.\n- `test_get_targets_offers_the_spell_on_the_stack` — `get_targets` returns one\n  STACK-zone requirement whose filter accepts the spell's stack object.\n- `test_get_targets_rejects_self` — the filter rejects Mana Sculpt's own stack\n  object (a counter cannot target itself).\n\n### TestManaSculptCounter\n- `test_counter_removes_spell_from_stack` — the targeted `StackObject` is removed\n  on resolve (requirement 2).\n- `test_countered_spell_goes_to_owners_graveyard` — the countered card lands in\n  its *owner's* graveyard and leaves the stack zone.\n- `test_counters_creature_spell_too` — \"counter target spell\" is not limited to\n  noncreature spells (contrast with Essence Scatter's creature-only counter).\n- `test_no_target_is_a_noop` — a counter with no legal target fizzles; an\n  unrelated spell on the stack is untouched (requirement 3).\n\n### TestManaSculptWizardCondition\n- `test_no_wizard_registers_no_delayed_trigger` — with only a non-Wizard creature,\n  the spell is still countered but no deferred-mana trigger is registered.\n- `test_no_wizard_adds_no_mana_now_or_via_pool` — without a Wizard the pool gains\n  no colorless mana.\n- `test_wizard_registers_a_delayed_trigger` — controlling a Wizard registers\n  exactly one new delayed trigger (requirement 4 + 5).\n- `test_delayed_trigger_is_controlled_by_caster` — the registered trigger is\n  controlled by Mana Sculpt's controller (\"you\").\n- `test_delayed_trigger_effect_adds_colorless_equal_to_mana_spent` — firing the\n  delayed effect adds `{C}` equal to the countered spell's mana value\n  ({2}{R} → 3 colorless).\n- `test_deferred_amount_scales_with_a_more_expensive_spell` — a 5-mana spell\n  yields 5 colorless (the amount scales with the spell's cost).\n- `test_deferred_mana_is_colorless_not_colored` — the added mana is `{C}` only; no\n  colored mana is added.\n- `test_opponents_wizard_does_not_enable_the_clause` — only \"you\" controlling a\n  Wizard counts; an opponent's Wizard does not register the deferred trigger.\n\n### TestManaSculptDeliveryTiming\n- `test_mana_lands_in_pool_after_firing_delayed_trigger` — end-to-end: the {C} is\n  not in the pool immediately after the counter resolves, but appears once the\n  delayed trigger's effect runs (the observable outcome of \"add ... at the\n  beginning of your next main phase\").\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- Empty stack (uncastable), self-targeting rejection, creature-spell counter,\n  no-target fizzle, opponent's Wizard not counting, colorless-only mana,\n  amount scaling with spell cost, and pre-vs-post delivery timing.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope / engine-limited)\n- **Exact \"amount of mana spent\" vs mana value** — the engine does not track the\n  literal amount of mana a player spent (only `last_payment_colors`, not a total\n  count). The tests therefore assert against the countered spell's mana value\n  (`mana_cost.cmc`), which equals the amount of mana spent for the normally-cast,\n  no-X / no-cost-reduction spells used here. Spells cast for X, with cost\n  reductions, or with alternative/additional costs would diverge — see\n  `untestable.json`.\n- **The precise engine event/step that fires the deferred trigger** — \"at the\n  beginning of your next main phase\" requires a main-phase-begin event the\n  engine does not currently fire (only upkeep/combat/end events exist in\n  `engine/events.py` + `engine/turn.py`). The delivery test executes the\n  registered trigger's effect directly instead of asserting on a specific new\n  event class, so it stays robust to whatever hook the Implementer adds. The\n  one-shot \"next main phase only\" timing (the trigger firing exactly once and\n  then being removed) is left to the Implementer's engine wiring and is recorded\n  in `untestable.json`.\n- General engine mechanics (stack LIFO, mana-pool emptying on phase transitions,\n  graveyard zone moves) — covered by `engine_tests/`, not re-tested here.\n","numLines":111,"startLine":1,"totalLines":111}}}
