{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_018AdA89FQgMZBaS6PztSQvF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JrjSqrK5iSGSVhnunL4QgD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n\nCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant (medium tier).\nOracle: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the\namount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n\nThe Tester wrote 21 tests (all currently red) and deferred 2 items for lack of engine support.\nYou must build that support — ADDITIVELY per AGENTS.md (add new methods/classes/helpers/enum\nmembers and modify existing function bodies; never rename/move/delete existing engine symbols).\nKeep the `Keyword` enum unchanged (a regression test hard-asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`).\n\n## Counter half (use the established pattern)\nMirror `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) and `cards/fdn/fdn_153` (Essence Scatter):\n`can_cast` gated on a counterable spell existing; `get_targets` returns one STACK-zone\n`TargetRequirement` that excludes Mana Sculpt's own stack object; resolution removes the\ntargeted `StackObject` and puts the countered card into its OWNER's graveyard\n(`_counter_spell` idiom). \"Counter target spell\" counters creature spells too (not creature-only).\nNo legal target ⇒ fizzle/no-op.\n\n## Engine gap 1 — track actual mana spent per cast (additive)\nThe engine records `colors_spent` but not the TOTAL amount of mana paid. Add additive tracking\nof the total mana paid for a cast (e.g. set `card.mana_spent = <total paid>` in\n`engine/casting.py` after payment, analogous to how `colors_spent` is set). The card's deferred\nclause should use the countered card's recorded `mana_spent`, FALLING BACK to\n`countered_card.mana_cost.cmc` when `mana_spent` is unavailable (e.g. tests place a spell\ndirectly on the stack without paying). For normally-cast spells `mana_spent == cmc`, so the\nexisting tests (which assert the deferred {C} equals the countered spell's mana value) still pass.\n\n## Engine gap 2 — main-phase-begin event + delayed one-shot trigger (additive)\n\"at the beginning of your next main phase\" has no engine hook today (only upkeep/combat/end\nevents exist). Add:\n1. A new `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` in `engine/events.py` carrying the active/\n   controlling player, fired from `engine/turn.py` at the start of the (pre-combat) main phase.\n2. A delayed / one-shot trigger registration mechanism the card uses so that, when the counter\n   resolves while you control a Wizard, a trigger is registered that fires EXACTLY ONCE at the\n   beginning of the controller's NEXT main phase, adds `{C}` equal to the recorded mana spent to\n   the controller's mana pool, and is then removed.\n\nThe Tester's tests observe this via the public trigger system: a Wizard-conditional counter must\nregister exactly one new delayed trigger CONTROLLED BY the caster (\"you\"), whose `effect(game)`\nadds the correct colorless mana. With no Wizard, register NO delayed trigger. An opponent's\nWizard must NOT enable the clause. Make sure these observable shapes hold.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` → all 21 pass.\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions.\n\nAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester once to add an engine-driven timing\ntest (advance via `run_turn` and assert the {C} appears at the controller's next main phase and\nthe trigger fires only once). Build the wiring so that behaviour is real.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2215,"cache_read_input_tokens":81672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2215},"output_tokens":63,"service_tier":"standard","infere