{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011wK16dTpyQrE7wkxMVXGU1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives — sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant (medium tier).\n4\tOracle: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the\n5\tamount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n6\t\n7\tThe Tester wrote 21 tests (all currently red) and deferred 2 items for lack of engine support.\n8\tYou must build that support — ADDITIVELY per AGENTS.md (add new methods/classes/helpers/enum\n9\tmembers and modify existing function bodies; never rename/move/delete existing engine symbols).\n10\tKeep the `Keyword` enum unchanged (a regression test hard-asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`).\n11\t\n12\t## Counter half (use the established pattern)\n13\tMirror `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) and `cards/fdn/fdn_153` (Essence Scatter):\n14\t`can_cast` gated on a counterable spell existing; `get_targets` returns one STACK-zone\n15\t`TargetRequirement` that excludes Mana Sculpt's own stack object; resolution removes the\n16\ttargeted `StackObject` and puts the countered card into its OWNER's graveyard\n17\t(`_counter_spell` idiom). \"Counter target spell\" counters creature spells too (not creature-only).\n18\tNo legal target ⇒ fizzle/no-op.\n19\t\n20\t## Engine gap 1 — track actual mana spent per cast (additive)\n21\tThe engine records `colors_spent` but not the TOTAL amount of mana paid. Add additive tracking\n22\tof the total mana paid for a cast (e.g. set `card.mana_spent = <total paid>` in\n23\t`engine/casting.py` after payment, analogous to how `colors_spent` is set). The card's deferred\n24\tclause should use the countered card's recorded `mana_spent`, FALLING BACK to\n25\t`countered_card.mana_cost.cmc` when `mana_spent` is unavailable (e.g. tests place a spell\n26\tdirectly on the stack without paying). For normally-cast spells `mana_spent == cmc`, so the\n27\texisting tests (which assert the deferred {C} equals the countered spell's mana value) still pass.\n28\t\n29\t## Engine gap 2 — main-phase-begin event + delayed one-shot trigger (additive)\n30\t\"at the beginning of your next main phase\" has no engine hook today (only upkeep/combat/end\n31\tevents exist). Add:\n32\t1. A new `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` in `engine/events.py` carrying the active/\n33\t   controlling player, fired from `engine/turn.py` at the start of the (pre-combat) main phase.\n34\t2. A delayed / one-shot trigger registration mechanism the card uses so that, when the counter\n35\t   resolves while you control a Wizard, a trigger is registered that fires EXACTLY ONCE at the\n36\t   beginning of the controller's NEXT main phase, adds `{C}` equal to the recorded mana spent to\n37\t   the controller's mana pool, and is then removed.\n38\t\n39\tThe Tester's tests observe this via the public trigger system: a Wizard-conditional counter must\n40\tregister exactly one new delayed trigger CONTROLLED BY the caster (\"you\"), whose `effect(game)`\n41\tadds the correct colorless mana. With no Wizard, register NO delayed trigger. An opponent's\n42\tWizard must NOT enable the clause. Make sure these observable shapes hold.\n43\t\n44\t## Verification\n45\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` → all 21 pass.\n46\t- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions.\n47\t\n48\tAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester once to add an engine-driven timing\n49\ttest (advance via `run_turn` and assert the {C} appears at the controller's next main phase and\n50\tthe trigger fires only once). Build the wiring so that behaviour is real.\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015rF4nfPePEJ7zX53WjYEJK","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"785fab16-5583-415a-970f-3b94d8edb409","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:22:32.745Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_57"}
