{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Viwrrw4KbqYkrptFLUXy5U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DZqiWVFgpUs5TNgdMwwFM1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n\nCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant.\nOracle: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C}\nequal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your\nnext main phase.\"\n\nAll 21 sos_57 tests pass; full `pytest` suite passes (1288 passed, no regressions).\n\n## Counter half (mirrors fdn_48 / fdn_153)\n`cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` → `ManaSculpt(Instant)`:\n- `can_cast` returns True only when another spell (not Mana Sculpt itself) is on\n  the stack — gated on `getattr(stack_obj, \"is_spell\", True)` so it counts any\n  spell, not creature-only (contrast Essence Scatter).\n- `get_targets` returns a single `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK)` whose\n  `filter_fn` accepts any stack object whose `source is not self` and is a spell,\n  and rejects Mana Sculpt's own stack object.\n- `on_resolve` uses the established `_counter_spell` idiom: pop the targeted\n  `StackObject` from `game.stack._items`, remove the card from its controller's\n  STACK zone, and add it to its **owner's** graveyard. `_counter_spell` now\n  returns a bool so resolution can tell a real counter from a fizzle; no legal\n  target ⇒ no-op (and no deferred mana).\n\n## Engine gap 1 — total mana spent per cast (additive, `engine/casting.py`)\nAfter payment, alongside the existing `card.colors_spent`, the cast pipeline now\nsets `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (the total mana paid, after any cost\nreduction). Stale `mana_spent` is cleared at the start of a cast next to the\nexisting `colors_spent` clear. For a normally-cast no-X / non-reduced spell\n`mana_spent == cmc`, so the tests (which assert the deferred {C} equals the\ncountered spell's mana value) hold.\n\nThe card reads the countered card's `mana_spent` via helper\n`_mana_spent_to_cast`, **falling back to `mana_cost.cmc`** when `mana_spent` is\nabsent — which is the case in the tests, where spells are placed on the stack\ndirectly without paying (e.g. `{2}{R}` → 3, `{3}{U}{U}` → 5, `{4}` → 4).\n\n## Engine gap 2 — main-phase-begin event + delayed one-shot trigger (additive)\nNew engine symbols:\n- `engine/events.py`: **`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)`**\n  with fields `player` (the active player whose main phase is beginning) and\n  `precombat: bool` (True for pre-combat main, False for post-combat).\n- `engine/turn.py`: `run_turn` now fires `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(\n  player=game.active_player, precombat=...)` whenever it reaches a main phase\n  (`PRECOMBAT_MAIN` or `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN`, `step is None`). This is purely\n  additive — it adds a new `elif` branch before the combat branch and does not\n  alter existing untap/upkeep/draw/combat/cleanup handling, so all turn-\n  progression regression tests still pass.\n- `engine/triggers.py`:\n  - `TriggerRegistration` gained an additive `one_shot: bool = False` field\n    (defaulted, so all existing call sites are unaffected).\n  - `TriggerManager.register_delayed(event_type, effect, source, controller,\n    condition=None) -> TriggerRegistration` registers a **one-shot delayed\n    trigger** and returns it.\n  - `fire_event` now removes any matched `one_shot` triggers from the registry\n    at fire time, so a delayed trigger fires **exactly once** and is then gone.\n\n## How the card wires it\nWhen the counter resolves and the controller controls a Wizard (checked at\nresolution via `_controls_a_wizard`, scanning the controller's battlefield for a\n`\"Wizard\"` subtype — an opponent's Wizard does NOT count), the card calls:\n\n```python\ngame.trigger_manager.register_delayed(\n    event_type=BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent,\n    effect=_add_deferred_mana,           # adds {C}=amount to controller's pool\n    source=self,\n    controller=controller,               # \"you\" — the caster\n    condition=lambda g, e: e.player is controller,\n)\n```\n\nWith no Wizard (or only an opponent's Wizard), **no** delayed trigger is\nregistered, and the pool gains nothing.\n\n## How a test observes the engine-driven timing\n- Immediate (per-card tests): after `on_resolve`, exactly one new trigger\n  controlled by `p1` exists; calling `trigger.effect(game)` adds `{C}` equal to\n  the countered spell's mana value (colorless only — no colored mana added).\n- End-to-end (`run_turn`): firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=p1)`\n  (which `run_turn` does at the controller's next main phase) pushes the delayed\n  trigger's effect onto the stack and removes the one-shot registration;\n  resolving that stack object deposits the `{C}` into the controller's pool.\n  Firing the event a second time (or for the opponent) adds nothing — confirming\n  the \"next main phase only\", fire-exactly-once semantics. Verified manually\n  via `run_turn`/`fire_event` (not committed to the test file, which keeps the\n  delivery test on the public trigger system per the Tester's contract).\n\n## Deviations / notes\n- \"amount of mana spent\" is modeled as the recorded `mana_spent` (== mana value\n  for the no-X / non-reduced spells used by the tests). The engine still does not\n  track partial/alternative-cost edge cases; documented in the Tester's\n  `untestable.json`. The fallback to `mana_cost.cmc` keeps directly-staged spells\n  (no payment) working.\n- `Keyword` enum untouched (still 16 members — `test_types.py` hard-asserts this).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":236,"cache_read_input_tokens":75453,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":236,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015rF4nfPePEJ7zX53WjYEJK","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"f67d6ac0-ba3e-4ef8-b4f0-8c21a1526b7a","request_id":"req_011Cbe7aDnCRkVkmz7RVyepL","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_57"}
