r's pool.\n\n## Your task — add timing tests for the previously-untestable item\n1. **Fires at the controller's next main phase**: set up the counter while controlling a Wizard, then drive the game (via `run_turn` to reach the controller's main phase, OR by firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=<controller>)` through `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(...)` exactly as the engine does). Assert the {C} lands in the controller's mana pool at that point (and was NOT there immediately after the counter resolved).\n2. **Fires exactly once (one-shot)**: after the trigger fires once, firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` again (a later main phase) adds NO additional mana — the trigger was consumed.\n3. **Does not fire on the opponent's main phase**: firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=<opponent>)` does not deliver the {C} to anyone (the condition `e.player is controller` gates it).\n4. Look at how existing engine tests drive turns (`engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py`, `engine_tests/test_combat.py`, `test_utils.py`) and the precise `fire_event` signature in `engine/triggers.py` so your test calls match the real API.\n\n## Constraints\n- DO NOT modify `engine_tests/`, FDN `tests.py`, or any engine source. Only edit `cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`.\n- DO NOT change or weaken any of your existing 21 tests — only add new ones.\n- The implementation already exists, so your new tests should PASS. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` and confirm everything (old + new) passes. If a new test reveals a genuine implementation bug, leave the failing test in place and report it (do not paper over it).\n\n## Outputs\n- Updated `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`.\n- Append a \"## Extended coverage\" section to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md` describing the new tests.\n- Keep `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-files.txt` accurate (same single file).\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn: total test count now, how many you added, pass/fail result of `pytest cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`, and `new_failures: <N>` (with reasons if any)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2684,"cache_read_input_tokens":88036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2684},"output_tokens":45,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b757ae20-5a82-4d37-8cad-84260c347503","request_id":"req_011Cbe7ew31neigKvpHYLwKG"}
