{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XKtAtKRpQsMZJbCZxriBZx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HUmNkgrnDpBGboxn2ZpqX8","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-rationale.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5113,"cache_read_input_tokens":8113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5113,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GzTivkk8UJSRY11VipzqHn","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"c7be0da7-9f45-4de1-b855-4077a504bdfc","request_id":"req_011Cbe7gREvzMqVxartZSXLq","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_57 timing"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HUmNkgrnDpBGboxn2ZpqX8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant.\n4\tOracle: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C}\n5\tequal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your\n6\tnext main phase.\"\n7\t\n8\tAll 21 sos_57 tests pass; full `pytest` suite passes (1288 passed, no regressions).\n9\t\n10\t## Counter half (mirrors fdn_48 / fdn_153)\n11\t`cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` → `ManaSculpt(Instant)`:\n12\t- `can_cast` returns True only when another spell (not Mana Sculpt itself) is on\n13\t  the stack — gated on `getattr(stack_obj, \"is_spell\", True)` so it counts any\n14\t  spell, not creature-only (contrast Essence Scatter).\n15\t- `get_targets` returns a single `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK)` whose\n16\t  `filter_fn` accepts any stack object whose `source is not self` and is a spell,\n17\t  and rejects Mana Sculpt's own stack object.\n18\t- `on_resolve` uses the established `_counter_spell` idiom: pop the targeted\n19\t  `StackObject` from `game.stack._items`, remove the card from its controller's\n20\t  STACK zone, and add it to its **owner's** graveyard. `_counter_spell` now\n21\t  returns a bool so resolution can tell a real counter from a fizzle; no legal\n22\t  target ⇒ no-op (and no deferred mana).\n23\t\n24\t## Engine gap 1 — total mana spent per cast (additive, `engine/casting.py`)\n25\tAfter payment, alongside the existing `card.colors_spent`, the cast pipeline now\n26\tsets `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (the total mana paid, after any cost\n27\treduction). Stale `mana_spent` is cleared at the start of a cast next to the\n28\texisting `colors_spent` clear. For a normally-cast no-X / non-reduced spell\n29\t`mana_spent == cmc`, so the tests (which assert the deferred {C} equals the\n30\tcountered spell's mana value) hold.\n31\t\n32\tThe card reads the countered card's `mana_spent` via helper\n33\t`_mana_spent_to_cast`, **falling back to `mana_cost.cmc`** when `mana_spent` is\n34\tabsent — which is the case in the tests, where spells are placed on the stack\n35\tdirectly without paying (e.g. `{2}{R}` → 3, `{3}{U}{U}` → 5, `{4}` → 4).\n36\t\n37\t## Engine gap 2 — main-phase-begin event + delayed one-shot trigger (additive)\n38\tNew engine symbols:\n39\t- `engine/events.py`: **`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)`**\n40\t  with fields `player` (the active player whose main phase is beginning) and\n41\t  `precombat: bool` (True for pre-combat main, False for post-combat).\n42\t- `engine/turn.py`: `run_turn` now fires `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(\n43\t  player=game.active_player, precombat=...)` whenever it reaches a main phase\n44\t  (`PRECOMBAT_MAIN` or `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN`, `step is None`). This is purely\n45\t  additive — it adds a new `elif` branch before the combat branch and does not\n46\t  alter existing untap/upkeep/draw/combat/cleanup handling, so all turn-\n47\t  progression regression tests still pass.\n48\t- `engine/triggers.py`:\n49\t  - `TriggerRegistration` gained an additive `one_shot: bool = False` field\n50\t    (defaulted, so all existing call sites are unaffected).\n51\t  - `TriggerManager.register_delayed(event_type, effect, source, controller,\n52\t    condition=None) -> TriggerRegistration` registers a **one-shot delayed\n53\t    trigger** and returns it.\n54\t  - `fire_event` now removes any matched `one_shot` triggers from the registry\n55\t    at fire time, so a delayed trigger fires **exactly once** and is then gone.\n56\t\n57\t## How the card wires it\n58\tWhen the counter resolves and the controller controls a Wizard (checked at\n59\tresolution via `_controls_a_wizard`, scanning the controller's battlefield for a\n60\t`\"Wizard\"` subtype — an opponent's Wizard does NOT count), the card calls:\n61\t\n62\t```python\n63\tgame.trigger_manager.register_delayed(\n64\t    event_type=BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent,\n65\t    effect=_add_deferred_mana,           # adds {C}=amount to controller's pool\n66\t    source=self,\n67\t    controller=controller,               # \"you\" — the caster\n68\t    condition=lambda g, e: e.player is controller,\n69\t)\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\tWith no Wizard (or only an opponent's Wizard), **no** delayed trigger is\n73\tregistered, and the pool gains nothing.\n74\t\n75\t## How a test observes the engine-driven timing\n76\t- Immediate (per-card tests): after `on_resolve`, exactly one new trigger\n77\t  controlled by `p1` exists; calling `trigger.effect(game)` adds `{C}` equal to\n78\t  the countered spell's mana value (colorless only — no colored mana added).\n79\t- End-to-end (`run_turn`): firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=p1)`\n80\t  (which `run_turn` does at the controller's next main phase) pushes the delayed\n81\t  trigger's effect onto the stack and removes the one-shot registration;\n82\t  resolving that stack object deposits the `{C}` into the controller's pool.\n83\t  Firing the event a second time (or for the opponent) adds nothing — confirming\n84\t  the \"next main phase only\", fire-exactly-once semantics. Verified manually\n85\t  via `run_turn`/`fire_event` (not committed to the test file, which keeps the\n86\t  delivery test on the public trigger system per the Tester's contract).\n87\t\n88\t## Deviations / notes\n89\t- \"amount of mana spent\" is modeled as the recorded `mana_spent` (== mana value\n90\t  for the no-X / non-reduced spells used by the tests). The engine still does not\n91\t  track partial/alternative-cost edge cases; documented in the Tester's\n92\t  `untestable.json`. The fallback to `mana_cost.cmc` keeps directly-staged spells\n93\t  (no payment) working.\n94\t- `Keyword` enum untouched (still 16 members — `test_types.py` hard-asserts this).\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GzTivkk8UJSRY11VipzqHn","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"902ca2c5-40bb-4e91-99f5-87bf715300b4","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:27:13.954Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_57 timing"}
