{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014newMeF6Z6PDRPn6HTeH6e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JRKYuNAenf8kNLSVYz598f","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md","old_string":"- General engine mechanics (stack LIFO, mana-pool emptying on phase transitions,\n  graveyard zone moves) — covered by `engine_tests/`, not re-tested here.","new_string":"- General engine mechanics (stack LIFO, mana-pool emptying on phase transitions,\n  graveyard zone moves) — covered by `engine_tests/`, not re-tested here.\n\n## Extended coverage\n\nThe Implementer added the engine surface that was previously deferred in\n`untestable.json` (item 2 — \"at the beginning of your next main phase\"):\n\n- `engine/events.py`: `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=..., precombat=...)`.\n- `engine/turn.py`: `run_turn` fires that event at the start of each main phase.\n- `engine/triggers.py`: `TriggerManager.register_delayed(...)` registers a\n  one-shot delayed trigger that `fire_event` removes the first time it matches.\n\nThe card wires this via `register_delayed` with `condition=lambda g, e: e.player is\ncontroller`. A new test class `TestManaSculptMainPhaseTiming` exercises the\n**engine-driven** delivery path rather than calling `trigger.effect(game)`\ndirectly. A helper `_fire_main_phase_begin(game, player, precombat=...)` mirrors\n`run_turn`: it sets the active player, fires\n`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=player, ...)` through\n`game.trigger_manager.fire_event`, then resolves the resulting stack object(s)\n(`fire_event` pushes the delayed effect onto the stack — it does not run it\ninline). The pool is asserted before the phase is advanced, since mana pools\nempty at phase transitions.\n\n### TestManaSculptMainPhaseTiming (new — 6 tests)\n- `test_main_phase_event_delivers_colorless_to_controller` — requirement 5\n  end-to-end via the engine event: the {C} is absent immediately after the\n  counter resolves and lands in the controller's pool once\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=p1)` is fired and resolved\n  ({2}{R} → 3 colorless).\n- `test_delayed_trigger_is_consumed_after_firing_once` — the one-shot trigger is\n  removed from the manager after it fires (exactly-once semantics); zero\n  Mana-Sculpt-owned triggers remain afterward.\n- `test_does_not_fire_again_on_a_later_main_phase` — firing the main-phase event\n  a second time (a later main phase) adds no further mana — \"your *next* main\n  phase\" is a single delivery.\n- `test_does_not_fire_on_opponents_main_phase` — the condition `e.player is\n  controller` gates the trigger: the opponent's main-phase event delivers no\n  mana and leaves the trigger registered for p1.\n- `test_opponent_phase_then_controller_phase_delivers_once` — ordering: the\n  opponent's main phase is inert (does not consume the one-shot), then the\n  controller's main phase delivers exactly the recorded {C} ({3}{U}{U} → 5).\n- `test_no_wizard_main_phase_event_delivers_nothing` — with no Wizard no trigger\n  is registered, so firing the controller's main-phase event is inert.\n\nThese six tests close out the previously-untestable timing item (one-shot,\ncontroller-gated, \"next main phase only\"). The original 21 tests are unchanged.\nThe remaining open item in `untestable.json` — the literal \"amount of mana spent\"\ndiverging from mana value for X / cost-reduced / alternative-cost spells — is\nstill out of scope here (the engine records `mana_spent == cmc` for the\ndirectly-staged, unpaid spells these tests use)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2003,"cache_read_input_tokens":60024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2003,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostic