{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GzTivkk8UJSRY11VipzqHn","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. The `test-files.txt` is already accurate (single file `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`).\n\nTESTS_REWRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 27 (21 existing + 6 added)\n\npytest result: 27 passed, 0 failed\nnew_failures: 0\n\nSummary:\n- Extended `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` with a new `TestManaSculptMainPhaseTiming` class (6 tests) covering the engine-driven timing item that was previously deferred in `untestable.json`. All 21 original tests are unchanged and still pass.\n- The new tests drive the real engine API: a helper `_fire_main_phase_begin` mirrors `run_turn` by setting the active player, firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=..., precombat=...)` through `game.trigger_manager.fire_event`, then resolving the stack (a necessary step — `fire_event` pushes the delayed effect as a `StackObject` rather than executing it inline). The mana pool is asserted before any phase transition since pools empty on transition.\n- New tests cover: (1) fires at the controller's next main phase and was not in the pool immediately after the counter, (2) the one-shot trigger is consumed and fires exactly once, (3) does not fire on the opponent's main phase (the `e.player is controller` gate), plus ordering (opponent phase is inert then controller phase delivers) and the no-Wizard inert case.\n- Updated `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md` with an \"## Extended coverage\" section. `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-files.txt` remains accurate (same single file).\n\nRelevant paths:\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-files.txt`\n\nNote: the second `untestable.json` item (literal \"amount of mana spent\" diverging from mana value for X / cost-reduced / alternative-cost spells) remains genuinel