{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017kt6B5XraUdk8TE8dB3mZx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"cards\": [\n3\t    {\n4\t      \"card\": \"sos_1\",\n5\t      \"tests\": [\n6\t        {\n7\t          \"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py\",\n8\t          \"summary\": \"tests for The Dawning Archaic: static data, cost reduction, attack trigger registration, free-recast and exile-instead-of-graveyard\"\n9\t        }\n10\t      ],\n11\t      \"implementation\": [\n12\t        {\n13\t          \"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n14\t          \"summary\": \"The Dawning Archaic: cost reduction per instant/sorcery in graveyard, attack trigger recasting a graveyard spell for free with exile redirect\"\n15\t        },\n16\t        {\n17\t          \"path\": \"engine/casting.py\",\n18\t          \"summary\": \"additive stack->graveyard redirect registry consulted by _resolve_spell so a free-cast spell can be exiled instead of going to graveyard\"\n19\t        }\n20\t      ]\n21\t    },\n22\t    {\n23\t      \"card\": \"sos_13\",\n24\t      \"tests\": [\n25\t        {\n26\t          \"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py\",\n27\t          \"summary\": \"tests for Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares: front-face stats, ETB Inkling token (target player, 1/1 W+B flying), conditional becomes-prepared (strictly-more opponents), {W} prepare-half cost, exile-copy creation, cast-from-exile + unprepare, and Swords effect\"\n28\t        }\n29\t      ],\n30\t      \"implementation\": [\n31\t        {\n32\t          \"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py\",\n33\t          \"summary\": \"Emeritus of Truce front-face creature + ETB (Inkling token then conditional mark_prepared); SwordsToPlowshares {W} instant prepare half (exile target creature, controller gains life=power)\"\n34\t        },\n35\t        {\n36\t          \"path\": \"engine/preparation.py\",\n37\t          \"summary\": \"additive Preparation-card framework (CR 722): mark_prepared/unprepare/is_prepared, copy-of-prepare-spell created in controller exile keyed to permanent; cast_prepared_copy casts the copy first and only unprepares the source/detaches the registry after the cast succeeds (722.3c)\"\n38\t        }\n39\t      ]\n40\t    },\n41\t    {\n42\t      \"card\": \"sos_4\",\n43\t      \"tests\": [\n44\t        {\n45\t          \"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py\",\n46\t          \"summary\": \"tests for Together as One: properties, two-target (player + any target) targeting, Converge X=distinct colors, draw/damage/lifegain clauses, and full-cast pipeline X==3\"\n47\t        }\n48\t      ],\n49\t      \"implementation\": [\n50\t        {\n51\t          \"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py\",\n52\t          \"summary\": \"Together as One: {6} sorcery, X=len(colors_spent); target player draws X, X damage to any target, controller gains X life\"\n53\t        }\n54\t      ]\n55\t    },\n56\t    {\n57\t      \"card\": \"sos_57\",\n58\t      \"tests\": [\n59\t        {\n60\t          \"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py\",\n61\t          \"summary\": \"tests for Mana Sculpt: static data, counter-any-spell targeting (excludes self), countered card to owner graveyard, creature-spell counter, no-target fizzle, Wizard-conditional delayed trigger (controlled by you, scales with mana spent, colorless-only, opponent Wizard excluded), and deferred {C} delivery timing\"\n62\t        }\n63\t      ],\n64\t      \"implementation\": [\n65\t        {\n66\t          \"path\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n67\t          \"summary\": \"Mana Sculpt: counter target spell via _counter_spell idiom; if controller controls a Wizard at resolution, register a one-shot delayed trigger adding {C}=mana_spent (fallback mana_cost.cmc) at controller's next main phase\"\n68\t        },\n69\t        {\n70\t          \"path\": \"engine/casting.py\",\n71\t          \"summary\": \"additive: record card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc after payment (total mana paid), cleared at cast start alongside colors_spent\"\n72\t        },\n73\t        {\n74\t          \"path\": \"engine/events.py\",\n75\t          \"summary\": \"additive: new BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, precombat) triggered event\"\n76\t        },\n77\t        {\n78\t          \"path\": \"engine/triggers.py\",\n79\t          \"summary\": \"additive: TriggerRegistration.one_shot field, TriggerManager.register_delayed() for one-shot delayed triggers, fire_event removes matched one-shot triggers so they fire exactly once\"\n80\t        },\n81\t        {\n82\t          \"path\": \"engine/turn.py\",\n83\t          \"summary\": \"additive: run_turn fires BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent at the start of each main phase (pre/post-combat)\"\n84\t        }\n85\t      ]\n86\t    }\n87\t  ]\n88\t}\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012WJm16sHZxbzFpVsTzGbaS","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"2fe60a39-7893-42f1-9229-fd6fd0d6659b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:29:34.930Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_57 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AYqX3VGdWbJM7pH4k3a6RY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent, append-only log of conventions and design decisions across runs.\n4\t\n5\t## Engine: stack->graveyard exile redirect (from sos_1)\n6\t- For \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" free-cast effects:\n7\t  `engine.casting` now has an additive per-game redirect registry:\n8\t  - `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card, destination)` — one-shot, identity-keyed by `id(card)`.\n9\t  - `clear_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card)`.\n10\t  - `_redirect_registry(game)` lazily attaches `game._stack_to_graveyard_redirects` (no GameState.__init__ change).\n11\t  - `_resolve_spell` pops any registered redirect for a non-permanent spell and routes it there instead of the graveyard; with no redirect registered, behavior is unchanged (defaults to GRAVEYARD).\n12\t- Usage in a card: call `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, chosen_card, \"exile\")` before `cast_spell_free(...)`. Clear it if the cast raises.\n13\t- Rationale: `engine.zones.move_to_zone` only consults replacement effects when `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`, so STACK->GRAVEYARD resolution would otherwise bypass an exile-instead replacement.\n14\t\n15\t## Convention: cost_reduction counts (from sos_1)\n16\t- Card `cost_reduction` returns the raw count (e.g. instants+sorceries in controller's graveyard); the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the generic portion of the cost. Mirrors fdn_167 (Tolarian Terror). Count only the controller's graveyard unless the card says otherwise.\n17\t## Convention: Converge / colors_spent (from sos_4)\n18\t- Converge X = number of distinct colors of mana spent to cast. Already wired in engine:\n19\t  `engine.casting.cast_spell` sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (distinct, colorless-excluded, sorted list of `engine.types.Color`).\n20\t- Card-side: default `self.colors_spent = []` in `__init__`; compute `X = len(self.colors_spent)`. No engine change needed for Converge.\n21\t- Player-vs-creature target detection idiom: `hasattr(obj, \"life\")` is True only for `engine.player.Player` (established FDN idiom, e.g. fdn_192).\n22\t## Engine: Preparation Card framework (from sos_13)\n23\t- New additive module `engine/preparation.py` implements the \"Prepared\" designation mechanic (CR 722). Public API:\n24\t  - `is_prepared(permanent) -> bool`\n25\t  - `mark_prepared(game, permanent) -> copy|None` — sets designation and creates a copy of the prepare spell in the controller's exile, keyed by `id(permanent)` in lazy per-game registry `game._prepared_copies`; idempotent.\n26\t  - `unprepare(game, permanent)` — clears designation, removes exile copy.\n27\t  - `get_prepared_copy(game, permanent)` / `get_prepared_source(game, copy)`.\n28\t  - `cast_prepared_copy(game, player, copy)` — casts the exiled copy via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`, then (only on cast success, CR 722.3c) clears the source's prepared designation and detaches the registry entry. On cast failure the source stays prepared and the copy stays in exile.\n29\t- Conventions for future Preparation cards:\n30\t  - \"Prepared\" is a DESIGNATION, NOT a `Keyword` enum member. Do NOT add it to `Keyword` — `engine_tests/test_types.py::test_exactly_sixteen_members` hard-asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`. Track via `is_prepared`/`prepared` boolean attrs; store the printed label in `printed_keywords` if needed.\n31\t  - The card exposes its prepare half via `make_prepare_spell()` factory; cost surface via `prepare_mana_cost`/`back_mana_cost`.\n32\t- Card-spec note: when a split/preparation card's `card_spec.json` omits the back-face oracle text, implement the canonical effect implied by the back-face name (sos_13's back half \"Swords to Plowshares\" = \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\"). Logged as a coordinator ruling in RUN_DECISIONS.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012WJm16sHZxbzFpVsTzGbaS","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"9205019a-0804-42ff-ba32-89d90c82b65d","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:29:34.930Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_57 implementation"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"aa8cd6a4cd0539dd9","tool_use_id":"toolu_012WJm16sHZxbzFpVsTzGbaS","description":"Reading engine/stack.py","subagent_type":"Reviewer","usage":{"total_tokens":31715,"tool_uses":9,"duration_ms":16278},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"4158f587-057d-4e3e-855b-84205bdd583a","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01U7V4mDAbFeyqZ6RLdENF5b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JwFf2RtiRvrAKgpczpBR4c","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/stack.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10107,"cache_read_input_tokens":21543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10107,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012WJm16sHZxbzFpVsTzGbaS","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"02e7c95a-1b89-4e68-b1e7-6cf41a945b4d","request_id":"req_011Cbe7sAaSEFCHCUFJWeSfE","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_57 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JwFf2RtiRvrAKgpczpBR4c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"The spell/ability stack with LIFO resolution and priority passing.\"\"\"\n2\t\n3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n4\t\n5\timport copy\n6\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n7\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable\n8\t\n9\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n10\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n11\t    from engine.player import Player\n12\t\n13\t\n14\t@dataclass\n15\tclass StackObject:\n16\t    \"\"\"An object on the stack representing a spell or ability.\n17\t\n18\t    Attributes:\n19\t        source: The card or ability that created this stack object.\n20\t        controller: The player who controls this stack object.\n21\t        targets: The chosen targets for the spell/ability.\n22\t        on_resolve: Callback invoked when this object resolves.\n23\t        is_mana_ability: Whether this is a mana ability (resolves immediately).\n24\t    \"\"\"\n25\t\n26\t    source: Any\n27\t    controller: Player\n28\t    targets: list[Any] = field(default_factory=list)\n29\t    on_resolve: Callable[[GameState], None] = field(default=lambda _game: None)\n30\t    is_mana_ability: bool = False\n31\t\n32\t\n33\tclass Stack:\n34\t    \"\"\"The game stack — a LIFO structure for spells and abilities.\n35\t\n36\t    The internal list stores objects with the last element being the top\n37\t    of the stack (most recently pushed).\n38\t    \"\"\"\n39\t\n40\t    def __init__(self) -> None:\n41\t        self._items: list[StackObject] = []\n42\t\n43\t    def push(self, obj: StackObject) -> None:\n44\t        \"\"\"Push *obj* onto the top of the stack.\"\"\"\n45\t        self._items.append(obj)\n46\t\n47\t    def pop(self) -> StackObject:\n48\t        \"\"\"Remove and return the top object from the stack.\n49\t\n50\t        Raises:\n51\t            IndexError: If the stack is empty.\n52\t        \"\"\"\n53\t        return self._items.pop()\n54\t\n55\t    def peek(self) -> StackObject | None:\n56\t        \"\"\"Return the top object without removing it, or ``None`` if empty.\"\"\"\n57\t        return self._items[-1] if self._items else None\n58\t\n59\t    def __len__(self) -> int:\n60\t        \"\"\"Return the number of objects on the stack.\"\"\"\n61\t        return len(self._items)\n62\t\n63\t    def is_empty(self) -> bool:\n64\t        \"\"\"Return ``True`` if the stack contains no objects.\"\"\"\n65\t        return len(self._items) == 0\n66\t\n67\t    def objects(self) -> list[StackObject]:\n68\t        \"\"\"Return all stack objects ordered from top to bottom.\"\"\"\n69\t        return list(reversed(self._items))\n70\t\n71\t\n72\tdef copy_spell(\n73\t    game: GameState,\n74\t    original: StackObject,\n75\t    controller: Player,\n76\t    new_targets: list[Any] | None = None,\n77\t) -> StackObject:\n78\t    \"\"\"Create a copy of a spell on the stack (for storm and similar effects).\n79\t\n80\t    Shallow-copies the source card so the copy has independent state\n81\t    (chosen_targets, etc.) while sharing class method bindings.  Binds\n82\t    on_resolve to call the copied card's on_resolve directly — no zone\n83\t    movement, which is correct for spell copies.\n84\t\n85\t    Args:\n86\t        game: The current game state.\n87\t        original: The StackObject being copied.\n88\t        controller: The player who controls the copy.\n89\t        new_targets: Optional replacement targets.  If ``None``, the\n90\t            original's target list is cloned.\n91\t\n92\t    Returns:\n93\t        A new StackObject representing the copy ready to be pushed.\n94\t    \"\"\"\n95\t    copied_card = copy.copy(original.source)\n96\t    copied_card.controller = controller\n97\t    copied_card.owner = getattr(original.source, \"owner\", controller)\n98\t\n99\t    targets = new_targets if new_targets is not None else list(original.targets)\n100\t\n101\t    copy_obj = StackObject(\n102\t        source=copied_card,\n103\t        controller=controller,\n104\t        targets=targets,\n105\t    )\n106\t\n107\t    def _copy_resolve(g: GameState) -> None:\n108\t        copied_card.chosen_targets = copy_obj.targets\n109\t        copied_card.on_resolve(g)\n110\t\n111\t    copy_obj.on_resolve = _copy_resolve\n112\t    return copy_obj\n113\t\n114\t\n115\tdef check_state_based_actions(game: GameState) -> None:\n116\t    \"\"\"Check and perform all state-based actions until the game state is stable.\n117\t\n118\t    This is a convenience wrapper around\n119\t    :func:`engine.state_based_actions.resolve_state_based_actions` that\n120\t    maintains the original ``-> None`` call-site contract used by\n121\t    :func:`priority_loop`.  For the single-pass boolean API, import\n122\t    :func:`~engine.state_based_actions.check_state_based_actions` directly\n123\t    from :mod:`engine.state_based_actions`.\n124\t    \"\"\"\n125\t    from engine.state_based_actions import resolve_state_based_actions\n126\t\n127\t    resolve_state_based_actions(game)\n128\t\n129\t\n130\tdef _get_legal_actions(game: GameState, player: Player) -> list[Any]:\n131\t    \"\"\"Return the legal actions available to *player*.\n132\t\n133\t    Placeholder — returns an empty list until spells/abilities are\n134\t    implemented in later items.\n135\t    \"\"\"\n136\t    return []\n137\t\n138\t\n139\tdef _handle_priority(game: GameState, player: Player) -> bool:\n140\t    \"\"\"Give priority to *player* and let them act or pass.\n141\t\n142\t    Returns ``True`` if the player passed priority, ``False`` if they\n143\t    took an action (in which case the priority loop restarts).\n144\t\n145\t    When the stack is non-empty, the player is always asked via\n146\t    :meth:`Player.choose` so they can respond.  When the stack is empty\n147\t    and no legal actions exist, the player auto-passes.\n148\t    \"\"\"\n149\t    actions = _get_legal_actions(game, player)\n150\t\n151\t    # Auto-pass when there is nothing to respond to and no actions.\n152\t    if not actions and game.stack.is_empty():\n153\t        return True\n154\t\n155\t    options = actions + [\"pass\"]\n156\t    choice = player.choose(options, \"priority: choose action or pass\")\n157\t\n158\t    if choice == \"pass\":\n159\t        return True\n160\t\n161\t    # Mana abilities resolve immediately without using the stack.\n162\t    if isinstance(choice, StackObject) and choice.is_mana_ability:\n163\t        choice.on_resolve(game)\n164\t        return False\n165\t\n166\t    # Regular spell / ability — push onto the stack.\n167\t    if isinstance(choice, StackObject):\n168\t        game.stack.push(choice)\n169\t\n170\t    return False\n171\t\n172\t\n173\tdef priority_loop(game: GameState) -> None:\n174\t    \"\"\"Run the priority-passing loop for the current phase/step.\n175\t\n176\t    Flow\n177\t    ----\n178\t    1. Active player gets priority.  They may play spells/abilities\n179\t       (pushed to stack) or pass.\n180\t    2. When a player takes an action they **retain** priority (MTG rule:\n181\t       the player who just acted gets to respond first).\n182\t    3. When a player passes, priority moves to the other player.\n183\t    4. If both players pass in succession with the stack **non-empty**,\n184\t       the top of the stack is resolved (``pop`` → ``on_resolve(game)``),\n185\t       state-based actions are checked, and the active player receives\n186\t       priority again.\n187\t    5. If both players pass with the stack **empty**, return (the game\n188\t       advances to the next phase/step).\n189\t\n190\t    ``game.priority_player_index`` is kept in sync throughout so that\n191\t    :pyattr:`GameState.priority_player` always reflects who currently\n192\t    holds priority.\n193\t\n194\t    Player decisions come from :meth:`Player.choose`.  When no legal\n195\t    actions exist and the stack is empty, the player auto-passes without\n196\t    being asked.\n197\t    \"\"\"\n198\t    while True:\n199\t        # Active player receives priority at the start of each\n200\t        # resolution round.\n201\t        current_index = game.active_player_index\n202\t        game.priority_player_index = current_index\n203\t        consecutive_passes = 0\n204\t\n205\t        while consecutive_passes < 2:\n206\t            player = game.players[current_index]\n207\t            game.priority_player_index = current_index\n208\t\n209\t            passed = _handle_priority(game, player)\n210\t\n211\t            if passed:\n212\t                consecutive_passes += 1\n213\t                # Priority moves to the other player.\n214\t                current_index = 1 - current_index\n215\t            else:\n216\t                # Player took an action — they retain priority.\n217\t                consecutive_passes = 0\n218\t\n219\t        # Both players passed consecutively.\n220\t        if game.stack.is_empty():\n221\t            return  # Advance to next phase/step\n222\t\n223\t        # Resolve top of stack (LIFO).\n224\t        obj = game.stack.pop()\n225\t        obj.on_resolve(game)\n226\t        check_state_based_actions(game)\n227\t        # Active player receives priority again — outer loop continues.\n228\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012WJm16sHZxbzFpVsTzGbaS","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"2ec576dd-5035-4f14-b5a7-9c8234faf92a","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:29:38.510Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_57 implementation"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"aa8cd6a4cd0539dd9","tool_use_id":"toolu_012WJm16sHZxbzFpVsTzGbaS","description":"Reading cards/fdn/fdn_153/card_impl.py","subagent_type":"Reviewer","usage":{"total_tokens":31724,"tool_uses":10,"duration_ms":16333},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"b0ef74b7-52b0-4428-a3e6-caaa4022c571","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01U7V4mDAbFeyqZ6RLdENF5b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012t8r9DmpFFmbsGF87Fnh5g","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_153/card_impl.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10107,"cache_read_input_tokens":21543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10107,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012WJm16sHZxbzFpVsTzGbaS","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"46521e1e-1a40-476d-8d41-c64d2c058a2a","request_id":"req_011Cbe7sAaSEFCHCUFJWeSfE","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_57 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012t8r9DmpFFmbsGF87Fnh5g","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Card implementation for Essence Scatter.\"\"\"\n2\t\n3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n4\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n5\tfrom engine.card import Instant, Sorcery\n6\tfrom engine.continuous_effects import (\n7\t    ContinuousEffect,\n8\t    DURATION_END_OF_TURN,\n9\t    Layer,\n10\t    SubLayer,\n11\t)\n12\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, TargetRequirement, Zone\n13\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n14\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n15\t\n16\t    from cards.registry import CardRegistry\n17\t\n18\tdef _get_chosen_target(card: Any, game: Any) -> Any:\n19\t    \"\"\"Retrieve the first chosen target for a spell.\n20\t\n21\t    Looks for ``chosen_targets`` (set by :func:`cast_spell` during the\n22\t    real casting pipeline) first, then falls back to the test-backdoor\n23\t    attribute ``_resolve_target``.\n24\t    \"\"\"\n25\t    chosen = getattr(card, \"chosen_targets\", None)\n26\t    if chosen:\n27\t        return chosen[0]\n28\t    return getattr(card, \"_resolve_target\", None)\n29\tdef _counter_spell(game: GameState, stack_obj: Any) -> None:\n30\t    \"\"\"Counter a spell — remove it from the stack and move the card to\n31\t    its owner's graveyard.\n32\t    \"\"\"\n33\t    from engine.stack import StackObject\n34\t\n35\t    if not isinstance(stack_obj, StackObject):\n36\t        return\n37\t\n38\t    card = stack_obj.source\n39\t\n40\t    # Check if the stack object is actually on the stack; if not, fizzle.\n41\t    stack_items = game.stack._items  # noqa: SLF001\n42\t    found = False\n43\t    for i, item in enumerate(stack_items):\n44\t        if item is stack_obj:\n45\t            stack_items.pop(i)\n46\t            found = True\n47\t            break\n48\t\n49\t    if not found:\n50\t        return\n51\t\n52\t    controller = stack_obj.controller\n53\t    owner = getattr(card, \"owner\", controller)\n54\t\n55\t    if controller is not None:\n56\t        stack_zone = controller.zones[Zone.STACK]\n57\t        if stack_zone.contains(card):\n58\t            stack_zone.remove(card)\n59\t\n60\t    if owner is not None:\n61\t        graveyard = owner.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD]\n62\t        graveyard.add(card)\n63\t\n64\tclass EssenceScatter(Instant):\n65\t    \"\"\"Essence Scatter — {1}{U} — Counter target creature spell.\n66\t\n67\t    FDN collector number 153.\n68\t    \"\"\"\n69\t\n70\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n71\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"Essence Scatter\")\n72\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}\"))\n73\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"rules_text\", \"Counter target creature spell.\")\n74\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n75\t\n76\t    def can_cast(self, game: GameState) -> bool:\n77\t        \"\"\"Cannot cast unless a creature spell is on the stack.\"\"\"\n78\t        for stack_obj in game.stack.objects():\n79\t            source = stack_obj.source\n80\t            if source is self:\n81\t                continue\n82\t            card_types = getattr(source, \"card_types\", set())\n83\t            if CardType.CREATURE in card_types:\n84\t                return True\n85\t        return False\n86\t\n87\t    def get_targets(self, game: GameState) -> list[Any]:\n88\t        \"\"\"Target creature spell on the stack.\"\"\"\n89\t        targets: list[Any] = []\n90\t        for stack_obj in game.stack.objects():\n91\t            source = stack_obj.source\n92\t            if source is self:\n93\t                continue\n94\t            card_types = getattr(source, \"card_types\", set())\n95\t            if CardType.CREATURE in card_types:\n96\t                targets.append(stack_obj)\n97\t        if not targets:\n98\t            return []\n99\t        return [\n100\t            TargetRequirement(\n101\t                filter_fn=lambda obj: CardType.CREATURE in getattr(getattr(obj, \"source\", obj), \"card_types\", set()),\n102\t                description=\"target creature spell\",\n103\t                zone=Zone.STACK,\n104\t            )\n105\t        ]\n106\t\n107\t    def on_resolve(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n108\t        \"\"\"Counter the target creature spell.\"\"\"\n109\t        target = _get_chosen_target(self, game)\n110\t        if target is None:\n111\t            return\n112\t        _counter_spell(game, target)\n113\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012WJm16sHZxbzFpVsTzGbaS","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b834fbcc-ec94-49f2-a77d-e8bb93c25759","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:29:38.567Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_57 implementation"}
