{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012WJm16sHZxbzFpVsTzGbaS","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. The implementation faithfully mirrors the established fdn_48/fdn_153 counter idiom and the engine changes are strictly additive.\n\nKey validations performed:\n- **Counter half** (`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`): targets another spell (excludes self via `getattr(obj, \"source\", obj) is not self` — actually more correct than fdn_48's `obj is not self`), counters creature spells, moves the countered card to its OWNER's graveyard, and fizzles cleanly on no/illegal target (`_counter_spell` returns `False` → no deferred mana).\n- **Wizard gate**: `_controls_a_wizard` scans only the controller's battlefield, checked at resolution; opponent Wizards correctly excluded (verified against the dedicated tests).\n- **`engine/casting.py`**: `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` is set after payment and cleared (`del card.mana_spent`) at the start of each cast alongside `colors_spent`, so no stale leak; `effective_cost` is always defined.\n- **`engine/turn.py`**: the new `elif` for `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` is mutually exclusive with the combat branch, fires once per main phase (`step is None`, confirmed in the turn sequence) for the active player, and leaves untap/upkeep/draw/combat/cleanup untouched.\n- **`engine/triggers.py`**: `register_delayed` + `one_shot` fires exactly once and is removed before the effect is pushed; removal iterates a pre-built `matching` list (no mutation-during-iteration); the opponent-event path doesn't consume the trigger; the `one_shot: bool = False` default keeps existing call sites working.\n- **Regression safety**: all changes additive — new event class, new method, new defaulted field, two added casting lines, one added turn branch. `Keyword` enum untouched.\n\nNo strict issues found.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aa8cd6a4cd0539dd9 (use SendMessage with to: 'aa8cd6a4cd0539dd9' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 55851\ntool_uses: 25\nduration_ms: 108313</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"d1ed88c0-0abf-495c-b11b-dfe0a06a5cd6","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:31:10.540Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are reviewing the implementation of a single Magic: The Gathering card plus additive engine changes. The card is **sos_57** (\"Mana Sculpt\", {1}{U}{U} Instant — \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\").\n\n## Inputs\n- Unified diff of the implementation + engine changes (NOT the tests): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl.diff` (covers `cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/turn.py`).\n- Implementer's rationale (read for design intent and new API): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-rationale.md`.\n- Coordinator directives (scope): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/coordinator-directives.md`.\n- Card spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_spec.json`.\n- Tests (already arbitrated — DO NOT demand test rewrites): `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` (27 tests, all passing).\n- Prior-card conventions to respect: `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` and `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n- Engine source for context: `engine/card.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/turn.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/zones.py`.\n- Rules: `/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt` (grep).\n\n## What to review\nReview the diff for correctness vs. spec/oracle intent, real bugs, missed edge cases, and convention violations. Scrutinize especially:\n- **Counter half**: targets another spell on the stack (excludes self), counters creature spells too, countered card goes to its OWNER's graveyard, no-target fizzle.\n- **Wizard gate**: only the controller's (\"you\") Wizard enables the clause; an opponent's Wizard must not. Checked at resolution time.\n- **Engine: `card.mana_spent`** in `engine/casting.py` — is it set after payment and cleared on a new cast so it can't leak stale values? Does the fallback to `mana_cost.cmc` make sense?\n- **Engine: `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`** fired from `engine/turn.py` — confirm the new firing is purely additive (added branch) and does NOT disturb existing untap/upkeep/draw/combat/cleanup turn progression. Any risk it fires at the wrong step or for the wrong player?\n- **Engine: `TriggerManager.register_delayed` + `one_shot`** in `engine/triggers.py` — does the one-shot trigger fire EXACTLY once and get removed? Any risk of removing non-one-shot triggers, mutating the registry during iteration, or the delayed trigger persisting across turns incorrectly?\n- **Regression safety**: confirm nothing existing in engine was renamed/removed (additive-only), the `Keyword` enum is unchanged (16 members), and the `one_shot` field default keeps existing `TriggerRegistration` call sites working.\n\n## Important guardrails\n- DO NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards (see `FILES_MODIFIED.json`) or conventions in `KEY_DECISIONS.md` (e.g., lazy per-game registries).\n- DO NOT demand test rewrites — tests were arbitrated. Any test-quality concern is `advisory` only.\n- The \"amount of mana spent == mana value\" modeling (no X/cost-reduction edge handling) is a known, accepted coordinator limitation — at most `advisory`, not strict.\n- Focus on what is visible in the diff.\n\n## Output (write this)\nWrite `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json` — a JSON array of:\n```json\n{\"severity\": \"strict\" | \"advisory\", \"file\": \"<path>\", \"line\": <int or null>, \"comment\": \"<actionable comment>\"}\n```\nUse `strict` only for must-fix issues (correctness bugs, spec violations, regression risks). Use `advisory` for style/clarity/known-limitations. Write `[]` if none.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\n```\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json\n```","agentId":"aa8cd6a4cd0539dd9","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. The implementation faithfully mirrors the established fdn_48/fdn_153 counter idiom and the engine changes are strictly additive.\n\nKey validations performed:\n- **Counter half** (`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`): targets another spell (excludes self via `getattr(obj, \"source\", obj) is not self` — actually more correct than fdn_48's `obj is not self`), counters creature spells, moves the countered card to its OWNER's graveyard, and fizzles cleanly on no/illegal target (`_counter_spell` returns `False` → no deferred mana).\n- **Wizard gate**: `_controls_a_wizard` scans only the controller's battlefield, checked at resolution; opponent Wizards correctly excluded (verified against the dedicated tests).\n- **`engine/casting.py`**: `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` is set after payment and cleared (`del card.mana_spent`) at the start of each cast alongside `colors_spent`, so no stale leak; `effective_cost` is always defined.\n- **`engine/turn.py`**: the new `elif` for `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` is mutually exclusive with the combat branch, fires once per main phase (`step is None`, confirmed in the turn sequence) for the active player, and leaves untap/upkeep/draw/combat/cleanup untouched.\n- **`engine/triggers.py`**: `register_delayed` + `one_shot` fires exactly once and is removed before the effect is pushed; removal iterates a pre-built `matching` list (no mutation-during-iteration); the opponent-event path doesn't consume the trigger; the `one_shot: bool = False` default keeps existing call sites working.\n- **Regression safety**: all changes additive — new event class, new method, new defaulted field, two added casting lines, one added turn branch. `Keyword` enum untouched.\n\nNo strict issues found.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json"}],"totalDurationMs":108313,"totalTokens":55851,"totalToolUseCount":25,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1336,"cache_read_input_tokens":53803,"output_tokens":710,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1336},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":710,"cache_read_input_tokens":53803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1336,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":15,"searchCount":9,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":1,"linesAdded":21,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
