{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VwgmXR5ZP3SB9uaEJhNUPE","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All outputs are written and validated. Summary of what I did:\n\nI wrote 26 pytest tests for **sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer** (a `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3) at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`. All 26 fail against the empty stub for the right reason (the card isn't implemented yet — TDD red phase), and the file collects cleanly with no import/collection errors.\n\nThe tests follow the established FDN reference-walker conventions (`get_loyalty_abilities()` returning `LoyaltyAbility` objects whose `effect(game)` reads `pw._resolve_target` / `pw._resolve_targets`) and the engine's existing surveil convention (`choose_yes_no` per top card, from `cards/fdn/fdn_157`).\n\nCoverage:\n- Static data (name, `{1}{B}{B}` cost, Planeswalker/Legendary/Ral subtype, starting loyalty 3) and the four-ability roster with costs `{+1, -1, -2, -7}`.\n- **+1 Surveil 2** — keep-both, put-both-in-graveyard, card-conservation invariant, no-leakage-to-other-zones, empty-library no-op.\n- **−1 discard** — single target, multiple targets each discard one, zero-target no-op, empty-hand target.\n- **−2 reanimate** — returns targeted mv≤3 creature to your battlefield under your control, no-target no-op, and target-filter boundary tests (accepts mv3, rejects mv4, rejects non-creature).\n- **−7 ultimate** — exists at cost −7 and resolves against a target opponent without raising.\n\nTwo requirements are flagged in `untestable.json` (the random coin-flip count X and the actual \"skips next X turns\" turn-skipping): the engine has no coin-flip RNG hook and no skip-turn mechanism (only an `extra_turns` queue), so X and the skip can't be deterministically asserted yet.\n\n```markdown\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 26\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md\nfiles_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-files.txt\nuntestable_count: 2\nuntestable_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/untestable.json\nnotes: wrote 26 tests for sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer (4 loyalty abilities); −7 coin-flip X and skip-turn flagged untestable (no engine RNG/skip-turn API)\n```"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aac7a10f0f9b7f978 (use SendMessage with to: 'aac7a10f0f9b7f978' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 109259\ntool_uses: 54\nduration_ms: 280461</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"fe6a2b84-2c61-4c63-af68-5307652d3f57","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:36:28.998Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are writing pytest tests for a single Magic: The Gathering card implementation (TDD red phase). The card is **sos_97**.\n\n## Inputs\n- Card spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_spec.json` (read this for name, mana cost, oracle text, P/T, keywords).\n- Implementation stub you are testing against: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py`.\n- Test conventions: study existing tests under `/workspace/engine_tests/` (e.g. `test_casting.py`, `test_triggers.py`, `test_combat.py`, `test_abilities.py`, `test_replacement_effects.py`) and the FDN reference tests that ship with a `tests.py`: `cards/fdn/fdn_13/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_142/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_205/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_215/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_244/tests.py`.\n- Test helpers: `/workspace/test_utils.py` and `/workspace/test_utils.md` (`create_game`, `set_board_state`, etc.).\n- Reference card implementations: `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_*/card_impl.py`.\n- Engine source with rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`, `engine/types.py`.\n- Workspace rules: `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`, `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` (read — records engine conventions/APIs added by earlier cards this run, including delayed one-shot triggers, a main-phase-begin event, a preparation framework, and a stack->graveyard redirect helper), `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n- Rules reference: `/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt` (grep, do not read whole; see `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n\n## Your task\n1. Read the card spec and understand the card's full behavior.\n2. Write thorough pytest tests at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` that verify the card's behavior per its oracle text. Cover main functionality plus relevant edge cases. Tests must follow existing engine/FDN test conventions and must FAIL against the current empty stub (TDD red) but PASS once the card is correctly implemented.\n3. Do NOT modify any files under `engine_tests/` or any FDN `tests.py`. Do NOT modify engine source. You only write `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`.\n4. Confirm the tests are well-formed by running them (they should fail/error because the card is unimplemented — that is expected). Do not try to make them pass.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` — your tests.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md` — what each test covers and the behavior contract you derived from the spec.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-files.txt` — list of test file path(s) you created (one per line).\n- If any spec requirement cannot be tested with the current engine/test API, write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/untestable.json` — a JSON array of `{\"requirement\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\", \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"...\"}`. Omit the file entirely if everything is testable.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn a short summary: number of tests written, the test file path, and `untestable_count: <N>` (0 if none). Do not paste the full test code.","agentId":"aac7a10f0f9b7f978","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All outputs are written and validated. Summary of what I did:\n\nI wrote 26 pytest tests for **sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer** (a `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3) at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`. All 26 fail against the empty stub for the right reason (the card isn't implemented yet — TDD red phase), and the file collects cleanly with no import/collection errors.\n\nThe tests follow the established FDN reference-walker conventions (`get_loyalty_abilities()` returning `LoyaltyAbility` objects whose `effect(game)` reads `pw._resolve_target` / `pw._resolve_targets`) and the engine's existing surveil convention (`choose_yes_no` per top card, from `cards/fdn/fdn_157`).\n\nCoverage:\n- Static data (name, `{1}{B}{B}` cost, Planeswalker/Legendary/Ral subtype, starting loyalty 3) and the four-ability roster with costs `{+1, -1, -2, -7}`.\n- **+1 Surveil 2** — keep-both, put-both-in-graveyard, card-conservation invariant, no-leakage-to-other-zones, empty-library no-op.\n- **−1 discard** — single target, multiple targets each discard one, zero-target no-op, empty-hand target.\n- **−2 reanimate** — returns targeted mv≤3 creature to your battlefield under your control, no-target no-op, and target-filter boundary tests (accepts mv3, rejects mv4, rejects non-creature).\n- **−7 ultimate** — exists at cost −7 and resolves against a target opponent without raising.\n\nTwo requirements are flagged in `untestable.json` (the random coin-flip count X and the actual \"skips next X turns\" turn-skipping): the engine has no coin-flip RNG hook and no skip-turn mechanism (only an `extra_turns` queue), so X and the skip can't be deterministically asserted yet.\n\n```markdown\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 26\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md\nfiles_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-files.txt\nuntestable_count: 2\nuntestable_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/untestable.json\nnotes: wrote 26 tests for sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer (4 loyalty abilities); −7 coin-flip X and skip-turn flagged untestable (no engine RNG/skip-turn API)\n```"}],"totalDurationMs":280461,"to