{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jp6eqBJiGgULHeQCQqo4Ar","type":"tool_result","content":"=== test-files.txt ===\n/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py\n\n=== untestable.json ===\n[\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"−7: Flip five coins ... where X is the number of coins that came up heads.\",\n    \"reason\": \"Coin flips are random and the engine provides no coin-flip helper or deterministic/injectable RNG hook (only engine/zones.py uses random, for shuffling). The exact number of heads (X, 0..5) cannot be asserted deterministically, so the test only checks the ability exists at loyalty cost -7 and resolves without raising.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Add a deterministic coin-flip helper in engine/ (e.g. engine.game.flip_coins(n) or a seedable RNG on GameState) that tests can stub/seed, so the number of heads is observable and X can be asserted.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"−7: Target opponent skips their next X turns.\",\n    \"reason\": \"The engine has an extra_turns FIFO queue (engine/game_state.py) but no skip-turn mechanism in turn advancement (engine/turn.py / GameState.advance_phase). There is no observable API to assert that an opponent's next X turns are actually skipped, and the shape of any new skip-turn surface the Implementer adds is unknown at test-authoring time.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Add a skip-turn mechanism to the engine (e.g. a per-player skipped_turns counter consumed during turn rotation, analogous to the extra_turns queue) that tests can read to confirm the opponent skips exactly X turns; then the −7 effect can be asserted end-to-end against a deterministic coin-flip count.\"\n  }\n]\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"fe6aa87d-9d5f-46a0-a0dd-48f019030cdc","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:36:34.249Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== test-files.txt ===\n/workspace/cards/sos/sos_9