{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011jCUc6iWsHRSiBX5a3qxf8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n2\t\n3\tCard: `Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer` — `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral — loyalty 3.\n4\t\n5\tOracle text:\n6\t- **+1:** Surveil 2.\n7\t- **−1:** Any number of target players each discard a card.\n8\t- **−2:** Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\n9\t- **−7:** Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of coins that came up heads.\n10\t\n11\tTest file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` (26 tests).\n12\t\n13\t## Behavior contract derived from the spec\n14\t\n15\tThe card is a planeswalker, so it follows the established FDN reference-walker\n16\tconventions (`cards/fdn/fdn_44` Kaito, `cards/fdn/fdn_134` Ajani,\n17\t`cards/fdn/fdn_81` Chandra):\n18\t\n19\t- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns one `engine.card.LoyaltyAbility` per printed\n20\t  ability, each with `loyalty_cost` equal to the printed loyalty adjustment\n21\t  (`+1`, `-1`, `-2`, `-7`).\n22\t- Each `LoyaltyAbility.effect` is a callable taking only `game`; the engine's\n23\t  loyalty-resolution (`engine/abilities.py::_activate_loyalty_ability`) invokes\n24\t  `ability.effect(game)`.\n25\t- Chosen targets are stashed on the planeswalker before the effect runs: a\n26\t  single target on `pw._resolve_target` and a variable number of targets on\n27\t  `pw._resolve_targets` (the Kaito/Ajani/Chandra idiom). Tests set these\n28\t  directly and call `effect(game)`, mirroring the resolution step.\n29\t- Surveil follows the engine's existing convention (`cards/fdn/fdn_157`\n30\t  Lightshell Duo): `controller.choose_yes_no(...)` per top card, processed\n31\t  top-card-first; \"yes\" moves that card to the graveyard, \"no\" keeps it on top.\n32\t\n33\t## Test-by-test coverage\n34\t\n35\t### TestRalZarekProperties (static data)\n36\t- `test_name`, `test_mana_cost` — name and `{1}{B}{B}` cost.\n37\t- `test_is_planeswalker` — `Planeswalker` subclass + `CardType.PLANESWALKER`.\n38\t- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` (Legendary Planeswalker).\n39\t- `test_has_ral_subtype` — `\"Ral\"` subtype (type line \"— Ral\").\n40\t- `test_starting_loyalty_is_three` — printed loyalty 3 (`starting_loyalty` and\n41\t  `loyalty`).\n42\t\n43\t### TestRalZarekLoyaltyRoster (ability roster)\n44\t- `test_returns_four_abilities` — exactly four loyalty abilities.\n45\t- `test_each_is_loyalty_ability` — each is a `LoyaltyAbility`.\n46\t- `test_loyalty_costs_match_spec` — the four loyalty costs are `{+1, -1, -2, -7}`.\n47\t\n48\t### TestRalZarekSurveil (+1: Surveil 2)\n49\t- `test_keeping_both_leaves_library_untouched` — scripting \"no\" twice keeps both\n50\t  top cards on the library; nothing in the graveyard.\n51\t- `test_putting_both_into_graveyard` — scripting \"yes\" twice moves both top cards\n52\t  to the graveyard.\n53\t- `test_card_count_is_conserved` — robust invariant: library+graveyard total is\n54\t  unchanged by surveil (no cards created/destroyed), independent of the exact\n55\t  choice plumbing.\n56\t- `test_surveil_does_not_leak_cards_to_other_zones` — each surveilled card ends in\n57\t  exactly one of library/graveyard and never in hand/exile/battlefield.\n58\t- `test_empty_library_is_a_noop` — surveil 2 with an empty library does nothing\n59\t  and does not raise (CR 701.25 handles fewer than N cards).\n60\t\n61\t### TestRalZarekDiscard (−1: any number of target players each discard a card)\n62\t- `test_single_targeted_player_discards` — the single targeted player discards\n63\t  their only card to their graveyard.\n64\t- `test_multiple_targets_each_discard_one` — two targeted players each discard\n65\t  exactly one card.\n66\t- `test_no_targets_is_a_noop` — \"any number\" permits zero targets; nobody discards.\n67\t- `test_targeted_player_with_empty_hand_does_not_crash` — a targeted player with\n68\t  no cards in hand simply discards nothing.\n69\t\n70\t### TestRalZarekReanimate (−2: return creature mv ≤ 3 from your graveyard)\n71\t- `test_returns_targeted_creature_to_battlefield` — targeted creature card leaves\n72\t  the controller's graveyard and enters their battlefield.\n73\t- `test_returned_creature_is_controlled_by_you` — the returned creature is\n74\t  controlled by the planeswalker's controller (\"to the battlefield\" under you).\n75\t- `test_no_target_is_a_noop` — with no target the creature stays in the graveyard.\n76\t- `test_target_filter_accepts_mana_value_three_creature` — the graveyard-scoped\n77\t  target requirement accepts a mana-value-3 creature (\"3 or less\").\n78\t- `test_target_filter_rejects_high_mana_value_creature` — rejects a mana-value-4\n79\t  creature.\n80\t- `test_target_filter_rejects_noncreature_card` — rejects a (cheap) non-creature\n81\t  card in the graveyard.\n82\t\n83\t### TestRalZarekUltimate (−7: flip five coins; opponent skips X turns)\n84\t- `test_ultimate_exists_at_minus_seven` — the ultimate is present at loyalty cost\n85\t  `-7`.\n86\t- `test_ultimate_resolves_against_target_opponent` — resolving the ultimate with a\n87\t  target opponent set does not raise. The number of skipped turns depends on\n88\t  random coin flips and the (currently absent) skip-turn engine mechanism, so the\n89\t  exact X is not asserted here.\n90\t\n91\t## Edge cases deliberately covered\n92\t- Surveil with fewer cards than N / empty library (CR 701.25 graceful handling).\n93\t- \"Any number of target players\" with zero targets (no-op) and with a player who\n94\t  has an empty hand.\n95\t- The −2 mana-value boundary (mv 3 accepted, mv 4 rejected) and creature-only\n96\t  restriction.\n97\t- No-target no-ops for the targeted abilities (a spell/ability with no legal\n98\t  target should fizzle without error).\n99\t\n100\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n101\t- **Exact coin-flip outcome / number of heads (−7).** Coin flips are random; the\n102\t  engine exposes no coin-flip injection or deterministic RNG hook, so X cannot be\n103\t  asserted deterministically. See `untestable.json`.\n104\t- **End-to-end \"skips their next X turns\" turn-advancement (−7).** The engine has\n105\t  an `extra_turns` FIFO queue but no skip-turn mechanism (confirmed in\n106\t  `engine/game_state.py` / `engine/turn.py`). Asserting that the opponent's next X\n107\t  turns are actually skipped requires new engine surface the Implementer must add;\n108\t  its exact shape is unknown at test-authoring time. See `untestable.json`.\n109\t- **Legend rule / once-per-turn loyalty restriction** — engine-level behavior\n110\t  already covered by `engine_tests/`; out of scope for this card's contract.\n111\t- **Surveil reordering of the kept cards** — CR 701.25 lets the player reorder the\n112\t  cards kept on top; with only generic vanilla fillers this has no observable\n113\t  game effect to assert, and the precise reorder API is implementer-defined.\n114\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"45a2be37-3655-498c-88c7-2ade7fa4e3b9","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:36:42.080Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n\nCard: `Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer` — `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral — loyalty 3.\n\nOracle text:\n- **+1:** Surveil 2.\n- **−1:** Any number of target players each discard a card.\n- **−2:** Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\n- **−7:** Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of coins that came up heads.\n\nTest file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` (26 tests).\n\n## Behavior contract derived from the spec\n\nThe card is a planeswalker, so it follows the established FDN reference-walker\nconventions (`cards/fdn/fdn_44` Kaito, `cards/fdn/fdn_134` Ajani,\n`cards/fdn/fdn_81` Chandra):\n\n- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns one `engine.card.LoyaltyAbility` per printed\n  ability, each with `loyalty_cost` equal to the printed loyalty adjustment\n  (`+1`, `-1`, `-2`, `-7`).\n- Each `LoyaltyAbility.effect` is a callable taking only `game`; the engine's\n  loyalty-resolution (`engine/abilities.py::_activate_loyalty_ability`) invokes\n  `ability.effect(game)`.\n- Chosen targets are stashed on the planeswalker before the effect runs: a\n  single target on `pw._resolve_target` and a variable number of targets on\n  `pw._resolve_targets` (the Kaito/Ajani/Chandra idiom). Tests set these\n  directly and call `effect(game)`, mirroring the resolution step.\n- Surveil follows the engine's existing convention (`cards/fdn/fdn_157`\n  Lightshell Duo): `controller.choose_yes_no(...)` per top card, processed\n  top-card-first; \"yes\" moves that card to the graveyard, \"no\" keeps it on top.\n\n## Test-by-test coverage\n\n### TestRalZarekProperties (static data)\n- `test_name`, `test_mana_cost` — name and `{1}{B}{B}` cost.\n- `test_is_planeswalker` — `Planeswalker` subclass + `CardType.PLANESWALKER`.\n- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` (Legendary Planeswalker).\n- `test_has_ral_subtype` — `\"Ral\"` subtype (type line \"— Ral\").\n- `test_starting_loyalty_is_three` — printed loyalty 3 (`starting_loyalty` and\n  `loyalty`).\n\n### TestRalZarekLoyaltyRoster (ability roster)\n- `test_returns_four_abilities` — exactly four loyalty abilities.\n- `test_each_is_loyalty_ability` — each is a `LoyaltyAbility`.\n- `test_loyalty_costs_match_spec` — the four loyalty costs are `{+1, -1, -2, -7}`.\n\n### TestRalZarekSurveil (+1: Surveil 2)\n- `test_keeping_both_leaves_library_untouched` — scripting \"no\" twice keeps both\n  top cards on the library; nothing in the graveyard.\n- `test_putting_both_into_graveyard` — scripting \"yes\" twice moves both top cards\n  to the graveyard.\n- `test_card_count_is_conserved` — robust invariant: library+graveyard total is\n  unchanged by surveil (no cards created/destroyed), independent of the exact\n  choice plumbing.\n- `test_surveil_does_not_leak_cards_to_other_zones` — each surveilled card ends in\n  exactly one of library/graveyard and never in hand/exile/battlefield.\n- `test_empty_library_is_a_noop` — surveil 2 with an empty library does nothing\n  and does not raise (CR 701.25 handles fewer than N cards).\n\n### TestRalZarekDiscard (−1: any number of target players each discard a card)\n- `test_single_targeted_player_discards` — the single targeted player discards\n  their only card to their graveyard.\n- `test_multiple_targets_each_discard_one` — two targeted players each discard\n  exactly one card.\n- `test_no_targets_is_a_noop` — \"any number\" permits zero targets; nobody discards.\n- `test_targeted_player_with_empty_hand_does_not_crash` — a targeted player with\n  no cards in hand simply discards nothing.\n\n### TestRalZarekReanimate (−2: return creature mv ≤ 3 from your graveyard)\n- `test_returns_targeted_creature_to_battlefield` — targeted creature card leaves\n  the controller's graveyard and enters their battlefield.\n- `test_returned_creature_is_controlled_by_you` — the returned creature is\n  controlled by the planeswalker's controller (\"to the battlefield\" under you).\n- `test_no_target_is_a_noop` — with no target the creature stays in the graveyard.\n- `test_target_filter_accepts_mana_value_three_creature` — the graveyard-scoped\n  target requirement accepts a mana-value-3 creature (\"3 or less\").\n- `test_target_filter_rejects_high_mana_value_creature` — rejects a mana-value-4\n  creature.\n- `test_target_filter_rejects_noncreature_card` — rejects a (cheap) non-creature\n  card in the graveyard.\n\n### TestRalZarekUltimate (−7: flip five coins; opponent skips X turns)\n- `test_ultimate_exists_at_minus_seven` — the ultimate is present at loyalty cost\n  `-7`.\n- `test_ultimate_resolves_against_target_opponent` — resolving the ultimate with a\n  target opponent set does not raise. The number of skipped turns depends on\n  random coin flips and the (currently absent) skip-turn engine mechanism, so the\n  exact X is not asserted here.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately covered\n- Surveil with fewer cards than N / empty library (CR 701.25 graceful handling).\n- \"Any number of target players\" with zero targets (no-op) and with a player who\n  has an empty hand.\n- The −2 mana-value boundary (mv 3 accepted, mv 4 rejected) and creature-only\n  restriction.\n- No-target no-ops for the targeted abilities (a spell/ability with no legal\n  target should fizzle without error).\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n- **Exact coin-flip outcome / number of heads (−7).** Coin flips are random; the\n  engine exposes no coin-flip injection or deterministic RNG hook, so X cannot be\n  asserted deterministically. See `untestable.json`.\n- **End-to-end \"skips their next X turns\" turn-advancement (−7).** The engine has\n  an `extra_turns` FIFO queue but no skip-turn mechanism (confirmed in\n  `engine/game_state.py` / `engine/turn.py`). Asserting that the opponent's next X\n  turns are actually skipped requires new engine surface the Implementer must add;\n  its exact shape is unknown at test-authoring time. See `untestable.json`.\n- **Legend rule / once-per-turn loyalty restriction** — engine-level behavior\n  already covered by `engine_tests/`; out of scope for this card's contract.\n- **Surveil reordering of the kept cards** — CR 701.25 lets the player reorder the\n  cards kept on top; with only generic vanilla fillers this has no observable\n  game effect to assert, and the precise reorder API is implementer-defined.\n","numLines":114,"startLine":1,"totalLines":114}}}
