{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K6g3UQRSDfGAcm7KoYrVPN","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/coordinator-directives.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"a598ee76-b945-45eb-96d8-c4deadca12cc","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:37:12.613Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n\nCard: `Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer` — `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral — loyalty 3\n(expert tier). Abilities:\n- **+1:** Surveil 2.\n- **−1:** Any number of target players each discard a card.\n- **−2:** Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\n- **−7:** Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X = number of heads.\n\nFollow the established FDN reference-walker conventions (`cards/fdn/fdn_44` Kaito,\n`cards/fdn/fdn_134` Ajani, `cards/fdn/fdn_81` Chandra): `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns\n`engine.card.LoyaltyAbility` objects whose `effect(game)` reads chosen targets stashed on the\nplaneswalker (`pw._resolve_target` single / `pw._resolve_targets` variable). Surveil follows\nthe engine convention used by `cards/fdn/fdn_157` (Lightshell Duo): `choose_yes_no` per top card.\n\nThe Tester wrote 26 tests (all currently red) and deferred 2 items on the −7 ultimate for lack\nof engine support. Build that support — ADDITIVELY per AGENTS.md (add new methods/classes/\nhelpers/fields, modify existing function bodies; never rename/move/delete existing engine\nsymbols). Keep the `Keyword` enum at 16 members (do NOT add to it).\n\n## Engine gap 1 — deterministic coin-flip helper (additive)\nAdd a coin-flip helper to the engine that is DETERMINISTIC/INJECTABLE for tests. Options:\n- `engine.game.flip_coins(game, n) -> int` (number of heads) that uses a seedable RNG stored\n  on `GameState` (e.g. `game._rng` / `game.rng`), OR\n- a module-level RNG that tests can seed/monkeypatch.\nMake it so a test can force a known number of heads (e.g. seed the RNG, or expose an\ninjectable hook) and assert X. Default behavior (unseeded) should be a fair coin.\n\n## Engine gap 2 — skip-turn mechanism (additive)\nAdd a per-player skip-turn surface analogous to the existing `extra_turns` FIFO queue:\n- A per-player `skipped_turns` counter (e.g. `player.skipped_turns` or a dict on GameState).\n- Consume it during turn rotation in `engine/turn.py` / `GameState.advance_phase` /\n  whatever advances the active player: when it would become a player's turn and that player\n  has `skipped_turns > 0`, decrement and skip their turn (pass to the next player).\n- This must be observable: a test should be able to read the counter to confirm an opponent\n  was given exactly X skipped turns, and ideally drive turns to confirm the turns are skipped.\n- Keep it additive and do NOT break existing turn-progression / extra-turns regression tests.\n\n## −7 wiring\nOn resolution: flip five coins via the new helper, count heads = X, and add X to the TARGET\nOPPONENT's `skipped_turns` (the target stashed on the planeswalker). X may be 0 (no skip).\n\n## The other three abilities\nImplement +1 Surveil 2, −1 any-number-of-target-players each discard a card (zero targets is a\nlegal no-op), and −2 reanimate a creature card with mana value ≤ 3 from YOUR graveyard to the\nbattlefield under your control. Make all 26 existing tests pass.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` → all 26 pass.\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (watch turn/extra-turn tests).\n\nAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester once to add deterministic −7 tests\n(seed the coin flip and assert the opponent's `skipped_turns` equals the number of heads, and\nthat the opponent actually skips that many turns). Build the surfaces so those tests are real.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
