er skip-turn mechanism (`skipped_turns` counter consumed during turn rotation in `engine/turn.py`), analogous to the existing `extra_turns` queue.\n3. Implement `cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py`: the planeswalker with +1 Surveil 2, −1 any-number-of-target-players each discard a card, −2 reanimate a creature mv≤3 from your graveyard to the battlefield under your control, and −7 flip five coins → target opponent gains X skipped turns (X = heads).\n4. Verify: `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` then the full `pytest` suite.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- Completed `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` and all engine source changes.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl.diff` — `git diff` of implementation+engine files only (exclude tests): `git add -N` any new files first, then `git diff -- cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py engine/ > /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl.diff` from `/workspace`.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md` — what you implemented, the new engine API/symbols (coin-flip helper name + how to seed it, skip-turn counter name + where consumed), key decisions, any spec deviations, and exactly how a test would: seed the coin flip to force a known number of heads, and observe the opponent's skipped turns end-to-end.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-files.txt` — list of all files changed (one per line).\n- Upsert this card's entry into `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` (match by `card: \"sos_97\"`; replace in place if present). Include engine files in `implementation`.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nIf all tests pass:\n```\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: <N>\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: <one-line, name the new engine symbols + how to seed the coin flip>\n```\nIf you must dispute a test (write reasoning to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-dispute.md`):\n```\nDISPUTE\ntests_failing: <N>\ndisputed_tests: <list>\ndispute_path: /tmp/coordi