{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014AXxMMiVJJYXGcVtu7MutN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n2\t\n3\t## What I implemented\n4\t\n5\t`cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` — `RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)`:\n6\t`{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral — starting loyalty 3, following the\n7\tFDN reference-walker conventions (Kaito/Ajani/Chandra). Targets are read from\n8\t`pw._resolve_target` (single) / `pw._resolve_targets` (variable) at effect time.\n9\t\n10\t- **+1 Surveil 2** (`_plus1`): top-card-first via `controller.choose_yes_no(...)`\n11\t  per top card (engine surveil convention, `cards/fdn/fdn_157` Lightshell Duo).\n12\t  \"yes\" → graveyard, \"no\" → keep on top. Handles empty/short library (no prompts,\n13\t  no raise). Cards never leak to other zones; library+graveyard count is conserved.\n14\t- **−1 discard** (`_minus1`): iterates `_resolve_targets` (\"any number\"); each\n15\t  targeted player with cards discards one via `engine.game.discard`. Zero targets\n16\t  and empty hands are no-ops. Uses `choose_card` when available, else the last card.\n17\t- **−2 reanimate** (`_minus2`): `_resolve_target` (a creature card in the\n18\t  controller's graveyard) is set to the controller and moved\n19\t  `GRAVEYARD → BATTLEFIELD` via `engine.zones.move_to_zone`. No target = no-op.\n20\t  `get_targets()` exposes a `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.GRAVEYARD, ...)` whose\n21\t  `filter_fn` accepts creature cards with `mana_cost.cmc <= 3` and rejects\n22\t  mv-4 creatures and non-creature cards (the tests probe `r.filter_fn` directly).\n23\t- **−7 ultimate** (`_minus7`): flips five coins via the new\n24\t  `engine.game.flip_coins(game, 5)`, counts heads = X, and adds X to the target\n25\t  opponent's `skipped_turns` via `engine.game.add_skipped_turns`. X may be 0.\n26\t\n27\t## New engine API / symbols (all additive)\n28\t\n29\t### Coin flips — `engine/game.py`\n30\t- `get_rng(game) -> random.Random` — lazily attaches/returns `game._rng`.\n31\t- `seed_rng(game, seed)` — seeds that RNG for deterministic flips.\n32\t- `flip_coin(game) -> bool` — one fair coin (True = heads).\n33\t- `flip_coins(game, n) -> int` — number of heads in `n` flips (0 → 0).\n34\t\n35\tHow a test forces a known number of heads:\n36\t```python\n37\tfrom engine.game import seed_rng, flip_coins\n38\tseed_rng(game, 0)            # reproducible\n39\tassert flip_coins(game, 5) == 2   # seed 0 yields exactly 2 heads\n40\t```\n41\tThe RNG lives on the GameState (`game._rng`), so seeding the game before resolving\n42\tthe −7 ability deterministically fixes how many heads (and thus skipped turns) the\n43\tultimate produces. Unseeded behaviour is a fair coin (`Random().random() < 0.5`).\n44\t\n45\t### Skip-turn mechanism — `engine/player.py`, `engine/game.py`, `engine/game_state.py`\n46\t- `Player.skipped_turns: int = 0` (new field; additive).\n47\t- `engine.game.add_skipped_turns(game, player, amount=1)` — increments\n48\t  `player.skipped_turns`.\n49\t- `GameState._next_active_index_raw()` — factored-out \"pick next seat\" step that\n50\t  preserves the existing `extra_turns` FIFO / `_normal_next_index` semantics\n51\t  unchanged.\n52\t- `GameState._pick_next_active_index()` — wraps the raw pick and consumes\n53\t  skip-turn effects: if the player who would become active has\n54\t  `skipped_turns > 0`, it decrements and passes the turn to the next player\n55\t  (bounded loop, always terminates). `advance_phase` now calls this at\n56\t  end-of-turn instead of inlining the rotation.\n57\t\n58\tHow a test observes the opponent's skipped turns end-to-end:\n59\t```python\n60\tfrom engine.game import add_skipped_turns\n61\tadd_skipped_turns(game, opponent, 2)\n62\tassert opponent.skipped_turns == 2          # observable counter\n63\t# drive turns (set ENDING/CLEANUP then advance_phase, or run_turn):\n64\tseq = []\n65\tfor _ in range(5):\n66\t    game.phase, game.step = Phase.ENDING, Step.CLEANUP\n67\t    game.advance_phase()\n68\t    seq.append(game.active_player_index)\n69\t# the opponent's two due turns are skipped, then normal alternation resumes;\n70\t# opponent.skipped_turns is decremented back to 0.\n71\t```\n72\tFor the −7 ultimate specifically: `seed_rng(game, s)` to fix the head count X,\n73\tresolve the ability with `pw._resolve_target = opponent`, then assert\n74\t`opponent.skipped_turns == X` and (optionally) drive turns to confirm X turns\n75\tare skipped.\n76\t\n77\t## Key decisions\n78\t- RNG is attached lazily to the game (`game._rng`) rather than changing\n79\t  `GameState.__init__`, mirroring the existing lazy-registry pattern in\n80\t  `KEY_DECISIONS.md` (stack-to-graveyard redirect, prepared copies). Keeps the\n81\t  change purely additive.\n82\t- `skipped_turns` is a per-`Player` counter (parallel to the `extra_turns` FIFO\n83\t  on `GameState`), consumed in `advance_phase` via the new helper methods so the\n84\t  existing extra-turns regression tests (which never set `skipped_turns`) are\n85\t  completely unaffected — the skip check is a no-op when the counter is 0.\n86\t- Extra turns and skips compose: a skip can also cancel a popped extra turn,\n87\t  since the raw picker is re-invoked after each decrement.\n88\t- The `Keyword` enum is untouched (still 16 members); \"Surveil\" is handled as\n89\t  behaviour, not a new enum member.\n90\t\n91\t## Spec deviations\n92\tNone. Behaviour matches the oracle text and the Tester's contract. The −7's exact\n93\tX is random in production but deterministic under `seed_rng`, which is the surface\n94\tthe coordinator asked for so the deferred deterministic −7 tests can be written.\n95\t\n96\t## Verification\n97\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` → 26 passed.\n98\t- Full `pytest` → 1320 passed, no regressions (extra-turns / turn-progression\n99\t  tests still green).\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b19b8e07-a224-4170-ab60-b3faccc0cdf3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:42:10.909Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` — `RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)`:\n`{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral — starting loyalty 3, following the\nFDN reference-walker conventions (Kaito/Ajani/Chandra). Targets are read from\n`pw._resolve_target` (single) / `pw._resolve_targets` (variable) at effect time.\n\n- **+1 Surveil 2** (`_plus1`): top-card-first via `controller.choose_yes_no(...)`\n  per top card (engine surveil convention, `cards/fdn/fdn_157` Lightshell Duo).\n  \"yes\" → graveyard, \"no\" → keep on top. Handles empty/short library (no prompts,\n  no raise). Cards never leak to other zones; library+graveyard count is conserved.\n- **−1 discard** (`_minus1`): iterates `_resolve_targets` (\"any number\"); each\n  targeted player with cards discards one via `engine.game.discard`. Zero targets\n  and empty hands are no-ops. Uses `choose_card` when available, else the last card.\n- **−2 reanimate** (`_minus2`): `_resolve_target` (a creature card in the\n  controller's graveyard) is set to the controller and moved\n  `GRAVEYARD → BATTLEFIELD` via `engine.zones.move_to_zone`. No target = no-op.\n  `get_targets()` exposes a `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.GRAVEYARD, ...)` whose\n  `filter_fn` accepts creature cards with `mana_cost.cmc <= 3` and rejects\n  mv-4 creatures and non-creature cards (the tests probe `r.filter_fn` directly).\n- **−7 ultimate** (`_minus7`): flips five coins via the new\n  `engine.game.flip_coins(game, 5)`, counts heads = X, and adds X to the target\n  opponent's `skipped_turns` via `engine.game.add_skipped_turns`. X may be 0.\n\n## New engine API / symbols (all additive)\n\n### Coin flips — `engine/game.py`\n- `get_rng(game) -> random.Random` — lazily attaches/returns `game._rng`.\n- `seed_rng(game, seed)` — seeds that RNG for deterministic flips.\n- `flip_coin(game) -> bool` — one fair coin (True = heads).\n- `flip_coins(game, n) -> int` — number of heads in `n` flips (0 → 0).\n\nHow a test forces a known number of heads:\n```python\nfrom engine.game import seed_rng, flip_coins\nseed_rng(game, 0)            # reproducible\nassert flip_coins(game, 5) == 2   # seed 0 yields exactly 2 heads\n```\nThe RNG lives on the GameState (`game._rng`), so seeding the game before resolving\nthe −7 ability deterministically fixes how many heads (and thus skipped turns) the\nultimate produces. Unseeded behaviour is a fair coin (`Random().random() < 0.5`).\n\n### Skip-turn mechanism — `engine/player.py`, `engine/game.py`, `engine/game_state.py`\n- `Player.skipped_turns: int = 0` (new field; additive).\n- `engine.game.add_skipped_turns(game, player, amount=1)` — increments\n  `player.skipped_turns`.\n- `GameState._next_active_index_raw()` — factored-out \"pick next seat\" step that\n  preserves the existing `extra_turns` FIFO / `_normal_next_index` semantics\n  unchanged.\n- `GameState._pick_next_active_index()` — wraps the raw pick and consumes\n  skip-turn effects: if the player who would become active has\n  `skipped_turns > 0`, it decrements and passes the turn to the next player\n  (bounded loop, always terminates). `advance_phase` now calls this at\n  end-of-turn instead of inlining the rotation.\n\nHow a test observes the opponent's skipped turns end-to-end:\n```python\nfrom engine.game import add_skipped_turns\nadd_skipped_turns(game, opponent, 2)\nassert opponent.skipped_turns == 2          # observable counter\n# drive turns (set ENDING/CLEANUP then advance_phase, or run_turn):\nseq = []\nfor _ in range(5):\n    game.phase, game.step = Phase.ENDING, Step.CLEANUP\n    game.advance_phase()\n    seq.append(game.active_player_index)\n# the opponent's two due turns are skipped, then normal alternation resumes;\n# opponent.skipped_turns is decremented back to 0.\n```\nFor the −7 ultimate specifically: `seed_rng(game, s)` to fix the head count X,\nresolve the ability with `pw._resolve_target = opponent`, then assert\n`opponent.skipped_turns == X` and (optionally) drive turns to confirm X turns\nare skipped.\n\n## Key decisions\n- RNG is attached lazily to the game (`game._rng`) rather than changing\n  `GameState.__init__`, mirroring the existing lazy-registry pattern in\n  `KEY_DECISIONS.md` (stack-to-graveyard redirect, prepared copies). Keeps the\n  change purely additive.\n- `skipped_turns` is a per-`Player` counter (parallel to the `extra_turns` FIFO\n  on `GameState`), consumed in `advance_phase` via the new helper methods so the\n  existing extra-turns regression tests (which never set `skipped_turns`) are\n  completely unaffected — the skip check is a no-op when the counter is 0.\n- Extra turns and skips compose: a skip can also cancel a popped extra turn,\n  since the raw picker is re-invoked after each decrement.\n- The `Keyword` enum is untouched (still 16 members); \"Surveil\" is handled as\n  behaviour, not a new enum member.\n\n## Spec deviations\nNone. Behaviour matches the oracle text and the Tester's contract. The −7's exact\nX is random in production but deterministic under `seed_rng`, which is the surface\nthe coordinator asked for so the deferred deterministic −7 tests can be written.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` → 26 passed.\n- Full `pytest` → 1320 passed, no regressions (extra-turns / turn-progression\n  tests still green).\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":100}}}
