ate (previously untestable)\n1. **Deterministic head count → skipped turns**: pick a seed; first establish the ground truth for that seed (e.g. seed and call `flip_coins(game, 5)` to learn X for that seed in a throwaway, OR just seed, resolve the −7 with `pw._resolve_target = opponent`, and assert `opponent.skipped_turns` equals the heads count produced by that same seed). Use the SAME seeding approach the Implementer documented so it is reproducible. Assert the opponent's `skipped_turns` equals the number of heads.\n2. **X can be 0**: find/seed a case (or directly via `add_skipped_turns(..., 0)` if needed) showing X=0 adds no skipped turns (no skip).\n3. **End-to-end skip**: give the opponent N skipped turns (via the −7 with a seed, or `add_skipped_turns`), then drive turn rotation per the Implementer's documented loop and assert the opponent's next N turns are actually skipped and the counter decrements to 0.\n4. **Targets the opponent, not you**: the −7 adds skipped turns to the targeted opponent, not to the controller.\n5. Look at `engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py` and `engine/game_state.py` to match the exact turn-driving API (Phase/Step enums, `advance_phase`, `active_player_index`).\n\n## Constraints\n- DO NOT modify `engine_tests/`, FDN `tests.py`, or any engine source. Only edit `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`.\n- DO NOT change or weaken any of your existing 26 tests — only add new ones.\n- The implementation already exists, so your new tests should PASS. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` and confirm everything (old + new) passes. If a new test reveals a genuine implementation bug, leave the failing test in place and report it (do not paper over it).\n\n## Outputs\n- Updated `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`.\n- Append a \"## Extended coverage\" section to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md` describing the new tests.\n- Keep `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-files.txt` accurate (same single file).\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn