{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PJsLyamRY5s6LsmWNDw4TW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 9 new deterministic −7 tests pass alongside the original 26.\n\nTESTS_REWRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 35 (added 9; was 26)\n\nResult of `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`: 35 passed, 0 failed.\nnew_failures: 0\n\nSummary:\n- Extended `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` with a new `TestRalZarekUltimateDeterministic` class (9 tests) covering the previously-deferred −7 ultimate, using the Implementer's documented API: `engine.game.seed_rng` + `flip_coins` for deterministic head counts and the `Phase.ENDING`/`Step.CLEANUP` → `advance_phase` loop (mirroring `engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py`) to drive turn rotation.\n- New coverage: deterministic heads → `opponent.skipped_turns` (seed 0 → X=2), all-heads upper bound (seed 4 → X=5), X=0 (seed 5), opponent-not-controller targeting, end-to-end skip (opponent never becomes active while skips burn, counter returns to 0, alternation resumes), one-per-turn decrement, X=0 end-to-end, no-target no-op, and a cross-check that resolution draws X from the documented coin-flip API.\n- Tests assert against ground-truth head counts observed at runtime via a `_heads_for_seed(seed)` probe rather than hard-coded magic numbers, so they remain correct if RNG internals change.\n- All 26 original tests are unchanged. The two entries in `untestable.json` are now fully covered; both `untestable.json` and the codebase are left intact (I did not delete the file — the rationale notes the items are superseded).\n- Updated `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md` with an \"## Extended coverage\" section. `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-files.txt` is still accurate (single file `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`).\n\nNo implementation bugs were found; the existing engine support behaves exactly as documented."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acc026030ca3af004 (use SendMessage with to: 'acc026030ca3af004' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 61540\ntool_uses: 19\nduration_ms: 108792</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"9e6f9e06-0c69-4d1c-845d-e6791007343f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:44:20.080Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You previously wrote 26 tests for card **sos_97** (\"Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\", a {1}{B}{B} Legendary Planeswalker — Ral). The Implementer has now built additive engine support for the previously-deferred −7 ultimate items (deterministic coin flips + a skip-turn mechanism). Extend your test file to cover them.\n\n## Context: your existing work\n- Existing tests: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` (26 tests, all passing). EXTEND this file — keep all existing tests unchanged, ADD new ones.\n- Your prior rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md`.\n- Your deferred items: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/untestable.json`.\n- Implementer's rationale with the EXACT new engine API and example test usage: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md` — READ THIS carefully (it shows exactly how to seed the RNG and drive turns).\n\n## New engine API to test against (from `engine/game.py`, `engine/player.py`)\n- `engine.game.seed_rng(game, seed)` — seed the game's RNG for deterministic coin flips.\n- `engine.game.flip_coins(game, n) -> int` (number of heads); `flip_coin(game) -> bool`; `get_rng(game)`.\n- `engine.game.add_skipped_turns(game, player, amount=1)` and the per-player counter `player.skipped_turns: int`.\n- Turn rotation consumes `skipped_turns` in `GameState._pick_next_active_index` (called from `advance_phase`). The Implementer's rationale shows a concrete turn-driving loop (set `game.phase = Phase.ENDING`, `game.step = Step.CLEANUP`, then `game.advance_phase()` and read `game.active_player_index`).\n- The card's −7 ability flips five coins (`flip_coins(game, 5)`) and adds X heads to the TARGET OPPONENT'