{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VuX4ime295TcmJXhCmqfLN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n2\t\n3\tCard: `Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer` — `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral — loyalty 3\n4\t(expert tier). Abilities:\n5\t- **+1:** Surveil 2.\n6\t- **−1:** Any number of target players each discard a card.\n7\t- **−2:** Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\n8\t- **−7:** Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X = number of heads.\n9\t\n10\tFollow the established FDN reference-walker conventions (`cards/fdn/fdn_44` Kaito,\n11\t`cards/fdn/fdn_134` Ajani, `cards/fdn/fdn_81` Chandra): `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns\n12\t`engine.card.LoyaltyAbility` objects whose `effect(game)` reads chosen targets stashed on the\n13\tplaneswalker (`pw._resolve_target` single / `pw._resolve_targets` variable). Surveil follows\n14\tthe engine convention used by `cards/fdn/fdn_157` (Lightshell Duo): `choose_yes_no` per top card.\n15\t\n16\tThe Tester wrote 26 tests (all currently red) and deferred 2 items on the −7 ultimate for lack\n17\tof engine support. Build that support — ADDITIVELY per AGENTS.md (add new methods/classes/\n18\thelpers/fields, modify existing function bodies; never rename/move/delete existing engine\n19\tsymbols). Keep the `Keyword` enum at 16 members (do NOT add to it).\n20\t\n21\t## Engine gap 1 — deterministic coin-flip helper (additive)\n22\tAdd a coin-flip helper to the engine that is DETERMINISTIC/INJECTABLE for tests. Options:\n23\t- `engine.game.flip_coins(game, n) -> int` (number of heads) that uses a seedable RNG stored\n24\t  on `GameState` (e.g. `game._rng` / `game.rng`), OR\n25\t- a module-level RNG that tests can seed/monkeypatch.\n26\tMake it so a test can force a known number of heads (e.g. seed the RNG, or expose an\n27\tinjectable hook) and assert X. Default behavior (unseeded) should be a fair coin.\n28\t\n29\t## Engine gap 2 — skip-turn mechanism (additive)\n30\tAdd a per-player skip-turn surface analogous to the existing `extra_turns` FIFO queue:\n31\t- A per-player `skipped_turns` counter (e.g. `player.skipped_turns` or a dict on GameState).\n32\t- Consume it during turn rotation in `engine/turn.py` / `GameState.advance_phase` /\n33\t  whatever advances the active player: when it would become a player's turn and that player\n34\t  has `skipped_turns > 0`, decrement and skip their turn (pass to the next player).\n35\t- This must be observable: a test should be able to read the counter to confirm an opponent\n36\t  was given exactly X skipped turns, and ideally drive turns to confirm the turns are skipped.\n37\t- Keep it additive and do NOT break existing turn-progression / extra-turns regression tests.\n38\t\n39\t## −7 wiring\n40\tOn resolution: flip five coins via the new helper, count heads = X, and add X to the TARGET\n41\tOPPONENT's `skipped_turns` (the target stashed on the planeswalker). X may be 0 (no skip).\n42\t\n43\t## The other three abilities\n44\tImplement +1 Surveil 2, −1 any-number-of-target-players each discard a card (zero targets is a\n45\tlegal no-op), and −2 reanimate a creature card with mana value ≤ 3 from YOUR graveyard to the\n46\tbattlefield under your control. Make all 26 existing tests pass.\n47\t\n48\t## Verification\n49\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` → all 26 pass.\n50\t- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (watch turn/extra-turn tests).\n51\t\n52\tAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester once to add deterministic −7 tests\n53\t(seed the coin flip and assert the opponent's `skipped_turns` equals the number of heads, and\n54\tthat the opponent actually skips that many turns). Build the surfaces so those tests are real.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FLN5x2mJgycms39NgV7mjz","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"af51c444-51c5-4621-aaee-6dad6d6d5a01","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:44:45.970Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ijbGutqg7EAgJCXwSmXg7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"name\": \"Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\",\n3\t  \"mana_cost\": \"{1}{B}{B}\",\n4\t  \"type_line\": \"Legendary Planeswalker — Ral\",\n5\t  \"oracle_text\": \"+1: Surveil 2.\\n−1: Any number of target players each discard a card.\\n−2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\n−7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of coins that came up heads.\",\n6\t  \"power\": null,\n7\t  \"toughness\": null,\n8\t  \"loyalty\": \"3\",\n9\t  \"colors\": [\n10\t    \"B\"\n11\t  ],\n12\t  \"keywords\": [\n13\t    \"Surveil\"\n14\t  ],\n15\t  \"rarity\": \"mythic\",\n16\t  \"set_code\": \"sos\",\n17\t  \"collector_number\": \"97\",\n18\t  \"complexity_tier\": \"expert\"\n19\t}\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FLN5x2mJgycms39NgV7mjz","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"c0a7d76b-a315-4ab0-8e96-b5ad363004c1","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:44:45.973Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
