{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FLN5x2mJgycms39NgV7mjz","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/review.json\n\nSummary of what I verified (no must-fix issues found):\n- All four abilities match the oracle/spec: +1 Surveil 2 (top-card-first, card-conserving, empty/short-library safe, no zone leakage), −1 any-number discard (zero/None and empty-hand no-ops, each player chooses own card), −2 reanimate (creature + mana value ≤3 + graveyard-scoped filter, returns under controller's control, no-target no-op), −7 ultimate (exactly five coins, X=heads added to the targeted opponent not the controller, X=0 and no-target safe).\n- Engine coin-flip helpers (`get_rng`/`seed_rng`/`flip_coin`/`flip_coins`) lazily attach `game._rng`, are deterministic when seeded and fair when unseeded.\n- Skip-turn mechanism (`Player.skipped_turns`, `add_skipped_turns`, `_pick_next_active_index`/`_next_active_index_raw`) consumes correctly during rotation, preserves the `extra_turns` FIFO semantics, terminates, and is correct for the 2-player rotation traced against the deterministic tests.\n- All changes are additive: no engine symbols renamed/removed, `Keyword` enum untouched, `skipped_turns` defaults to 0, card class lives at `cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py`, and `engine_tests/`/`cards/fdn/*/tests.py` are not modified.\n- Ran `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` (35 pass), `engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py` and `engine_tests/test_types.py` (160 pass together), and the full `engine_tests/` suite (1145 pass) — no regressions.\n\nThe three advisory notes are non-blocking (broad `except Exception` in `_minus1`, an unreachable defensive fallback in `_pick_next_active_index`, and the documented extra-turn/skip composition choice).\n\nRelevant file: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/review.json`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aab2668a0b3dec0d1 (use SendMessage with to: 'aab2668a0b3dec0d1' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 62601\ntool_uses: 29\nduration_ms: 132650</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"c104ebfc-4408-4893-a4eb-d0b0a68cf95d","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:46:55.094Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are reviewing the implementation of a single Magic: The Gathering card plus additive engine changes. The card is **sos_97** (\"Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\", a {1}{B}{B} Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3, expert tier).\n\nOracle: +1 Surveil 2; −1 any number of target players each discard a card; −2 return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield; −7 flip five coins, target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).\n\n## Inputs\n- Unified diff of the implementation + engine changes (NOT the tests): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl.diff` (covers `cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py`, `engine/game.py`, `engine/game_state.py`, `engine/player.py`).\n- Implementer's rationale (read for design intent and new API): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md`.\n- Coordinator directives (scope): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/coordinator-directives.md`.\n- Card spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_spec.json`.\n- Tests (already arbitrated — DO NOT demand test rewrites): `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` (35 tests, all passing).\n- Prior-card conventions to respect: `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` and `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` (note: lazy per-game registry/attribute pattern is an established, sanctioned convention).\n- Engine source for context: `engine/card.py`, `engine/abilities.py`, `engine/game.py`, `engine/game_state.py`, `engine/player.py`, `engine/turn.py`, `engine/zones.py`.\n- Rules: `/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt` (grep — Surveil CR 701.25, coin flips CR 705).\n\n## What to review\nReview the diff for correctness vs. spec/oracle intent, real bugs, missed edge cases, and convention violations. Scrutinize especially:\n- **+1 Surveil 2**: top-card-first choose_yes_no; cards go to graveyard or stay on top; no leakage; graceful with short/empty library.\n- **−1 discard**: \"any number of target players\" each discard exactly one; zero targets and empty hands are no-ops.\n- **−2 reanimate**: target filter (creature card, mana value ≤ 3, from YOUR graveyard); returns under controller's control; no-target no-op.\n- **−7 ultimate**: flips exactly five coins; X = heads; adds X to the TARGET OPPONENT's skipped_turns (not the controller); X=0 ok.\n- **Engine coin-flip helper** (`flip_coins`/`flip_coin`/`get_rng`/`seed_rng` in `engine/game.py`): lazy RNG attach, deterministic when seeded, fair when unseeded.\n- **Engine skip-turn mechanism** (`Player.skipped_turns`, `add_skipped_turns`, `GameState._pick_next_active_index` / `_next_active_index_raw`): consumed correctly during turn rotation; does NOT disturb the existing `extra_turns` FIFO semantics; the skip-consume loop always terminates and can't infinite-loop or skip the wrong player; multi-player correctness.\n- **Regression safety**: confirm nothing existing in engine was renamed/removed (additive-only); `Player.skipped_turns` defaults to 0 so existing players/turn tests are unaffected; `Keyword` enum unchanged (16 members).\n\n## Important guardrails\n- DO NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards (see `FILES_MODIFIED.json`) or conventions in `KEY_DECISIONS.md` (e.g., lazy per-game RNG/registry attach is sanctioned — do not flag it).\n- DO NOT demand test rewrites — tests were arbitrated. Any test-quality concern is `advisory` only.\n- Focus on what is visible in the diff.\n\n## Output (write this)\nWrite `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/review.json` — a JSON array of:\n```json\n{\"severity\": \"strict\" | \"advisory\", \"file\": \"<path>\", \"line\": <int or null>, \"comment\": \"<actionable comment>\"}\n```\nUse `strict` only for must-fix issues (correctness bugs, spec violations, regression risks). Use `advisory` for style/clarity. Write `[]` if none.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\n```\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/review.json\n```","agentId":"aab2668a0b3dec0d1","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/review.json\n\nSummary of what I verified (no must-fix issues found):\n- All four abilities match the oracle/spec: +1 Surveil 2 (top-card-first, card-conserving, empty/short-library safe, no zone leakage), −1 any-number discard (zero/None and empty-hand no-ops, each player chooses own card), −2 reanimate (creature + mana value ≤3 + graveyard-scoped filter, returns under controller's control, no-target no-op), −7 ultimate (exactly five coins, X=heads added to the targeted opponent not the controller, X=0 and no-target safe).\n- Engine coin-flip helpers (`get_rng`/`seed_rng`/`flip_coin`/`flip_coins`) lazily attach `game._rng`, are deterministic when seeded and fair when unseeded.\n- Skip-turn mechanism (`Player.skipped_turns`, `add_skipped_turns`, `_pick_next_active_index`/`_next_active_index_raw`) consumes correctly during rotation, preserves the `extra_turns` FIFO semantics, terminates, and is correct for the 2-player rotation traced against the deterministic tests.\n- All changes are additive: no engine symbols renamed/removed, `Keyword` enum untouched, `skipped_turns` defaults to 0, card class lives at `cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py`, and `engine_tests/`/`cards/fdn/*/tests.py` are not modified.\n- Ran `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` (35 pass), `engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py` and `engine_tests/test_types.py` (160 pass together), and the full `engine_tests/` suite (1145 pass) — no regressions.\n\nThe three advisory notes are non-blocking (broad `except Exception` in `_minus1`, an unreachable defensive fallback in `_pick_next_active_index`, and the documented extra-turn/skip composi