{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CiYtg7tcny4g9wznL12bhe","type":"tool_result","content":"5403:702.192. Paradigm\n5405:702.192a Paradigm represents two spell abilities, one of which creates a delayed triggered ability. Paradigm means “If this is the first time a spell you control with this spell’s name has resolved this game, at the beginning of each of your precombat main phases for the rest of the game, create a copy of this object in exile. You may cast the copy without paying its mana cost” and “Exile this spell.” See rule 707.10.\n8453:Paradigm\n8454:A keyword ability that allows you to cast a copy of a spell at the beginning of each of your first main phases. See rule 702.192, “Paradigm.”","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016vGKoq4rn862gyfhY4rSDc","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"c30e05d8-2c77-470e-a6a0-57035e490d7c","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:48:12.540Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_120"}
