digm_copy_factory\ncards/sos/sos_120/tests.py::TestParadigmCopyMechanism::test_paradigm_copy_can_be_cast_for_free_from_exile\n\n=============================== warnings summary ===============================\n../usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages/_pytest/config/__init__.py:1434\n  /usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages/_pytest/config/__init__.py:1434: PytestConfigWarning: Unknown config option: timeout\n  \n    self._warn_or_fail_if_strict(f\"Unknown config option: {key}\\n\")\n\n-- Docs: https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/capture-warnings.html\n24 tests collected in 0.02s","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016vGKoq4rn862gyfhY4rSDc","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"629602fb-23ea-4703-a9ca-19ff62a6486d","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:50:48.648Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_120"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"acdf3193d30e48bc5","tool_use_id":"toolu_016vGKoq4rn862gyfhY4rSDc","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Tester","usage":{"total_tokens":133992,"tool_uses":39,"duration_ms":232928},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"9de3c0d7-b68a-4e04-8046-f1befd8e31ac","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01MDmnC6bPLPucA5xeEm4Qak","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U6MpNk5V8XJghGhnwKdaJ9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n\nCard: **Improvisation Capstone** — `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson, red, mythic, keyword **Paradigm**.\n\nOracle text:\n> Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana\n> value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them without\n> paying their mana costs.\n> Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this\n> name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the\n> beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n\n## Test file\n\n`cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` — 24 tests across 5 classes.\n\nThe card splits into three behavioural blocks: static data, the main\nlibrary-exile-and-cast effect, and the Paradigm keyword (CR 702.192). Helpers\nbuild vanilla spells/lands and seed the controller's library top-first\n(`_set_library` puts `cards[-1]` on top, matching `ZoneContainer`'s top-at-end\nconvention).\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneProperties (8 tests)\nStatic contract from the spec:\n- `test_name`, `test_mana_cost` (`{5}{R}{R}`), `test_is_sorcery`,\n  `test_not_a_creature`, `test_is_red` (via `get_colors`),\n  `test_is_a_lesson` (Lesson subtype), `test_mana_value_is_seven` (cmc==7).\n- `test_has_paradigm_keyword` — Paradigm is *not* an evergreen `Keyword` enum\n  member (the `Keyword` enum is frozen at 16 members per\n  `engine_tests/test_types.py`, per KEY_DECISIONS from sos_13), so this probes\n  the common printed-label spellings and rules text tolerantly.\n\n### TestExileThreshold (8 tests) — \"exile from top until total mana value >= 4\"\n- `test_exiles_until_total_mana_value_reaches_four` — three 2-MV cards: first\n  two (running total 4) are exiled, third stays in library.\n- `test_single_high_mana_value_card_stops_immediately` — one MV-4 card stops\n  the process after that single card.\n- `test_threshold_is_inclusive_of_exactly_four` — boundary: exactly 4 stops it\n  (`>= 4`, not `> 4`).\n- `test_zero_mana_value_cards_do_not_stop_the_process` — MV-0 lands keep going\n  until a nonzero card crosses the threshold (the threshold-crosser is the last\n  exiled; the next card is left in library).\n- `test_exiled_cards_leave_the_library` — exiled cards are removed from library\n  (no duplication).\n- `test_empty_library_exiles_nothing_and_does_not_crash` — empty-library edge\n  case: no exile, no crash / infinite loop.\n- `test_library_smaller_than_threshold_exiles_all_remaining` — library runs dry\n  before reaching MV 4: every card is exiled, process terminates.\n- `test_only_controllers_library_is_used` — \"*your* library\": the opponent's\n  library is untouched.\n\n### TestCastFromAmongExiled (5 tests) — \"may cast any number of spells for free\"\nDeterministicPlayer scripts drive the optional `may`/choose loop\n(`[True, <card>, ..., False]`).\n- `test_chosen_spell_is_cast_for_free` — a chosen spell leaves exile and lands\n  on the stack with an empty mana pool (free cast).\n- `test_declining_leaves_spells_in_exile` — `may` is optional: declining leaves\n  the cards in exile, stack empty.\n- `test_can_cast_multiple_spells` — \"any number\": two exiled spells can both be\n  cast.\n- `test_lands_among_exiled_cards_are_not_castable` — lands are not spells; they\n  are exiled but cannot be cast and stay in exile.\n- `test_resolved_free_cast_spell_does_not_require_payment` — with an empty pool\n  and an expensive instant, the spell must have left the library, been cast,\n  resolved off the stack, and landed in the graveyard — proving it was cast\n  without paying (strengthened so it fails against the no-op stub).\n\n### TestParadigmExileThisSpell (1 test) — \"Then exile this spell.\"\n- `test_capstone_is_exiled_after_resolving_via_cast_pipeline` — cast and resolve\n  through the real `engine.casting.cast_spell` pipeline (empty library isolates\n  this clause); the spell ends in **exile**, not the graveyard.\n\n### TestParadigmCopyMechanism (2 tests) — copy-cast-from-exile\nThe recurring \"cast a copy from exile at the beginning of each of your first\nmain phases\" mechanic is brand-new (no engine framework exists for it, unlike\nthe Preparation framework). These probe the observable surface *tolerantly* and\n`pytest.skip` if the implementation chose a different shape, so they assert the\npositive behaviour when present but never produce a false red against an\nunknown-but-valid implementation:\n- `test_card_exposes_a_paradigm_copy_factory` — a copy factory returns a fresh\n  same-named `ImprovisationCapstone`.\n- `test_paradigm_copy_can_be_cast_for_free_from_exile` — a copy placed in exile\n  can be cast for free via `cast_spell_free` (leaves exile, lands on stack).\n\n## Edge cases deliberately covered\n- Threshold boundary (exactly 4), MV-0 cards not stopping the count, single\n  high-MV card, empty library, library smaller than threshold, opponent library\n  isolation, optional-cast decline, multi-cast, lands-are-not-spells, free cast\n  with an empty pool.\n\n## Edge cases / requirements NOT fully covered (see untestable.json)\n- The **recurring per-main-phase** delivery of the Paradigm copy (\"at the\n  beginning of *each* of your first main phases\", and the \"after you *first*\n  resolve a spell with this name\" gating) is only partially covered: the\n  copy-creation and free-cast surface is probed, but the delayed-trigger timing\n  and the once-per-game first-resolution gate depend on an engine API that does\n  not yet exist for the Paradigm mechanic. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- General targeting/legality of the free-cast spells (e.g. a free-cast spell\n  with mandatory targets that has no legal target) is out of scope — it is the\n  cast pipeline's and the individual spell's responsibility, not this card's.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1624,"cache_read_input_tokens":132073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1624,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016vGKoq4rn862gyfhY4rSDc","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"936d0dad-d1cd-4910-88a0-504db90ddf72","request_id":"req_011Cbe9V3hozym19uVviSqSt","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_120"}
