{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016vGKoq4rn862gyfhY4rSDc","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is in order. The tests are well-formed, run cleanly, and exhibit the expected TDD red-phase behavior (20 failing against the empty stub, 2 passing as meaningful invariants/edge-cases, 2 skipping as tolerant probes for the brand-new Paradigm copy surface).\n\n## Summary\n\nI wrote 24 pytest tests for **sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone** (`{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson, red, mythic, keyword Paradigm) at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`, organized into 5 classes:\n\n- **TestImprovisationCapstoneProperties (8)** — name, mana cost, Sorcery type, not-creature, red color, Lesson subtype, mana value 7, and a tolerant Paradigm-designation probe (Paradigm is not a `Keyword` enum member per the frozen-enum decision in KEY_DECISIONS).\n- **TestExileThreshold (8)** — the \"exile from top of library until total mana value ≥ 4\" core: running-total stop, single high-MV card, the inclusive `>= 4` boundary, MV-0 lands not stopping the count, cards leaving the library, empty library, library-runs-dry, and opponent-library isolation.\n- **TestCastFromAmongExiled (5)** — the optional \"cast any number of spells for free\" clause: free cast from exile with empty pool, declining (the `may`), multi-cast, lands-aren't-spells, and a strengthened end-to-end free-resolution check.\n- **TestParadigmExileThisSpell (1)** — \"Then exile this spell\": resolving through the real cast pipeline lands the card in exile, not the graveyard.\n- **TestParadigmCopyMechanism (2)** — tolerant probes (skip if absent) for the copy factory and free-cast-from-exile of a Paradigm copy.\n\nRed-phase confirmed: 20 fail, 2 pass (meaningful invariants), 2 skip. Under the 30-test cap.\n\n**Outputs written:**\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-files.txt`\n