{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019RXW74zDjcSiwvUcqUm9Q7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WBqsSHPxC21RQcnXpasDUe","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone)\n\nCard: **Improvisation Capstone** — `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson, red, mythic, keyword **Paradigm**\n(complex tier).\nOracle:\n> Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana value 4 or\n> greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs.\n> Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a\n> copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main\n> phases.)\n\nThe Tester wrote 24 tests (20 red, 2 invariant-pass, 2 tolerant skips). Build the missing engine\nsupport — ADDITIVELY per AGENTS.md (add new methods/classes/helpers/fields, modify existing\nfunction bodies; never rename/move/delete existing engine symbols). Keep the `Keyword` enum at 16\nmembers; Paradigm is a printed label, NOT a `Keyword` enum member.\n\n## Reuse existing infrastructure (already built earlier this run — see KEY_DECISIONS.md)\n- `engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, precombat)` — fired by `engine/turn.py`\n  at each main phase (from sos_57). Use the `precombat=True` firing for \"your first main phases\".\n- `engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register_delayed(...)` is ONE-SHOT. Paradigm needs a RECURRING\n  trigger (fires at EACH of your first main phases), so add a recurring registration option\n  additively (e.g. a `recurring=True`/`one_shot=False` path, or a per-game registry consulted by\n  the main-phase event) — do NOT break the existing one-shot semantics.\n- `engine.casting.cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)` — cast a copy from exile.\n- `engine.casting.register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card, \"exile\")` (from sos_1) — to\n  satisfy \"Then exile this spell\" (the sorcery resolves STACK -> EXILE instead of graveyard).\n\n## Build an additive `engine/paradigm.py` framework (analogous to engine/preparation.py)\nPublic API (suggested; pick clean names and document them in your rationale):\n- A per-game **first-resolution registry**: `mark_paradigm_resolved(game, name)` /\n  `has_paradigm_resolved(game, name) -> bool` (lazy per-game attach, e.g. `game._paradigm_resolved`).\n- A copy factory on the card: `make_paradigm_copy()` returning a fresh same-named\n  `ImprovisationCapstone`.\n- A registration so that, once a spell with this name has FIRST resolved this game, at the\n  beginning of EACH of the controller's precombat main phases, a free copy is created in the\n  controller's exile and the controller MAY cast it for free (decline leaves it/does nothing).\n- Keep it observable: tests must be able to assert the first-resolution gate (no copy offered\n  before the first resolution) and the recurring per-main-phase delivery.\n\n## Card implementation (`cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py`)\n- Static: `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery, Lesson subtype, red, mana value 7. Paradigm printed label.\n- Main effect on resolve:\n  1. Exile cards from the top of the CONTROLLER's library, accumulating mana value, until the\n     total exiled mana value is `>= 4` (INCLUSIVE) or the library is empty. MV-0 cards do not stop\n     it. Empty library = no exile, no crash/infinite loop.\n  2. The controller MAY cast any number of those exiled spells for free (lands are not spells and\n     stay in exile). Decline leaves them in exile.\n  3. \"Then exile this spell\": the Capstone itself goes to EXILE (not graveyard) when it resolves —\n     use the sos_1 redirect helper.\n  4. On first resolution, register the Paradigm recurring copy mechanic (mark first-resolution;\n     wire the per-main-phase free-copy-from-exile).\n\n## Make ALL 24 tests pass\nIncluding the 2 currently-tolerant `TestParadigmCopyMechanism` tests — implement a real\n`make_paradigm_copy()` factory and free-cast-from-exile so those become real passing assertions\n(not skips).\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` → all pass (no skips if avoidable).\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions.\n\nAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester once to add tests for the recurring\nper-main-phase copy delivery and the first-resolution gate. Build the hooks so those are real.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2335,"cache_read_input_tokens":127142,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2335},"output_tokens":62,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"8a506a10-1241-47c1-945a-5c8a5d7d0875","request_id":"req_011Cbe9cbRV6ecy5w3mSzvqE"}
