kspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`, `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n- Rules reference: `/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt` (grep — Paradigm is CR 702.192; see `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n\n## Constraints\n- DO NOT modify any test file (`cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`), anything under `engine_tests/`, or any FDN `tests.py`.\n- Engine changes ADDITIVE: add a new `engine/paradigm.py` module, add methods/fields, modify existing function bodies; do NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Keep the `Keyword` enum at 16 members (Paradigm is a printed label, not a Keyword).\n- Make ALL 24 tests for sos_120 pass — including the 2 currently-tolerant `TestParadigmCopyMechanism` tests (implement a real `make_paradigm_copy()` factory + free-cast-from-exile so they pass rather than skip).\n- Run the FULL `pytest` suite from `/workspace`; NO existing engine regression test may break (watch turn/main-phase tests).\n- If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible (not just hard), do NOT edit it — return DISPUTE.\n\n## Your task\n1. Read directives, spec, tests, rationale, KEY_DECISIONS.md, and `engine/preparation.py`.\n2. Build an additive `engine/paradigm.py` framework: a per-game first-resolution registry (mark/has by spell name), a recurring per-precombat-main-phase free-copy-in-exile mechanism gated on first resolution, reusing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`. (The existing `register_delayed` is one-shot — add a recurring path additively if needed.)\n3. Implement `cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py`: exile from top of your library until total mana value >= 4 (inclusive; MV-0 cards don't stop; empty-library safe); may cast any number of those for free (lands aren't spells); then exile this spell (reuse the sos_1 redirect); on first resolution wire the Paradigm recurring copy. Expose `make_paradigm_copy()`.\n4. Verify: `pytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` then the full `pytest` suite.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- Completed `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` and all engine source changes (incl. new `engine/paradigm.py`).\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl.diff` — `git diff` of implementation+engine files only (exclude tests): `git add -N` new files first, then `git diff -- cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py engine/ > /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl.diff` from `/workspace`.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-rationale.md` — what you implemented, the new `engine/paradigm.py` API (symbol names), how the recurring trigger + first-resolution gate work, what you reused from earlier cards, any spec deviations, and EXACTLY how a test would observe: (a) the first-resolution gate (no copy before first resolve), (b) the recurring per-main-phase copy delivery, (c) `make_paradigm_copy()`, (d) \"then exile this spell\".\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-files.txt` — list of all files changed (one per line).\n- Upsert this card's entry into `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` (match by `card: \"sos_120\"`; replace in place if present). Include engine files in `implementation`.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nIf all tests pass:\n```\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: <N>\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: <one-line, name the engine/paradigm.py symbols + what you reused>\n```\nIf you must dispute a test (write reasoning to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-dispute.md`):\n```\nDISPUTE\ntests_failing: <N>\ndisputed_tests: <list>\ndispute_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-dispute.md\nnotes: <one-line>\n```"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1795,"cache_read_input_tokens":129477,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1795},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id"