{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H13xdEGkckQx5GrzL6nPqi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Improvisation Capstone** — `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson, red, mythic, keyword **Paradigm**.\n4\t\n5\tOracle text:\n6\t> Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana\n7\t> value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them without\n8\t> paying their mana costs.\n9\t> Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this\n10\t> name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the\n11\t> beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n12\t\n13\t## Test file\n14\t\n15\t`cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` — 24 tests across 5 classes.\n16\t\n17\tThe card splits into three behavioural blocks: static data, the main\n18\tlibrary-exile-and-cast effect, and the Paradigm keyword (CR 702.192). Helpers\n19\tbuild vanilla spells/lands and seed the controller's library top-first\n20\t(`_set_library` puts `cards[-1]` on top, matching `ZoneContainer`'s top-at-end\n21\tconvention).\n22\t\n23\t### TestImprovisationCapstoneProperties (8 tests)\n24\tStatic contract from the spec:\n25\t- `test_name`, `test_mana_cost` (`{5}{R}{R}`), `test_is_sorcery`,\n26\t  `test_not_a_creature`, `test_is_red` (via `get_colors`),\n27\t  `test_is_a_lesson` (Lesson subtype), `test_mana_value_is_seven` (cmc==7).\n28\t- `test_has_paradigm_keyword` — Paradigm is *not* an evergreen `Keyword` enum\n29\t  member (the `Keyword` enum is frozen at 16 members per\n30\t  `engine_tests/test_types.py`, per KEY_DECISIONS from sos_13), so this probes\n31\t  the common printed-label spellings and rules text tolerantly.\n32\t\n33\t### TestExileThreshold (8 tests) — \"exile from top until total mana value >= 4\"\n34\t- `test_exiles_until_total_mana_value_reaches_four` — three 2-MV cards: first\n35\t  two (running total 4) are exiled, third stays in library.\n36\t- `test_single_high_mana_value_card_stops_immediately` — one MV-4 card stops\n37\t  the process after that single card.\n38\t- `test_threshold_is_inclusive_of_exactly_four` — boundary: exactly 4 stops it\n39\t  (`>= 4`, not `> 4`).\n40\t- `test_zero_mana_value_cards_do_not_stop_the_process` — MV-0 lands keep going\n41\t  until a nonzero card crosses the threshold (the threshold-crosser is the last\n42\t  exiled; the next card is left in library).\n43\t- `test_exiled_cards_leave_the_library` — exiled cards are removed from library\n44\t  (no duplication).\n45\t- `test_empty_library_exiles_nothing_and_does_not_crash` — empty-library edge\n46\t  case: no exile, no crash / infinite loop.\n47\t- `test_library_smaller_than_threshold_exiles_all_remaining` — library runs dry\n48\t  before reaching MV 4: every card is exiled, process terminates.\n49\t- `test_only_controllers_library_is_used` — \"*your* library\": the opponent's\n50\t  library is untouched.\n51\t\n52\t### TestCastFromAmongExiled (5 tests) — \"may cast any number of spells for free\"\n53\tDeterministicPlayer scripts drive the optional `may`/choose loop\n54\t(`[True, <card>, ..., False]`).\n55\t- `test_chosen_spell_is_cast_for_free` — a chosen spell leaves exile and lands\n56\t  on the stack with an empty mana pool (free cast).\n57\t- `test_declining_leaves_spells_in_exile` — `may` is optional: declining leaves\n58\t  the cards in exile, stack empty.\n59\t- `test_can_cast_multiple_spells` — \"any number\": two exiled spells can both be\n60\t  cast.\n61\t- `test_lands_among_exiled_cards_are_not_castable` — lands are not spells; they\n62\t  are exiled but cannot be cast and stay in exile.\n63\t- `test_resolved_free_cast_spell_does_not_require_payment` — with an empty pool\n64\t  and an expensive instant, the spell must have left the library, been cast,\n65\t  resolved off the stack, and landed in the graveyard — proving it was cast\n66\t  without paying (strengthened so it fails against the no-op stub).\n67\t\n68\t### TestParadigmExileThisSpell (1 test) — \"Then exile this spell.\"\n69\t- `test_capstone_is_exiled_after_resolving_via_cast_pipeline` — cast and resolve\n70\t  through the real `engine.casting.cast_spell` pipeline (empty library isolates\n71\t  this clause); the spell ends in **exile**, not the graveyard.\n72\t\n73\t### TestParadigmCopyMechanism (2 tests) — copy-cast-from-exile\n74\tThe recurring \"cast a copy from exile at the beginning of each of your first\n75\tmain phases\" mechanic is brand-new (no engine framework exists for it, unlike\n76\tthe Preparation framework). These probe the observable surface *tolerantly* and\n77\t`pytest.skip` if the implementation chose a different shape, so they assert the\n78\tpositive behaviour when present but never produce a false red against an\n79\tunknown-but-valid implementation:\n80\t- `test_card_exposes_a_paradigm_copy_factory` — a copy factory returns a fresh\n81\t  same-named `ImprovisationCapstone`.\n82\t- `test_paradigm_copy_can_be_cast_for_free_from_exile` — a copy placed in exile\n83\t  can be cast for free via `cast_spell_free` (leaves exile, lands on stack).\n84\t\n85\t## Edge cases deliberately covered\n86\t- Threshold boundary (exactly 4), MV-0 cards not stopping the count, single\n87\t  high-MV card, empty library, library smaller than threshold, opponent library\n88\t  isolation, optional-cast decline, multi-cast, lands-are-not-spells, free cast\n89\t  with an empty pool.\n90\t\n91\t## Edge cases / requirements NOT fully covered (see untestable.json)\n92\t- The **recurring per-main-phase** delivery of the Paradigm copy (\"at the\n93\t  beginning of *each* of your first main phases\", and the \"after you *first*\n94\t  resolve a spell with this name\" gating) is only partially covered: the\n95\t  copy-creation and free-cast surface is probed, but the delayed-trigger timing\n96\t  and the once-per-game first-resolution gate depend on an engine API that does\n97\t  not yet exist for the Paradigm mechanic. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n98\t- General targeting/legality of the free-cast spells (e.g. a free-cast spell\n99\t  with mandatory targets that has no legal target) is out of scope — it is the\n100\t  cast pipeline's and the individual spell's responsibility, not this card's.\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KzbV64VrxFyeMJaYKxaCDa","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"1d0d05b8-d895-4afc-901d-29cf587ca5de","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:53:20.460Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_120"}
