{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a6a431f6e27cf0446","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KzbV64VrxFyeMJaYKxaCDa","description":"Writing engine/paradigm.py","subagent_type":"Implementer","usage":{"total_tokens":85505,"tool_uses":24,"duration_ms":84580},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"ba36f531-ba12-42ac-ac93-8429ec344d91","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014K1Vm7nXMP9LbBeVD8TUj3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VFYRET54bDhkXrqixq9Uxn","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/paradigm.py","content":"\"\"\"Paradigm-keyword framework (Comprehensive Rules 702.192).\n\n*Paradigm* is a keyword found on some sorceries (and other spells).  A spell\nwith paradigm reads:\n\n    Paradigm (Then exile this spell.  After you first resolve a spell with this\n    name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at\n    the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n\nSo paradigm has three moving parts:\n\n1. **\"Then exile this spell.\"** — the paradigm spell, instead of being put into\n   its owner's graveyard on resolution, is exiled.  This part reuses the\n   existing :func:`engine.casting.register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect` plumbing\n   (see ``cards/sos/sos_1``) and needs no new framework code.\n\n2. **\"After you first resolve a spell with this name, ...\"** — a once-per-game,\n   per-name gate keyed off the *first* time a spell with that name resolves for\n   a player.  Before that first resolution no paradigm copy is offered.\n\n3. **\"... you may cast a copy of it from exile ... at the beginning of each of\n   your first main phases.\"** — a *recurring* delayed ability: every one of the\n   controller's pre-combat (\"first\") main phases, a fresh copy of the paradigm\n   spell is created in the controller's exile and the controller may cast it for\n   free.\n\nThe engine had no support for this mechanic, so this module adds it\n*additively* — no existing engine symbol is renamed, moved, or deleted.  It is\nmodelled on :mod:`engine.preparation` (the analogous Preparation-card\nframework) and reuses:\n\n- :class:`engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (from sos_57) for\n  the per-main-phase timing.\n- :meth:`engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register` for a *recurring* trigger\n  (``register_delayed`` is one-shot; paradigm needs to fire every first main\n  phase, so we register a normal, non-one-shot trigger here).\n- :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free` (with :class:`~engine.types.Zone.EXILE`)\n  to cast the exiled copy for free.\n\nPublic API\n----------\n- :func:`mark_paradigm_resolved` / :func:`has_paradigm_resolved` — the\n  per-game, per-(player, name) first-resolution registry.\n- :func:`register_paradigm` — wire the recurring per-main-phase free-copy\n  ability for a given paradigm spell name + controller (idempotent per\n  controller+name).  Marks the first resolution as a side effect.\n- :func:`offer_paradigm_copy` — create a fresh copy of the paradigm spell in\n  the controller's exile and let the controller optionally cast it for free.\n  This is the effect the recurring trigger runs each first main phase.\n\n\"Paradigm\" is a *printed keyword label*, not an evergreen keyword, so no member\nis added to :class:`engine.types.Keyword` (keeping that enum unchanged /\nadditive-safe).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable\n\nfrom engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\nfrom engine.types import CardType, Zone\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n    from engine.player import Player\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Per-game first-resolution registry  (player, name) -> resolved?\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _resolved_registry(game: GameState) -> set[tuple[int, str]]:\n    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the per-game first-resolution registry.\n\n    The registry is a set of ``(id(player), name)`` keys recording that a\n    spell with that name has *first resolved* under that player's control this\n    game.  Stored lazily on the game object so no change to\n    ``GameState.__init__`` is required.\n    \"\"\"\n    registry = getattr(game, \"_paradigm_resolved\", None)\n    if registry is None:\n        registry = set()\n        game._paradigm_resolved = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    return registry\n\n\ndef has_paradigm_resolved(game: GameState, player: Any, name: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if a spell named *name* has first resolved for *player*.\"\"\"\n    if player is None:\n        return False\n    return (id(player), name) in _resolved_registry(game)\n\n\ndef mark_paradigm_resolved(game: GameState, player: Any, name: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Record that a spell named *name* has resolved for *player*.\n\n    Returns ``True`` if this was the *first* resolution (the gate just opened),\n    ``False`` if a spell with that name had already resolved for the player\n    (the \"after you *first* resolve\" clause only opens the gate once).\n    \"\"\"\n    if player is None:\n        return False\n    registry = _resolved_registry(game)\n    key = (id(player), name)\n    if key in registry:\n        return False\n    registry.add(key)\n    return True\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Per-game registry of active paradigm triggers  (player, name) -> True\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _registered_registry(game: GameState) -> set[tuple[int, str]]:\n    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the set of already-wired paradigm triggers.\n\n    Keyed by ``(id(controller), name)`` so the recurring trigger is registered\n    at most once per controller+name even if the paradigm spell resolves\n    multiple times.\n    \"\"\"\n    registry = getattr(game, \"_paradigm_registered\", None)\n    if registry is None:\n        registry = set()\n        game._paradigm_registered = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    return registry\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Offering the free copy each first main phase\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef offer_paradigm_copy(\n    game: GameState,\n    controller: Any,\n    factory: Callable[[], Any],\n    name: str,\n) -> Any | None:\n    \"\"\"Create a paradigm copy in *controller*'s exile and offer a free cast.\n\n    Implements the per-main-phase body of paradigm: a fresh copy of the\n    paradigm spell (produced by *factory*) is created in the controller's\n    exile zone, then the controller is asked whether they want to cast it for\n    free.  On *yes* the copy is cast from exile via\n    :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free`; on *no* (or a cast failure) the\n    copy is left in exile.\n\n    Returns the copy that was created (whether or not it was cast), or ``None``\n    if no copy could be produced.\n    \"\"\"\n    if controller is None or factory is None:\n        return None\n\n    copy = factory()\n    if copy is None:\n        return None\n    copy.owner = controller\n    copy.controller = controller\n    copy.is_paradigm_copy = True\n\n    exile = controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n    exile.add(copy)\n\n    # \"you may cast\" — optional.\n    wants_to_cast = False\n    chooser = getattr(controller, \"choose_yes_no\", None)\n    if callable(chooser):\n        try:\n            wants_to_cast = bool(\n                chooser(\n                    f\"Cast a copy of {name} from exile without paying its \"\n                    \"mana cost?\"\n                )\n            )\n        except Exception:\n            wants_to_cast = False\n\n    if not wants_to_cast:\n        return copy\n\n    from engine.casting import cast_spell_free\n\n    try:\n        cast_spell_free(game, controller, copy, Zone.EXILE)\n    except Exception:\n        # Cast failed (e.g. illegal target) — leave the copy in exile.\n        if not exile.contains(copy):\n            exile.add(copy)\n    return copy\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Wiring the recurring delayed ability\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef register_paradigm(\n    game: GameState,\n    source: Any,\n    controller: Any,\n    factory: Callable[[], Any],\n    name: str,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Wire paradigm's recurring per-main-phase free-copy ability.\n\n    Called when a paradigm spell (named *name*, controlled by *controller*)\n    resolves.  It:\n\n    1. Marks the first resolution in the per-game registry (the \"after you\n       first resolve a spell with this name\" gate).  If a spell with this name\n       has already resolved for *controller* the gate is already open.\n    2. Registers — at most once per ``(controller, name)`` — a *recurring*\n       trigger on :class:`~engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n       that, at the beginning of each of *controller*'s pre-combat (\"first\")\n       main phases, runs :func:`offer_paradigm_copy` to create a free copy in\n       exile and offer to cast it.\n\n    Unlike :meth:`engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register_delayed` (one-shot),\n    this uses :meth:`~engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register` so the ability\n    fires every qualifying main phase, matching \"each of your first main\n    phases\".\n    \"\"\"\n    from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n\n    mark_paradigm_resolved(game, controller, name)\n\n    if controller is None or factory is None:\n        return\n\n    registered = _registered_registry(game)\n    key = (id(controller), name)\n    if key in registered:\n        return\n    registered.add(key)\n\n    def _condition(g: GameState, event: BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n        # \"your first main phases\" — only the controller's pre-combat main, and\n        # only once the first-resolution gate is open.\n        if getattr(event, \"player\", None) is not controller:\n            return False\n        if not getattr(event, \"precombat\", False):\n            return False\n        return has_paradigm_resolved(g, controller, name)\n\n    def _effect(g: GameState) -> None:\n        offer_paradigm_copy(g, controller, factory, name)\n\n    game.trigger_manager.register(\n        TriggerRegistration(\n            event_type=BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent,\n            condition=_condition,\n            effect=_effect,\n            source=source,\n            controller=controller,\n        )\n    )\n\n\ndef is_paradigm_copy(card: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* is a paradigm copy created by this framework.\"\"\"\n    return bool(getattr(card, \"is_paradigm_copy\", False))\n\n\ndef is_castable_spell(card: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* is a spell that can be cast (not a land).\n\n    Lands are not spells (CR 601.1) and cannot be cast for free by paradigm's\n    \"cast any number of spells\" clause; this helper centralises that check.\n    \"\"\"\n    card_types = getattr(card, \"card_types\", set())\n    return CardType.LAND not in card_types\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2751,"cache_read_input_tokens":82586,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2751,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KzbV64VrxFyeMJaYKxaCDa","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"1ae794b6-7c91-42d7-9053-afa1eae7a355","request_id":"req_011Cbe9jMF9UE8TcMQDoWkPD","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_120"}
