{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016t8UT5cWDi6NckuYufHbGK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale — sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n2\t\n3\t## What I implemented\n4\t\n5\t`cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` — `ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery)`:\n6\t- Static: `{5}{R}{R}`, `subtypes={\"Lesson\"}`, explicit `self.colors=[Color.RED]`,\n7\t  `self.printed_keywords=[\"Paradigm\"]` (Paradigm is a printed label, NOT a\n8\t  `Keyword` enum member — the enum stays at 16). `rules_text` contains \"Paradigm\".\n9\t- `on_resolve` does four things in order:\n10\t  1. `_exile_from_library` — exile from the TOP of the controller's library\n11\t     (`library.top(1)[-1]`, matching `ZoneContainer`'s top-at-end convention),\n12\t     accumulating mana value, while `total < EXILE_THRESHOLD (4)`. Inclusive\n13\t     (`>= 4` stops). MV-0 cards add 0 so they don't stop it. Loop breaks when the\n14\t     library is empty (no crash / infinite loop).\n15\t  2. `_offer_free_casts` — optional `choose_yes_no` / `choose_card` loop letting\n16\t     the controller cast any number of the exiled spells for free via\n17\t     `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`. Lands are filtered out (`is_castable_spell`\n18\t     -> not `CardType.LAND`). A failed cast (CastingError) drops the card from the\n19\t     offer list to avoid an infinite loop.\n20\t  3. `_exile_this_spell` — reuses sos_1's\n21\t     `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, self, \"exile\")` so the Capstone\n22\t     resolves STACK -> EXILE instead of the graveyard (\"Then exile this spell.\").\n23\t  4. `_wire_paradigm` — calls the new `engine.paradigm.register_paradigm(...)`.\n24\t- `make_paradigm_copy()` — factory returning a fresh same-named\n25\t  `ImprovisationCapstone` inheriting owner/controller (used by the recurring\n26\t  ability and probed directly by the tolerant `TestParadigmCopyMechanism` tests).\n27\t\n28\t## New engine module: `engine/paradigm.py` (additive, modelled on `engine/preparation.py`)\n29\t\n30\tPublic API symbols:\n31\t- `mark_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool` / `has_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool`\n32\t  — per-game first-resolution registry. Keyed by `(id(player), name)` in a lazily\n33\t  attached `game._paradigm_resolved` set (no `GameState.__init__` change). `mark`\n34\t  returns True only on the FIRST resolution (the \"after you first resolve\" gate).\n35\t- `register_paradigm(game, source, controller, factory, name)` — marks first\n36\t  resolution, then registers (at most once per `(controller, name)`, tracked in\n37\t  lazy `game._paradigm_registered`) a RECURRING trigger on\n38\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` via `TriggerManager.register` (NOT\n39\t  `register_delayed`, which is one-shot). Its condition is\n40\t  `event.player is controller AND event.precombat AND has_paradigm_resolved(...)`.\n41\t- `offer_paradigm_copy(game, controller, factory, name)` — the recurring body:\n42\t  builds a copy in the controller's exile, asks `choose_yes_no`, and on yes casts\n43\t  it via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)` (leaving it in exile on decline/failure).\n44\t- Helpers `is_paradigm_copy(card)` and `is_castable_spell(card)` (lands aren't spells).\n45\t\n46\t## How the recurring trigger + first-resolution gate work\n47\t\n48\t- The \"after you first resolve a spell with this name\" gate is the per-game\n49\t  `(id(player), name)` registry. Before the Capstone first resolves, nothing is\n50\t  registered, so a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` does nothing.\n51\t- On first resolution, `register_paradigm` opens the gate and installs ONE\n52\t  recurring trigger. The trigger fires at EVERY one of the controller's precombat\n53\t  main phases (it is a normal `register` trigger, not `one_shot`), each time\n54\t  creating a fresh copy in exile and offering a free cast. Postcombat mains\n55\t  (`precombat=False`) and the opponent's mains are excluded by the condition.\n56\t- Registration is deduped per `(controller, name)` so resolving the spell (or its\n57\t  copies) repeatedly does not stack up multiple recurring triggers.\n58\t\n59\t## What I reused from earlier cards\n60\t- sos_1: `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect` (STACK->EXILE on resolve).\n61\t- sos_57: `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (+ `precombat` flag) and the\n62\t  `event.player is controller` condition idiom; here driven via a recurring\n63\t  `register` rather than the one-shot `register_delayed`.\n64\t- sos_13/`engine/preparation.py`: the lazy per-game registry pattern and a\n65\t  per-card copy `factory` (`make_paradigm_copy` mirrors `make_prepare_spell`),\n66\t  plus the cast-from-exile-via-`cast_spell_free` shape.\n67\t\n68\t## Spec deviations\n69\tNone of substance. The card matches the oracle. The free-cast loop additionally\n70\tguards against a CastingError-looping spell by dropping a failed candidate; this\n71\tis defensive and not observable by the current tests (all scripted spells cast\n72\tcleanly). I added `engine/paradigm.py` rather than extending `register_delayed`\n73\tto a recurring mode, because a per-game-registered recurring trigger is cleaner\n74\tand keeps `register_delayed`'s one-shot semantics untouched (additive-only).\n75\t\n76\t## Exactly how a test would observe each behaviour\n77\t\n78\t(a) First-resolution gate — fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=p1,\n79\t    precombat=True)` and drain the stack BEFORE the Capstone has ever resolved:\n80\t    `p1.zones[Zone.EXILE]` contains no `ImprovisationCapstone` (and\n81\t    `has_paradigm_resolved(game, p1, \"Improvisation Capstone\")` is False).\n82\t\n83\t(b) Recurring per-main-phase copy delivery — after the Capstone resolves (or\n84\t    after calling `register_paradigm`), fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(\n85\t    player=p1, precombat=True)` and drain the stack: one new\n86\t    `ImprovisationCapstone` copy appears in `p1`'s exile (declining the cast).\n87\t    Firing it AGAIN yields a SECOND copy (proving it's recurring, not one-shot).\n88\t    Firing with `precombat=False`, or with `player=p2`, adds NO copy. (Verified\n89\t    via an end-to-end harness during implementation.)\n90\t\n91\t(c) `make_paradigm_copy()` — `ImprovisationCapstone(owner=None).make_paradigm_copy()`\n92\t    returns a distinct `ImprovisationCapstone` with the same `name`\n93\t    (`TestParadigmCopyMechanism::test_card_exposes_a_paradigm_copy_factory`).\n94\t    Placed in exile it can be cast for free with `cast_spell_free(game, p1, copy,\n95\t    Zone.EXILE)` (leaves exile, lands on the stack with `stack.peek().source is\n96\t    copy`).\n97\t\n98\t(d) \"Then exile this spell\" — cast the Capstone through `engine.casting.cast_spell`\n99\t    and resolve it; the redirect registered in `_exile_this_spell` routes it to\n100\t    `p1.zones[Zone.EXILE]`, NOT the graveyard\n101\t    (`TestParadigmExileThisSpell::test_capstone_is_exiled_after_resolving_via_cast_pipeline`).\n102\t\n103\t## Verification\n104\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` — 24 passed (no skips).\n105\t- Full `pytest` — 1353 passed, no regressions.\n106\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"8387ce37-bc04-4fc2-b77c-1f1fbe0f7fc8","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:56:58.353Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale — sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` — `ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery)`:\n- Static: `{5}{R}{R}`, `subtypes={\"Lesson\"}`, explicit `self.colors=[Color.RED]`,\n  `self.printed_keywords=[\"Paradigm\"]` (Paradigm is a printed label, NOT a\n  `Keyword` enum member — the enum stays at 16). `rules_text` contains \"Paradigm\".\n- `on_resolve` does four things in order:\n  1. `_exile_from_library` — exile from the TOP of the controller's library\n     (`library.top(1)[-1]`, matching `ZoneContainer`'s top-at-end convention),\n     accumulating mana value, while `total < EXILE_THRESHOLD (4)`. Inclusive\n     (`>= 4` stops). MV-0 cards add 0 so they don't stop it. Loop breaks when the\n     library is empty (no crash / infinite loop).\n  2. `_offer_free_casts` — optional `choose_yes_no` / `choose_card` loop letting\n     the controller cast any number of the exiled spells for free via\n     `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`. Lands are filtered out (`is_castable_spell`\n     -> not `CardType.LAND`). A failed cast (CastingError) drops the card from the\n     offer list to avoid an infinite loop.\n  3. `_exile_this_spell` — reuses sos_1's\n     `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, self, \"exile\")` so the Capstone\n     resolves STACK -> EXILE instead of the graveyard (\"Then exile this spell.\").\n  4. `_wire_paradigm` — calls the new `engine.paradigm.register_paradigm(...)`.\n- `make_paradigm_copy()` — factory returning a fresh same-named\n  `ImprovisationCapstone` inheriting owner/controller (used by the recurring\n  ability and probed directly by the tolerant `TestParadigmCopyMechanism` tests).\n\n## New engine module: `engine/paradigm.py` (additive, modelled on `engine/preparation.py`)\n\nPublic API symbols:\n- `mark_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool` / `has_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool`\n  — per-game first-resolution registry. Keyed by `(id(player), name)` in a lazily\n  attached `game._paradigm_resolved` set (no `GameState.__init__` change). `mark`\n  returns True only on the FIRST resolution (the \"after you first resolve\" gate).\n- `register_paradigm(game, source, controller, factory, name)` — marks first\n  resolution, then registers (at most once per `(controller, name)`, tracked in\n  lazy `game._paradigm_registered`) a RECURRING trigger on\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` via `TriggerManager.register` (NOT\n  `register_delayed`, which is one-shot). Its condition is\n  `event.player is controller AND event.precombat AND has_paradigm_resolved(...)`.\n- `offer_paradigm_copy(game, controller, factory, name)` — the recurring body:\n  builds a copy in the controller's exile, asks `choose_yes_no`, and on yes casts\n  it via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)` (leaving it in exile on decline/failure).\n- Helpers `is_paradigm_copy(card)` and `is_castable_spell(card)` (lands aren't spells).\n\n## How the recurring trigger + first-resolution gate work\n\n- The \"after you first resolve a spell with this name\" gate is the per-game\n  `(id(player), name)` registry. Before the Capstone first resolves, nothing is\n  registered, so a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` does nothing.\n- On first resolution, `register_paradigm` opens the gate and installs ONE\n  recurring trigger. The trigger fires at EVERY one of the controller's precombat\n  main phases (it is a normal `register` trigger, not `one_shot`), each time\n  creating a fresh copy in exile and offering a free cast. Postcombat mains\n  (`precombat=False`) and the opponent's mains are excluded by the condition.\n- Registration is deduped per `(controller, name)` so resolving the spell (or its\n  copies) repeatedly does not stack up multiple recurring triggers.\n\n## What I reused from earlier cards\n- sos_1: `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect` (STACK->EXILE on resolve).\n- sos_57: `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (+ `precombat` flag) and the\n  `event.player is controller` condition idiom; here driven via a recurring\n  `register` rather than the one-shot `register_delayed`.\n- sos_13/`engine/preparation.py`: the lazy per-game registry pattern and a\n  per-card copy `factory` (`make_paradigm_copy` mirrors `make_prepare_spell`),\n  plus the cast-from-exile-via-`cast_spell_free` shape.\n\n## Spec deviations\nNone of substance. The card matches the oracle. The free-cast loop additionally\nguards against a CastingError-looping spell by dropping a failed candidate; this\nis defensive and not observable by the current tests (all scripted spells cast\ncleanly). I added `engine/paradigm.py` rather than extending `register_delayed`\nto a recurring mode, because a per-game-registered recurring trigger is cleaner\nand keeps `register_delayed`'s one-shot semantics untouched (additive-only).\n\n## Exactly how a test would observe each behaviour\n\n(a) First-resolution gate — fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=p1,\n    precombat=True)` and drain the stack BEFORE the Capstone has ever resolved:\n    `p1.zones[Zone.EXILE]` contains no `ImprovisationCapstone` (and\n    `has_paradigm_resolved(game, p1, \"Improvisation Capstone\")` is False).\n\n(b) Recurring per-main-phase copy delivery — after the Capstone resolves (or\n    after calling `register_paradigm`), fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(\n    player=p1, precombat=True)` and drain the stack: one new\n    `ImprovisationCapstone` copy appears in `p1`'s exile (declining the cast).\n    Firing it AGAIN yields a SECOND copy (proving it's recurring, not one-shot).\n    Firing with `precombat=False`, or with `player=p2`, adds NO copy. (Verified\n    via an end-to-end harness during implementation.)\n\n(c) `make_paradigm_copy()` — `ImprovisationCapstone(owner=None).make_paradigm_copy()`\n    returns a distinct `ImprovisationCapstone` with the same `name`\n    (`TestParadigmCopyMechanism::test_card_exposes_a_paradigm_copy_factory`).\n    Placed in exile it can be cast for free with `cast_spell_free(game, p1, copy,\n    Zone.EXILE)` (leaves exile, lands on the stack with `stack.peek().source is\n    copy`).\n\n(d) \"Then exile this spell\" — cast the Capstone through `engine.casting.cast_spell`\n    and resolve it; the redirect registered in `_exile_this_spell` routes it to\n    `p1.zones[Zone.EXILE]`, NOT the graveyard\n    (`TestParadigmExileThisSpell::test_capstone_is_exiled_after_resolving_via_cast_pipeline`).\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` — 24 passed (no skips).\n- Full `pytest` — 1353 passed, no regressions.\n","numLines":106,"startLine":1,"totalLines":106}}}
