{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TsgYHARdLznA13ir858DMn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"requirement\": \"Paradigm: After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.\",\n4\t    \"reason\": \"The recurring delayed-triggered ability (CR 702.192a) — a copy created in exile at the beginning of each precombat main phase, gated on the first resolution of a spell with this name this game — has no engine framework yet (unlike the existing Preparation framework). There is no established API to register the once-per-game first-resolution gate or to drive the per-main-phase copy creation, so the recurring timing and the first-resolution gate cannot be asserted at red-phase time. The copy-creation surface and free-cast-from-exile behaviour ARE covered by TestParadigmCopyMechanism (tolerantly, via pytest.skip if a different surface is chosen).\",\n5\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"An additive engine 'Paradigm' framework (analogous to engine/preparation.py): e.g. a per-game registry that marks 'a spell with this name has first resolved', a make_paradigm_copy() factory on the card, and a delayed trigger on BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (precombat) that creates a free copy in the controller's exile. Once those public hooks exist, the recurring per-main-phase delivery and the first-resolution gate become directly assertable (mirroring the sos_57 main-phase delayed-trigger tests).\"\n6\t  }\n7\t]\n8\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7riNeuBBpSdqgv2NRz8iA","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"e274a8d0-f4d3-4858-b6dd-74fbe70b4c10","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:57:22.750Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_120 Paradigm"}
