{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WxBLMxmLZ7tXb8HRSn9fNM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Paradigm-keyword framework (Comprehensive Rules 702.192).\n2\t\n3\t*Paradigm* is a keyword found on some sorceries (and other spells).  A spell\n4\twith paradigm reads:\n5\t\n6\t    Paradigm (Then exile this spell.  After you first resolve a spell with this\n7\t    name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at\n8\t    the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n9\t\n10\tSo paradigm has three moving parts:\n11\t\n12\t1. **\"Then exile this spell.\"** — the paradigm spell, instead of being put into\n13\t   its owner's graveyard on resolution, is exiled.  This part reuses the\n14\t   existing :func:`engine.casting.register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect` plumbing\n15\t   (see ``cards/sos/sos_1``) and needs no new framework code.\n16\t\n17\t2. **\"After you first resolve a spell with this name, ...\"** — a once-per-game,\n18\t   per-name gate keyed off the *first* time a spell with that name resolves for\n19\t   a player.  Before that first resolution no paradigm copy is offered.\n20\t\n21\t3. **\"... you may cast a copy of it from exile ... at the beginning of each of\n22\t   your first main phases.\"** — a *recurring* delayed ability: every one of the\n23\t   controller's pre-combat (\"first\") main phases, a fresh copy of the paradigm\n24\t   spell is created in the controller's exile and the controller may cast it for\n25\t   free.\n26\t\n27\tThe engine had no support for this mechanic, so this module adds it\n28\t*additively* — no existing engine symbol is renamed, moved, or deleted.  It is\n29\tmodelled on :mod:`engine.preparation` (the analogous Preparation-card\n30\tframework) and reuses:\n31\t\n32\t- :class:`engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (from sos_57) for\n33\t  the per-main-phase timing.\n34\t- :meth:`engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register` for a *recurring* trigger\n35\t  (``register_delayed`` is one-shot; paradigm needs to fire every first main\n36\t  phase, so we register a normal, non-one-shot trigger here).\n37\t- :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free` (with :class:`~engine.types.Zone.EXILE`)\n38\t  to cast the exiled copy for free.\n39\t\n40\tPublic API\n41\t----------\n42\t- :func:`mark_paradigm_resolved` / :func:`has_paradigm_resolved` — the\n43\t  per-game, per-(player, name) first-resolution registry.\n44\t- :func:`register_paradigm` — wire the recurring per-main-phase free-copy\n45\t  ability for a given paradigm spell name + controller (idempotent per\n46\t  controller+name).  Marks the first resolution as a side effect.\n47\t- :func:`offer_paradigm_copy` — create a fresh copy of the paradigm spell in\n48\t  the controller's exile and let the controller optionally cast it for free.\n49\t  This is the effect the recurring trigger runs each first main phase.\n50\t\n51\t\"Paradigm\" is a *printed keyword label*, not an evergreen keyword, so no member\n52\tis added to :class:`engine.types.Keyword` (keeping that enum unchanged /\n53\tadditive-safe).\n54\t\"\"\"\n55\t\n56\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n57\t\n58\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable\n59\t\n60\tfrom engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n61\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Zone\n62\t\n63\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n64\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n65\t    from engine.player import Player\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n69\t# Per-game first-resolution registry  (player, name) -> resolved?\n70\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n71\t\n72\t\n73\tdef _resolved_registry(game: GameState) -> set[tuple[int, str]]:\n74\t    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the per-game first-resolution registry.\n75\t\n76\t    The registry is a set of ``(id(player), name)`` keys recording that a\n77\t    spell with that name has *first resolved* under that player's control this\n78\t    game.  Stored lazily on the game object so no change to\n79\t    ``GameState.__init__`` is required.\n80\t    \"\"\"\n81\t    registry = getattr(game, \"_paradigm_resolved\", None)\n82\t    if registry is None:\n83\t        registry = set()\n84\t        game._paradigm_resolved = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n85\t    return registry\n86\t\n87\t\n88\tdef has_paradigm_resolved(game: GameState, player: Any, name: str) -> bool:\n89\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if a spell named *name* has first resolved for *player*.\"\"\"\n90\t    if player is None:\n91\t        return False\n92\t    return (id(player), name) in _resolved_registry(game)\n93\t\n94\t\n95\tdef mark_paradigm_resolved(game: GameState, player: Any, name: str) -> bool:\n96\t    \"\"\"Record that a spell named *name* has resolved for *player*.\n97\t\n98\t    Returns ``True`` if this was the *first* resolution (the gate just opened),\n99\t    ``False`` if a spell with that name had already resolved for the player\n100\t    (the \"after you *first* resolve\" clause only opens the gate once).\n101\t    \"\"\"\n102\t    if player is None:\n103\t        return False\n104\t    registry = _resolved_registry(game)\n105\t    key = (id(player), name)\n106\t    if key in registry:\n107\t        return False\n108\t    registry.add(key)\n109\t    return True\n110\t\n111\t\n112\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n113\t# Per-game registry of active paradigm triggers  (player, name) -> True\n114\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n115\t\n116\t\n117\tdef _registered_registry(game: GameState) -> set[tuple[int, str]]:\n118\t    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the set of already-wired paradigm triggers.\n119\t\n120\t    Keyed by ``(id(controller), name)`` so the recurring trigger is registered\n121\t    at most once per controller+name even if the paradigm spell resolves\n122\t    multiple times.\n123\t    \"\"\"\n124\t    registry = getattr(game, \"_paradigm_registered\", None)\n125\t    if registry is None:\n126\t        registry = set()\n127\t        game._paradigm_registered = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n128\t    return registry\n129\t\n130\t\n131\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n132\t# Offering the free copy each first main phase\n133\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n134\t\n135\t\n136\tdef offer_paradigm_copy(\n137\t    game: GameState,\n138\t    controller: Any,\n139\t    factory: Callable[[], Any],\n140\t    name: str,\n141\t) -> Any | None:\n142\t    \"\"\"Create a paradigm copy in *controller*'s exile and offer a free cast.\n143\t\n144\t    Implements the per-main-phase body of paradigm: a fresh copy of the\n145\t    paradigm spell (produced by *factory*) is created in the controller's\n146\t    exile zone, then the controller is asked whether they want to cast it for\n147\t    free.  On *yes* the copy is cast from exile via\n148\t    :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free`; on *no* (or a cast failure) the\n149\t    copy is left in exile.\n150\t\n151\t    Returns the copy that was created (whether or not it was cast), or ``None``\n152\t    if no copy could be produced.\n153\t    \"\"\"\n154\t    if controller is None or factory is None:\n155\t        return None\n156\t\n157\t    copy = factory()\n158\t    if copy is None:\n159\t        return None\n160\t    copy.owner = controller\n161\t    copy.controller = controller\n162\t    copy.is_paradigm_copy = True\n163\t\n164\t    exile = controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n165\t    exile.add(copy)\n166\t\n167\t    # \"you may cast\" — optional.\n168\t    wants_to_cast = False\n169\t    chooser = getattr(controller, \"choose_yes_no\", None)\n170\t    if callable(chooser):\n171\t        try:\n172\t            wants_to_cast = bool(\n173\t                chooser(\n174\t                    f\"Cast a copy of {name} from exile without paying its \"\n175\t                    \"mana cost?\"\n176\t                )\n177\t            )\n178\t        except Exception:\n179\t            wants_to_cast = False\n180\t\n181\t    if not wants_to_cast:\n182\t        return copy\n183\t\n184\t    from engine.casting import cast_spell_free\n185\t\n186\t    try:\n187\t        cast_spell_free(game, controller, copy, Zone.EXILE)\n188\t    except Exception:\n189\t        # Cast failed (e.g. illegal target) — leave the copy in exile.\n190\t        if not exile.contains(copy):\n191\t            exile.add(copy)\n192\t    return copy\n193\t\n194\t\n195\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n196\t# Wiring the recurring delayed ability\n197\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n198\t\n199\t\n200\tdef register_paradigm(\n201\t    game: GameState,\n202\t    source: Any,\n203\t    controller: Any,\n204\t    factory: Callable[[], Any],\n205\t    name: str,\n206\t) -> None:\n207\t    \"\"\"Wire paradigm's recurring per-main-phase free-copy ability.\n208\t\n209\t    Called when a paradigm spell (named *name*, controlled by *controller*)\n210\t    resolves.  It:\n211\t\n212\t    1. Marks the first resolution in the per-game registry (the \"after you\n213\t       first resolve a spell with this name\" gate).  If a spell with this name\n214\t       has already resolved for *controller* the gate is already open.\n215\t    2. Registers — at most once per ``(controller, name)`` — a *recurring*\n216\t       trigger on :class:`~engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n217\t       that, at the beginning of each of *controller*'s pre-combat (\"first\")\n218\t       main phases, runs :func:`offer_paradigm_copy` to create a free copy in\n219\t       exile and offer to cast it.\n220\t\n221\t    Unlike :meth:`engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register_delayed` (one-shot),\n222\t    this uses :meth:`~engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register` so the ability\n223\t    fires every qualifying main phase, matching \"each of your first main\n224\t    phases\".\n225\t    \"\"\"\n226\t    from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n227\t\n228\t    mark_paradigm_resolved(game, controller, name)\n229\t\n230\t    if controller is None or factory is None:\n231\t        return\n232\t\n233\t    registered = _registered_registry(game)\n234\t    key = (id(controller), name)\n235\t    if key in registered:\n236\t        return\n237\t    registered.add(key)\n238\t\n239\t    def _condition(g: GameState, event: BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n240\t        # \"your first main phases\" — only the controller's pre-combat main, and\n241\t        # only once the first-resolution gate is open.\n242\t        if getattr(event, \"player\", None) is not controller:\n243\t            return False\n244\t        if not getattr(event, \"precombat\", False):\n245\t            return False\n246\t        return has_paradigm_resolved(g, controller, name)\n247\t\n248\t    def _effect(g: GameState) -> None:\n249\t        offer_paradigm_copy(g, controller, factory, name)\n250\t\n251\t    game.trigger_manager.register(\n252\t        TriggerRegistration(\n253\t            event_type=BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent,\n254\t            condition=_condition,\n255\t            effect=_effect,\n256\t            source=source,\n257\t            controller=controller,\n258\t        )\n259\t    )\n260\t\n261\t\n262\tdef is_paradigm_copy(card: Any) -> bool:\n263\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* is a paradigm copy created by this framework.\"\"\"\n264\t    return bool(getattr(card, \"is_paradigm_copy\", False))\n265\t\n266\t\n267\tdef is_castable_spell(card: Any) -> bool:\n268\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* is a spell that can be cast (not a land).\n269\t\n270\t    Lands are not spells (CR 601.1) and cannot be cast for free by paradigm's\n271\t    \"cast any number of spells\" clause; this helper centralises that check.\n272\t    \"\"\"\n273\t    card_types = getattr(card, \"card_types\", set())\n274\t    return CardType.LAND not in card_types\n275\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7riNeuBBpSdqgv2NRz8iA","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"4bddb7f6-0f9e-4aba-be82-d6b31176f274","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:57:25.273Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_120 Paradigm"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"ac8d407658417f781","tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7riNeuBBpSdqgv2NRz8iA","description":"Reading cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py","subagent_type":"Tester","usage":{"total_tokens":29067,"tool_uses":6,"duration_ms":6101},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"34a03c2f-b29f-430b-88a6-418142e2bf72","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014WMBNEVaMRX66ncT5ovjDJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JWm8N7AvuN8u3ab2X6gxYN","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15623,"cache_read_input_tokens":13422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15623,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7riNeuBBpSdqgv2NRz8iA","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"835ec342-2be6-462b-aae7-6d881d7716ec","request_id":"req_011Cbe9z6GADC4xoyEU4rPYe","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_120 Paradigm"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JWm8N7AvuN8u3ab2X6gxYN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Card implementation for Improvisation Capstone.\"\"\"\n2\t\n3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n4\t\n5\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n6\t\n7\tfrom engine.card import Sorcery\n8\tfrom engine.types import Color, ManaCost, Zone\n9\t\n10\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n11\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n12\t\n13\t\n14\tdef _mana_value(card: Any) -> int:\n15\t    \"\"\"Return *card*'s mana value (converted mana cost).\n16\t\n17\t    Lands and other zero-cost cards have mana value 0.\n18\t    \"\"\"\n19\t    mana_cost = getattr(card, \"mana_cost\", None)\n20\t    if mana_cost is None:\n21\t        return 0\n22\t    return mana_cost.cmc\n23\t\n24\t\n25\tdef _is_castable_spell(card: Any) -> bool:\n26\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* is a spell that can be cast (not a land).\"\"\"\n27\t    from engine.paradigm import is_castable_spell\n28\t\n29\t    return is_castable_spell(card)\n30\t\n31\t\n32\tclass ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery):\n33\t    \"\"\"Improvisation Capstone — {5}{R}{R} — Sorcery — Lesson.\n34\t\n35\t    Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total\n36\t    mana value 4 or greater.  You may cast any number of spells from among them\n37\t    without paying their mana costs.\n38\t    Paradigm (Then exile this spell.  After you first resolve a spell with this\n39\t    name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at\n40\t    the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n41\t\n42\t    SOS collector number 120.\n43\t    \"\"\"\n44\t\n45\t    #: The printed paradigm keyword label (Paradigm is NOT an evergreen\n46\t    #: ``engine.types.Keyword`` enum member — that enum is frozen at 16\n47\t    #: members — so it is recorded here as a printed-keyword label).\n48\t    PARADIGM_LABEL = \"Paradigm\"\n49\t\n50\t    #: Total mana value the exile process accumulates to before stopping.\n51\t    EXILE_THRESHOLD = 4\n52\t\n53\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n54\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"Improvisation Capstone\")\n55\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{5}{R}{R}\"))\n56\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Lesson\"})\n57\t        kwargs.setdefault(\n58\t            \"rules_text\",\n59\t            \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards \"\n60\t            \"with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of \"\n61\t            \"spells from among them without paying their mana costs.\\n\"\n62\t            \"Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell \"\n63\t            \"with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without \"\n64\t            \"paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main \"\n65\t            \"phases.)\",\n66\t        )\n67\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n68\t        # Red is given explicitly so colour is correct even off the stack\n69\t        # (the cost pips are also red, but being explicit keeps colour stable\n70\t        # for copies and for cards stripped of their cost).\n71\t        self.colors: list[Color] = [Color.RED]\n72\t        # Printed-keyword label surface — Paradigm is a printed keyword, not an\n73\t        # evergreen ``Keyword`` enum member.\n74\t        self.printed_keywords: list[str] = [self.PARADIGM_LABEL]\n75\t\n76\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n77\t    # Paradigm copy factory\n78\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n79\t\n80\t    def make_paradigm_copy(self) -> \"ImprovisationCapstone\":\n81\t        \"\"\"Return a fresh same-named copy of this spell for paradigm.\n82\t\n83\t        The copy is a brand-new :class:`ImprovisationCapstone` (so it can be\n84\t        placed in exile and cast for free at the beginning of each of the\n85\t        controller's first main phases).  Owner/controller are inherited from\n86\t        this card so the copy belongs to the right player.\n87\t        \"\"\"\n88\t        copy = ImprovisationCapstone(owner=self.owner, controller=self.controller)\n89\t        copy.is_paradigm_copy = True\n90\t        return copy\n91\t\n92\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n93\t    # Main resolution\n94\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n95\t\n96\t    def on_resolve(self, game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n97\t        \"\"\"Resolve Improvisation Capstone.\n98\t\n99\t        1. Exile cards from the top of the controller's library until the total\n100\t           exiled mana value reaches 4 or greater (or the library is empty).\n101\t        2. The controller may cast any number of those exiled spells for free.\n102\t        3. \"Then exile this spell.\" — register a stack->exile redirect so the\n103\t           Capstone is exiled rather than put into the graveyard.\n104\t        4. On first resolution, wire the recurring paradigm copy ability.\n105\t        \"\"\"\n106\t        controller = self.controller\n107\t        if controller is None:\n108\t            controller = game.active_player\n109\t        if controller is None:\n110\t            return\n111\t\n112\t        exiled = self._exile_from_library(game, controller)\n113\t        self._offer_free_casts(game, controller, exiled)\n114\t        self._exile_this_spell(game)\n115\t        self._wire_paradigm(game, controller)\n116\t\n117\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n118\t    # Step 1 — exile from library until total mana value >= 4\n119\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n120\t\n121\t    def _exile_from_library(self, game: \"GameState\", controller: Any) -> list[Any]:\n122\t        \"\"\"Exile from the top of *controller*'s library until total MV >= 4.\n123\t\n124\t        Returns the list of cards exiled (top-of-library order).  Mana-value-0\n125\t        cards do not stop the process; an empty (or too-small) library simply\n126\t        stops once it runs dry — no crash / infinite loop.\n127\t        \"\"\"\n128\t        library = controller.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]\n129\t        exile = controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n130\t        exiled: list[Any] = []\n131\t        total = 0\n132\t\n133\t        while total < self.EXILE_THRESHOLD:\n134\t            # Top of the library is the last element of the internal list.\n135\t            top = library.top(1)\n136\t            if not top:\n137\t                break  # Library is empty — stop (no infinite loop).\n138\t            card = top[-1]\n139\t            library.remove(card)\n140\t            card.owner = controller\n141\t            card.controller = controller\n142\t            exile.add(card)\n143\t            exiled.append(card)\n144\t            total += _mana_value(card)\n145\t\n146\t        return exiled\n147\t\n148\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n149\t    # Step 2 — may cast any number of those spells for free\n150\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n151\t\n152\t    def _offer_free_casts(\n153\t        self, game: \"GameState\", controller: Any, exiled: list[Any]\n154\t    ) -> None:\n155\t        \"\"\"Let *controller* cast any number of the *exiled* spells for free.\n156\t\n157\t        Lands are not spells and are skipped.  The choice loop is optional\n158\t        (\"may\"): each iteration the controller decides whether to cast another\n159\t        spell, and if so chooses which exiled spell to cast for free from\n160\t        exile.  Declining ends the loop.\n161\t        \"\"\"\n162\t        from engine.casting import CastingError, cast_spell_free\n163\t\n164\t        chooser = getattr(controller, \"choose_yes_no\", None)\n165\t        picker = getattr(controller, \"choose_card\", None)\n166\t        if not callable(chooser) or not callable(picker):\n167\t            return\n168\t\n169\t        while True:\n170\t            # Only spells still in exile that are castable (not lands).\n171\t            exile = controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n172\t            candidates = [\n173\t                c\n174\t                for c in exiled\n175\t                if exile.contains(c) and _is_castable_spell(c)\n176\t            ]\n177\t            if not candidates:\n178\t                return\n179\t\n180\t            try:\n181\t                wants = bool(\n182\t                    chooser(\n183\t                        \"Cast a spell from among the exiled cards without \"\n184\t                        \"paying its mana cost?\"\n185\t                    )\n186\t                )\n187\t            except Exception:\n188\t                return\n189\t            if not wants:\n190\t                return\n191\t\n192\t            try:\n193\t                chosen = picker(\n194\t                    candidates,\n195\t                    \"spell to cast for free from among the exiled cards\",\n196\t                )\n197\t            except Exception:\n198\t                return\n199\t            if chosen is None or not exile.contains(chosen):\n200\t                continue\n201\t            if not _is_castable_spell(chosen):\n202\t                continue\n203\t\n204\t            try:\n205\t                cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.EXILE)\n206\t            except CastingError:\n207\t                # Cast failed (e.g. no legal target) — the card is rolled back\n208\t                # into exile; do not offer it again to avoid an infinite loop.\n209\t                if chosen in exiled:\n210\t                    exiled.remove(chosen)\n211\t\n212\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n213\t    # Step 3 — \"Then exile this spell.\"\n214\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n215\t\n216\t    def _exile_this_spell(self, game: \"GameState\") -> None:\n217\t        \"\"\"Register a stack->exile redirect so this spell is exiled on resolve.\n218\t\n219\t        Reuses the sos_1 redirect helper: when this sorcery finishes resolving\n220\t        and would go to the graveyard, it is routed to exile instead.\n221\t        \"\"\"\n222\t        from engine.casting import register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect\n223\t\n224\t        register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, self, \"exile\")\n225\t\n226\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n227\t    # Step 4 — wire the recurring paradigm copy ability\n228\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n229\t\n230\t    def _wire_paradigm(self, game: \"GameState\", controller: Any) -> None:\n231\t        \"\"\"Mark first resolution + register the recurring paradigm ability.\"\"\"\n232\t        from engine.paradigm import register_paradigm\n233\t\n234\t        register_paradigm(\n235\t            game,\n236\t            source=self,\n237\t            controller=controller,\n238\t            factory=self.make_paradigm_copy,\n239\t            name=self.name,\n240\t        )\n241\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7riNeuBBpSdqgv2NRz8iA","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"42ee623a-97df-40b0-bd0e-9bb288fa27c5","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:57:25.330Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_120 Paradigm"}
