{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01AzPTigTxgWe9vXCbB7gsD9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Jk3jqxd963DKcLLP4JYnq","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","old_string":"- General targeting/legality of the free-cast spells (e.g. a free-cast spell\n  with mandatory targets that has no legal target) is out of scope — it is the\n  cast pipeline's and the individual spell's responsibility, not this card's.","new_string":"- General targeting/legality of the free-cast spells (e.g. a free-cast spell\n  with mandatory targets that has no legal target) is out of scope — it is the\n  cast pipeline's and the individual spell's responsibility, not this card's.\n\n## Extended coverage\n\nThe Implementer built an additive `engine/paradigm.py` framework, so the item\npreviously deferred in `untestable.json` (the recurring per-main-phase copy\ndelivery and the once-per-game first-resolution gate) is now directly testable.\n12 new tests were added to `cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` across 5 new classes\n(total now **36** tests). They drive the real engine timing path:\n`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=..., precombat=...)` is fired via\n`game.trigger_manager.fire_event` and the stack is drained — the same pattern\nsos_57's `_fire_main_phase_begin` uses. A new local `_fire_main_phase_begin`\nhelper (with a `drain` flag) and a `_capstone_copies_in_exile` helper observe the\ncontroller's exile zone (`player.zones[Zone.EXILE]`). The copy offer is scripted\nvia `choose_yes_no` (`[False]` = decline so the copy stays in exile to be\nobserved; `[True]` = accept the free cast).\n\nThe two previously-tolerant `TestParadigmCopyMechanism` tests were tightened to\nremove their `pytest.skip` fallbacks now that the surface (`make_paradigm_copy`)\nis known; both still pass.\n\n### TestParadigmFirstResolutionGate (3 tests) — \"After you *first* resolve ...\"\n- `test_gate_closed_before_capstone_resolves` — `has_paradigm_resolved` reads\n  False before any Capstone resolves.\n- `test_no_copy_before_first_resolution` — firing the controller's precombat\n  main-phase event BEFORE any resolution creates NO copy in exile, the stack\n  stays empty, and the gate stays closed (no recurring trigger wired yet).\n- `test_resolving_capstone_opens_the_gate` — resolving a Capstone flips\n  `has_paradigm_resolved` to True for the controller.\n\n### TestParadigmRecurringCopyDelivery (3 tests) — \"each of your first main phases\"\n- `test_one_copy_appears_on_first_main_phase_after_resolution` — after\n  resolution, the controller's first precombat main phase delivers exactly one\n  new `ImprovisationCapstone` copy to exile (offer declined).\n- `test_recurs_a_second_copy_on_the_next_main_phase` — firing the event AGAIN\n  yields a SECOND copy, proving the ability recurs (contrast sos_57's one-shot\n  delayed trigger which fires exactly once).\n- `test_recurring_trigger_is_not_consumed` — the registered trigger count stays\n  at one across a firing (it is a normal `register` trigger, not a one-shot\n  `register_delayed`).\n\n### TestParadigmCopyGating (3 tests) — gated by player and phase\n- `test_postcombat_main_phase_creates_no_copy` — `precombat=False` (postcombat\n  main) delivers nothing (\"your *first* main phases\").\n- `test_opponents_main_phase_creates_no_copy_for_controller` — firing with\n  `player=opponent` delivers no copy to either player (\"*your* main phases\").\n- `test_opponent_phase_then_controller_phase_delivers_once` — the opponent's\n  main phase is inert; the controller's then delivers exactly one copy.\n\n### TestParadigmCopyAcceptCast (2 tests) — optional free cast from exile\n- `test_accepting_casts_the_copy_for_free_from_exile` — scripting yes casts the\n  copy for free with an empty mana pool: the trigger is resolved (without\n  draining the rest of the stack), and the cast copy is observed on the stack\n  and no longer in exile.\n- `test_declining_leaves_the_copy_in_exile` — scripting no leaves the copy in\n  exile and the stack empty.\n\n### TestParadigmRegisterDirectly (1 test) — public hook\n- `test_register_paradigm_opens_gate_and_delivers_recurring_copies` — calling\n  `register_paradigm` directly opens the gate and installs the recurring\n  trigger; two successive precombat main-phase events deliver two copies.\n\n### Now-resolved untestable item\nThe single entry in `untestable.json` (the recurring per-main-phase delivery and\nfirst-resolution gate) is now fully covered by the classes above. The file is\nleft in place for the historical record; coverage for that requirement is no\nlonger zero."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":148,"cache_read_input_tokens":75811,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":148,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7riNeuBBpSdqgv2NRz8iA","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"28278994-53f7-4f47-af95-1e0481c4a302","request_id":"req_011CbeA8BwSqfQzAiYxWXFJc","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_120 Paradigm"}
