{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7riNeuBBpSdqgv2NRz8iA","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green. The new tests pass against the existing implementation, confirming the Paradigm framework works as specified.\n\nTESTS_REWRITTEN\n\n```\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 36 (24 original, +12 added)\npytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py: 36 passed, 0 failed (1 pre-existing config warning: \"Unknown config option: timeout\", unrelated)\nnew_failures: 0\n```\n\n## What I added (12 new tests, 5 new classes)\n\nAll new tests drive the real engine timing path: fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=..., precombat=...)` via `game.trigger_manager.fire_event`, then drain the stack (same pattern as sos_57). Copies are observed in `player.zones[Zone.EXILE]`; the copy offer is scripted via `choose_yes_no`.\n\n- **TestParadigmFirstResolutionGate (3)** — gate closed before resolution; firing the precombat main event pre-resolution produces NO copy and leaves `has_paradigm_resolved` False; resolving the Capstone opens the gate.\n- **TestParadigmRecurringCopyDelivery (3)** — one copy on the first post-resolution main phase; a SECOND copy on the next firing (proves it recurs, contra sos_57's one-shot); the registered trigger is not consumed.\n- **TestParadigmCopyGating (3)** — `precombat=False` delivers nothing; opponent's main phase delivers nothing to either player; opponent-then-controller delivers exactly once.\n- **TestParadigmCopyAcceptCast (2)** — accept path: copy is cast for free from exile (lands on the stack, leaves exile, empty mana pool); decline path: copy stays in exile, stack empty.\n- **TestParadigmRegisterDirectly (1)** — driving `register_paradigm` directly opens the gate and delivers copies recurringly.\n\nI also tightened the 2 previously-tolerant `TestParadigmCopyMechanism` tests to use `make_paradigm_copy()` directly and removed their `pytest.skip` fallbacks now that the surface is confirmed; both still pass. All 24 original tests are unchanged in behavior.\n\n## Files\n- Updated: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`\n- Updated: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md` (appended `## Extended coverage`)\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-files.txt` already accurate (single file, unchanged)\n\nThe formerly-deferred `untestable.json` item (recurring per-main-phase delivery + first-resolution gate) is now fully covered; I left the file in place for the historical record."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ac8d407658417f781 (use SendMessage with to: 'ac8d407658417f781' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 79048\ntool_uses: 23\nduration_ms: 150139</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"fd881429-b756-427f-9351-9ebdc4dc964c","timestamp":"2026-06-02T08:59:49.358Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You previously wrote 24 tests for card **sos_120** (\"Improvisation Capstone\", a {5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, keyword Paradigm). The Implementer has now built an additive `engine/paradigm.py` framework, so the previously-deferred recurring per-main-phase copy delivery and the first-resolution gate are now testable. Extend your test file to cover them.\n\n## Context: your existing work\n- Existing tests: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` (24 tests, all passing). EXTEND this file — keep all existing tests unchanged, ADD new ones.\n- Your prior rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md`.\n- Your deferred item: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/untestable.json`.\n- Implementer's rationale with the EXACT new API and concrete observation recipes: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-rationale.md` — READ THIS (section \"Exactly how a test would observe each behaviour\").\n\n## New engine API (`engine/paradigm.py`) to test against\n- `mark_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool` / `has_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool` — per-game first-resolution gate.\n- `register_paradigm(game, source, controller, factory, name)` — marks first resolution and installs ONE recurring trigger on `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (precombat, controller-only).\n- `offer_paradigm_copy(game, controller, factory, name)` — the recurring body.\n- `make_paradigm_copy()` on the card — copy factory.\n- Driving: fire `engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=<p>, precombat=<bool>)` via `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(...)` then drain/resolve the stack (the trigger pushes its effect as a StackObject — resolve it). The copy appears in the controller's exile (`player.zones[Zone.EXILE]` — confirm the exact accessor from the impl-rationale / `engine/zones.py`).\n\n## Your task — add tests for the previously-untestable Paradigm timing\n1. **First-resolution gate**: BEFORE the Capstone has resolved, firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller, precombat=True)` and draining the stack produces NO Capstone copy in exile, and `has_paradigm_resolved(...)` is False.\n2. **Recurring per-main-phase delivery**: after the Capstone resolves (or after calling `register_paradigm`), firing the precombat main-phase event for the controller creates one new `ImprovisationCapstone` copy in the controller's exile (script DECLINE so it stays in exile to be observed). Firing AGAIN yields a SECOND copy — proving it recurs (not one-shot, contrast the sos_57 one-shot delayed trigger).\n3. **Gating by player / phase**: firing with `player=opponent`, or with `precombat=False` (postcombat main), creates NO copy.\n4. **Optional cast / accept path**: when the controller accepts (script yes), the copy is cast for free from exile (leaves exile, lands on the stack) — assert at least one accept path.\n5. Match the exact `fire_event` signature and Phase/Step usage by checking `engine/triggers.py` and how sos_57's tests drove `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (look at the existing sos_120 / sos_57-style patterns and `engine_tests/`).\n\n## Constraints\n- DO NOT modify `engine_tests/`, FDN `tests.py`, or any engine source. Only edit `cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`.\n- DO NOT change or weaken any of your existing 24 tests — only add new ones. (You may, if you wish, tighten the 2 previously-tolerant `TestParadigmCopyMechanism` tests to remove their `pytest.skip` fallback now that the surface is known — but only if you are certain; otherwise leave them.)\n- The implementation already exists, so your new tests should PASS. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` and confirm everything passes. If a new test reveals a genuine implementation bug, leave the failing test in place and report it (do not paper over it).\n\n## Outputs\n- Updated `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`.\n- Append a \"## Extended coverage\" section to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md`.\n- Keep `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-files.txt` accurate (same single file).\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn: total test count now, how many you added, pass/fail result of `pytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`, and `new_failures: <N>` (with reasons if any).","agentId":"ac8d407658417f781","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green. The new tests pass against the existing implementation, confirming the Paradigm framework works as specified.\n\nTESTS_REWRITTEN\n\n```\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 36 (24 original, +12 added)\npytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py: 36 passed, 0 failed (1 pre-existing config warning: \"Unknown config option: timeout\", unrelated)\nnew_failures: 0\n```\n\n## What I added (12 new tests, 5 new classes)\n\nAll new tests drive the real engine timing path: fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=..., precombat=...)` via `game.trigger_manager.fire_event`, then drain the stack (same pattern as sos_57). Copies are observed in `player.zones[Zone.EXILE]`; the copy offer is scripted via `choose_yes_no`.\n\n- **TestParadigmFirstResolutionGate (3)** — gate closed before resolution; firing the precombat main event pre-resolution produces NO copy and leaves `has_paradigm_resolved` False; resolving the Capstone opens the gate.\n- **TestParadigmRecurringCopyDelivery (3)** — one copy on the first post-resolution main phase; a SECOND copy on the next firing (proves it recurs, contra sos_57's one-shot); the registered trigger is not consumed.\n- **TestParadigmCopyGating (3)** — `precombat=False` delivers nothing; opponent's main phase delivers nothing to either player; opponent-then-controller delivers exactly once.\n- **TestParadigmCopyAcceptCast (2)** — accept path: copy is cast for free from exile (lands on the stack, leaves exile, empty mana pool); decline path: copy stays in exile, stack empty.\n- **TestParadigmRegisterDirectly (1)** — driving `register_paradigm` directly opens the gate and delivers copies recurringly.\n\nI also tightened the 2 previously-tolerant `TestParadigmCopyMechanism` tests to use `make_paradigm_copy()` directly and removed their `pytest.skip` fallbacks now that the surface is confirmed; both still pass. All 24 original tests are unchanged in behavior.\n\n## Files\n- Updated: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`\n- Updated: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md` (appended `## Extended coverage`)\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-files.txt` already accurate (single file, unchanged)\n\nThe formerly-deferred `untestable.json` item (recurring per-main-phase delivery + first-resolution gate) is now fully covered; I left the file in place for the historical record."}],"totalDurationMs":150139,"totalTokens":79048,"totalToolUseCount":23,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":269,"cache_read_input_tokens":77850,"output_tokens":927,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":269},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tok