{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012wnvUuhc9sr84hixb3Ye8s","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Paradigm-keyword framework (Comprehensive Rules 702.192).\n2\t\n3\t*Paradigm* is a keyword found on some sorceries (and other spells).  A spell\n4\twith paradigm reads:\n5\t\n6\t    Paradigm (Then exile this spell.  After you first resolve a spell with this\n7\t    name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at\n8\t    the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n9\t\n10\tSo paradigm has three moving parts:\n11\t\n12\t1. **\"Then exile this spell.\"** — the paradigm spell, instead of being put into\n13\t   its owner's graveyard on resolution, is exiled.  This part reuses the\n14\t   existing :func:`engine.casting.register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect` plumbing\n15\t   (see ``cards/sos/sos_1``) and needs no new framework code.\n16\t\n17\t2. **\"After you first resolve a spell with this name, ...\"** — a once-per-game,\n18\t   per-name gate keyed off the *first* time a spell with that name resolves for\n19\t   a player.  Before that first resolution no paradigm copy is offered.\n20\t\n21\t3. **\"... you may cast a copy of it from exile ... at the beginning of each of\n22\t   your first main phases.\"** — a *recurring* delayed ability: every one of the\n23\t   controller's pre-combat (\"first\") main phases, a fresh copy of the paradigm\n24\t   spell is created in the controller's exile and the controller may cast it for\n25\t   free.\n26\t\n27\tThe engine had no support for this mechanic, so this module adds it\n28\t*additively* — no existing engine symbol is renamed, moved, or deleted.  It is\n29\tmodelled on :mod:`engine.preparation` (the analogous Preparation-card\n30\tframework) and reuses:\n31\t\n32\t- :class:`engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (from sos_57) for\n33\t  the per-main-phase timing.\n34\t- :meth:`engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register` for a *recurring* trigger\n35\t  (``register_delayed`` is one-shot; paradigm needs to fire every first main\n36\t  phase, so we register a normal, non-one-shot trigger here).\n37\t- :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free` (with :class:`~engine.types.Zone.EXILE`)\n38\t  to cast the exiled copy for free.\n39\t\n40\tPublic API\n41\t----------\n42\t- :func:`mark_paradigm_resolved` / :func:`has_paradigm_resolved` — the\n43\t  per-game, per-(player, name) first-resolution registry.\n44\t- :func:`register_paradigm` — wire the recurring per-main-phase free-copy\n45\t  ability for a given paradigm spell name + controller (idempotent per\n46\t  controller+name).  Marks the first resolution as a side effect.\n47\t- :func:`offer_paradigm_copy` — create a fresh copy of the paradigm spell in\n48\t  the controller's exile and let the controller optionally cast it for free.\n49\t  This is the effect the recurring trigger runs each first main phase.\n50\t\n51\t\"Paradigm\" is a *printed keyword label*, not an evergreen keyword, so no member\n52\tis added to :class:`engine.types.Keyword` (keeping that enum unchanged /\n53\tadditive-safe).\n54\t\"\"\"\n55\t\n56\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n57\t\n58\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable\n59\t\n60\tfrom engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n61\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Zone\n62\t\n63\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n64\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n65\t    from engine.player import Player\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n69\t# Per-game first-resolution registry  (player, name) -> resolved?\n70\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n71\t\n72\t\n73\tdef _resolved_registry(game: GameState) -> set[tuple[int, str]]:\n74\t    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the per-game first-resolution registry.\n75\t\n76\t    The registry is a set of ``(id(player), name)`` keys recording that a\n77\t    spell with that name has *first resolved* under that player's control this\n78\t    game.  Stored lazily on the game object so no change to\n79\t    ``GameState.__init__`` is required.\n80\t    \"\"\"\n81\t    registry = getattr(game, \"_paradigm_resolved\", None)\n82\t    if registry is None:\n83\t        registry = set()\n84\t        game._paradigm_resolved = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n85\t    return registry\n86\t\n87\t\n88\tdef has_paradigm_resolved(game: GameState, player: Any, name: str) -> bool:\n89\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if a spell named *name* has first resolved for *player*.\"\"\"\n90\t    if player is None:\n91\t        return False\n92\t    return (id(player), name) in _resolved_registry(game)\n93\t\n94\t\n95\tdef mark_paradigm_resolved(game: GameState, player: Any, name: str) -> bool:\n96\t    \"\"\"Record that a spell named *name* has resolved for *player*.\n97\t\n98\t    Returns ``True`` if this was the *first* resolution (the gate just opened),\n99\t    ``False`` if a spell with that name had already resolved for the player\n100\t    (the \"after you *first* resolve\" clause only opens the gate once).\n101\t    \"\"\"\n102\t    if player is None:\n103\t        return False\n104\t    registry = _resolved_registry(game)\n105\t    key = (id(player), name)\n106\t    if key in registry:\n107\t        return False\n108\t    registry.add(key)\n109\t    return True\n110\t\n111\t\n112\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n113\t# Per-game registry of active paradigm triggers  (player, name) -> True\n114\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n115\t\n116\t\n117\tdef _registered_registry(game: GameState) -> set[tuple[int, str]]:\n118\t    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the set of already-wired paradigm triggers.\n119\t\n120\t    Keyed by ``(id(controller), name)`` so the recurring trigger is registered\n121\t    at most once per controller+name even if the paradigm spell resolves\n122\t    multiple times.\n123\t    \"\"\"\n124\t    registry = getattr(game, \"_paradigm_registered\", None)\n125\t    if registry is None:\n126\t        registry = set()\n127\t        game._paradigm_registered = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n128\t    return registry\n129\t\n130\t\n131\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n132\t# Offering the free copy each first main phase\n133\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n134\t\n135\t\n136\tdef offer_paradigm_copy(\n137\t    game: GameState,\n138\t    controller: Any,\n139\t    factory: Callable[[], Any],\n140\t    name: str,\n141\t) -> Any | None:\n142\t    \"\"\"Create a paradigm copy in *controller*'s exile and offer a free cast.\n143\t\n144\t    Implements the per-main-phase body of paradigm: a fresh copy of the\n145\t    paradigm spell (produced by *factory*) is created in the controller's\n146\t    exile zone, then the controller is asked whether they want to cast it for\n147\t    free.  On *yes* the copy is cast from exile via\n148\t    :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free`; on *no* (or a cast failure) the\n149\t    copy is left in exile.\n150\t\n151\t    Returns the copy that was created (whether or not it was cast), or ``None``\n152\t    if no copy could be produced.\n153\t    \"\"\"\n154\t    if controller is None or factory is None:\n155\t        return None\n156\t\n157\t    copy = factory()\n158\t    if copy is None:\n159\t        return None\n160\t    copy.owner = controller\n161\t    copy.controller = controller\n162\t    copy.is_paradigm_copy = True\n163\t\n164\t    exile = controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n165\t    exile.add(copy)\n166\t\n167\t    # \"you may cast\" — optional.\n168\t    wants_to_cast = False\n169\t    chooser = getattr(controller, \"choose_yes_no\", None)\n170\t    if callable(chooser):\n171\t        try:\n172\t            wants_to_cast = bool(\n173\t                chooser(\n174\t                    f\"Cast a copy of {name} from exile without paying its \"\n175\t                    \"mana cost?\"\n176\t                )\n177\t            )\n178\t        except Exception:\n179\t            wants_to_cast = False\n180\t\n181\t    if not wants_to_cast:\n182\t        return copy\n183\t\n184\t    from engine.casting import cast_spell_free\n185\t\n186\t    try:\n187\t        cast_spell_free(game, controller, copy, Zone.EXILE)\n188\t    except Exception:\n189\t        # Cast failed (e.g. illegal target) — leave the copy in exile.\n190\t        if not exile.contains(copy):\n191\t            exile.add(copy)\n192\t    return copy\n193\t\n194\t\n195\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n196\t# Wiring the recurring delayed ability\n197\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n198\t\n199\t\n200\tdef register_paradigm(\n201\t    game: GameState,\n202\t    source: Any,\n203\t    controller: Any,\n204\t    factory: Callable[[], Any],\n205\t    name: str,\n206\t) -> None:\n207\t    \"\"\"Wire paradigm's recurring per-main-phase free-copy ability.\n208\t\n209\t    Called when a paradigm spell (named *name*, controlled by *controller*)\n210\t    resolves.  It:\n211\t\n212\t    1. Marks the first resolution in the per-game registry (the \"after you\n213\t       first resolve a spell with this name\" gate).  If a spell with this name\n214\t       has already resolved for *controller* the gate is already open.\n215\t    2. Registers — at most once per ``(controller, name)`` — a *recurring*\n216\t       trigger on :class:`~engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n217\t       that, at the beginning of each of *controller*'s pre-combat (\"first\")\n218\t       main phases, runs :func:`offer_paradigm_copy` to create a free copy in\n219\t       exile and offer to cast it.\n220\t\n221\t    Unlike :meth:`engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register_delayed` (one-shot),\n222\t    this uses :meth:`~engine.triggers.TriggerManager.register` so the ability\n223\t    fires every qualifying main phase, matching \"each of your first main\n224\t    phases\".\n225\t    \"\"\"\n226\t    from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n227\t\n228\t    mark_paradigm_resolved(game, controller, name)\n229\t\n230\t    if controller is None or factory is None:\n231\t        return\n232\t\n233\t    registered = _registered_registry(game)\n234\t    key = (id(controller), name)\n235\t    if key in registered:\n236\t        return\n237\t    registered.add(key)\n238\t\n239\t    def _condition(g: GameState, event: BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n240\t        # \"your first main phases\" — only the controller's pre-combat main, and\n241\t        # only once the first-resolution gate is open.\n242\t        if getattr(event, \"player\", None) is not controller:\n243\t            return False\n244\t        if not getattr(event, \"precombat\", False):\n245\t            return False\n246\t        return has_paradigm_resolved(g, controller, name)\n247\t\n248\t    def _effect(g: GameState) -> None:\n249\t        offer_paradigm_copy(g, controller, factory, name)\n250\t\n251\t    game.trigger_manager.register(\n252\t        TriggerRegistration(\n253\t            event_type=BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent,\n254\t            condition=_condition,\n255\t            effect=_effect,\n256\t            source=source,\n257\t            controller=controller,\n258\t        )\n259\t    )\n260\t\n261\t\n262\tdef is_paradigm_copy(card: Any) -> bool:\n263\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* is a paradigm copy created by this framework.\"\"\"\n264\t    return bool(getattr(card, \"is_paradigm_copy\", False))\n265\t\n266\t\n267\tdef is_castable_spell(card: Any) -> bool:\n268\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* is a spell that can be cast (not a land).\n269\t\n270\t    Lands are not spells (CR 601.1) and cannot be cast for free by paradigm's\n271\t    \"cast any number of spells\" clause; this helper centralises that check.\n272\t    \"\"\"\n273\t    card_types = getattr(card, \"card_types\", set())\n274\t    return CardType.LAND not in card_types\n275\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SjZQCEbiximMqCdwAdjEmg","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"3c79b1e3-d045-46a7-afe7-5fd12fc372bf","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:00:26.556Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DBXj79Ds3Sym4mmPshapdf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Preparation-card framework (Comprehensive Rules 722).\n2\t\n3\tA *preparation card* (CR 722) is a permanent that, in addition to its normal\n4\tcharacteristics, carries an alternative \"prepare spell\" half.  The card can\n5\t\"become prepared\"; when it does, its controller creates a castable copy of the\n6\tprepare spell in exile that they may cast, and casting that copy \"unprepares\"\n7\tthe source permanent (CR 722.3a–c).\n8\t\n9\tThe engine had no support for this mechanic, so this module adds it\n10\t*additively* — no existing engine symbol is renamed, moved, or deleted:\n11\t\n12\t- :func:`mark_prepared` — give a permanent the ``prepared`` designation and\n13\t  create a copy of its prepare spell in the controller's exile (722.3c).\n14\t- :func:`unprepare` — clear the designation and remove the exiled copy\n15\t  (722.3b; the copy only lasts while the permanent stays prepared, 722.3c).\n16\t- :func:`is_prepared` — read the designation off a permanent.\n17\t- :func:`get_prepared_copy` — fetch the exiled prepare-spell copy keyed to a\n18\t  prepared permanent.\n19\t- :func:`get_prepared_source` — reverse lookup: the permanent a given exiled\n20\t  copy was created for.\n21\t- :func:`cast_prepared_copy` — cast an exiled prepare-spell copy from exile\n22\t  (via :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free`); the cast unprepares the source\n23\t  (722.3c — \"loses the prepared designation at the time the spell becomes\n24\t  cast\").\n25\t\n26\tA permanent advertises a prepare spell by exposing a ``make_prepare_spell()``\n27\tfactory (returning a fresh :class:`~engine.card.CardImpl` for the {W} instant,\n28\tetc.).  The framework calls that factory to materialise the copy.\n29\t\n30\tThe prepared designation is stored on the permanent both as ``is_prepared`` and\n31\t``prepared`` boolean attributes (so probes against either spelling work), and\n32\tthe permanent⇄copy bookkeeping lives in a per-game registry attached lazily to\n33\tthe game object (no ``GameState.__init__`` change required).  \"Prepared\" is a\n34\t*designation*, not an evergreen keyword, so no member is added to\n35\t``engine.types.Keyword`` (keeping that enum unchanged / additive-safe).\n36\t\"\"\"\n37\t\n38\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n39\t\n40\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n41\t\n42\tfrom engine.types import Zone\n43\t\n44\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n45\t    from engine.card import CardImpl\n46\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n47\t    from engine.player import Player\n48\t\n49\t\n50\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n51\t# Per-game registry of prepared permanents ⇄ their exiled prepare-spell copies\n52\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n53\t\n54\t\n55\tdef _prepare_registry(game: GameState) -> dict[int, Any]:\n56\t    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the per-game preparation registry.\n57\t\n58\t    The registry maps ``id(permanent)`` to the exiled prepare-spell copy that\n59\t    was created for it (CR 722.3c).  Stored lazily on the game object so no\n60\t    change to ``GameState.__init__`` is required.\n61\t    \"\"\"\n62\t    registry = getattr(game, \"_prepared_copies\", None)\n63\t    if registry is None:\n64\t        registry = {}\n65\t        game._prepared_copies = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n66\t    return registry\n67\t\n68\t\n69\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n70\t# Designation read / write\n71\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n72\t\n73\t\n74\tdef is_prepared(permanent: Any) -> bool:\n75\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *permanent* currently has the prepared designation.\"\"\"\n76\t    val = getattr(permanent, \"is_prepared\", None)\n77\t    if isinstance(val, bool):\n78\t        return val\n79\t    val = getattr(permanent, \"prepared\", None)\n80\t    if isinstance(val, bool):\n81\t        return val\n82\t    return False\n83\t\n84\t\n85\tdef _set_designation(permanent: Any, value: bool) -> None:\n86\t    \"\"\"Write the prepared designation under both common attribute spellings.\"\"\"\n87\t    permanent.is_prepared = value\n88\t    permanent.prepared = value\n89\t\n90\t\n91\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n92\t# Becoming prepared (722.3a, 722.3c)\n93\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n94\t\n95\t\n96\tdef mark_prepared(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> Any | None:\n97\t    \"\"\"Give *permanent* the prepared designation and create the exiled copy.\n98\t\n99\t    Implements CR 722.3a (gaining the designation) and 722.3c (creating a\n100\t    copy of the prepare spell in the controller's exile zone).  The copy is a\n101\t    fresh object produced by the permanent's ``make_prepare_spell()`` factory;\n102\t    it is owned/controlled by the prepared permanent's controller and lives in\n103\t    that controller's exile zone, keyed to the source permanent.\n104\t\n105\t    A permanent that already has the designation is left unchanged (722.3a — a\n106\t    permanent can't gain the designation if it already has it).\n107\t\n108\t    Returns:\n109\t        The exiled prepare-spell copy, or ``None`` if the permanent has no\n110\t        prepare-spell factory / no controller.\n111\t    \"\"\"\n112\t    if is_prepared(permanent):\n113\t        return get_prepared_copy(game, permanent)\n114\t\n115\t    factory = getattr(permanent, \"make_prepare_spell\", None)\n116\t    if factory is None:\n117\t        return None\n118\t    controller = getattr(permanent, \"controller\", None)\n119\t    if controller is None:\n120\t        return None\n121\t\n122\t    _set_designation(permanent, True)\n123\t\n124\t    copy = factory()\n125\t    if copy is None:\n126\t        return None\n127\t    copy.owner = controller\n128\t    copy.controller = controller\n129\t    # Mark the copy as a prepare-spell copy and back-link it to its source so\n130\t    # casting it can find and unprepare the source permanent (722.3c).\n131\t    copy.is_prepare_copy = True\n132\t    copy.prepare_source = permanent\n133\t\n134\t    exile = controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n135\t    exile.add(copy)\n136\t    _prepare_registry(game)[id(permanent)] = copy\n137\t    return copy\n138\t\n139\t\n140\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n141\t# Becoming unprepared (722.3b, 722.3c)\n142\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n143\t\n144\t\n145\tdef unprepare(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> None:\n146\t    \"\"\"Clear the prepared designation from *permanent* and drop its copy.\n147\t\n148\t    Implements CR 722.3b (removing the designation).  Per 722.3c the exiled\n149\t    copy only persists while the permanent stays prepared, so the copy is\n150\t    removed from exile here (if it is still there).\n151\t    \"\"\"\n152\t    _set_designation(permanent, False)\n153\t    copy = _prepare_registry(game).pop(id(permanent), None)\n154\t    if copy is None:\n155\t        return\n156\t    controller = getattr(copy, \"controller\", None) or getattr(permanent, \"controller\", None)\n157\t    if controller is not None:\n158\t        exile = controller.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n159\t        if exile.contains(copy):\n160\t            exile.remove(copy)\n161\t\n162\t\n163\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n164\t# Lookups\n165\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n166\t\n167\t\n168\tdef get_prepared_copy(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> Any | None:\n169\t    \"\"\"Return the exiled prepare-spell copy keyed to *permanent* (or ``None``).\"\"\"\n170\t    return _prepare_registry(game).get(id(permanent))\n171\t\n172\t\n173\tdef get_prepared_source(game: GameState, copy: Any) -> Any | None:\n174\t    \"\"\"Return the prepared permanent a given exiled *copy* was created for.\n175\t\n176\t    Resolution relies on the ``prepare_source`` back-link the framework sets on\n177\t    every copy it materialises (:func:`mark_prepared`).  ``id(...)`` keys in the\n178\t    registry cannot be reversed to an object, so there is no further fallback.\n179\t    \"\"\"\n180\t    return getattr(copy, \"prepare_source\", None)\n181\t\n182\t\n183\tdef _registry_key_for_copy(game: GameState, copy: Any) -> int | None:\n184\t    \"\"\"Reverse-scan the per-game registry for the key whose value is *copy*.\n185\t\n186\t    Used to detach a copy from the registry when its ``prepare_source``\n187\t    back-link is missing (e.g. an externally-supplied copy).  Returns the\n188\t    matching ``id(permanent)`` key, or ``None`` if the copy is not registered.\n189\t    \"\"\"\n190\t    for source_id, registered in _prepare_registry(game).items():\n191\t        if registered is copy:\n192\t            return source_id\n193\t    return None\n194\t\n195\t\n196\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n197\t# Casting the exiled copy (722.3c — unprepare on cast)\n198\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n199\t\n200\t\n201\tdef cast_prepared_copy(game: GameState, player: Player, copy: Any) -> None:\n202\t    \"\"\"Cast an exiled prepare-spell *copy* from exile, unpreparing its source.\n203\t\n204\t    Uses :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free` to put the copy on the stack\n205\t    from the exile zone (the prepare half is cast for its own {W} cost in\n206\t    paper Magic; the engine's free-cast path is the closest existing plumbing\n207\t    and keeps this additive).\n208\t\n209\t    Per CR 722.3c the source permanent loses the prepared designation **at the\n210\t    time the spell becomes cast** — i.e. only when the cast actually succeeds.\n211\t    :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell_free` can raise\n212\t    :class:`~engine.casting.CastingError` (e.g. no legal target, or the target\n213\t    has protection) and roll the copy back into exile.  So the order here is:\n214\t    cast the copy *first*; only after the cast returns without error do we clear\n215\t    the source's designation and detach the registry entry.  On a cast failure\n216\t    the source stays prepared and the copy stays in exile (the error\n217\t    propagates), matching the rules.\n218\t\n219\t    ``cast_spell_free`` already moves the copy from exile onto the stack, so we\n220\t    must **not** also remove it from exile here — we only pop the registry entry\n221\t    (a dict key), never re-touch the in-flight copy, avoiding any double-removal.\n222\t\n223\t    Raises:\n224\t        engine.casting.CastingError: If the copy cannot be cast.  In that case\n225\t            the source remains prepared and the copy remains in exile.\n226\t    \"\"\"\n227\t    from engine.casting import cast_spell_free\n228\t\n229\t    source = get_prepared_source(game, copy)\n230\t\n231\t    # Cast first.  If this raises (CastingError), the copy is rolled back into\n232\t    # exile by cast_spell_free and the source is left untouched (still prepared)\n233\t    # because the error propagates before we clear anything below.\n234\t    cast_spell_free(game, player, copy, Zone.EXILE)\n235\t\n236\t    # The spell has now \"become cast\" (722.3c): clear the source's designation\n237\t    # and detach the registry entry.  We only pop the registry key here; the\n238\t    # copy itself already left exile as part of the cast, so it is not removed\n239\t    # again (no double-removal of the in-flight copy).\n240\t    if source is not None:\n241\t        _set_designation(source, False)\n242\t        _prepare_registry(game).pop(id(source), None)\n243\t    else:\n244\t        # Externally-supplied copy with no prepare_source back-link: still\n245\t        # detach any matching registry entry so the source unprepares.\n246\t        key = _registry_key_for_copy(game, copy)\n247\t        if key is not None:\n248\t            _prepare_registry(game).pop(key, None)\n249\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SjZQCEbiximMqCdwAdjEmg","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"1ae25450-fede-488a-b569-2c13bc652da0","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:00:26.556Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120 implementation"}
