{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SjZQCEbiximMqCdwAdjEmg","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. I verified the implementation against the card spec, oracle text, the engine APIs it depends on (`cast_spell_free`, `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect`, `ZoneContainer.top/add/remove/contains`, `TriggerManager.register`/`TriggerRegistration`, `Sorcery` constructor, `get_colors`, `Land`/`CardType.LAND`), and the prior-card conventions in `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\nFindings summary (all advisory — no strict issues):\n- The exile-threshold logic is correct: tops the controller's library via `top(1)[-1]`, accumulates MV with an inclusive `< THRESHOLD` loop, MV-0 cards don't stop it, and an empty library breaks cleanly (no infinite loop). Only the controller's library is used.\n- The free-cast loop is optional, allows any number, filters lands (`is_castable_spell` + `cast_spell_free` double-guards), and is genuinely free.\n- \"Then exile this spell\" correctly reuses the sanctioned sos_1 redirect.\n- The Paradigm framework is correct: the first-resolution gate is per-game/per-(player,name), `register_paradigm` installs exactly one recurring trigger deduped per (controller,name), the condition fires only at the controller's precombat main, and `offer_paradigm_copy` creates the copy in the controller's exile and casts-free on accept / leaves it on decline.\n- Additive-only: `engine/paradigm.py` is a new file; no existing engine symbol is renamed/moved/deleted; the `Keyword` enum is untouched (Paradigm is a printed label). No changes to `engine_tests/` or `cards/fdn/*/tests.py`.\n\nThe three advisories concern a broad `except Exception` around `cast_spell_free` in `offer_paradigm_copy` (could mask real bugs — relevant to the explicit guardrail), an unnecessary `card.owner` reassignment on exiled cards, and a broad catch in the card's free-cast loop.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a67dce2a06881e3b7 (use SendMessage with to: 'a67dce2a06881e3b7' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 73028\ntool_uses: 21\nduration_ms: 114170</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b44d1aae-f862-420c-b373-f7174832fe9c","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:02:08.868Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are reviewing the implementation of a single Magic: The Gathering card plus a new additive engine framework. The card is **sos_120** (\"Improvisation Capstone\", a {5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, complex tier) introducing a new **Paradigm** mechanic (CR 702.192).\n\nOracle: \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n\n## Inputs\n- Unified diff of the implementation + engine changes (NOT the tests): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl.diff` (covers `cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` and the new `engine/paradigm.py`).\n- Implementer's rationale (read for design intent and API): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-rationale.md`.\n- Coordinator directives (scope): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/coordinator-directives.md`.\n- Card spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/card_spec.json`.\n- Tests (already arbitrated — DO NOT demand test rewrites): `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` (36 tests, all passing).\n- Prior-card conventions to respect: `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` and `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` (lazy per-game registry, reused `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` from sos_57, `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect` from sos_1, copy-factory pattern from sos_13 — all sanctioned; do NOT flag these).\n- Engine source for context: `engine/paradigm.py`, `engine/preparation.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/turn.py`, `engine/zones.py`.\n- Rules: `/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt` (grep — Paradigm CR 702.192).\n\n## What to review\nReview the diff for correctness vs. spec/oracle intent, real bugs, missed edge cases, and convention violations. Scrutinize especially:\n- **Exile threshold**: exiles from the TOP of the controller's library; running total of mana value; stops INCLUSIVELY at `>= 4`; MV-0 cards don't stop it; empty-library safe (no infinite loop); only the controller's library used.\n- **Free-cast loop**: optional (\"you may\"); \"any number\"; lands are not castable spells; declining leaves cards in exile; free (empty mana pool).\n- **\"Then exile this spell\"**: the Capstone resolves STACK -> EXILE (not graveyard) via the reused sos_1 redirect.\n- **Paradigm framework (`engine/paradigm.py`)**: the first-resolution gate (`mark`/`has_paradigm_resolved`) is per-game and per-(player,name); `register_paradigm` installs at most ONE recurring trigger per (controller,name) — confirm no duplicate-stacking across repeated resolutions; the recurring trigger fires only at the controller's PRECOMBAT main phase (not postcombat, not opponent's); `offer_paradigm_copy` creates the copy in the controller's exile and casts free on accept / leaves it on decline; CastingError handling doesn't mask real bugs.\n- **Regression safety**: confirm nothing existing in engine was renamed/removed (additive-only — `engine/paradigm.py` is new); `Keyword` enum unchanged (16 members); the recurring trigger registered via `TriggerManager.register` does not leak across games or interfere with existing triggers.\n\n## Important guardrails\n- DO NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards or conventions in `KEY_DECISIONS.md` (lazy per-game registries, reused main-phase event, redirect helper, copy-factory — all deliberate and sanctioned).\n- DO NOT demand test rewrites — tests were arbitrated. Any test-quality concern is `advisory` only.\n- Focus on what is visible in the diff.\n\n## Output (write this)\nWrite `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json` — a JSON array of:\n```json\n{\"severity\": \"strict\" | \"advisory\", \"file\": \"<path>\", \"line\": <int or null>, \"comment\": \"<actionable comment>\"}\n```\nUse `strict` only for must-fix issues (correctness bugs, spec violations, regression risks). Use `advisory` for style/clarity. Write `[]` if none.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\n```\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json\n```","agentId":"a67dce2a06881e3b7","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. I verified the implementation against the card spec, oracle text, the engine APIs it depends on (`cast_spell_free`, `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect`, `ZoneContainer.top/add/remove/contains`, `TriggerManager.register`/`TriggerRegistration`, `Sorcery` constructor, `get_colors`, `Land`/`CardType.LAND`), and the prior-card conventions in `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\nFindings summary (all advisory — no strict issues):\n- The exile-threshold logic is correct: tops the controller's library via `top(1)[-1]`, accumulates MV with an inclusive `< THRESHOLD` loop, MV-0 cards don't stop it, and an empty library breaks cleanly (no infinite loop). Only the controller's library is used.\n- The free-cast loop is optional, allows any number, filters lands (`is_castable_spell` + `cast_spell_free` double-guards), and is genuinely free.\n- \"Then exile this spell\" correctly reuses the sanctioned sos_1 redirect.\n- The Paradigm framework is correct: the first-resolution gate is per-game/per-(player,name), `register_paradigm` installs exactly one recurring trigger deduped per (controller,name), the condition fires only at the controller's precombat main, and `offer_paradigm_copy` creates the copy in the controller's exile and casts-free on accept / leaves it on decline.\n- Additive-only: `engine/paradigm.py` is a new file; no existing engine symbol is renamed/moved/deleted; the `Keyword` enum is untouched (Paradigm is a printed label). No changes to `engine_tests/` or `cards/fdn/*/tests.py`.\n\nThe three advisories concern a broad `except Exception` around `cast_spell_free` in `offer_paradigm_copy` (could mask real bugs — relevant to the explicit guardrail), an unnecessary `card.owner` reassignment on exiled cards, and a broad catch in the card's free-cast loop.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json"}],"totalDurationMs":114170,"totalTokens":73028,"totalToolUseCount":21,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1595,"cache_read_input_tokens":70686,"output_tokens":745,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1595},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":745,"cache_read_input_tokens":70686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1595,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":14,"searchCount":5,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":1,"linesAdded":21,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
