{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H6pxqW1YJhVScLqeG4XwUq","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests are well-formed and in the TDD red phase: 18 concrete tests fail with genuine behavioral assertions, and 4 miracle-grant tests skip (they activate once the implementer exposes a miracle-cost query surface).\n\n## Summary\n\n**Card:** sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian ({3}{R}{W} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, Flying + Haste).\n\n**Tests written:** 22 tests in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`, across 5 classes:\n- `TestLoreholdProperties` (10) — static data: type, name, cost/MV, P/T, legendary, Elder Dragon, Flying, Haste, R+W colors.\n- `TestLoreholdUpkeepTriggerRegistration` (2) — registers exactly one `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger.\n- `TestLoreholdUpkeepTiming` (2) — fires on an opponent's upkeep but NOT the controller's own.\n- `TestLoreholdLootEffect` (4) — \"you may discard, if you do draw\": yes ⇒ discard + draw; decline ⇒ nothing; empty hand ⇒ no-op; draw is conditional on the discard.\n- `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` (4) — instants/sorceries in the controller's hand get miracle {2}; creatures and the opponent's spells do not (tolerant probe that skips if no surface exists, so it never passes vacuously).\n\n**Red-phase confirmed:** 18 fail with real behavioral assertions (no import/syntax errors); the 4 miracle tests skip until a miracle-cost surface is exposed. I deliberately strengthened the timing and loot no-op tests (anchoring on the trigger actually being registered/firing) so none pass vacuously against the empty stub.\n\n**Untestable:** 1 — the draw-time \"you may cast it for its miracle cost when you draw it (first card drawn this turn)\" timing has no engine hook to assert; the grant itself is tested, the draw-time cast is recorded in `untestable.json`.\n\nOutput files:\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md`\n