ine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`, `engine/types.py`.\n- Workspace rules: `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`, `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` (read — records engine conventions/APIs added by earlier cards this run, e.g. coin-flip RNG, skip-turn counter, main-phase event, delayed triggers, preparation/paradigm frameworks), `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n- Rules reference: `/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt` (grep, do not read whole; see `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n\n## Your task\n1. Read the card spec and understand the card's full behavior.\n2. Write thorough pytest tests at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` that verify the card's behavior per its oracle text. Cover main functionality plus relevant edge cases. Tests must follow existing engine/FDN test conventions and must FAIL against the current empty stub (TDD red) but PASS once the card is correctly implemented.\n3. Do NOT modify any files under `engine_tests/` or any FDN `tests.py`. Do NOT modify engine source. You only write `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`.\n4. Confirm the tests are well-formed by running them (they should fail/error because the card is unimplemented — that is expected). Do not try to make them pass.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` — your tests.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md` — what each test covers and the behavior contract you derived from the spec.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-files.txt` — list of test file path(s) you created (one per line).\n- If any spec requirement cannot be tested with the current engine/test API, write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/untestable.json` — a JSON array of `{\"requirement\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\", \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"...\"}`. Omit the file entirely if everything is testable.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn a short summary: number of tests written, the test file path, and `untestable_count: <N>` (0 if none). Do not paste the full tes