{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019fFmgDkrAC8A5r9YakEyDu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_201 Lorehold, the Historian\n2\t\n3\tCard (from `card_spec.json`):\n4\t\n5\t- Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, `{3}{R}{W}`, 5/5, colors R+W.\n6\t- Flying, haste.\n7\t- \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\"\n8\t- \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you\n9\t  do, draw a card.\"\n10\t\n11\tTest file: `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` (22 tests across 5 classes).\n12\t\n13\t## Behaviour contract derived from the oracle text\n14\t\n15\t1. **Static data.** Must be a `Creature` named \"Lorehold, the Historian\" with\n16\t   cost `{3}{R}{W}` (mana value 5), base P/T 5/5, supertype LEGENDARY, subtypes\n17\t   {Dragon, Elder}, and keywords Flying + Haste. Colors are red+white (one R\n18\t   pip, one W pip, no others).\n19\t2. **Miracle-granting static ability.** While Lorehold is on the battlefield,\n20\t   every instant and sorcery card in its *controller's* hand has miracle {2}.\n21\t   This is a grant, not a cast — the engine has no miracle pipeline, so the\n22\t   implementation must expose some observable surface (a query method on the\n23\t   card, or an attribute on the affected hand card) that reports the granted\n24\t   cost. Only instants/sorceries are affected (not creatures), and only cards\n25\t   in the controller's hand (not the opponent's).\n26\t3. **Loot trigger on each opponent's upkeep.** A\n27\t   `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger that fires ONLY when an opponent is\n28\t   the active player (not on the controller's own upkeep). It is optional\n29\t   (\"you may discard a card\"); the draw is conditional (\"If you do, draw a\n30\t   card\"). Declining, or having an empty hand, results in no discard and no\n31\t   draw.\n32\t\n33\t## Tests by class\n34\t\n35\t### `TestLoreholdProperties` (10 tests)\n36\tStatic-data assertions: `test_is_creature`, `test_name`, `test_mana_cost`,\n37\t`test_mana_value_is_five`, `test_power_toughness`, `test_is_legendary`,\n38\t`test_is_elder_dragon`, `test_has_flying`, `test_has_haste`,\n39\t`test_is_red_white`. Each validates one concrete printed characteristic from\n40\tthe spec.\n41\t\n42\t### `TestLoreholdUpkeepTriggerRegistration` (2 tests)\n43\t- `test_registers_an_upkeep_trigger` — `register_triggers` adds at least one\n44\t  trigger.\n45\t- `test_trigger_watches_upkeep_event` — exactly one of the card's triggers\n46\t  watches `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (the loot ability).\n47\t\n48\t### `TestLoreholdUpkeepTiming` (2 tests) — \"each *opponent's* upkeep\"\n49\t- `test_does_not_fire_on_controllers_own_upkeep` — first asserts an upkeep\n50\t  trigger is registered (so an empty stub fails rather than vacuously passing),\n51\t  then confirms that firing an upkeep event while the controller is the active\n52\t  player puts nothing on the stack.\n53\t- `test_fires_on_opponents_upkeep` — firing the upkeep event while the opponent\n54\t  is active pushes a trigger controlled by the Lorehold controller.\n55\t\n56\t### `TestLoreholdLootEffect` (4 tests) — discard-then-draw resolution\n57\tA shared setup fires an opponent's-upkeep event and asserts the trigger landed\n58\ton the stack (so the no-op cases below cannot pass against an empty stub),\n59\tthen resolves it with a scripted yes/no + card choice.\n60\t- `test_discard_then_draw_on_yes` — yes ⇒ chosen hand card goes to graveyard\n61\t  AND the top of library moves to hand.\n62\t- `test_decline_discards_and_draws_nothing` — no ⇒ hand card stays, top of\n63\t  library stays, nothing drawn or discarded.\n64\t- `test_empty_hand_is_a_noop` — empty hand ⇒ cannot discard, so no draw; does\n65\t  not raise.\n66\t- `test_draw_is_conditional_on_discard` — declining leaves library size\n67\t  unchanged, proving the draw is gated on the discard (\"If you do\").\n68\t\n69\t### `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` (4 tests) — miracle {2} grant\n70\tThese probe the grant surface tolerantly (`_miracle_cost_for` tries a query\n71\tmethod on the card or an attribute on the hand card; it `pytest.skip`s if no\n72\trecognised surface exists, so the contract is never silently green).\n73\t- `test_instant_in_hand_gets_miracle_two` — an instant in the controller's\n74\t  hand reports miracle cost {2}.\n75\t- `test_sorcery_in_hand_gets_miracle_two` — same for a sorcery.\n76\t- `test_creature_in_hand_does_not_get_miracle` — anchored on a real instant\n77\t  (skips if no surface), then asserts a creature is NOT granted miracle.\n78\t- `test_opponents_spell_does_not_get_miracle` — anchored on the controller's\n79\t  own instant, then asserts an instant in the opponent's hand is NOT granted\n80\t  miracle (\"in *your* hand\").\n81\t\n82\t## Edge cases covered\n83\t- \"Each opponent's upkeep\" vs the controller's own upkeep (timing condition).\n84\t- Optional discard declined; empty-hand no-op; draw conditional on discard.\n85\t- Miracle grant scoped to instants/sorceries only, and to the controller's\n86\t  hand only.\n87\t\n88\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n89\t- **Casting a miracled card at draw time** (the operative \"you may cast it when\n90\t  you draw it\" behaviour) — no engine draw-time cast hook exists. Recorded in\n91\t  `untestable.json`.\n92\t- **Flying/haste combat mechanics** — these are engine-level keyword behaviours\n93\t  already covered by `engine_tests` / FDN reference tests (e.g. fdn_142). We\n94\t  only assert that Lorehold *has* the keywords, which is the card's contract.\n95\t- Legend-rule / summoning-sickness interactions — engine concerns, out of scope\n96\t  for this card's text.\n97\t\n98\t## Red-phase confirmation\n99\tAgainst the empty stub: 18 concrete tests FAIL (genuine behavioral assertions,\n100\tno import/syntax errors) and the 4 miracle tests SKIP because no miracle-grant\n101\tsurface exists yet. They activate once the implementer exposes one.\n102\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"a45f312b-cb9d-446d-92ba-e4cf7070860a","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:08:01.178Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_201 Lorehold, the Historian\n\nCard (from `card_spec.json`):\n\n- Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, `{3}{R}{W}`, 5/5, colors R+W.\n- Flying, haste.\n- \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\"\n- \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you\n  do, draw a card.\"\n\nTest file: `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` (22 tests across 5 classes).\n\n## Behaviour contract derived from the oracle text\n\n1. **Static data.** Must be a `Creature` named \"Lorehold, the Historian\" with\n   cost `{3}{R}{W}` (mana value 5), base P/T 5/5, supertype LEGENDARY, subtypes\n   {Dragon, Elder}, and keywords Flying + Haste. Colors are red+white (one R\n   pip, one W pip, no others).\n2. **Miracle-granting static ability.** While Lorehold is on the battlefield,\n   every instant and sorcery card in its *controller's* hand has miracle {2}.\n   This is a grant, not a cast — the engine has no miracle pipeline, so the\n   implementation must expose some observable surface (a query method on the\n   card, or an attribute on the affected hand card) that reports the granted\n   cost. Only instants/sorceries are affected (not creatures), and only cards\n   in the controller's hand (not the opponent's).\n3. **Loot trigger on each opponent's upkeep.** A\n   `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger that fires ONLY when an opponent is\n   the active player (not on the controller's own upkeep). It is optional\n   (\"you may discard a card\"); the draw is conditional (\"If you do, draw a\n   card\"). Declining, or having an empty hand, results in no discard and no\n   draw.\n\n## Tests by class\n\n### `TestLoreholdProperties` (10 tests)\nStatic-data assertions: `test_is_creature`, `test_name`, `test_mana_cost`,\n`test_mana_value_is_five`, `test_power_toughness`, `test_is_legendary`,\n`test_is_elder_dragon`, `test_has_flying`, `test_has_haste`,\n`test_is_red_white`. Each validates one concrete printed characteristic from\nthe spec.\n\n### `TestLoreholdUpkeepTriggerRegistration` (2 tests)\n- `test_registers_an_upkeep_trigger` — `register_triggers` adds at least one\n  trigger.\n- `test_trigger_watches_upkeep_event` — exactly one of the card's triggers\n  watches `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (the loot ability).\n\n### `TestLoreholdUpkeepTiming` (2 tests) — \"each *opponent's* upkeep\"\n- `test_does_not_fire_on_controllers_own_upkeep` — first asserts an upkeep\n  trigger is registered (so an empty stub fails rather than vacuously passing),\n  then confirms that firing an upkeep event while the controller is the active\n  player puts nothing on the stack.\n- `test_fires_on_opponents_upkeep` — firing the upkeep event while the opponent\n  is active pushes a trigger controlled by the Lorehold controller.\n\n### `TestLoreholdLootEffect` (4 tests) — discard-then-draw resolution\nA shared setup fires an opponent's-upkeep event and asserts the trigger landed\non the stack (so the no-op cases below cannot pass against an empty stub),\nthen resolves it with a scripted yes/no + card choice.\n- `test_discard_then_draw_on_yes` — yes ⇒ chosen hand card goes to graveyard\n  AND the top of library moves to hand.\n- `test_decline_discards_and_draws_nothing` — no ⇒ hand card stays, top of\n  library stays, nothing drawn or discarded.\n- `test_empty_hand_is_a_noop` — empty hand ⇒ cannot discard, so no draw; does\n  not raise.\n- `test_draw_is_conditional_on_discard` — declining leaves library size\n  unchanged, proving the draw is gated on the discard (\"If you do\").\n\n### `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` (4 tests) — miracle {2} grant\nThese probe the grant surface tolerantly (`_miracle_cost_for` tries a query\nmethod on the card or an attribute on the hand card; it `pytest.skip`s if no\nrecognised surface exists, so the contract is never silently green).\n- `test_instant_in_hand_gets_miracle_two` — an instant in the controller's\n  hand reports miracle cost {2}.\n- `test_sorcery_in_hand_gets_miracle_two` — same for a sorcery.\n- `test_creature_in_hand_does_not_get_miracle` — anchored on a real instant\n  (skips if no surface), then asserts a creature is NOT granted miracle.\n- `test_opponents_spell_does_not_get_miracle` — anchored on the controller's\n  own instant, then asserts an instant in the opponent's hand is NOT granted\n  miracle (\"in *your* hand\").\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- \"Each opponent's upkeep\" vs the controller's own upkeep (timing condition).\n- Optional discard declined; empty-hand no-op; draw conditional on discard.\n- Miracle grant scoped to instants/sorceries only, and to the controller's\n  hand only.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n- **Casting a miracled card at draw time** (the operative \"you may cast it when\n  you draw it\" behaviour) — no engine draw-time cast hook exists. Recorded in\n  `untestable.json`.\n- **Flying/haste combat mechanics** — these are engine-level keyword behaviours\n  already covered by `engine_tests` / FDN reference tests (e.g. fdn_142). We\n  only assert that Lorehold *has* the keywords, which is the card's contract.\n- Legend-rule / summoning-sickness interactions — engine concerns, out of scope\n  for this card's text.\n\n## Red-phase confirmation\nAgainst the empty stub: 18 concrete tests FAIL (genuine behavioral assertions,\nno import/syntax errors) and the 4 miracle tests SKIP because no miracle-grant\nsurface exists yet. They activate once the implementer exposes one.\n","numLines":102,"startLine":1,"totalLines":102}}}
