{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Ptegr96MxMLQWJoD4HCSQm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SrKYFU3xz7HdpZkTpzJG7B","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace; cat >> RUN_DECISIONS.md <<'EOF'\n## Untestable item: sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian (Miracle grant)\n- Expert-tier {3}{R}{W} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, Flying+Haste.\n- Abilities: (1) \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\" (Miracle, CR 702.93); (2) \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\"\n- Tester wrote 22 tests; 18 concrete fail, 4 Miracle-grant tests SKIP pending a queryable miracle-cost surface. Untestable: the draw-time miracle cast (offer a reduced-cost cast on the first draw of the turn).\n- Engine already has `draw_card()` firing `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` and `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`.\n- **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to build an additive Miracle framework: (i) a continuous grant making instants/sorceries in the controller's hand have miracle {2}, exposed via a queryable surface (method on the card and/or attribute on the hand card) so the 4 skipped tests become real passes; (ii) a draw-time hook that, on the first draw of the turn (DrawsCardTriggeredEvent + cards_drawn_this_turn == 1) of a granted card, offers the drawer a cast at the miracle cost.\n- After Implementer builds it, re-invoke Tester ONCE to cover the draw-time miracle cast (draw a granted instant as the turn's first draw, accept, assert cast paying only {2}; non-first draw doesn't offer).\nEOF\necho \"logged sos_201 decisions\"","description":"Log sos_201 untestable decisions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3401,"cache_read_input_tokens":148358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3401},"output_