{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JjHZivBFWDn2qYunLihhtj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C3QkzhCHdkRY5ANmSGE2yk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n\nCard: **Lorehold, the Historian** — `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon — 5/5 —\nFlying, Haste (expert tier).\nOracle:\n> Flying, haste\n> Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may cast a card for its\n> miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.)\n> At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\n\nThe Tester wrote 22 tests (18 red, 4 Miracle-grant tests currently SKIP pending a queryable\nmiracle-cost surface). Build the missing engine support — ADDITIVELY per AGENTS.md (add new\nmethods/classes/helpers/fields/modules, modify existing function bodies; never rename/move/\ndelete existing engine symbols). Keep the `Keyword` enum at 16 members (Miracle is a printed\nkeyword/label, NOT necessarily a new enum member — do not add to the enum).\n\n## Statics + loot trigger (straightforward — make these pass first)\n- Creature \"Lorehold, the Historian\", `{3}{R}{W}` (mv 5), 5/5, LEGENDARY, subtypes {Dragon, Elder},\n  keywords Flying + Haste, colors R+W.\n- Loot trigger: register exactly one `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger that fires ONLY on\n  each OPPONENT's upkeep (active player is an opponent), NOT the controller's own upkeep. Effect is\n  optional: \"you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\" Decline or empty hand = no discard,\n  no draw (the draw is gated on the discard). Use the standard FDN upkeep-trigger / loot idiom.\n\n## Build an additive Miracle framework\nTwo observable pieces:\n1. **The grant (continuous static ability).** While Lorehold is on the battlefield, every instant\n   and sorcery card in ITS CONTROLLER's hand has miracle {2}. Expose a QUERYABLE surface so a test\n   can read the granted miracle cost — the Tester's tolerant probe `_miracle_cost_for` tries either\n   a query method on the Lorehold card OR an attribute on the affected hand card. Implement at least\n   one of those shapes (e.g. a method `get_miracle_cost(card) -> ManaCost|None` on Lorehold, and/or\n   set a `miracle_cost` attribute on granted hand cards). The grant must be scoped to:\n   - instants and sorceries only (not creatures),\n   - cards in the CONTROLLER's hand only (not the opponent's hand).\n   Make the 4 currently-SKIPPED `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` tests become real PASSES (not skips).\n2. **The draw-time miracle cast hook (CR 702.93).** Add an additive engine miracle hook so that when\n   a player draws a card that has a granted miracle cost AND it is the FIRST card they drew this turn\n   (`DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` + `player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`), the drawer is OFFERED the option\n   to cast it for its miracle cost ({2}). The engine already fires `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` and tracks\n   `cards_drawn_this_turn` — reuse them. Provide a queryable/observable way for a test to: draw a\n   granted instant as the turn's first draw, accept the miracle offer, and confirm it was cast paying\n   only the miracle cost ({2}); and that a non-first draw does NOT offer it.\n\nKeep it additive (a new `engine/miracle.py` module is fine, mirroring `engine/preparation.py` /\n`engine/paradigm.py`). Do NOT break existing draw/upkeep/continuous-effect regression tests.\n\n## Make ALL 22 tests pass (no skips if avoidable)\nIncluding the 4 Miracle-grant tests — implement the real grant surface so they pass.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` → all pass.\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions.\n\nAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester once to add draw-time miracle-cast tests\n(first-draw offer + accept casts for {2}; non-first draw doesn't offer). Build the hook so those are real.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2028,"cache_read_input_tokens":151759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2028},"output_tokens":54,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"04136aaa-7f7b-4797-bde7-d760ec1a477b","request_id":"req_011CbeApvTv4oW7mqUXj9K2c"}
