fy any test file (`cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`), anything under `engine_tests/`, or any FDN `tests.py`.\n- Engine changes ADDITIVE: add a new module/methods/fields, modify existing function bodies; do NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Keep the `Keyword` enum at 16 members (do not add Miracle to the enum).\n- Make ALL 22 tests for sos_201 pass — including the 4 currently-SKIPPED `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` tests (implement a real queryable miracle-cost surface so they pass instead of skip).\n- Run the FULL `pytest` suite from `/workspace`; NO existing engine regression test may break (watch draw/upkeep/continuous-effect tests).\n- If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible (not just hard), do NOT edit it — return DISPUTE.\n\n## Your task\n1. Read directives, spec, tests, rationale, KEY_DECISIONS.md, and `engine/preparation.py`/`engine/paradigm.py`.\n2. Implement `cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`: statics (Elder Dragon, 5/5, Flying+Haste, R+W); the loot trigger on each opponent's upkeep (optional discard, conditional draw); the Miracle {2} grant to instants/sorceries in the controller's hand (queryable surface).\n3. Build an additive Miracle framework (e.g. `engine/miracle.py`): a continuous grant making the controller's hand instants/sorceries report miracle {2}, AND a draw-time hook (first draw of the turn via `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` + `cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`) that offers the drawer a cast at the miracle cost.\n4. Verify: `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` then the full `pytest` suite.\n\n## Outputs (write these)\n- Completed `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` and all engine source changes (incl. any new module).\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl.diff` — `git diff` of implementation+engine files only (exclude tests): `git add -N` new files first, then `git diff -- cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py engine/ > /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl.diff` from `/workspace`.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md` — what you implemented, the Miracle framework API (symbol names), how the grant surface is queried, how the draw-time cast hook works and is gated to the first draw, what you reused, any spec deviations, and EXACTLY how a test would: (a) read the granted miracle cost on a hand instant/sorcery, (b) draw a granted card as the first draw and accept the miracle cast for {2}, (c) confirm a non-first draw does not offer it.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-files.txt` — list of all files changed (one per line).\n- Upsert this card's entry into `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` (match by `card: \"sos_201\"`; replace in place if present). Include engine files in `implementation`.\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nIf all tests pass:\n```\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: <N>\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: <one-line, name the new engine miracle symbols + the grant query surface>\n```\nIf you must dispute a test (write reasoning to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-dispute.md`):\n```\nDISPUTE\ntests_failing: <N>\ndisputed_tests: <list>\ndispute_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-dispute.md\nnotes: <one-line>\n```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SxABS2LYMPLt5MCvzy5rCk","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"14fbd69a-0851-440b-a3fa-40cb963c07a1","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:09:08.150Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_201"}
