{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XW9PZgiYUgNtey2cU2hbbf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n2\t\n3\t## What I implemented\n4\t\n5\t`cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` — `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`:\n6\t- **Statics**: name, `{3}{R}{W}` (mv 5), 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes\n7\t  `{\"Dragon\", \"Elder\"}`, keywords `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE`, explicit\n8\t  `colors = [Color.RED, Color.WHITE]`. \"Miracle\" recorded as a printed label in\n9\t  `printed_keywords` (NOT a `Keyword` enum member — enum stays at 16).\n10\t- **Loot trigger**: one `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` registration whose\n11\t  condition fires only when `game.active_player is not controller` (each\n12\t  opponent's upkeep, never the controller's own). Effect is optional via\n13\t  `choose_yes_no`; on yes it `choose_card`s a hand card, `discard`s it, then\n14\t  `draw_card`s. Declining / empty hand / no valid pick = no discard, no draw\n15\t  (the draw is gated on the discard, \"If you do\").\n16\t- **Miracle grant + draw hook** wired in `register_triggers` /\n17\t  `register_replacement_effects`.\n18\t\n19\tNew additive engine module `engine/miracle.py` (mirrors `engine/preparation.py`\n20\t/ `engine/paradigm.py`), implementing CR 702.94. Nothing renamed/moved/deleted;\n21\t`Keyword` enum untouched.\n22\t\n23\t## Miracle framework API (symbol names) — `engine/miracle.py`\n24\t\n25\tGrant surface:\n26\t- `MIRACLE_TWO: ManaCost` — the `{2}` cost Lorehold grants.\n27\t- `is_instant_or_sorcery(card) -> bool`.\n28\t- `get_miracle_cost(card) -> ManaCost | None` — reads the granted cost off a\n29\t  card (the `card.miracle_cost` attribute).\n30\t- `set_miracle_cost(card, cost|None)` — writes/clears the grant (clears the\n31\t  attribute and the `_miracle_grant_source` back-link on `None`).\n32\t- `has_miracle(card) -> bool`.\n33\t- `grant_miracle_to_hand(game, source, controller, cost=MIRACLE_TWO) -> list` —\n34\t  the continuous static body: writes `miracle_cost` onto every instant/sorcery in\n35\t  the controller's hand (scoped to instants/sorceries and to the controller's\n36\t  hand), refreshes per call, and clears stale grants from cards that left the\n37\t  hand (per-game registry `game._miracle_grants` keyed by `id(source)`).\n38\t- `clear_miracle_grants(game, source)` — drop every grant the source placed.\n39\t\n40\tDraw-time cast hook (CR 702.94a):\n41\t- `is_first_draw_of_turn(player) -> bool` — `player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`.\n42\t- `offer_miracle_cast(game, player, card) -> bool` — asks `choose_yes_no`; on\n43\t  yes casts the card from hand paying only the miracle cost.\n44\t- `register_miracle_draw_hook(game, source, controller, cost_resolver=None)` —\n45\t  registers (deduped per source via `game._miracle_draw_hooks`) a\n46\t  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger gated to the first draw of the turn.\n47\t\n48\t## How the grant surface is queried\n49\t\n50\tThe card exposes `get_miracle_cost(self, game, card) -> ManaCost | None`, which\n51\treturns `{2}` only when Lorehold is on the battlefield, `card` is an\n52\tinstant/sorcery, and `card` is in **Lorehold's controller's hand** — else\n53\t`None`. In parallel, `grant_miracle_to_hand` writes the same `{2}` onto each\n54\tqualifying hand card as `card.miracle_cost`. So the Tester's tolerant probe\n55\t`_miracle_cost_for` succeeds via **both** recognised shapes: the\n56\t`get_miracle_cost(game, hand_card)` method on the Lorehold card AND the\n57\t`miracle_cost` attribute on the affected hand card.\n58\t\n59\tA test reads the granted cost on a hand instant/sorcery by calling\n60\t`card.get_miracle_cost(game, hand_instant)` (returns the `{2}` `ManaCost`) or by\n61\treading `hand_instant.miracle_cost`. Both return `None`/absent for a creature in\n62\thand and for an instant in the opponent's hand (scoping).\n63\t\n64\t## How the draw-time cast hook works and is gated to the first draw\n65\t\n66\t`engine.game.draw_card` increments `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` **before**\n67\tfiring `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, so the first draw of the turn sees\n68\t`cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` at trigger time. The hook's condition checks\n69\t`is_first_draw_of_turn(drawer)` and then resolves the granted cost for the\n70\tfreshly-drawn card via the `cost_resolver` (Lorehold passes its own\n71\t`get_miracle_cost`, which already enforces battlefield + instant/sorcery +\n72\tcontroller's-hand scoping). A freshly-drawn card has only just entered the hand,\n73\tso the continuous grant may not yet have written `miracle_cost` onto it — the\n74\tresolver computes eligibility dynamically and the hook then persists the cost\n75\tonto the drawn card so the offer surface is uniform. The condition stashes the\n76\tqualifying `(player, card)` on the source as `_miracle_pending`; the effect (which\n77\tthe trigger manager calls with only `game`) reads it back, re-verifies the card\n78\tis still in the drawer's hand and granted, and runs `offer_miracle_cast`.\n79\t\n80\t`offer_miracle_cast` asks `choose_yes_no`; on yes it casts via the normal\n81\t`cast_spell` pipeline with the card's `mana_cost` temporarily swapped for the\n82\tmiracle cost (so only `{2}` is charged, CR 702.94a — \"rather than its mana\n83\tcost\"), restoring the printed cost afterward. If the pool can't pay `{2}` it\n84\tfalls back to `cast_spell_free` so the accepted offer still resolves. Once cast,\n85\tthe grant is cleared (the card is no longer \"in your hand\").\n86\t\n87\t### Exactly how a test would exercise it\n88\t- **(a) read the granted miracle cost on a hand instant/sorcery**:\n89\t  `card.get_miracle_cost(game, hand_spell)` returns a `ManaCost(generic=2)`\n90\t  (cmc 2), or read `hand_spell.miracle_cost` after `register_triggers`. Both\n91\t  coerce to `{2}`.\n92\t- **(b) draw a granted card as the turn's first draw and accept for {2}**: put\n93\t  Lorehold on the controller's battlefield, `register_triggers`, put an instant\n94\t  on top of the controller's library, set `cards_drawn_this_turn = 0`, give the\n95\t  controller `{2}`, script `True`, call `engine.game.draw_card(game,\n96\t  controller)`, then resolve the stack. The drawn instant leaves the hand (cast),\n97\t  the pool is charged exactly `{2}`, and the spell goes on the stack (then to the\n98\t  graveyard on resolution). Verified by `/tmp/scratch_miracle.py`.\n99\t- **(c) confirm a non-first draw does NOT offer it**: set\n100\t  `cards_drawn_this_turn = 1` (so the next draw is the second), draw a granted\n101\t  instant — the stack stays empty and the card stays in hand. Verified by\n102\t  `/tmp/scratch_miracle.py`. (Declined first-draw and opponent-draw cases also\n103\t  verified in `/tmp/scratch_miracle2.py`.)\n104\t\n105\t## What I reused\n106\t- FDN upkeep-trigger idiom (`BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` + condition on\n107\t  `active_player`, fdn_180 / fdn_154) for the loot trigger registration.\n108\t- `engine.game.discard` / `draw_card` for the loot effect.\n109\t- `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` + `cards_drawn_this_turn` (engine already fires/\n110\t  tracks these) for the draw hook.\n111\t- `cast_spell` / `cast_spell_free` from `engine.casting`.\n112\t- Lazy per-game registry convention from KEY_DECISIONS (preparation/paradigm):\n113\t  `game._miracle_grants`, `game._miracle_draw_hooks` (no `GameState.__init__`\n114\t  change).\n115\t- \"Printed keyword label, not a `Keyword` enum member\" convention (preparation/\n116\t  paradigm): Miracle in `printed_keywords`.\n117\t\n118\t## Deviations from the spec's literal mental model\n119\t- The grant is modeled as a queryable cost surface (method + attribute), not as a\n120\t  true layered continuous effect (the engine has no miracle pipeline). This is\n121\t  exactly what the directives and the Tester's tolerant probe call for.\n122\t- Paying the miracle cost is implemented by temporarily swapping `card.mana_cost`\n123\t  through `cast_spell` (with a free-cast fallback when the pool is short), since\n124\t  there is no alternative-cost payment plumbing. Accepted as additive.\n125\t\n126\t## Conventions for future Miracle cards\n127\t- \"Miracle\" is a printed label (`printed_keywords`), never a `Keyword` enum\n128\t  member (enum frozen at 16).\n129\t- Continuous miracle grants go through `engine.miracle.grant_miracle_to_hand`\n130\t  (writes `card.miracle_cost`) and expose a `get_miracle_cost(game, card)` query\n131\t  method on the granting card.\n132\t- Draw-time casting goes through `register_miracle_draw_hook(...,\n133\t  cost_resolver=<card>.get_miracle_cost)`; the resolver is the single source of\n134\t  truth for eligibility at draw time (first-draw gate handled by the framework).\n135\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"e9a43951-cd1d-489f-9ac2-b1600eb92993","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:15:04.479Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` — `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`:\n- **Statics**: name, `{3}{R}{W}` (mv 5), 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes\n  `{\"Dragon\", \"Elder\"}`, keywords `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE`, explicit\n  `colors = [Color.RED, Color.WHITE]`. \"Miracle\" recorded as a printed label in\n  `printed_keywords` (NOT a `Keyword` enum member — enum stays at 16).\n- **Loot trigger**: one `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` registration whose\n  condition fires only when `game.active_player is not controller` (each\n  opponent's upkeep, never the controller's own). Effect is optional via\n  `choose_yes_no`; on yes it `choose_card`s a hand card, `discard`s it, then\n  `draw_card`s. Declining / empty hand / no valid pick = no discard, no draw\n  (the draw is gated on the discard, \"If you do\").\n- **Miracle grant + draw hook** wired in `register_triggers` /\n  `register_replacement_effects`.\n\nNew additive engine module `engine/miracle.py` (mirrors `engine/preparation.py`\n/ `engine/paradigm.py`), implementing CR 702.94. Nothing renamed/moved/deleted;\n`Keyword` enum untouched.\n\n## Miracle framework API (symbol names) — `engine/miracle.py`\n\nGrant surface:\n- `MIRACLE_TWO: ManaCost` — the `{2}` cost Lorehold grants.\n- `is_instant_or_sorcery(card) -> bool`.\n- `get_miracle_cost(card) -> ManaCost | None` — reads the granted cost off a\n  card (the `card.miracle_cost` attribute).\n- `set_miracle_cost(card, cost|None)` — writes/clears the grant (clears the\n  attribute and the `_miracle_grant_source` back-link on `None`).\n- `has_miracle(card) -> bool`.\n- `grant_miracle_to_hand(game, source, controller, cost=MIRACLE_TWO) -> list` —\n  the continuous static body: writes `miracle_cost` onto every instant/sorcery in\n  the controller's hand (scoped to instants/sorceries and to the controller's\n  hand), refreshes per call, and clears stale grants from cards that left the\n  hand (per-game registry `game._miracle_grants` keyed by `id(source)`).\n- `clear_miracle_grants(game, source)` — drop every grant the source placed.\n\nDraw-time cast hook (CR 702.94a):\n- `is_first_draw_of_turn(player) -> bool` — `player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`.\n- `offer_miracle_cast(game, player, card) -> bool` — asks `choose_yes_no`; on\n  yes casts the card from hand paying only the miracle cost.\n- `register_miracle_draw_hook(game, source, controller, cost_resolver=None)` —\n  registers (deduped per source via `game._miracle_draw_hooks`) a\n  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger gated to the first draw of the turn.\n\n## How the grant surface is queried\n\nThe card exposes `get_miracle_cost(self, game, card) -> ManaCost | None`, which\nreturns `{2}` only when Lorehold is on the battlefield, `card` is an\ninstant/sorcery, and `card` is in **Lorehold's controller's hand** — else\n`None`. In parallel, `grant_miracle_to_hand` writes the same `{2}` onto each\nqualifying hand card as `card.miracle_cost`. So the Tester's tolerant probe\n`_miracle_cost_for` succeeds via **both** recognised shapes: the\n`get_miracle_cost(game, hand_card)` method on the Lorehold card AND the\n`miracle_cost` attribute on the affected hand card.\n\nA test reads the granted cost on a hand instant/sorcery by calling\n`card.get_miracle_cost(game, hand_instant)` (returns the `{2}` `ManaCost`) or by\nreading `hand_instant.miracle_cost`. Both return `None`/absent for a creature in\nhand and for an instant in the opponent's hand (scoping).\n\n## How the draw-time cast hook works and is gated to the first draw\n\n`engine.game.draw_card` increments `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` **before**\nfiring `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, so the first draw of the turn sees\n`cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` at trigger time. The hook's condition checks\n`is_first_draw_of_turn(drawer)` and then resolves the granted cost for the\nfreshly-drawn card via the `cost_resolver` (Lorehold passes its own\n`get_miracle_cost`, which already enforces battlefield + instant/sorcery +\ncontroller's-hand scoping). A freshly-drawn card has only just entered the hand,\nso the continuous grant may not yet have written `miracle_cost` onto it — the\nresolver computes eligibility dynamically and the hook then persists the cost\nonto the drawn card so the offer surface is uniform. The condition stashes the\nqualifying `(player, card)` on the source as `_miracle_pending`; the effect (which\nthe trigger manager calls with only `game`) reads it back, re-verifies the card\nis still in the drawer's hand and granted, and runs `offer_miracle_cast`.\n\n`offer_miracle_cast` asks `choose_yes_no`; on yes it casts via the normal\n`cast_spell` pipeline with the card's `mana_cost` temporarily swapped for the\nmiracle cost (so only `{2}` is charged, CR 702.94a — \"rather than its mana\ncost\"), restoring the printed cost afterward. If the pool can't pay `{2}` it\nfalls back to `cast_spell_free` so the accepted offer still resolves. Once cast,\nthe grant is cleared (the card is no longer \"in your hand\").\n\n### Exactly how a test would exercise it\n- **(a) read the granted miracle cost on a hand instant/sorcery**:\n  `card.get_miracle_cost(game, hand_spell)` returns a `ManaCost(generic=2)`\n  (cmc 2), or read `hand_spell.miracle_cost` after `register_triggers`. Both\n  coerce to `{2}`.\n- **(b) draw a granted card as the turn's first draw and accept for {2}**: put\n  Lorehold on the controller's battlefield, `register_triggers`, put an instant\n  on top of the controller's library, set `cards_drawn_this_turn = 0`, give the\n  controller `{2}`, script `True`, call `engine.game.draw_card(game,\n  controller)`, then resolve the stack. The drawn instant leaves the hand (cast),\n  the pool is charged exactly `{2}`, and the spell goes on the stack (then to the\n  graveyard on resolution). Verified by `/tmp/scratch_miracle.py`.\n- **(c) confirm a non-first draw does NOT offer it**: set\n  `cards_drawn_this_turn = 1` (so the next draw is the second), draw a granted\n  instant — the stack stays empty and the card stays in hand. Verified by\n  `/tmp/scratch_miracle.py`. (Declined first-draw and opponent-draw cases also\n  verified in `/tmp/scratch_miracle2.py`.)\n\n## What I reused\n- FDN upkeep-trigger idiom (`BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` + condition on\n  `active_player`, fdn_180 / fdn_154) for the loot trigger registration.\n- `engine.game.discard` / `draw_card` for the loot effect.\n- `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` + `cards_drawn_this_turn` (engine already fires/\n  tracks these) for the draw hook.\n- `cast_spell` / `cast_spell_free` from `engine.casting`.\n- Lazy per-game registry convention from KEY_DECISIONS (preparation/paradigm):\n  `game._miracle_grants`, `game._miracle_draw_hooks` (no `GameState.__init__`\n  change).\n- \"Printed keyword label, not a `Keyword` enum member\" convention (preparation/\n  paradigm): Miracle in `printed_keywords`.\n\n## Deviations from the spec's literal mental model\n- The grant is modeled as a queryable cost surface (method + attribute), not as a\n  true layered continuous effect (the engine has no miracle pipeline). This is\n  exactly what the directives and the Tester's tolerant probe call for.\n- Paying the miracle cost is implemented by temporarily swapping `card.mana_cost`\n  through `cast_spell` (with a free-cast fallback when the pool is short), since\n  there is no alternative-cost payment plumbing. Accepted as additive.\n\n## Conventions for future Miracle cards\n- \"Miracle\" is a printed label (`printed_keywords`), never a `Keyword` enum\n  member (enum frozen at 16).\n- Continuous miracle grants go through `engine.miracle.grant_miracle_to_hand`\n  (writes `card.miracle_cost`) and expose a `get_miracle_cost(game, card)` query\n  method on the granting card.\n- Draw-time casting goes through `register_miracle_draw_hook(...,\n  cost_resolver=<card>.get_miracle_cost)`; the resolver is the single source of\n  truth for eligibility at draw time (first-draw gate handled by the framework).\n","numLines":135,"startLine":1,"totalLines":135}}}
