{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0179Abuq9QyL9UkqzRSE5EK3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KJbA7QyF9c3QV9RxaZh8H1","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Extend tests for sos_201 miracle draw","subagent_type":"Tester","prompt":"You previously wrote 22 tests for card **sos_201** (\"Lorehold, the Historian\", a {3}{R}{W} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon). The Implementer has now built an additive `engine/miracle.py` framework, so the previously-deferred draw-time Miracle cast (and the now-real grant surface) are testable. Extend your test file to cover them.\n\n## Context: your existing work\n- Existing tests: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` (22 tests; the 4 `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` tests should now PASS rather than skip — verify). EXTEND this file — keep existing tests unchanged, ADD new ones.\n- Your prior rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md`.\n- Your deferred item: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/untestable.json`.\n- Implementer's rationale with the EXACT new API and concrete observation recipes: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md` — READ THIS (esp. \"Exactly how a test would exercise it\").\n\n## New API to test against\n- On the Lorehold card: `card.get_miracle_cost(game, hand_card) -> ManaCost | None` (returns {2} for a controller's-hand instant/sorcery while Lorehold is on the battlefield; None otherwise). Also `hand_card.miracle_cost` is set on granted cards.\n- `engine.miracle`: `is_first_draw_of_turn(player)`, `offer_miracle_cast(game, player, card)`, `register_miracle_draw_hook(...)`, `grant_miracle_to_hand(...)`, `MIRACLE_TWO`.\n- Draw-time flow (per impl-rationale recipe (b)): put Lorehold on the controller's battlefield, call the card's `register_triggers`, put an instant on top of the controller's library, set `controller.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0`, give the controller `{2}` mana, script `True` (accept), call `engine.game.draw_card(game, controller)`, then resolve the stack. The drawn instant should be cast paying exactly {2} (leaves hand, lands on stack, then graveyard).\n\n## Your task — add tests for the previously-untestable draw-time miracle cast\n1. **First-draw accept casts for {2}**: follow recipe (b). Assert the drawn granted instant is cast (leaves hand, on stack / resolves to graveyard) and the controller's pool was charged exactly {2} (not its full cost). \n2. **First-draw decline keeps it in hand**: script `False` — the drawn instant stays in hand, stack empty, mana not spent.\n3. **Non-first draw does NOT offer**: set `controller.cards_drawn_this_turn = 1` so the next draw is the second; draw a granted instant — no offer (stack empty, card stays in hand).\n4. **Opponent's draw is not offered Lorehold's grant**, and a drawn CREATURE (non-instant/sorcery) is not offered miracle.\n5. Match the exact `draw_card` / `fire_event` / stack-resolution API by checking `engine/game.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, and how existing tests resolve the stack (e.g. sos_57/sos_120 patterns, `engine_tests/`).\n\n## Constraints\n- DO NOT modify `engine_tests/`, FDN `tests.py`, or any engine source. Only edit `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`.\n- DO NOT change or weaken existing tests — only add new ones. You MAY remove the `pytest.skip` fallback from the 4 `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` tests now that the grant surface is real (only if you are certain they pass).\n- The implementation already exists, so your new tests should PASS. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` and confirm everything passes. If a new test reveals a genuine implementation bug, leave the failing test in place and report it (do not paper over it).\n\n## Outputs\n- Updated `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`.\n- Append a \"## Extended coverage\" section to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md`.\n- Keep `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-files.txt` accurate (same single file).\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn: total test count now, how many you added, pass/fail result of `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`, and `new_failures: <N>` (with reasons if any)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3823,"cache_read_input_tokens":158334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3823},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"ebbdba1e-2022-4c97-b357-8ee4b23eff0c","request_id":"req_011CbeBLNFm7rBb8JRAhLhYo"}
