{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019r29LEt11owZUgHcHbeBgx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"requirement\": \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.)\",\n4\t    \"reason\": \"The 'you may cast it for its miracle cost as you draw it (if it's the first card drawn this turn)' timing has no engine surface to assert against. There is no miracle pipeline: draw_card() does fire DrawsCardTriggeredEvent and tracks player.cards_drawn_this_turn, but there is no engine hook that offers a draw-time cast at the reduced cost, and no API to query/exercise the reduced-cost cast. The tests assert the GRANT (that an instant/sorcery in the controller's hand reports miracle {2}, scoped to instants/sorceries and to the controller's hand) via a tolerant probe, but cannot assert the actual draw-time cast-for-{2} behaviour or the first-card-drawn-this-turn gating.\",\n5\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"An additive engine miracle hook: e.g. a casting helper that, on the first draw of the turn (DrawsCardTriggeredEvent + cards_drawn_this_turn == 1), offers the drawn card's controller a free/alternative cast at the granted miracle cost, plus a queryable surface for the granted miracle cost on a hand card. With that, a test could draw a granted instant as the turn's first draw, accept the miracle offer, and assert it was cast paying only {2}.\"\n6\t  }\n7\t]\n8\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KJbA7QyF9c3QV9RxaZh8H1","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"905172c7-e70c-480b-a04e-2aee1e5d0da4","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:15:27.443Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_201 miracle draw"}
