{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QYUoZq1SjD5XRcLgPviCj4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DCAmNmzgRv7f7WtnQPRBbW","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md","old_string":"## Red-phase confirmation\nAgainst the empty stub: 18 concrete tests FAIL (genuine behavioral assertions,\nno import/syntax errors) and the 4 miracle tests SKIP because no miracle-grant\nsurface exists yet. They activate once the implementer exposes one.","new_string":"## Red-phase confirmation\nAgainst the empty stub: 18 concrete tests FAIL (genuine behavioral assertions,\nno import/syntax errors) and the 4 miracle tests SKIP because no miracle-grant\nsurface exists yet. They activate once the implementer exposes one.\n\n## Extended coverage\n\nAfter the Implementer shipped the additive `engine/miracle.py` framework\n(continuous grant + draw-time cast hook, wired by `register_triggers`), the\npreviously-deferred draw-time miracle cast became testable. The 4\n`TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` tests now PASS (no longer skip) because the real\ngrant surface (`card.get_miracle_cost(game, hand_card)` and the `miracle_cost`\nattribute the framework writes) satisfies the tolerant `_miracle_cost_for`\nprobe.\n\n### New class `TestLoreholdMiracleDrawCast` (7 tests)\nExercises CR 702.94a — \"you may cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw\nit if it's the first card you drew this turn\" — through the real engine pipeline\n(`engine.game.draw_card` fires `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`; the hook's offer lands\non the stack and is resolved like any other trigger). Setup helpers:\n`_put_on_top_of_library` deterministically stocks one card on top of a player's\nlibrary; `_expensive_instant` uses a `{4}{R}{R}` (mv 6) instant so \"charged\nexactly {2}\" is unambiguous against the printed cost.\n\n- `test_first_draw_accept_casts_for_two` — accept on the turn's first draw: the\n  drawn instant leaves hand and resolves to graveyard. Anchored on\n  \"offer reached the stack as a result of the draw\" so a missing hook fails\n  loudly rather than passing vacuously.\n- `test_first_draw_accept_charges_exactly_two` — with a 5-mana pool, exactly two\n  are spent (three remain), proving the miracle cost {2} is paid rather than the\n  printed {6}; the printed `mana_cost` is restored afterward (not mutated).\n- `test_first_draw_decline_keeps_card_in_hand` — decline: card stays in hand, no\n  mana spent, stack empty after resolution (the yes/no is asked when the offer\n  resolves, and \"no\" is a no-op).\n- `test_non_first_draw_is_not_offered` — `cards_drawn_this_turn = 1` so the next\n  draw is the second: no offer, stack empty, card stays in hand. No yes/no\n  scripted, so an unconditioned hook would raise `ScriptExhaustedError`.\n- `test_opponent_first_draw_is_not_offered_loreholds_grant` — Lorehold grants\n  only to ITS controller's hand; an opponent's first draw is not offered.\n- `test_drawn_creature_is_not_offered_miracle` — a drawn creature (non\n  instant/sorcery) triggers no offer.\n- `test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two` — the grant covers sorceries\n  too; accepting a first-drawn sorcery should cast it for {2}.\n\n### Known failing test (genuine implementation limitation — left in place)\n`test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two` FAILS. Root cause (diagnosed\ndirectly): the draw-time miracle cast routes through\n`engine.casting.cast_spell`, which enforces sorcery-speed timing\n(`is_sorcery_speed(game, player)`). The instant cases pass because instants\nbypass that gate (`can_cast_at_instant_speed` is True), but a sorcery cast at\ndraw time — which is exactly when miracle fires, and which is generally NOT a\nsorcery-speed window — is rejected; `_cast_for_miracle_cost` swallows the\nresulting `CastingError` and returns False, so the sorcery silently stays in\nhand. When the game state is forced to sorcery speed, the same sorcery casts\ncorrectly for {2}, confirming the gate is the cause. This is a real\nasymmetry: the grant explicitly covers \"each instant and sorcery card\", and\nmiracle creates its own casting window, so a granted sorcery should be castable\nat draw time. The test is left FAILING per the directive not to paper over a\ngenuine implementation bug.\n\n### Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (extended)\n- Multiple eligible draws in one turn (only the first is offerable; the\n  `test_non_first_draw_is_not_offered` case already pins the first-draw gate).\n- Interaction with replacement-based extra draws or simultaneous multi-card\n  draws — out of scope for this card's text and not exercised by a single\n  `draw_card` call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_read_input_tokens":74972,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":339,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KJbA7QyF9c3QV9RxaZh8H1","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"cb508bec-6722-4517-8e0a-05c4b7c35e8c","request_id":"req_011CbeBbHGnefYMG85e6pH5n","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_201 miracle draw"}
