y edit `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`.\n- DO NOT change or weaken existing tests — only add new ones. You MAY remove the `pytest.skip` fallback from the 4 `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` tests now that the grant surface is real (only if you are certain they pass).\n- The implementation already exists, so your new tests should PASS. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` and confirm everything passes. If a new test reveals a genuine implementation bug, leave the failing test in place and report it (do not paper over it).\n\n## Outputs\n- Updated `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`.\n- Append a \"## Extended coverage\" section to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md`.\n- Keep `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-files.txt` accurate (same single file).\n\n## Return (status summary only)\nReturn: total test count now, how many you added, pass/fail result of `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`, and `new_failures: <N>` (with reasons if any).","agentId":"ad3088282b3e85bc0","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TESTS_EXTENDED\n\ntotal_test_cases: 29 (was 22, added 7)\ntest_files: 1 (`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`)\npytest_result: 28 passed, 1 failed\nnew_failures: 1\n\nThe 4 pre-existing `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` tests now PASS (no longer skip) — the real `get_miracle_cost` / `miracle_cost` grant surface satisfies the tolerant probe, so I left the dead `pytest.skip` fallback harmlessly in place rather than touching existing tests.\n\nNew class `TestLoreholdMiracleDrawCast` (7 tests) covers the previously-deferred CR 702.94a draw-time cast through the real `engine.miracle` hook:\n- `test_first_draw_accept_casts_for_two` — accept on first draw casts the instant (leaves hand, resolves to graveyard); anchored on the offer reaching the stack.\n- `test_first_draw_accept_charges_exactly_two` — charges exactly {2} (pool 5 → 3), printed {6} cost restored, not the full cost.\n- `test_first_draw_decline_keeps_card_in_hand` — decline keeps it in hand, no mana spent, stack empties.\n- `test_non_first_draw_is_not_offered` — `cards_drawn_this_turn = 1` → no offer.\n- `test_opponent_first_draw_is_not_offered_loreholds_grant` — opponent's draw not offered (controller-hand scoping).\n- `test_drawn_creature_is_not_offered_miracle` — non-instant/sorcery not offered.\n- `test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two` — **FAILING** (see below).\n\n**new_failures reason (genuine implementation limitation, left in place per directive):** `test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two` fails because the draw-time miracle cast routes a sorcery through `engine.casting.cast_spell`, which enforces sorcery-speed timing (`is_sorcery_speed`). Miracle fires during the draw — generally not a sorcery-speed window — so the sorcery cast raises `CastingError`, which `_cast_for_miracle_cost` silently swallows, leaving the sorcery in hand. Instants pass because they bypass the timing gate. I confirmed via diagnosis that forcing sorcery-speed timing makes the same sorcery cast correctly for {2}, so the gate is the root cause. The grant text explicitly covers \"each instant and sorcery card\", and miracle creates its own casting window, so a granted sorcery should be castable at draw time — this is a real asymmetry worth surfacing. Not papered over.\n\nUpdated `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md` (appended \"## Extended coverage\") and emptied `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/untestable.json` (the deferred item is now exercised; the residual sorcery-timing gap is carried by the failing test). `test-files.txt` unchanged (still the single file)."}],"totalDurationMs":229826,"totalTokens":79060,"totalToolUseCount":33,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":361,"cache_read_input_tokens":77658,"output_tokens":1039,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":361},"inference_geo":"not_available","iteratio