{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's explicit request: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics... Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   \n   I operate as a \"Coordinator\" agent orchestrating three subagents (Tester, Implementer, Reviewer) in a TDD loop per card.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG card implementation engine (Python), workspace root on sys.path (bare imports like `from cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl import ...`, `from engine.card import Creature, Instant`)\n   - TDD red→green→review workflow with subagents (Tester/Implementer/Reviewer at `~/.claude/agents/`)\n   - Engine modules: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/turn.py`, `engine/game.py`, `engine/game_state.py`, `engine/player.py`, `engine/types.py`, `engine/continuous_effects.py`, `engine/abilities.py`, `engine/mana.py`\n   - ADDITIVE-only engine changes: may add methods/classes/helpers/enum members and modify function bodies; MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing symbols\n   - `Keyword` enum FROZEN at 16 members (`engine_tests/test_types.py::test_exactly_sixteen_members` hard-asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`) — new keywords stored as `printed_keywords` labels, NOT enum members\n   - Lazy per-game registry pattern (e.g. `game._prepared_copies`, `game._paradigm_resolved`, `game._miracle_grants`) — avoids modifying `GameState.__init__`\n   - New mechanics frameworks built: Preparation (CR 722), Paradigm (CR 702.192), Miracle (CR 702.94), coin-flip RNG, skip-turn counter, main-phase event, delayed/one-shot triggers, mana_spent tracking, stack→graveyard redirect\n   - `python` command NOT available — use `pytest` directly. Tests run from `/workspace`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md` — workspace orientation/rules. Card paths: `cards/sos/sos_<N>/{card_spec.json,card_impl.py,tests.py}`. FDN cards with tests.py: fdn_13, fdn_142, fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_244.\n   - `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` — persistent append-only log; I've appended conventions for each completed card (stack→graveyard redirect, Converge/colors_spent, Preparation framework, delayed one-shot triggers + main-phase event + mana_spent, coin-flip RNG + skip-turn, Paradigm framework). Each amended into the card's commit.\n   - `/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md` — per-run decisions log (untestable arbitrations).\n   - `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` — `{\"cards\": [...]}` upserted by Implementer per card.\n   - `engine/casting.py` — added `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card, destination)`, `clear_stack_to_graveyard_redirect`, `_redirect_registry`, `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc`; modified `_resolve_spell` body.\n   - `engine/preparation.py` (NEW) — `mark_prepared`, `unprepare`, `is_prepared`, `get_prepared_copy`, `get_prepared_source`, `cast_prepared_copy` (casts first, unprepares only on success per CR 722.3c).\n   - `engine/events.py` — added `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, precombat)`.\n   - `engine/turn.py` — fires `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` at main phases (additive elif).\n   - `engine/triggers.py` — added `TriggerRegistration.one_shot: bool = False`, `TriggerManager.register_delayed(...)`; `fire_event` removes matched one_shot triggers.\n   - `engine/game.py` — added `get_rng`, `seed_rng`, `flip_coin`, `flip_coins`, `add_skipped_turns`.\n   - `engine/player.py` — added `Player.skipped_turns: int = 0`.\n   - `engine/game_state.py` — added `_next_active_index_raw()`, `_pick_next_active_index()` (consumes skipped_turns).\n   - `engine/paradigm.py` (NEW) — `mark_paradigm_resolved`, `has_paradigm_resolved`, `register_paradigm` (recurring trigger via TriggerManager.register), `offer_paradigm_copy`, `is_paradigm_copy`, `is_castable_spell`.\n   - `engine/miracle.py` (NEW, current card sos_201) — `MIRACLE_TWO: ManaCost` ({2}), `is_instant_or_sorcery`, `get_miracle_cost(card)`, `set_miracle_cost`, `has_miracle`, `grant_miracle_to_hand(game, source, controller, cost)`, `clear_miracle_grants`, `is_first_draw_of_turn(player)` (`cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`), `offer_miracle_cast(game, player, card)`, `register_miracle_draw_hook(game, source, controller, cost_resolver)`. The draw-time cast uses `_cast_for_miracle_cost` which temporarily swaps `card.mana_cost` for the miracle cost through `cast_spell` (free-cast fallback if pool short). **BUG: it silently swallows CastingError, and `cast_spell` enforces sorcery-speed timing so sorceries fail.**\n   - `cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` — `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`: statics, opponent-upkeep loot trigger, `get_miracle_cost(self, game, card)` query (returns {2} for controller's-hand instants/sorceries while on battlefield), wires `grant_miracle_to_hand` + `register_miracle_draw_hook`.\n   - `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` — 29 tests; new class `TestLoreholdMiracleDrawCast` (7 tests), one failing: `test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **sos_1**: \"exile it instead\" clause untestable via natural path — fixed by adding stack→graveyard redirect registry to engine/casting.py.\n   - **sos_13**: Reviewer found 1 strict bug — `cast_prepared_copy` unprepared the source BEFORE casting (if cast raises, source wrongly unprepared + copy orphaned). Fixed: cast first, clear designation only on cast success (CR 722.3c). Implementer also reverted an initial `Keyword.PREPARED` enum addition because it broke `test_exactly_sixteen_members`.\n   - **sos_201 (CURRENT, UNRESOLVED)**: Tester's extended test `test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two` FAILS. Root cause confirmed genuine: draw-time miracle cast routes a sorcery through `engine.casting.cast_spell` which enforces sorcery-speed timing (`is_sorcery_speed`); miracle fires during a draw (not a sorcery-speed window), so the sorcery cast raises `CastingError`, silently swallowed by `_cast_for_miracle_cost`, leaving the sorcery in hand. Instants pass (bypass the gate). I grepped RULEBOOK.txt line 4670 (CR 702.94a) confirming Miracle grants permission to \"cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost\" when revealed on draw — this casting window should bypass normal sorcery-speed timing. The test is CORRECT; the implementation must be fixed. **NOT YET FIXED.**\n   - Recurring minor: leftover `FILES_MODIFIED.json.tmp` removed before each commit; `python` not found (use `pytest`).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Established a robust pattern: when Tester flags untestable engine-gap items on a new mechanic, I arbitrate as case (a) — write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_<N>/coordinator-directives.md`, direct Implementer to build additive engine support, then re-invoke Tester ONCE to extend coverage of now-testable behavior, then Reviewer.\n   - Built 4 reusable engine frameworks (Preparation, Paradigm, Miracle) plus infrastructure (coin-flip RNG, skip-turn, main-phase event, delayed triggers) that later cards reuse (documented in KEY_DECISIONS.md).\n   - Currently solving: sos_201 sorcery-timing bug in the miracle draw-cast.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - (Final message) Instruction to produce a TEXT-ONLY summary with no tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Fix sos_201 miracle sorcery-timing bug** (make draw-time miracle cast bypass sorcery-speed timing so granted sorceries cast for {2}), get all 29 tests passing.\n   - Complete sos_201: Reviewer pass, commit, log conventions, clean scratch.\n   - Implement remaining cards: **sos_226, sos_245, sos_257** (4 of 10 remaining: 201 in progress, plus 226, 245, 257).\n   - Before run ends: ensure RUN_DECISIONS.md content worth preserving is migrated into KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I was on **sos_201 \"Lorehold, the Historian\"**. The Implementer built `engine/miracle.py` and the card, all 22 original tests + the 4 grant tests passed (1387 total). I re-invoked the Tester to extend coverage of the draw-time miracle cast. The Tester reported 29 tests (28 passed, 1 failed): `test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two` FAILS because the miracle draw-cast routes a sorcery through `engine.casting.cast_spell` which enforces sorcery-speed timing, raising a swallowed `CastingError`. I confirmed the test is correct by grepping RULEBOOK.txt: line 4670 \"702.94a Miracle is a static ability linked to a triggered ability... 'When you reveal this card this way, you may cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost.'\" This confirms the miracle casting window should bypass normal sorcery-speed timing. I had just decided to direct the Implementer to fix this real bug (NOT a test dispute — the Tester found a legitimate implementation limitation). The scratch dir `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/` contains: tests.py (in workspace), test-rationale.md, impl-rationale.md, coordinator-directives.md, impl.diff, FILES_MODIFIED.json upserted; untestable.json was emptied by the Tester. The full suite was last at 1387 passed (before the failing extended test was added — note: the failing test is in the workspace tests.py now).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Re-invoke the Implementer for sos_201 to fix the genuine bug the Tester found: make the draw-time miracle cast bypass the sorcery-speed timing gate so a granted sorcery can be cast at draw time for {2}, making all 29 tests pass without breaking regressions. The Tester's exact finding: \"test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two fails because the draw-time miracle cast routes a sorcery through engine.casting.cast_spell, which enforces sorcery-speed timing (is_sorcery_speed). Miracle fires during the draw — generally not a sorcery-speed window — so the sorcery cast raises CastingError, which _cast_for_miracle_cost silently swallows, leaving the sorcery in hand. Instants pass because they bypass the timing gate... a granted sorcery should be castable at draw time — this is a real asymmetry worth surfacing