{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QyNDtVK9dyor24ezzEMPd4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Lorehold, the Historian** — `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon — 5/5 —\n4\tFlying, Haste (expert tier).\n5\tOracle:\n6\t> Flying, haste\n7\t> Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may cast a card for its\n8\t> miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.)\n9\t> At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\n10\t\n11\tThe Tester wrote 22 tests (18 red, 4 Miracle-grant tests currently SKIP pending a queryable\n12\tmiracle-cost surface). Build the missing engine support — ADDITIVELY per AGENTS.md (add new\n13\tmethods/classes/helpers/fields/modules, modify existing function bodies; never rename/move/\n14\tdelete existing engine symbols). Keep the `Keyword` enum at 16 members (Miracle is a printed\n15\tkeyword/label, NOT necessarily a new enum member — do not add to the enum).\n16\t\n17\t## Statics + loot trigger (straightforward — make these pass first)\n18\t- Creature \"Lorehold, the Historian\", `{3}{R}{W}` (mv 5), 5/5, LEGENDARY, subtypes {Dragon, Elder},\n19\t  keywords Flying + Haste, colors R+W.\n20\t- Loot trigger: register exactly one `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger that fires ONLY on\n21\t  each OPPONENT's upkeep (active player is an opponent), NOT the controller's own upkeep. Effect is\n22\t  optional: \"you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\" Decline or empty hand = no discard,\n23\t  no draw (the draw is gated on the discard). Use the standard FDN upkeep-trigger / loot idiom.\n24\t\n25\t## Build an additive Miracle framework\n26\tTwo observable pieces:\n27\t1. **The grant (continuous static ability).** While Lorehold is on the battlefield, every instant\n28\t   and sorcery card in ITS CONTROLLER's hand has miracle {2}. Expose a QUERYABLE surface so a test\n29\t   can read the granted miracle cost — the Tester's tolerant probe `_miracle_cost_for` tries either\n30\t   a query method on the Lorehold card OR an attribute on the affected hand card. Implement at least\n31\t   one of those shapes (e.g. a method `get_miracle_cost(card) -> ManaCost|None` on Lorehold, and/or\n32\t   set a `miracle_cost` attribute on granted hand cards). The grant must be scoped to:\n33\t   - instants and sorceries only (not creatures),\n34\t   - cards in the CONTROLLER's hand only (not the opponent's hand).\n35\t   Make the 4 currently-SKIPPED `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` tests become real PASSES (not skips).\n36\t2. **The draw-time miracle cast hook (CR 702.93).** Add an additive engine miracle hook so that when\n37\t   a player draws a card that has a granted miracle cost AND it is the FIRST card they drew this turn\n38\t   (`DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` + `player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`), the drawer is OFFERED the option\n39\t   to cast it for its miracle cost ({2}). The engine already fires `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` and tracks\n40\t   `cards_drawn_this_turn` — reuse them. Provide a queryable/observable way for a test to: draw a\n41\t   granted instant as the turn's first draw, accept the miracle offer, and confirm it was cast paying\n42\t   only the miracle cost ({2}); and that a non-first draw does NOT offer it.\n43\t\n44\tKeep it additive (a new `engine/miracle.py` module is fine, mirroring `engine/preparation.py` /\n45\t`engine/paradigm.py`). Do NOT break existing draw/upkeep/continuous-effect regression tests.\n46\t\n47\t## Make ALL 22 tests pass (no skips if avoidable)\n48\tIncluding the 4 Miracle-grant tests — implement the real grant surface so they pass.\n49\t\n50\t## Verification\n51\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` → all pass.\n52\t- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions.\n53\t\n54\tAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester once to add draw-time miracle-cast tests\n55\t(first-draw offer + accept casts for {2}; non-first draw doesn't offer). Build the hook so those are real.\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## FOLLOW-UP DIRECTIVE (round 2): fix the genuine sorcery draw-cast bug\n60\t\n61\tThe Tester extended coverage with `TestLoreholdMiracleDrawCast` (7 tests). 28/29 pass.\n62\tONE genuine implementation bug remains — this is NOT a test dispute; the test is correct\n63\tand must pass:\n64\t\n65\t`test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two` FAILS. Root cause (confirmed):\n66\t`engine/miracle.py::_cast_for_miracle_cost` routes the draw-time cast through\n67\t`engine.casting.cast_spell`, which enforces sorcery-speed timing\n68\t(`is_sorcery_speed(game, player)`). Miracle fires during a draw — generally NOT a\n69\tsorcery-speed window — so casting a granted SORCERY raises `CastingError`, which\n70\t`_cast_for_miracle_cost` silently swallows, leaving the sorcery in hand. Instants pass\n71\tbecause they bypass the timing gate.\n72\t\n73\tPer CR 702.94a, miracle creates its own casting permission (\"you may cast it by paying\n74\t[cost] rather than its mana cost\") when the card is revealed on draw — this casting\n75\twindow is NOT bound by normal sorcery-speed timing. The grant explicitly covers \"each\n76\tinstant and sorcery card\", so a granted sorcery MUST be castable at draw time for {2}.\n77\t\n78\tFix it ADDITIVELY so the miracle draw-cast bypasses the sorcery-speed timing gate for\n79\tsorceries (e.g. pass a timing-override/ignore_timing flag through the cast path, or use\n80\tthe existing free-cast/`cast_spell_free` path which already bypasses timing, or add an\n81\tadditive parameter to `cast_spell` that callers can opt into). Do NOT weaken normal\n82\tsorcery-speed enforcement for ordinary casts — only the miracle draw-cast may bypass it.\n83\tAlso STOP silently swallowing a genuine `CastingError` in a way that hides real failures:\n84\tthe miracle cast must actually succeed for a granted sorcery.\n85\t\n86\tConstraints:\n87\t- Do NOT modify any test file in test-files.txt.\n88\t- Keep all 29 tests in cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py passing (instants AND the sorcery).\n89\t- ADDITIVE engine changes only (no rename/move/delete of existing symbols); `Keyword`\n90\t  enum stays at 16.\n91\t- Full `pytest` from /workspace must show no regressions.\n92\t\n93\tRegenerate impl.diff / impl-rationale.md / impl-files.txt and upsert FILES_MODIFIED.json.\n94\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0161xMeCEMDGx7Qwdiz8uz1c","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"6e9050a8-d329-432b-864e-6816550559dd","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:21:42.222Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Fix sos_201 miracle sorcery draw-cast"}
