{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ajkveMfaggHkTY2NvZLjS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Tests for SOS 201 — Lorehold, the Historian.\n2\t\n3\tOracle text (from card_spec.json):\n4\t\n5\t    Flying, haste\n6\t    Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may cast\n7\t    a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you\n8\t    drew this turn.)\n9\t    At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you\n10\t    do, draw a card.\n11\t\n12\tBehaviour contract derived from that text:\n13\t\n14\t* Static: Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, red+white, with\n15\t  Flying and Haste.\n16\t* Miracle-granting static ability: while Lorehold is on the battlefield, every\n17\t  instant and sorcery card in its controller's hand \"has miracle {2}\". There is\n18\t  no engine-level miracle pipeline, so the implementation must expose some\n19\t  observable surface that reports the miracle cost ({2}) for an instant/sorcery\n20\t  in the controller's hand (and grants it to no other cards / no other\n21\t  players). These tests probe that surface tolerantly: they accept any of the\n22\t  conventional spellings the implementer is likely to use, and skip-with-reason\n23\t  only if none exists. The \"cast it when you draw it\" timing is recorded in\n24\t  untestable.json (no engine draw-time cast hook exists).\n25\t* Upkeep trigger: a ``BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`` trigger that fires only\n26\t  on an OPPONENT's upkeep (not the controller's own upkeep). It is optional\n27\t  (\"you may discard a card\"); if a card is discarded the controller draws a\n28\t  card. Declining discards nothing and draws nothing. With an empty hand there\n29\t  is nothing to discard, so nothing is drawn.\n30\t\n31\tThese tests are written for the TDD red phase: they must FAIL against the empty\n32\tstub and PASS once the card is implemented correctly.\n33\t\"\"\"\n34\t\n35\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n36\t\n37\tfrom typing import Any\n38\t\n39\timport pytest\n40\t\n41\tfrom cards.sos.sos_201.card_impl import LoreholdTheHistorian\n42\tfrom engine.card import Creature, Instant, Sorcery\n43\tfrom engine.events import BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent\n44\tfrom engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n45\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Supertype, Zone\n46\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n47\t\n48\t\n49\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n50\t# Test helper cards\n51\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n52\t\n53\t\n54\tdef _vanilla_instant(name: str = \"Test Instant\") -> Instant:\n55\t    return Instant(name=name, mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{R}\"))\n56\t\n57\t\n58\tdef _vanilla_sorcery(name: str = \"Test Sorcery\") -> Sorcery:\n59\t    return Sorcery(name=name, mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{2}{B}\"))\n60\t\n61\t\n62\tdef _vanilla_creature(name: str = \"Test Bear\") -> Creature:\n63\t    return Creature(\n64\t        name=name,\n65\t        mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{G}\"),\n66\t        base_power=2,\n67\t        base_toughness=2,\n68\t    )\n69\t\n70\t\n71\tdef _resolve_full_stack(game: Any) -> None:\n72\t    \"\"\"Resolve every object currently on the stack, top-down.\"\"\"\n73\t    from engine.state_based_actions import resolve_state_based_actions\n74\t\n75\t    while not game.stack.is_empty():\n76\t        obj = game.stack.pop()\n77\t        obj.on_resolve(game)\n78\t        resolve_state_based_actions(game)\n79\t\n80\t\n81\tdef _miracle_cost_for(card_obj: Any, game: Any, hand_card: Any) -> Any:\n82\t    \"\"\"Best-effort probe for the granted miracle cost of *hand_card*.\n83\t\n84\t    The miracle mechanic has no engine pipeline, so the implementation is free\n85\t    to surface the granted cost in a number of conventional ways. This helper\n86\t    tries each in turn and returns the reported cost, or raises\n87\t    ``pytest.skip`` if no recognised surface exists (so the contract is not\n88\t    silently green).\n89\t    \"\"\"\n90\t    # 1. A method on the Lorehold card that reports the miracle cost it grants\n91\t    #    to a given hand card.\n92\t    for meth_name in (\"miracle_cost_for\", \"get_miracle_cost\", \"miracle_cost\"):\n93\t        meth = getattr(card_obj, meth_name, None)\n94\t        if callable(meth):\n95\t            try:\n96\t                return meth(game, hand_card)\n97\t            except TypeError:\n98\t                try:\n99\t                    return meth(hand_card)\n100\t                except TypeError:\n101\t                    continue\n102\t    # 2. The grant written directly onto the hand card.\n103\t    for attr_name in (\"miracle_cost\", \"granted_miracle_cost\", \"miracle\"):\n104\t        val = getattr(hand_card, attr_name, None)\n105\t        if val is not None:\n106\t            return val\n107\t    pytest.skip(\n108\t        \"No observable surface for the granted miracle cost — implementation \"\n109\t        \"must expose miracle_cost_for(...)/get_miracle_cost(...) on the card \"\n110\t        \"or a miracle_cost attribute on the affected hand card.\"\n111\t    )\n112\t\n113\t\n114\tdef _coerce_to_two(value: Any) -> bool:\n115\t    \"\"\"Return True if *value* represents a mana value / cost of {2}.\"\"\"\n116\t    if value is None:\n117\t        return False\n118\t    if isinstance(value, ManaCost):\n119\t        return value.cmc == 2 and value.generic == 2\n120\t    if isinstance(value, int):"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0161xMeCEMDGx7Qwdiz8uz1c","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"7e471e1c-8ed2-4d15-a089-ecfe3ec8dc81","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:21:54.689Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Fix sos_201 miracle sorcery draw-cast"}
