{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RjecFTHSPb2V1g8ekXq3e9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VQX7MU428epAGvJBt7Md4o","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md","old_string":"## Conventions for future Miracle cards\n- \"Miracle\" is a printed label (`printed_keywords`), never a `Keyword` enum\n  member (enum frozen at 16).\n- Continuous miracle grants go through `engine.miracle.grant_miracle_to_hand`\n  (writes `card.miracle_cost`) and expose a `get_miracle_cost(game, card)` query\n  method on the granting card.\n- Draw-time casting goes through `register_miracle_draw_hook(...,\n  cost_resolver=<card>.get_miracle_cost)`; the resolver is the single source of\n  truth for eligibility at draw time (first-draw gate handled by the framework).","new_string":"## Conventions for future Miracle cards\n- \"Miracle\" is a printed label (`printed_keywords`), never a `Keyword` enum\n  member (enum frozen at 16).\n- Continuous miracle grants go through `engine.miracle.grant_miracle_to_hand`\n  (writes `card.miracle_cost`) and expose a `get_miracle_cost(game, card)` query\n  method on the granting card.\n- Draw-time casting goes through `register_miracle_draw_hook(...,\n  cost_resolver=<card>.get_miracle_cost)`; the resolver is the single source of\n  truth for eligibility at draw time (first-draw gate handled by the framework).\n\n## Round 2 fix — granted SORCERY draw-cast bypasses sorcery-speed timing\n\n### The bug\n`test_first_draw_sorcery_accept_casts_for_two` failed. The grant covers \"each\ninstant and sorcery card\", so a first-drawn sorcery must be castable for {2} at\ndraw time. But miracle fires during a *draw*, which is not a sorcery-speed window\n(not the active player's main phase with an empty stack). `cast_spell` enforces\nsorcery-speed timing for any non-instant/non-flash card, so casting the granted\nsorcery raised `CastingError` — which the old `_cast_for_miracle_cost` caught in a\nbroad `except CastingError: return False`, silently swallowing the failure and\nleaving the sorcery in hand. Instants passed because `can_cast_at_instant_speed`\nshort-circuits the timing gate for them.\n\nPer CR 702.94a, miracle creates its own casting permission when the card is\nrevealed on draw (\"you may cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost\").\nThat window is not bound by normal sorcery-speed timing, so a granted sorcery must\nbe castable then.\n\n### The fix (additive only)\n1. **`engine/casting.py::cast_spell`** — added an opt-in keyword parameter\n   `ignore_timing: bool = False` (safe default preserves existing behaviour for\n   every current caller). When `True`, only the step-1 sorcery-speed timing gate\n   is skipped; all other legality checks (`can_cast`, hand membership, targeting,\n   protection, mana payment) are unchanged. No symbol was renamed/moved/deleted;\n   this is a pure signature extension plus a guard on the existing timing branch\n   (`if not ignore_timing and not can_cast_at_instant_speed(...) and not\n   is_sorcery_speed(...)`). Normal sorcery-speed enforcement for ordinary casts is\n   untouched — callers that don't opt in still hit the full gate.\n\n2. **`engine/miracle.py::_cast_for_miracle_cost`** — the draw-time miracle cast\n   now calls `cast_spell(game, player, card, ignore_timing=True)`, so a granted\n   sorcery casts at draw time for {2} just like an instant. The mana-pool-short\n   fallback still uses `cast_spell_free` (which has no timing gate). Crucially,\n   the broad `except CastingError: return False` was removed: a genuine\n   `CastingError` raised by the cast itself (after the timing gate is bypassed)\n   now propagates instead of being silently swallowed, so a real failure surfaces\n   rather than hiding behind a card left in hand.\n\n### Why normal enforcement is not weakened\n`ignore_timing` defaults to `False`, and the only caller that passes `True` is the\nmiracle draw-cast path. Every other cast (player actions, other cards, the engine)\ncontinues to go through the unchanged timing gate. A sorcery cast outside a\nsorcery-speed window via the ordinary path still raises `CastingError` exactly as\nbefore.\n\n### Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` → 29 passed (instants AND the sorcery).\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → 1394 passed, 0 failed (no regressions; the\n  warnings are pre-existing `ScriptExhaustedError` cleanup-discard warnings\n  unrelated to this change).\n\n### Convention added\nCasting permissions that create their own timing window (miracle today; flashback\nfrom-graveyard-at-sorcery-speed-only variants, \"cast this as though it had flash\",\netc. in future) should funnel through `cast_spell(..., ignore_timing=True)` rather\nthan re-implementing the cast pipeline or relying on `cast_spell_free` when a real\ncost must still be paid. Do not catch `CastingError` broadly around such a cast —\nlet genuine failures propagate."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":207,"cache_read_input_tokens":50422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":207,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0161xMeCEMDGx7Qwdiz8uz1c","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"238a81e9-2480-4b81-be8c-dbcb89e5085b","request_id":"req_011CbeBxKpR95PXJYTtwwjr1","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Fix sos_201 miracle sorcery draw-cast"}
