{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_018mf4ZHffKpCtHnD5i5QUq4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FATb1Ln12X4EzLkcKrxM8b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 8,\n    \"comment\": \"Unused imports: `CardType` and `Zone` are imported from engine.types but never referenced in card_impl.py (the type/zone checks live in engine.miracle). Harmless and likely flagged by ruff/flake8 F401; drop them to keep the import list honest.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 72,\n    \"comment\": \"`self.colors = [Color.RED, Color.WHITE]` stores Color enum members, whereas the existing card-stub convention (cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py) stores string color codes like ['W']. No engine code in this diff reads `colors`, and the red/white test asserts on pips not `self.colors`, so this is cosmetic — but the mismatch could surprise any future consumer that expects the string form. Consider matching the established representation.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 206,\n    \"comment\": \"Broad `except Exception` around `choose_yes_no` (line 207) and `choose_card` (line 219) in _resolve_loot silently turns any chooser failure into a no-op. This will also swallow a genuine bug signal such as ScriptExhaustedError, masking a divergence between the implementation's choice flow and what callers expect. Prefer catching nothing here (let real errors surface) or narrowing to the specific decline/abort signal you intend to tolerate.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 160,\n    \"comment\": \"The upkeep trigger's `_condition` predicate has a side effect: it calls `source._apply_miracle_grant(g)` while merely evaluating whether the trigger should fire. Because fire_event evaluates conditions for every BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (including those that don't ultimately fire), the grant refresh runs as a condition side effect rather than as part of the resolved effect. It works for the tests, but mixing mutation into a should-this-fire predicate is a smell; consider refreshing the grant in the effect body or via a dedicated upkeep hook.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"engine/miracle.py\",\n    \"line\": 638,\n    \"comment\": \"register_miracle_draw_hook's `_condition` mutates state during should-fire evaluation: it writes set_miracle_cost(drawn, cost) and stashes source._miracle_pending. This is functionally fine for a single source/single draw (the `_effect` re-validates has_miracle + hand membership and clears the pending), but conditions are expected to be side-effect-free predicates. The stash-on-source pattern would also be fragile if the same source registered/evaluated overlapping draws; an explicit per-event payload would be cleaner.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":712,"cache_read_input_tokens":83417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":712,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JCfMWFKdgoCucx4JkLHXXa","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"a20482d7-d6ed-4ab6-99b8-7cd2ca7a2c73","request_id":"req_011CbeC9kzYmxDdf5JJ5ArJv","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_201 implementation"}
