{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JCfMWFKdgoCucx4JkLHXXa","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've completed a thorough review of the sos_201 implementation. The implementation is correct against the card spec and tests, with all the key sanity checks passing:\n\n- **Statics** ({3}{R}{W}, 5/5, Legendary Elder Dragon, Flying+Haste, R+W) all match the spec.\n- **Opponent-only upkeep loot trigger** is correctly gated (`g.active_player is not ctrl`), optional, and the draw is conditional on the discard.\n- **`ignore_timing`** defaults to `False` (ordinary casts still enforce sorcery-speed timing) and is only opted into by the miracle draw-cast path.\n- **Draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s** — the cast in `_cast_for_miracle_cost` runs inside a `try/finally` that only restores `mana_cost`, and the free-cast fallback has no swallowing wrapper, so real failures propagate.\n- **Additive discipline** holds: `Keyword` stays at 16 members, `engine/casting.py` only adds a defaulted parameter, `engine/miracle.py` is a new file, and no existing engine symbols were renamed/moved/deleted. The card class lives at the required path.\n\nNo strict issues found. I filed 5 advisory notes (unused imports, `Color`-enum vs string-color convention mismatch, broad exception swallowing in the loot resolver, and side-effecting trigger condition predicates in both the loot and draw hooks).\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 5\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a54e403f577020131 (use SendMessage with to: 'a54e403f577020131' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 87079\ntool_uses: 20\nduration_ms: 123401</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"ed6ef69f-0df1-4027-a797-35e7f97aaa64","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:26:25.168Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Review the implementation for card sos_201 \"Lorehold, the Historian\" ({3}{R}{W} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, Flying + Haste; grants miracle {2} to instants/sorceries in its controller's hand; loot trigger on each opponent's upkeep).\n\nInputs:\n- Diff to review: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl.diff`\n- `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` — cards completed earlier this run; do NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards.\n- `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` — established conventions; do NOT flag anything that conforms to these.\n\nWhat to review: correctness vs. the card's spec intent, real bugs, missed edge cases, and convention violations VISIBLE IN THE DIFF. Key things to sanity-check:\n- The card statics (cost/PT/types/keywords/colors) and the opponent-only upkeep loot trigger (optional discard; draw gated on the discard).\n- The additive Miracle framework in `engine/miracle.py` and the new `ignore_timing` opt-in parameter added to `engine/casting.py::cast_spell`: confirm it defaults to False (so ordinary casts still enforce sorcery-speed timing) and is only opted into by the miracle draw-cast path. Confirm the draw-cast no longer silently swallows genuine CastingErrors in a way that hides real failures.\n- Additive-only discipline: no rename/move/delete of existing engine symbols; `Keyword` enum stays at 16 members.\n\nImportant constraints:\n- Do NOT demand test rewrites — the tests were already arbitrated. Test-quality concerns are `advisory` only.\n- Do NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards (see FILES_MODIFIED.json) or conventions in KEY_DECISIONS.md (e.g. the printed-keyword-label convention, lazy per-game registries).\n\nWrite `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json` as a JSON array of objects `{\"severity\": \"strict\"|\"advisory\", \"file\", \"line\", \"comment\"}`. Use empty array `[]` if no comments.\n\nReturn:\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json","agentId":"a54e403f577020131","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've completed a thorough review of the sos_201 implementation. The implementation is correct against the card spec and tests, with all the key sanity checks passing:\n\n- **Statics** ({3}{R}{W}, 5/5, Legendary Elder Dragon, Flying+Haste, R+W) all match the spec.\n- **Opponent-only upkeep loot trigger** is correctly gated (`g.active_player is not ctrl`), optional, and the draw is conditional on the discard.\n- **`ignore_timing`** defaults to `False` (ordinary casts still enforce sorcery-speed timing) and is only opted into by the miracle draw-cast path.\n- **Draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s** — the cast in `_cast_for_miracle_cost` runs inside a `try/finally` that only restores `mana_cost`, and the free-cast fallback has no swallowing wrapper, so real failures propagate.\n- **Additive discipline** holds: `Keyword` stays at 16 members, `engine/casting.py` only adds a defaulted parameter, `engine/miracle.py` is a new file, and no existing engine symbols were renamed/moved/deleted. The card class lives at the required path.\n\nNo strict issues found. I filed 5 advisory notes (unused imports, `Color`-enum vs string-color convention mismatch, broad exception swallowing in the loot resolver, and side-effecting trigger condition predicates in both the loot and draw hooks).\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 5\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json"}],"totalDurationMs":123401,"totalTokens":87079,"totalToolUseCount":20,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2403,"cache_read_input_tokens":84129,"output_tokens":545,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2403},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":545,"cache_read_input_tokens":84129,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2403,"cache_creation":{"ephemer