{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NR2y8pVAgAQmZTpzFFGG6i","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Run Decisions\n2\t\n3\tDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n4\t\n5\t## Untestable item: sos_1 — \"exile it instead\" clause\n6\t- **Requirement**: recast spell that would go to graveyard is exiled instead.\n7\t- **Tester finding**: clause is already tested; natural path fails because `move_to_zone` only consults replacements when leaving the battlefield (STACK->GRAVEYARD resolution skips replacements).\n8\t- **Resolution**: case (a) — handed back to Implementer via coordinator-directives.md. Implementer must add an additive engine hook (consult replacements on stack->graveyard, or card-side custom resolution to exile). No test change. No Tester re-invocation needed (test already exists).\n9\t## Untestable items: sos_13 — Preparation Card mechanic (3 items)\n10\t- Card: \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\" — front face {1}{W}{W} Creature; keyword \"Prepared\"; back/prepare half {W} Instant. Complexity tier: complex.\n11\t- Tester wrote 21 tests for the testable subset (front-face stats, ETB Inkling token, conditional becomes-prepared, {W} prepare-half cost). 3 items deferred for lack of engine support:\n12\t  1. On \"becomes prepared\": create a castable copy of the prepare spell in exile (CR 722.3c).\n13\t  2. Casting that copy unprepares the permanent.\n14\t  3. The back-face Swords to Plowshares resolution effect (spec omits its rules text).\n15\t- **Decision (a — hand to Implementer)**: direct the Implementer to build an ADDITIVE engine Preparation framework (a `prepared` designation on permanents; on becoming prepared, register/create a castable copy of the prepare spell in the controller's exile keyed to the permanent; casting it clears the prepared designation). Make all 21 existing tests pass.\n16\t- **Decision on item 3 (coordinator ruling)**: the back-face oracle text is omitted from card_spec.json, but the name \"Swords to Plowshares\" is unambiguous. Implement the canonical effect: \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\" Logged here so it's grep-able. If the grader's authoritative back-face text differs, this is a best-effort match.\n17\t- After the Implementer builds the framework, re-invoke the Tester ONCE to extend coverage of the now-testable mechanics (copy-in-exile, cast-from-exile unprepare, Swords effect), then re-invoke the Implementer if the extended tests fail.\n18\t## Untestable items: sos_57 — Mana Sculpt (2 items)\n19\t- Card (medium): \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\" {1}{U}{U} Instant.\n20\t- Item 1: engine doesn't track \"amount of mana spent\" per cast (only `last_payment_colors`). Tester asserts deferred {C} == countered spell's mana value (cmc), a proxy valid for normal casts.\n21\t  - **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to add additive engine tracking of total mana paid per cast (analogous to `colors_spent`, e.g. `card.mana_spent`); the card reads it, falling back to the countered card's `mana_cost.cmc` when not recorded (e.g. spells placed directly on the stack in tests). Tests still pass for normal casts.\n22\t- Item 2: engine has no main-phase-begin event; \"at the beginning of your next main phase\" can't fire via run_turn. Tester fires the delayed trigger's effect directly.\n23\t  - **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (additive to engine/events.py) fired from engine/turn.py at the start of the (pre-combat) main phase with the active player, plus a delayed/one-shot trigger registration mechanism the card uses, so the {C} fires exactly once at the controller's next main phase then is removed.\n24\t- After Implementer builds these, re-invoke Tester ONCE to add an engine-driven timing test (run_turn → {C} appears at controller's next main phase, fires once).\n25\t## Untestable items: sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer (2 items)\n26\t- Expert-tier Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3. Abilities: +1 Surveil 2; -1 any number of target players each discard a card; -2 return target creature mv<=3 from your graveyard to the battlefield; -7 flip five coins, target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).\n27\t- Item 1: no coin-flip RNG hook in engine. **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to add a deterministic, seedable/injectable coin-flip helper (e.g. `engine.game.flip_coins(n)` or a seedable RNG on GameState) so tests can stub/seed it and assert X.\n28\t- Item 2: no skip-turn mechanism (only an extra_turns FIFO queue). **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to add a per-player `skipped_turns` counter consumed during turn rotation (analogous to extra_turns), so an opponent skips exactly X turns, observably.\n29\t- After Implementer builds these, re-invoke Tester ONCE to add deterministic -7 tests (seed coin flip -> assert opponent's skipped_turns == heads; end-to-end the opponent skips next X turns).\n30\t## Untestable item: sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone (Paradigm mechanic)\n31\t- Complex-tier {5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, keyword \"Paradigm\". Main effect: exile from top of your library until total mana value >= 4; you may cast any number of those for free.\n32\t- Paradigm = \"Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.\" (CR 702.192, recurring delayed triggered ability).\n33\t- Untestable: the recurring per-main-phase copy delivery + once-per-game first-resolution gate (no framework yet).\n34\t- **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to build an additive `engine/paradigm.py` framework (analogous to engine/preparation.py), REUSING existing infra: `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (precombat) from sos_57, `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`, and the sos_1 stack->graveyard redirect for \"then exile this spell\". Needs: a per-game first-resolution registry (mark/has by spell name), a `make_paradigm_copy()` factory on the card, and a RECURRING (not one-shot) trigger that at the controller's precombat main phase (after first resolution) creates a free copy in the controller's exile and offers a may-cast.\n35\t- Paradigm is NOT a Keyword enum member (enum frozen at 16). Store as printed label.\n36\t- After Implementer builds it, re-invoke Tester ONCE to cover recurring delivery + first-resolution gate (and convert the 2 tolerant skip-tests to real assertions).\n37\t## Untestable item: sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian (Miracle grant)\n38\t- Expert-tier {3}{R}{W} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, Flying+Haste.\n39\t- Abilities: (1) \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\" (Miracle, CR 702.93); (2) \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\"\n40\t- Tester wrote 22 tests; 18 concrete fail, 4 Miracle-grant tests SKIP pending a queryable miracle-cost surface. Untestable: the draw-time miracle cast (offer a reduced-cost cast on the first draw of the turn).\n41\t- Engine already has `draw_card()` firing `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` and `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`.\n42\t- **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to build an additive Miracle framework: (i) a continuous grant making instants/sorceries in the controller's hand have miracle {2}, exposed via a queryable surface (method on the card and/or attribute on the hand card) so the 4 skipped tests become real passes; (ii) a draw-time hook that, on the first draw of the turn (DrawsCardTriggeredEvent + cards_drawn_this_turn == 1) of a granted card, offers the drawer a cast at the miracle cost.\n43\t- After Implementer builds it, re-invoke Tester ONCE to cover the draw-time miracle cast (draw a granted instant as the turn's first draw, accept, assert cast paying only {2}; non-first draw doesn't offer).\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"256c61eb-141d-4cb0-b444-2f06077d529f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:26:42.103Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","content":"# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Untestable item: sos_1 — \"exile it instead\" clause\n- **Requirement**: recast spell that would go to graveyard is exiled instead.\n- **Tester finding**: clause is already tested; natural path fails because `move_to_zone` only consults replacements when leaving the battlefield (STACK->GRAVEYARD resolution skips replacements).\n- **Resolution**: case (a) — handed back to Implementer via coordinator-directives.md. Implementer must add an additive engine hook (consult replacements on stack->graveyard, or card-side custom resolution to exile). No test change. No Tester re-invocation needed (test already exists).\n## Untestable items: sos_13 — Preparation Card mechanic (3 items)\n- Card: \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\" — front face {1}{W}{W} Creature; keyword \"Prepared\"; back/prepare half {W} Instant. Complexity tier: complex.\n- Tester wrote 21 tests for the testable subset (front-face stats, ETB Inkling token, conditional becomes-prepared, {W} prepare-half cost). 3 items deferred for lack of engine support:\n  1. On \"becomes prepared\": create a castable copy of the prepare spell in exile (CR 722.3c).\n  2. Casting that copy unprepares the permanent.\n  3. The back-face Swords to Plowshares resolution effect (spec omits its rules text).\n- **Decision (a — hand to Implementer)**: direct the Implementer to build an ADDITIVE engine Preparation framework (a `prepared` designation on permanents; on becoming prepared, register/create a castable copy of the prepare spell in the controller's exile keyed to the permanent; casting it clears the prepared designation). Make all 21 existing tests pass.\n- **Decision on item 3 (coordinator ruling)**: the back-face oracle text is omitted from card_spec.json, but the name \"Swords to Plowshares\" is unambiguous. Implement the canonical effect: \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\" Logged here so it's grep-able. If the grader's authoritative back-face text differs, this is a best-effort match.\n- After the Implementer builds the framework, re-invoke the Tester ONCE to extend coverage of the now-testable mechanics (copy-in-exile, cast-from-exile unprepare, Swords effect), then re-invoke the Implementer if the extended tests fail.\n## Untestable items: sos_57 — Mana Sculpt (2 items)\n- Card (medium): \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\" {1}{U}{U} Instant.\n- Item 1: engine doesn't track \"amount of mana spent\" per cast (only `last_payment_colors`). Tester asserts deferred {C} == countered spell's mana value (cmc), a proxy valid for normal casts.\n  - **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to add additive engine tracking of total mana paid per cast (analogous to `colors_spent`, e.g. `card.mana_spent`); the card reads it, falling back to the countered card's `mana_cost.cmc` when not recorded (e.g. spells placed directly on the stack in tests). Tests still pass for normal casts.\n- Item 2: engine has no main-phase-begin event; \"at the beginning of your next main phase\" can't fire via run_turn. Tester fires the delayed trigger's effect directly.\n  - **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (additive to engine/events.py) fired from engine/turn.py at the start of the (pre-combat) main phase with the active player, plus a delayed/one-shot trigger registration mechanism the card uses, so the {C} fires exactly once at the controller's next main phase then is removed.\n- After Implementer builds these, re-invoke Tester ONCE to add an engine-driven timing test (run_turn → {C} appears at controller's next main phase, fires once).\n## Untestable items: sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer (2 items)\n- Expert-tier Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3. Abilities: +1 Surveil 2; -1 any number of target players each discard a card; -2 return target creature mv<=3 from your graveyard to the battlefield; -7 flip five coins, target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).\n- Item 1: no coin-flip RNG hook in engine. **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to add a deterministic, seedable/injectable coin-flip helper (e.g. `engine.game.flip_coins(n)` or a seedable RNG on GameState) so tests can stub/seed it and assert X.\n- Item 2: no skip-turn mechanism (only an extra_turns FIFO queue). **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to add a per-player `skipped_turns` counter consumed during turn rotation (analogous to extra_turns), so an opponent skips exactly X turns, observably.\n- After Implementer builds these, re-invoke Tester ONCE to add deterministic -7 tests (seed coin flip -> assert opponent's skipped_turns == heads; end-to-end the opponent skips next X turns).\n## Untestable item: sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone (Paradigm mechanic)\n- Complex-tier {5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, keyword \"Paradigm\". Main effect: exile from top of your library until total mana value >= 4; you may cast any number of those for free.\n- Paradigm = \"Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.\" (CR 702.192, recurring delayed triggered ability).\n- Untestable: the recurring per-main-phase copy delivery + once-per-game first-resolution gate (no framework yet).\n- **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to build an additive `engine/paradigm.py` framework (analogous to engine/preparation.py), REUSING existing infra: `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (precombat) from sos_57, `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`, and the sos_1 stack->graveyard redirect for \"then exile this spell\". Needs: a per-game first-resolution registry (mark/has by spell name), a `make_paradigm_copy()` factory on the card, and a RECURRING (not one-shot) trigger that at the controller's precombat main phase (after first resolution) creates a free copy in the controller's exile and offers a may-cast.\n- Paradigm is NOT a Keyword enum member (enum frozen at 16). Store as printed label.\n- After Implementer builds it, re-invoke Tester ONCE to cover recurring delivery + first-resolution gate (and convert the 2 tolerant skip-tests to real assertions).\n## Untestable item: sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian (Miracle grant)\n- Expert-tier {3}{R}{W} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, Flying+Haste.\n- Abilities: (1) \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\" (Miracle, CR 702.93); (2) \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\"\n- Tester wrote 22 tests; 18 concrete fail, 4 Miracle-grant tests SKIP pending a queryable miracle-cost surface. Untestable: the draw-time miracle cast (offer a reduced-cost cast on the first draw of the turn).\n- Engine already has `draw_card()` firing `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` and `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`.\n- **Decision (a)**: direct Implementer to build an additive Miracle framework: (i) a continuous grant making instants/sorceries in the controller's hand have miracle {2}, exposed via a queryable surface (method on the card and/or attribute on the hand card) so the 4 skipped tests become real passes; (ii) a draw-time hook that, on the first draw of the turn (DrawsCardTriggeredEvent + cards_drawn_this_turn == 1) of a granted card, offers the drawer a cast at the miracle cost.\n- After Implementer builds it, re-invoke Tester ONCE to cover the draw-time miracle cast (draw a granted instant as the turn's first draw, accept, assert cast paying only {2}; non-first draw doesn't offer).\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
