so the first draw sees count==1 at trigger time.\n- Card-side: the granting card exposes a `get_miracle_cost(self, game, card) -> ManaCost|None` query (returns the grant only when the source is on the battlefield, `card` is instant/sorcery, and `card` is in the source's controller's hand). Wire `grant_miracle_to_hand` + `register_miracle_draw_hook(..., cost_resolver=self.get_miracle_cost)` in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects`. \"Miracle\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, NOT a Keyword enum member (frozen at 16).\n- Engine: `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` gained an additive `ignore_timing: bool = False` parameter. When True it bypasses the sorcery-speed timing gate (`is_sorcery_speed`/`can_cast_at_instant_speed`) — used ONLY by the miracle draw-cast so a granted SORCERY can be cast at draw time (its own casting window per CR 702.94a, not bound by sorcery-speed). Defaults False so all existing callers are unaffected. Convention: alternative casting windows that grant their own timing permission opt into `ignore_timing=True`; never weaken normal enforcement for ordinary casts. The miracle draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s in a way that hides real failures."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4019,"cache_read_input_tokens":42030,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4019},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"2df15e3b-4123-442d-b071-0489aea050cc","request_id":"req_011CbeCEHL3Cx6DxYMmUHSey"}
