{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a57a6047c5c96a17c","tool_use_id":"toolu_01AepSwRZkXZzkfUhV74jmjw","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Tester","usage":{"total_tokens":78525,"tool_uses":27,"duration_ms":166554},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"ed2a7b8d-2052-47cd-bac8-d61729fb864f","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_015rdqkaBNxvC4xGeX7iicxf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B3mQkW4Ff5dEA3MkhX8Wup","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_226 \"Silverquill, the Disputant\"\n\n## Behaviour contract under test\n\n`{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4, colors B+W, Flying + Vigilance.\n\nOracle:\n> Flying, vigilance\n> Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you cast that spell,\n> you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When you do, copy the spell\n> and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\n\nTwo contracts:\n\n1. **Static card data** — types, cost (mv 4), P/T 4/4, LEGENDARY supertype,\n   {Dragon, Elder} subtypes, Flying + Vigilance evergreen keywords, B+W colors.\n2. **Casualty-granting continuous static ability** — while Silverquill is on the\n   battlefield, every instant and sorcery SPELL its controller casts \"has\n   casualty 1\" (CR 702.153a). Casualty 1 = \"as an additional cost you may\n   sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater; when you do, copy the spell and\n   may choose new targets for the copy.\"\n\nThe engine has **no casualty pipeline** (confirmed: only sos_226's own spec and\nRULEBOOK.txt mention \"casualty\"). Following the precedent set by sos_201's\nmiracle tests, the casualty *grant* is probed through a tolerant observable\nsurface (a query method on the card and/or an attribute on the affected spell),\nand the casualty *resolution* mechanic (paying the cost by sacrificing a\npower>=1 creature, then producing a copy with optional new targets) is deferred\nto `untestable.json` until the Coordinator decides whether to build engine\nsupport.\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`\n\n### `TestSilverquillProperties` — static data\n- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature` subclass.\n- `test_name` — name is exactly \"Silverquill, the Disputant\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — cost parses to `{2}{W}{B}`.\n- `test_mana_value_is_four` — mana value 4.\n- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T is 4/4.\n- `test_is_legendary` — LEGENDARY supertype.\n- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes include both \"Dragon\" and \"Elder\".\n- `test_has_flying` — FLYING evergreen keyword present.\n- `test_has_vigilance` — VIGILANCE evergreen keyword present.\n- `test_is_white_black` — cost pips are exactly one W and one B, zero R/U/G.\n  This is the canonical, surface-independent colour pin (sos_201 used the same\n  pip-based approach).\n- `test_colors_are_black_and_white` — if the impl exposes a `colors` attribute\n  it must be exactly `{WHITE, BLACK}`; skips (the pip test covers colours)\n  otherwise, so it never fails just because the impl chose not to expose a\n  redundant attribute.\n- `test_casualty_is_printed_keyword_label_not_enum` — enforces the frozen-enum\n  convention from KEY_DECISIONS: \"Casualty\" is NOT a `Keyword` enum member\n  (`Keyword` is frozen at 16; `engine_tests/test_types.py` hard-asserts that).\n  Asserts `Keyword` has no `CASUALTY` member; if the card exposes\n  `printed_keywords`, \"Casualty\" must be among the labels (skips that half if no\n  such surface exists).\n\n### `TestSilverquillCasualtyGrant` — the casualty grant surface\nTolerant probe `_casualty_value_for(...)` tries, in order: card query methods\n(`casualty_value_for`/`get_casualty_value`/`casualty_for`/`get_casualty`/\n`casualty_value`) then spell attributes (`casualty_value`/`casualty`/\n`granted_casualty`); `pytest.skip` with a clear reason if none exists (so the\ncontract is never silently green). `_coerce_to_one(...)` normalises the reported\nvalue (int / numeric string / object `.value`/`.n`/`.amount`/`.cmc`) to \"== 1\",\nand deliberately treats a bare `True` flag as NOT a confirmation of the specific\nvalue 1 (a card that merely flags \"has casualty\" without N=1 should not pass).\n\n- `test_instant_gets_casualty_one` — a controller-hand instant is granted\n  casualty 1.\n- `test_sorcery_gets_casualty_one` — a controller-hand sorcery is granted\n  casualty 1 (the grant covers sorceries, not just instants).\n- `test_creature_spell_does_not_get_casualty` — scope: a creature spell is\n  neither instant nor sorcery, so no casualty. **Anchored** on a real instant\n  (via the skipping probe) so an empty stub fails rather than passing vacuously,\n  then asserts the creature is excluded via the silent probe.\n- `test_opponents_instant_does_not_get_casualty` — scope: only spells YOU cast\n  get casualty; an opponent's instant is unaffected. Anchored on a\n  controller-side instant.\n- `test_no_grant_while_off_battlefield` — a permanent's static ability functions\n  only while on the battlefield. With Silverquill in hand the grant is off.\n  Anchored on a parallel on-battlefield setup that DOES grant, so an impl that\n  always returns a value is caught while a genuinely-absent surface skips.\n\n### `TestSilverquillGrantWiring`\n- `test_card_exposes_a_casualty_grant_surface` — the **hard anchor**: the impl\n  must expose at least one recognised casualty-grant surface (a card query\n  method, or an attribute it writes onto an affected spell). This is the one\n  grant-side test that FAILS (not skips) against the empty stub, guaranteeing\n  the casualty contract is never silently green even if every tolerant probe\n  skips.\n\n## Why \"spell\" is modelled as a hand card\n\nThe probe puts the affected instant/sorcery in the controller's hand and queries\nthe grant there. CR 702.153 grants casualty \"as you cast\" the spell; the grant\nis a continuous static ability whose effect modifies how the spell is cast. With\nno casting/casualty pipeline, the controller's-hand instants/sorceries are the\nnatural observable proxy (mirrors exactly how sos_201's miracle grant is probed\non hand cards). The implementer is free to surface the grant on the actual\nstack-side spell too — the probe checks the spell object regardless of zone.\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- Instants AND sorceries both granted (two separate tests).\n- Creature spells excluded (wrong card type).\n- Opponent's spells excluded (wrong controller).\n- Off-battlefield → no grant (static-ability functioning zone).\n- \"Casualty\" is a printed label, not a smuggled Keyword enum member.\n- A bare `True` \"has-casualty\" flag does not satisfy the N==1 assertions.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered here (see untestable.json)\n- **Paying the casualty cost** (optionally sacrificing a power>=1 creature as an\n  additional cost as the spell is cast).\n- **The power threshold** itself (only creatures with power >= 1 are legal\n  sacrifices for casualty 1).\n- **The copy trigger** (\"When you do, copy the spell\") and the **optional new\n  targets** for the copy.\n- **Stacking of casualty** (the spell having casualty from elsewhere too — CR\n  702.153b — out of scope for this single card).\nThese all require an engine casualty pipeline (additional-cost hook + copy +\nretarget) that does not exist; asserting them now would only test a fixture we'd\nhave to invent. Recorded in `untestable.json` with concrete unblock notes so the\nCoordinator can decide whether to commission the engine support and re-invoke.\n\n## Red-phase status\nAgainst the empty stub: **11 failed, 7 skipped, 0 errors** (no import errors).\n- The static-data tests and the hard grant-wiring anchor FAIL.\n- The 7 tolerant grant/colour/printed-label probes SKIP-with-reason (no surface\n  yet), so the contract is explicit, not silently green.\nVerified with a throwaway reference implementation that all 18 tests turn green,\nconfirming the tolerant probes recognise a correct implementation.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":246,"cache_read_input_tokens":78071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":246,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AepSwRZkXZzkfUhV74jmjw","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"fd060af3-06f4-4499-984f-70c1889637bc","request_id":"req_011CbeCTQaiR9cyD4bkTFkcr","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_226"}
