{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AepSwRZkXZzkfUhV74jmjw","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All outputs are in place and validated.\n\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_count: 18\nred_confirmed: yes — against the empty stub: 11 fail, 7 skip-with-reason, 0 errors (no import errors). The 11 failures are the 10 static-data assertions plus the hard `test_card_exposes_a_casualty_grant_surface` grant anchor; the 7 skips are the tolerant casualty-value/colors/printed-label probes that skip-with-reason until a grant surface exists (so the contract is never silently green). Verified via a throwaway reference impl that all 18 turn green.\nuntestable_count: 3\ntest_files_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-files.txt\n\nNotes:\n- Test file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`\n- Rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md`\n- Untestable: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json`\n- Static statics (Creature, name, `{2}{W}{B}` / mv 4, 4/4, LEGENDARY, Dragon+Elder, Flying, Vigilance, W+B pips) are pinned directly. Colors and the \"Casualty\" printed-keyword label follow KEY_DECISIONS' frozen-`Keyword`-enum convention (asserting `Keyword` has no `CASUALTY` member) and probe tolerantly.\n- The casualty 1 GRANT is probed tolerantly (modeled on sos_201's miracle grant): controller's instants AND sorceries get casualty 1; creature spells, opponents' spells, and an off-battlefield Silverquill do not. One non-skipping anchor (`test_card_exposes_a_casualty_grant_surface`) guarantees the grant contract fails loudly on an empty stub.\n- The casualty RESOLUTION mechanic (pay-by-sacrifice of a power>=1 creature, the power threshold, and the copy-with-new-targets trigger) is deferred to `untestable.json` with concrete unblock notes — the engine has no casualty/additional-cost/spell-copy pipeline yet. The stub `card_impl.py` was left untouched (restored after the green-phase verification)."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a57a6047c5c96a17c (use SendMessage with to: 'a57a6047c5c96a17c' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 83554\ntool_uses: 30\nduration_ms: 194178</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"5273ed3c-be41-495e-80d7-88285d6080b3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:30:49.891Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Write pytest tests (TDD red phase) for card sos_226 \"Silverquill, the Disputant\".\n\nCard spec: `cards/sos/sos_226/card_spec.json`. Read it. Summary: {2}{W}{B} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4, colors B+W, keywords Flying + Vigilance. Oracle: \"Flying, vigilance. Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\"\n\nWhere to learn conventions (read these, do NOT inline-copy blindly):\n- Test conventions + fixtures: look at `engine_tests/` and an example like `engine_tests/test_casting.py`. Tests run from `/workspace`; the workspace root is on sys.path so imports are bare (e.g. `from cards.sos.sos_226.card_impl import ...`, `from engine.card import Creature, Instant`, `from engine.types import Color, Keyword`).\n- FDN reference cards live at `cards/fdn/fdn_{N}/`. PROJECT_MAP.md lists which ship with `tests.py` (fdn_13, fdn_142, fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_244) — use them as test-style templates.\n- Card-mechanic / convention context: `KEY_DECISIONS.md` (IMPORTANT — read this; it documents prior-card engine frameworks and conventions you should reuse, e.g. the printed-keyword-label convention: NEW keywords like \"Casualty\" are NOT `Keyword` enum members — the enum is frozen at 16 — they are stored as printed labels in `printed_keywords`). Also read `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT_MAP.md`, `FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n\nWhat the tests must cover (derive concrete assertions from the spec):\n1. Static data: is a Creature named \"Silverquill, the Disputant\", cost {2}{W}{B} (mana value 4), base P/T 4/4, supertype LEGENDARY, subtypes {Dragon, Elder}, keywords Flying + Vigilance, colors B+W.\n2. The granted ability: \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1.\" This is a continuous static ability that grants Casualty 1 to the controller's instant/sorcery spells. Casualty N (CR 702.153): as you cast the spell you MAY sacrifice a creature with power N-or-greater (here power >= 1); when you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.\n   - Test the OBSERVABLE contract this card creates. Since the engine likely has no casualty pipeline, probe the grant surface TOLERANTLY (a query method on the Silverquill card, and/or an attribute on the affected instant/sorcery spell) the way sos_201's miracle tests did — and `pytest.skip` only if no recognised surface exists yet, so the contract is never silently green.\n   - Scope: only the CONTROLLER's instant/sorcery spells get casualty (not creature spells, not opponents' spells).\n   - If the copy/sacrifice resolution mechanic is not yet expressible against the engine, record those items in `untestable.json` (the coordinator will arbitrate building engine support, then re-invoke you once to extend coverage).\n\nMake tests FAIL against the current empty stub (genuine behavioral assertions, not import errors) — TDD red. The 4/4 flying-vigilance statics will be straightforward; the casualty grant is the hard part.\n\nOutputs:\n- Write the test file at `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md` — behaviour contract + per-test rationale + what you deferred and why.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-files.txt` — list of test file paths you wrote.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json` — JSON array of any requirements you could NOT test yet and what would unblock each (empty array `[]` if none).\n\nReturn a short status summary:\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_count: <N>\nred_confirmed: <yes/no — how many fail vs skip against the stub>\nuntestable_count: <N>\ntest_files_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-files.txt","agentId":"a57a6047c5c96a17c","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All outputs are in place and validated.\n\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_count: 18\nred_confirmed: yes — against the empty stub: 11 fail, 7 skip-with-reason, 0 errors (no import errors). The 11 failures are the 10 static-data assertions plus the hard `test_card_exposes_a_casualty_grant_surface` grant anchor; the 7 skips are the tolerant casualty-value/colors/printed-label probes that skip-with-reason until a grant surface exists (so the contract is never silently green). Verified via a throwaway reference impl that all 18 turn green.\nuntestable_count: 3\ntest_files_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-files.txt\n\nNotes:\n- Test file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`\n- Rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md`\n- Untestable: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json`\n- Static statics (Creature, name, `{2}{W}{B}` / mv 4, 4/4, LEGENDARY, Dragon+Elder, Flying, Vigilance, W+B pips) are pinned directly. Colors and the \"Casualty\" printed-keyword label follow KEY_DECISIONS' frozen-`Keyword`-enum convention (asserting `Keyword` has no `CASUALTY` member) and probe tolerantly.\n- The casualty 1 GRANT is probed tolerantly (modeled on sos_201's miracle grant): controller's instants AND sorceries get casualty 1; creature spells, opponents' spells, and an off-battlefield Silverquill do not. One non-skipping anchor (`test_card_exposes_a_casualty_grant_surface`) guarantees the grant contract fails loudly on an empty stub.\n- The casualty RESOLUTION mechanic (pay-by-sacrifice of a power>=1 creature, the power threshold, and the copy-with-new-targets trigger) is deferred to `untestable.json` with concrete unblock notes — the engine has no casualty/additional-cost/spell-copy pipeline yet. The stub `card_impl.py` was left untouched (restored after the green-phase verification)."}],"totalDurationMs":194178,"totalTokens":83554,"totalToolUseCount":30,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":265,"cache_read_input_tokens":82524,"output_tokens":763,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":265},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":763,"cache_read_input_tokens":82524,"cache_creation_input_tokens":265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":265,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":13,"searchCount":6,"bashCount":7,"editFileCount":4,"linesAdded":531,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
