{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01C42JoHqvnhCAeBmXftLeNY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011jTViY5nfJw2beYeBmu519","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n\nCard: **Silverquill, the Disputant** — `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon — 4/4 —\nFlying, Vigilance (medium tier).\nOracle:\n> Flying, vigilance\n> Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you cast that spell, you may\n> sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When you do, copy the spell and you may choose\n> new targets for the copy.)\n\nThe Tester wrote 18 tests: 10 static-data assertions + a non-skipping grant anchor\n(`test_card_exposes_a_casualty_grant_surface`) all FAIL on the empty stub; 7 tolerant\ncasualty-grant probes SKIP pending a queryable casualty-grant surface. Your job: make the\nstatics + the grant surface real so all 18 turn green, AND build an additive Casualty\nframework so the deferred resolution mechanic (3 untestable items) becomes testable.\n\nADDITIVE per AGENTS.md: add new methods/classes/helpers/fields/modules; you may modify\nexisting function BODIES; NEVER rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. The `Keyword`\nenum MUST stay at 16 members — \"Casualty\" is a printed label (`printed_keywords`), NOT a new\nenum member. Reuse the prior-card conventions in KEY_DECISIONS.md (esp. the sos_201 Miracle\nframework, which is the closest analogue: a queryable grant surface + a per-game lazy\nregistry + a cast/draw hook).\n\n## Statics + the casualty grant surface (make these pass first)\n- Creature \"Silverquill, the Disputant\", `{2}{W}{B}` (mv 4), 4/4, LEGENDARY, subtypes\n  {Dragon, Elder}, keywords Flying + Vigilance, colors B+W.\n- \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1.\" This is a continuous static\n  ability. Expose a QUERYABLE grant surface (mirror sos_201's miracle grant) so the 7 skipped\n  probes become real PASSES:\n  - A query method on the Silverquill card (e.g. `get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) -> int|None`\n    returning `1` only when Silverquill is on the battlefield AND `spell` is an instant/sorcery\n    AND `spell`'s controller is Silverquill's controller) AND/OR an attribute the grant writes\n    onto affected spells (e.g. `spell.casualty = 1`). Implement at least the shape(s) the\n    Tester's tolerant probe recognises — read `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` to see exactly which\n    surface(s) it queries, and satisfy them.\n  - Scope: only the CONTROLLER's instants/sorceries (not creature spells, not opponents'\n    spells, and nothing while Silverquill is off the battlefield).\n\n## Build an additive Casualty framework (CR 702.153)\nCreate `engine/casualty.py` (mirroring `engine/miracle.py` / `engine/preparation.py`). It must\nmake the 3 deferred items in `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json` testable:\n1. **Optional additional cost — sacrifice a creature with power >= N (here N=1) as you cast.**\n   Provide an API to offer/pay the casualty sacrifice during a cast and RECORD the payment on\n   the spell/StackObject (e.g. `spell.casualty_paid = True` and the sacrificed creature moves\n   to the graveyard). Expose the set of legal sacrifice candidates (creatures with power >= N)\n   so the power boundary is observable (power 0 illegal, power 1 legal).\n2. **Power threshold validation** — a power-0 creature is NOT a legal casualty sacrifice; a\n   power-1 (or greater) creature IS.\n3. **Copy-on-payment (CR 702.153c).** When the casualty cost is paid, COPY the spell onto the\n   stack under the controller's control, with the option to choose new targets for the copy.\n   Provide an engine spell-copy primitive if none exists (check `engine/casting.py`,\n   `engine/zones.py`, `engine/stack.py` first and reuse anything available; only add if\n   missing). Make the copy observable on the stack so a test can assert it exists.\n\nWire the grant + the casualty hook into Silverquill's `register_triggers` /\n`register_replacement_effects` (mirror how sos_201 wires `grant_miracle_to_hand` +\n`register_miracle_draw_hook`). Use a lazy per-game registry (`game._casualty_grants` or\nsimilar) — do NOT modify `GameState.__init__`.\n\n## Make ALL 18 tests pass (no skips if avoidable)\nRead `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` and satisfy every assertion + grant probe. Do NOT modify any\ntest file. If a test is genuinely wrong, return DISPUTE.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` → all pass.\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (report totals).\n\nAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to add casualty-resolution\ntests (pay-by-sacrifice of a power>=1 creature, power-0 rejected, copy-on-stack with optional\nnew targets). Build the framework so those are real, observable, and pass.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1075,"cache_read_input_tokens":51091,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1075},"output_tokens":36,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"da9b5376-5067-4386-9046-4c24df1c7e8d","request_id":"req_011CbeCYH2S92bjwmKBtNVSV"}
