{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HsXnJFQhzPuTgpc7JE8vAQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives — sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Silverquill, the Disputant** — `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon — 4/4 —\n4\tFlying, Vigilance (medium tier).\n5\tOracle:\n6\t> Flying, vigilance\n7\t> Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you cast that spell, you may\n8\t> sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When you do, copy the spell and you may choose\n9\t> new targets for the copy.)\n10\t\n11\tThe Tester wrote 18 tests: 10 static-data assertions + a non-skipping grant anchor\n12\t(`test_card_exposes_a_casualty_grant_surface`) all FAIL on the empty stub; 7 tolerant\n13\tcasualty-grant probes SKIP pending a queryable casualty-grant surface. Your job: make the\n14\tstatics + the grant surface real so all 18 turn green, AND build an additive Casualty\n15\tframework so the deferred resolution mechanic (3 untestable items) becomes testable.\n16\t\n17\tADDITIVE per AGENTS.md: add new methods/classes/helpers/fields/modules; you may modify\n18\texisting function BODIES; NEVER rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. The `Keyword`\n19\tenum MUST stay at 16 members — \"Casualty\" is a printed label (`printed_keywords`), NOT a new\n20\tenum member. Reuse the prior-card conventions in KEY_DECISIONS.md (esp. the sos_201 Miracle\n21\tframework, which is the closest analogue: a queryable grant surface + a per-game lazy\n22\tregistry + a cast/draw hook).\n23\t\n24\t## Statics + the casualty grant surface (make these pass first)\n25\t- Creature \"Silverquill, the Disputant\", `{2}{W}{B}` (mv 4), 4/4, LEGENDARY, subtypes\n26\t  {Dragon, Elder}, keywords Flying + Vigilance, colors B+W.\n27\t- \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1.\" This is a continuous static\n28\t  ability. Expose a QUERYABLE grant surface (mirror sos_201's miracle grant) so the 7 skipped\n29\t  probes become real PASSES:\n30\t  - A query method on the Silverquill card (e.g. `get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) -> int|None`\n31\t    returning `1` only when Silverquill is on the battlefield AND `spell` is an instant/sorcery\n32\t    AND `spell`'s controller is Silverquill's controller) AND/OR an attribute the grant writes\n33\t    onto affected spells (e.g. `spell.casualty = 1`). Implement at least the shape(s) the\n34\t    Tester's tolerant probe recognises — read `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` to see exactly which\n35\t    surface(s) it queries, and satisfy them.\n36\t  - Scope: only the CONTROLLER's instants/sorceries (not creature spells, not opponents'\n37\t    spells, and nothing while Silverquill is off the battlefield).\n38\t\n39\t## Build an additive Casualty framework (CR 702.153)\n40\tCreate `engine/casualty.py` (mirroring `engine/miracle.py` / `engine/preparation.py`). It must\n41\tmake the 3 deferred items in `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json` testable:\n42\t1. **Optional additional cost — sacrifice a creature with power >= N (here N=1) as you cast.**\n43\t   Provide an API to offer/pay the casualty sacrifice during a cast and RECORD the payment on\n44\t   the spell/StackObject (e.g. `spell.casualty_paid = True` and the sacrificed creature moves\n45\t   to the graveyard). Expose the set of legal sacrifice candidates (creatures with power >= N)\n46\t   so the power boundary is observable (power 0 illegal, power 1 legal).\n47\t2. **Power threshold validation** — a power-0 creature is NOT a legal casualty sacrifice; a\n48\t   power-1 (or greater) creature IS.\n49\t3. **Copy-on-payment (CR 702.153c).** When the casualty cost is paid, COPY the spell onto the\n50\t   stack under the controller's control, with the option to choose new targets for the copy.\n51\t   Provide an engine spell-copy primitive if none exists (check `engine/casting.py`,\n52\t   `engine/zones.py`, `engine/stack.py` first and reuse anything available; only add if\n53\t   missing). Make the copy observable on the stack so a test can assert it exists.\n54\t\n55\tWire the grant + the casualty hook into Silverquill's `register_triggers` /\n56\t`register_replacement_effects` (mirror how sos_201 wires `grant_miracle_to_hand` +\n57\t`register_miracle_draw_hook`). Use a lazy per-game registry (`game._casualty_grants` or\n58\tsimilar) — do NOT modify `GameState.__init__`.\n59\t\n60\t## Make ALL 18 tests pass (no skips if avoidable)\n61\tRead `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` and satisfy every assertion + grant probe. Do NOT modify any\n62\ttest file. If a test is genuinely wrong, return DISPUTE.\n63\t\n64\t## Verification\n65\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` → all pass.\n66\t- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (report totals).\n67\t\n68\tAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to add casualty-resolution\n69\ttests (pay-by-sacrifice of a power>=1 creature, power-0 rejected, copy-on-stack with optional\n70\tnew targets). Build the framework so those are real, observable, and pass.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015WsNuwKx3ww7UKaCjA1Mn7","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"f7b609e1-4332-4849-9562-aa52d2ef8e7f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:31:40.233Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226 + casualty framework"}
