{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Juzshb7gssM1mZ41kC9Szj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MCk4C64ZZ91MHuV32a4PEw","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Extend sos_226 casualty tests","subagent_type":"Tester","prompt":"Follow-up on card sos_226 \"Silverquill, the Disputant\". You previously wrote 18 tests and deferred 3 casualty-resolution items to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json`. The Implementer has now built an additive `engine/casualty.py` framework and wired it into the card. Extend `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` with real tests for the now-testable casualty resolution mechanic.\n\nRead first:\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json` — the 3 deferred items you must now cover.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md` — the Implementer's description of the casualty framework API (symbol names in `engine/casualty.py`), the grant surface, how pay-by-sacrifice records `spell.casualty_paid`, and how copy-on-payment works (which engine spell-copy primitive it reused). Use these exact APIs to drive the tests.\n- `engine/casualty.py` — the framework source, to confirm the actual function/attribute names.\n- `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` — your existing file; ADD to it, do not remove existing tests.\n\nNew coverage to add (CR 702.153 — Casualty 1, \"you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater; when you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy\"):\n1. **Pay-by-sacrifice**: with Silverquill on the controller's battlefield and a power>=1 creature available, casting one of the controller's instants/sorceries and choosing to pay casualty sacrifices that creature (it moves to the graveyard) and records the payment (e.g. `spell.casualty_paid == True`).\n2. **Power threshold**: a power-0 creature is NOT a legal casualty sacrifice; a power-1 (or greater) creature IS legal. Assert the boundary.\n3. **Copy-on-payment**: when casualty is paid, a COPY of the spell is put on the stack under the controller's control (assert the copy exists on the stack), and new targets MAY be chosen for the copy.\n4. **Optional / decline**: declining to pay casualty makes no sacrifice and produces no copy (a clean no-op), and the original spell still resolves normally.\n5. Scope sanity if not already pinned: opponents' spells and creature spells get no casualty grant.\n\nConstraints:\n- These must be REAL passing tests against the now-built framework (not skips). Anchor any tolerant probe so a missing surface fails loudly.\n- Do NOT weaken or delete the existing 18 tests.\n- Tests run from `/workspace`; bare imports.\n\nRun `pytest cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` and confirm the full count passes. If you find a genuine implementation bug (the framework doesn't actually do what CR 702.153 / the card text requires), write the failing test anyway and describe the bug clearly in the rationale — do NOT paper over it.\n\nOutputs:\n- Update `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`.\n- Update `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md` with an \"Extended coverage\" section describing the new tests and any bug found.\n- Overwrite `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json` with `[]` (or any items STILL untestable, with reasons).\n- Keep `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-files.txt` accurate.\n\nReturn a short status summary:\nTESTS_EXTENDED\ntotal_test_count: <N>\nnew_tests: <N>\nall_passing: <yes/no — if no, list failing tests and why>\nuntestable_remaining: <N>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2409,"cache_read_input_tokens":54449,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2409},"output_tokens":35,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"eedba2