{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a942c222f8717b38d","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCk4C64ZZ91MHuV32a4PEw","description":"Editing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Tester","usage":{"total_tokens":79723,"tool_uses":36,"duration_ms":246799},"last_tool_name":"Edit","uuid":"8f743dd3-6fae-43f0-8be6-36affe98abe7","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014fCWvyvJPQEgvNv17GqqD9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ULJUHeAUSuhBvzyVntRRTT","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","old_string":"## Red-phase status\nAgainst the empty stub: **11 failed, 7 skipped, 0 errors** (no import errors).\n- The static-data tests and the hard grant-wiring anchor FAIL.\n- The 7 tolerant grant/colour/printed-label probes SKIP-with-reason (no surface\n  yet), so the contract is explicit, not silently green.\nVerified with a throwaway reference implementation that all 18 tests turn green,\nconfirming the tolerant probes recognise a correct implementation.","new_string":"## Red-phase status\nAgainst the empty stub: **11 failed, 7 skipped, 0 errors** (no import errors).\n- The static-data tests and the hard grant-wiring anchor FAIL.\n- The 7 tolerant grant/colour/printed-label probes SKIP-with-reason (no surface\n  yet), so the contract is explicit, not silently green.\nVerified with a throwaway reference implementation that all 18 tests turn green,\nconfirming the tolerant probes recognise a correct implementation.\n\n## Extended coverage — casualty RESOLUTION mechanic (CR 702.153a/c)\n\nAfter the original 18 tests landed, the Implementer built the additive\n`engine/casualty.py` framework and wired it into the card. The three\nrequirements previously parked in `untestable.json` (pay-by-sacrifice, the\npower>=1 legality boundary, copy-on-payment) are now backed by **18 new REAL\npassing tests** (no skips). The new tests drive the framework's actual public\nAPI — `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice`, `legal_casualty_sacrifices`, `pay_casualty`,\n`was_casualty_paid`, `copy_spell_on_casualty`, `offer_casualty`,\n`set_casualty_value` — and the card's own `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` cast hook\n(`register_triggers`). A spell is modelled on the stack as a real `StackObject`\n(`source is spell`) because `copy_spell_on_casualty` finds the original on the\nstack by identity. **Total file count: 36 tests, all passing.**\n\n### `TestCasualtyPayBySacrifice` (3) — CR 702.153a payment\n- `test_pay_casualty_sacrifices_creature_to_graveyard` — paying with a power>=1\n  creature removes it from the battlefield and puts it in the owner's graveyard\n  (via `engine.game.sacrifice`).\n- `test_pay_casualty_records_payment_on_spell` — `pay_casualty` records the\n  payment (`spell.casualty_paid == True` / `was_casualty_paid`), asserting the\n  pre-state is `False` so the flip is meaningful, not a constant.\n- `test_pay_casualty_rejects_creature_not_controlled` — an opponent's creature is\n  not a legal sacrifice for the caster: `pay_casualty` returns `False`, the\n  creature stays on the opponent's battlefield, and no payment is recorded.\n\n### `TestCasualtyPowerThreshold` (5) — CR 702.153a legality boundary\n- `test_power_zero_creature_is_not_a_legal_sacrifice` — power 0 is illegal.\n- `test_power_one_creature_is_a_legal_sacrifice` — power 1 is legal (the exact\n  boundary for casualty 1).\n- `test_higher_power_creature_is_a_legal_sacrifice` — power 5 (strictly greater)\n  is also legal (confirms `>=`, not `==`).\n- `test_legal_candidate_set_excludes_power_zero_includes_power_one` — the\n  observable candidate set from `legal_casualty_sacrifices` excludes the power-0\n  creature and includes the power-1 creature.\n- `test_pay_casualty_with_power_zero_creature_fails` — the boundary is enforced\n  at payment time too: paying with a power-0 creature fails (no sacrifice, no\n  record).\n\n### `TestCasualtyCopyOnPayment` (4) — CR 702.153c copy-on-payment\n- `test_copy_is_put_on_the_stack_under_controller_control` — paying casualty and\n  copying puts a copy on the stack (stack grows by one), the copy is the new top,\n  controlled by the caster, a distinct object from the original (`source is not\n  spell`) but sharing identity (same name).\n- `test_copy_may_take_new_targets` — new targets may be chosen for the copy\n  (`new_targets=[p1]`), and the original spell's targets are NOT mutated\n  (independent state — a real bug magnet, so asserted explicitly).\n- `test_copy_defaults_to_original_targets_when_not_retargeted` — declining new\n  targets keeps the original targets on the copy (\"you MAY choose new targets\").\n- `test_no_copy_when_spell_not_on_stack` — a guard: if the spell is not on the\n  stack, `copy_spell_on_casualty` returns `None` and fabricates nothing.\n\n### `TestCasualtyOptionalDeclineAndOfferFlow` (3) — CR 702.153a optionality\n- `test_offer_accept_pays_and_copies` — the bundled `offer_casualty` flow with a\n  scripted yes + creature choice pays, records, and copies.\n- `test_offer_decline_is_a_clean_noop` — a scripted \"no\" is a clean no-op: no\n  sacrifice, no recorded payment, no copy; only the original spell remains on the\n  stack.\n- `test_offer_with_no_legal_sacrifice_is_a_noop` — with only a power-0 creature\n  available, the cost cannot be paid: `offer_casualty` is a no-op even before\n  prompting.\n\n### `TestCasualtyCastHookScope` (3) — grant scope through the card's cast hook\n- `test_controllers_instant_offers_casualty` — positive anchor: firing\n  `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` for the controller's instant pushes exactly one\n  casualty offer trigger (so the two exclusions below are not vacuous).\n- `test_opponents_instant_offers_no_casualty` — an opponent's instant pushes no\n  casualty trigger (only spells YOU cast).\n- `test_creature_spell_offers_no_casualty` — a creature spell pushes no casualty\n  trigger (only instants/sorceries).\n\n### Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (still out of scope)\n- **Casualty N > 1 stacking** (CR 702.153b — a spell with casualty from multiple\n  sources) — out of scope for this single card, which only grants casualty 1.\n- **Full priority-loop resolution of the copy** (copy resolving its own effect on\n  the real engine `priority_loop`) — the vanilla test instants have no resolution\n  effect; the contract here is \"a copy is put on the stack with the right\n  controller/targets\", which is what CR 702.153c specifies. Resolving an arbitrary\n  copied effect is the copied spell's own contract, not Silverquill's.\n\n### Bugs found\nNone. The framework behaves as CR 702.153a/c requires for casualty 1: the\npower-1 boundary is exact, payment routes the sacrifice to the graveyard and\nrecords `casualty_paid`, the copy lands on the stack under the caster's control\nwith independent (optionally retargeted) state, and declining / no-legal-sac is a\nclean no-op. All 36 tests pass."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_read_input_tokens":78506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":662,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCk4C64ZZ91MHuV32a4PEw","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"ff360cc6-4206-470c-a2b8-2538653f110b","request_id":"req_011CbeDFHJSy25wmfSH8y8hU","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_226 casualty tests"}
