{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XHGBMFnj4HpDvXHtf7CEpH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013UBFykgiiSiB6f4uFPAG2s","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","old_string":"## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered here (see untestable.json)\n- **Paying the casualty cost** (optionally sacrificing a power>=1 creature as an\n  additional cost as the spell is cast).\n- **The power threshold** itself (only creatures with power >= 1 are legal\n  sacrifices for casualty 1).\n- **The copy trigger** (\"When you do, copy the spell\") and the **optional new\n  targets** for the copy.\n- **Stacking of casualty** (the spell having casualty from elsewhere too — CR\n  702.153b — out of scope for this single card).\nThese all require an engine casualty pipeline (additional-cost hook + copy +\nretarget) that does not exist; asserting them now would only test a fixture we'd\nhave to invent. Recorded in `untestable.json` with concrete unblock notes so the\nCoordinator can decide whether to commission the engine support and re-invoke.","new_string":"## Casualty resolution — originally deferred, now COVERED\nThe three items below were deferred to `untestable.json` in the first round\nbecause no engine casualty pipeline existed. The Implementer has since built\n`engine/casualty.py` and wired it into the card, so all three are now covered by\nreal passing tests (see \"Extended coverage\" below). `untestable.json` is now `[]`.\n- **Paying the casualty cost** (optionally sacrificing a power>=1 creature as an\n  additional cost as the spell is cast) — now `TestCasualtyPayBySacrifice` /\n  `TestCasualtyOptionalDeclineAndOfferFlow`.\n- **The power threshold** (only creatures with power >= 1 are legal sacrifices\n  for casualty 1) — now `TestCasualtyPowerThreshold`.\n- **The copy trigger** (\"When you do, copy the spell\") and the **optional new\n  targets** for the copy — now `TestCasualtyCopyOnPayment`.\n\nStill out of scope (NOT a single-card concern):\n- **Stacking of casualty** (the spell having casualty from elsewhere too — CR\n  702.153b) — out of scope for this single card, which only grants casualty 1."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2805,"cache_read_input_tokens":79168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2805,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCk4C64ZZ91MHuV32a4PEw","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"78b3931c-6b9b-4832-a4df-46da32fe4aa9","request_id":"req_011CbeDHZFTAMvH3QZf5aj4p","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_226 casualty tests"}
