{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018GmEL7Ns3yBUZBZpcJCUmz","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/review.json\n\nSummary: The implementation is correct against the card's intent and respects additive-only discipline. Statics ({2}{W}{B} mv 4, 4/4, LEGENDARY Elder Dragon, Flying+Vigilance, B+W) all match `card_spec.json` and the tests. The casualty grant is properly scoped to the controller's instants/sorceries while Silverquill is on the battlefield (creature spells, opponents' spells, and off-battlefield Silverquill correctly yield no grant). The casualty-1 mechanic enforces the power>=1 boundary (power-0 illegal, power-1 legal via `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice`), sacrifices to the graveyard via the existing `engine.game.sacrifice`, records `spell.casualty_paid`, and produces an independent copy via the reused `engine.stack.copy_spell` primitive (new targets do not mutate the original — verified at `engine/stack.py:99`). No `engine/types.py` change (Keyword stays at 16), no `GameState.__init__` change (lazy per-game registries `game._casualty_grants` / `game._casualty_cast_hooks`), no renamed/moved/deleted engine symbols, card lives at `cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py`, and no `engine_tests/` or `cards/fdn/*/tests.py` touched.\n\nAll three findings are advisory nitpicks (private-attribute access in `_find_stack_object`, ad-hoc target-legality in `_maybe_choose_new_targets`, and the zone-agnostic controller proxy in `_spell_is_controllers`). No strict issues.\n\nRelevant file paths:\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/review.json` (written)\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py`\n- `/workspace/engine/casualty.py`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab1c29db9e4baf918 (use SendMessage with to: 'ab1c29db9e4baf918' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 82758\ntool_uses: 19\nduration_ms: 107544</usage>"}]}]},"parent_to