{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011F3GfxLJjCvVXBNQcnd55f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_226 \"Silverquill, the Disputant\"\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\t\n5\tImplemented `SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature)` plus a new additive engine module\n6\t`engine/casualty.py` that mirrors the sos_201 Miracle framework\n7\t(`engine/miracle.py`): a queryable grant surface + a lazy per-game registry +\n8\ta cast hook. All 18 tests pass; full suite 1412 passed, no regressions.\n9\t\n10\t## The casualty grant surface (what the Tester probes)\n11\t\n12\tThe tolerant probe `_casualty_value_for(card, game, spell)` tries card query\n13\tmethods (`casualty_value_for`/`get_casualty_value`/`casualty_for`/`get_casualty`/\n14\t`casualty_value`) and then spell attributes (`casualty_value`/`casualty`/\n15\t`granted_casualty`). I satisfy **both** recognised shapes:\n16\t\n17\t1. **Card query method** — `SilverquillTheDisputant.get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) -> int | None`\n18\t   returns `1` only when (a) Silverquill is on the battlefield, (b) `spell` is an\n19\t   instant or sorcery, and (c) the spell is the controller's (its `controller` is\n20\t   Silverquill's controller, or it is in the controller's hand — the natural\n21\t   observable proxy, matching how Miracle is probed on hand cards). Returns `None`\n22\t   otherwise (creatures, opponents' spells, off-battlefield).\n23\t2. **Spell attribute** — the continuous grant writes `spell.casualty = 1` onto\n24\t   every instant/sorcery in the controller's hand via\n25\t   `engine.casualty.grant_casualty_to_hand`, wired in `register_triggers` /\n26\t   `register_replacement_effects` (exactly mirroring Lorehold's\n27\t   `grant_miracle_to_hand`).\n28\t\n29\tScope is enforced in both surfaces: only the controller's instants/sorceries get\n30\tcasualty; creature spells, opponents' spells, and off-battlefield Silverquill\n31\tyield no grant.\n32\t\n33\t## The additive Casualty framework — `engine/casualty.py` (CR 702.153)\n34\t\n35\tPublic symbols (mirrors `engine.miracle`):\n36\t\n37\t- **Grant surface**: `CASUALTY_ONE: int = 1`; `is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`;\n38\t  `get_casualty_value(card)` / `set_casualty_value(card, value|None)` /\n39\t  `has_casualty(card)` (read/write a `card.casualty` int attribute);\n40\t  `grant_casualty_to_hand(game, source, controller, value=CASUALTY_ONE)` —\n41\t  continuous static body that writes `casualty` onto every instant/sorcery in the\n42\t  controller's hand, refreshes per call, clears stale grants (lazy per-game\n43\t  registry `game._casualty_grants` keyed by `id(source)`);\n44\t  `clear_casualty_grants(game, source)`.\n45\t- **Optional additional cost — sacrifice a creature with power >= N (702.153a)**:\n46\t  `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice(creature, value) -> bool` (power boundary: power 0\n47\t  illegal, power 1 legal); `legal_casualty_sacrifices(game, player, value) ->\n48\t  list` (exposes the legal-candidate set so the boundary is observable);\n49\t  `pay_casualty(game, player, spell, creature, value=None) -> bool` — validates\n50\t  the candidate against the threshold AND control, sacrifices it via\n51\t  `engine.game.sacrifice` (so it moves to the graveyard), and records the payment\n52\t  with `mark_casualty_paid(spell)` → `spell.casualty_paid = True`;\n53\t  `was_casualty_paid(spell) -> bool`.\n54\t- **Copy-on-payment (702.153c)**: `copy_spell_on_casualty(game, player, spell,\n55\t  new_targets=None) -> StackObject|None` and the all-in-one\n56\t  `offer_casualty(game, player, spell, value=None)` which asks the player whether\n57\t  to pay, picks a legal sacrifice, pays, then copies the spell with optional new\n58\t  targets. `_maybe_choose_new_targets` implements the \"you may choose new targets\n59\t  for the copy\" prompt.\n60\t\n61\t### How the copy-on-payment works (reused primitive, not a new one)\n62\t\n63\tThe directives asked to check for an existing spell-copy primitive before adding\n64\tone. There already is one: `engine.stack.copy_spell(game, original, controller,\n65\tnew_targets)` (used by fdn_248 Thousand-Year Storm). I **reuse** it — no new copy\n66\tprimitive added. `copy_spell_on_casualty` locates the original `StackObject` on\n67\tthe stack (by identity, `so.source is spell`), calls `copy_spell(...)`, pushes\n68\tthe copy, and returns it so a test can assert the copy exists on the stack and\n69\tthat new targets may be chosen.\n70\t\n71\t### Cast-hook wiring on the card\n72\t\n73\t`SilverquillTheDisputant._register_casualty_cast_hook` registers (deduped per\n74\tsource via lazy `game._casualty_cast_hooks`) a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger\n75\tgated to the controller's instants/sorceries while Silverquill is on the\n76\tbattlefield; on fire it runs `offer_casualty(...)`. This mirrors Lorehold's\n77\t`register_miracle_draw_hook` wiring. (`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` already exists in\n78\t`engine/events.py`; the engine does not yet fire it from `cast_spell`, so the\n79\thook is exercised by firing the event — consistent with how fdn_248's storm\n80\ttrigger is driven.)\n81\t\n82\t## What I reused\n83\t\n84\t- Pattern + structure: `engine/miracle.py` (grant surface, lazy per-game\n85\t  registry, hook wiring) and the Lorehold card (`cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`).\n86\t- Spell-copy primitive: `engine.stack.copy_spell` (no new primitive).\n87\t- Sacrifice: `engine.game.sacrifice` (routes to graveyard via `move_to_zone`,\n88\t  honouring replacement effects).\n89\t- `_is_on_battlefield` helper idiom from Lorehold.\n90\t\n91\t## Spec deviations / decisions\n92\t\n93\t- The grant is modelled as casualty on \"each instant/sorcery spell you cast\"\n94\t  (CR 702.153a wording) but is *observed* on the controller's hand cards (the\n95\t  same proxy Miracle uses), because the engine has no live cast/casualty pipeline.\n96\t  `get_casualty_value` also accepts a spell whose `controller` already equals\n97\t  Silverquill's controller (a spell on the stack), so the surface is zone-agnostic.\n98\t- \"Casualty\" is recorded as a printed-keyword label (`printed_keywords =\n99\t  [\"Casualty 1\"]`), NOT a `Keyword` enum member — the enum stays frozen at 16\n100\t  (`engine_tests/test_types.py::test_exactly_sixteen_members` still passes).\n101\t- `colors = [Color.WHITE, Color.BLACK]` is exposed for the optional colour test;\n102\t  the pip-based test pins colours independently.\n103\t\n104\t## Conventions for future Casualty cards\n105\t\n106\t- **Module**: use `engine.casualty`. The grant value is an `int` stored on\n107\t  `spell.casualty`; query via `get_casualty_value` / write via\n108\t  `grant_casualty_to_hand` (continuous) keyed by `id(source)` in the lazy\n109\t  `game._casualty_grants` registry. Clear on leave-play with\n110\t  `clear_casualty_grants`.\n111\t- **Card-side grant query**: expose `get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) ->\n112\t  int | None` returning the value only when the source is on the battlefield,\n113\t  `spell` is an instant/sorcery, and the spell is the controller's. Wire\n114\t  `grant_casualty_to_hand` in `register_triggers` / `register_replacement_effects`.\n115\t- **Pay + copy**: drive payment with `pay_casualty` (validates power >= N via\n116\t  `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice`, sacrifices, records `spell.casualty_paid`), then\n117\t  produce the copy with `copy_spell_on_casualty` (reusing `engine.stack.copy_spell`).\n118\t  `offer_casualty` bundles the whole optional flow (yes/no → choose sacrifice →\n119\t  pay → copy with optional new targets).\n120\t- **Cast hook**: register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger deduped per source\n121\t  in `game._casualty_cast_hooks`, gated to the controller's instants/sorceries.\n122\t- **Printed label, not enum**: \"Casualty\" goes in `printed_keywords`; never add\n123\t  it to the `Keyword` enum (frozen at 16).\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"cfd4f6f6-fc61-409c-99b1-c05a7f62e9dd","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:43:25.778Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_226 \"Silverquill, the Disputant\"\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature)` plus a new additive engine module\n`engine/casualty.py` that mirrors the sos_201 Miracle framework\n(`engine/miracle.py`): a queryable grant surface + a lazy per-game registry +\na cast hook. All 18 tests pass; full suite 1412 passed, no regressions.\n\n## The casualty grant surface (what the Tester probes)\n\nThe tolerant probe `_casualty_value_for(card, game, spell)` tries card query\nmethods (`casualty_value_for`/`get_casualty_value`/`casualty_for`/`get_casualty`/\n`casualty_value`) and then spell attributes (`casualty_value`/`casualty`/\n`granted_casualty`). I satisfy **both** recognised shapes:\n\n1. **Card query method** — `SilverquillTheDisputant.get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) -> int | None`\n   returns `1` only when (a) Silverquill is on the battlefield, (b) `spell` is an\n   instant or sorcery, and (c) the spell is the controller's (its `controller` is\n   Silverquill's controller, or it is in the controller's hand — the natural\n   observable proxy, matching how Miracle is probed on hand cards). Returns `None`\n   otherwise (creatures, opponents' spells, off-battlefield).\n2. **Spell attribute** — the continuous grant writes `spell.casualty = 1` onto\n   every instant/sorcery in the controller's hand via\n   `engine.casualty.grant_casualty_to_hand`, wired in `register_triggers` /\n   `register_replacement_effects` (exactly mirroring Lorehold's\n   `grant_miracle_to_hand`).\n\nScope is enforced in both surfaces: only the controller's instants/sorceries get\ncasualty; creature spells, opponents' spells, and off-battlefield Silverquill\nyield no grant.\n\n## The additive Casualty framework — `engine/casualty.py` (CR 702.153)\n\nPublic symbols (mirrors `engine.miracle`):\n\n- **Grant surface**: `CASUALTY_ONE: int = 1`; `is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`;\n  `get_casualty_value(card)` / `set_casualty_value(card, value|None)` /\n  `has_casualty(card)` (read/write a `card.casualty` int attribute);\n  `grant_casualty_to_hand(game, source, controller, value=CASUALTY_ONE)` —\n  continuous static body that writes `casualty` onto every instant/sorcery in the\n  controller's hand, refreshes per call, clears stale grants (lazy per-game\n  registry `game._casualty_grants` keyed by `id(source)`);\n  `clear_casualty_grants(game, source)`.\n- **Optional additional cost — sacrifice a creature with power >= N (702.153a)**:\n  `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice(creature, value) -> bool` (power boundary: power 0\n  illegal, power 1 legal); `legal_casualty_sacrifices(game, player, value) ->\n  list` (exposes the legal-candidate set so the boundary is observable);\n  `pay_casualty(game, player, spell, creature, value=None) -> bool` — validates\n  the candidate against the threshold AND control, sacrifices it via\n  `engine.game.sacrifice` (so it moves to the graveyard), and records the payment\n  with `mark_casualty_paid(spell)` → `spell.casualty_paid = True`;\n  `was_casualty_paid(spell) -> bool`.\n- **Copy-on-payment (702.153c)**: `copy_spell_on_casualty(game, player, spell,\n  new_targets=None) -> StackObject|None` and the all-in-one\n  `offer_casualty(game, player, spell, value=None)` which asks the player whether\n  to pay, picks a legal sacrifice, pays, then copies the spell with optional new\n  targets. `_maybe_choose_new_targets` implements the \"you may choose new targets\n  for the copy\" prompt.\n\n### How the copy-on-payment works (reused primitive, not a new one)\n\nThe directives asked to check for an existing spell-copy primitive before adding\none. There already is one: `engine.stack.copy_spell(game, original, controller,\nnew_targets)` (used by fdn_248 Thousand-Year Storm). I **reuse** it — no new copy\nprimitive added. `copy_spell_on_casualty` locates the original `StackObject` on\nthe stack (by identity, `so.source is spell`), calls `copy_spell(...)`, pushes\nthe copy, and returns it so a test can assert the copy exists on the stack and\nthat new targets may be chosen.\n\n### Cast-hook wiring on the card\n\n`SilverquillTheDisputant._register_casualty_cast_hook` registers (deduped per\nsource via lazy `game._casualty_cast_hooks`) a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger\ngated to the controller's instants/sorceries while Silverquill is on the\nbattlefield; on fire it runs `offer_casualty(...)`. This mirrors Lorehold's\n`register_miracle_draw_hook` wiring. (`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` already exists in\n`engine/events.py`; the engine does not yet fire it from `cast_spell`, so the\nhook is exercised by firing the event — consistent with how fdn_248's storm\ntrigger is driven.)\n\n## What I reused\n\n- Pattern + structure: `engine/miracle.py` (grant surface, lazy per-game\n  registry, hook wiring) and the Lorehold card (`cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`).\n- Spell-copy primitive: `engine.stack.copy_spell` (no new primitive).\n- Sacrifice: `engine.game.sacrifice` (routes to graveyard via `move_to_zone`,\n  honouring replacement effects).\n- `_is_on_battlefield` helper idiom from Lorehold.\n\n## Spec deviations / decisions\n\n- The grant is modelled as casualty on \"each instant/sorcery spell you cast\"\n  (CR 702.153a wording) but is *observed* on the controller's hand cards (the\n  same proxy Miracle uses), because the engine has no live cast/casualty pipeline.\n  `get_casualty_value` also accepts a spell whose `controller` already equals\n  Silverquill's controller (a spell on the stack), so the surface is zone-agnostic.\n- \"Casualty\" is recorded as a printed-keyword label (`printed_keywords =\n  [\"Casualty 1\"]`), NOT a `Keyword` enum member — the enum stays frozen at 16\n  (`engine_tests/test_types.py::test_exactly_sixteen_members` still passes).\n- `colors = [Color.WHITE, Color.BLACK]` is exposed for the optional colour test;\n  the pip-based test pins colours independently.\n\n## Conventions for future Casualty cards\n\n- **Module**: use `engine.casualty`. The grant value is an `int` stored on\n  `spell.casualty`; query via `get_casualty_value` / write via\n  `grant_casualty_to_hand` (continuous) keyed by `id(source)` in the lazy\n  `game._casualty_grants` registry. Clear on leave-play with\n  `clear_casualty_grants`.\n- **Card-side grant query**: expose `get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) ->\n  int | None` returning the value only when the source is on the battlefield,\n  `spell` is an instant/sorcery, and the spell is the controller's. Wire\n  `grant_casualty_to_hand` in `register_triggers` / `register_replacement_effects`.\n- **Pay + copy**: drive payment with `pay_casualty` (validates power >= N via\n  `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice`, sacrifices, records `spell.casualty_paid`), then\n  produce the copy with `copy_spell_on_casualty` (reusing `engine.stack.copy_spell`).\n  `offer_casualty` bundles the whole optional flow (yes/no → choose sacrifice →\n  pay → copy with optional new targets).\n- **Cast hook**: register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger deduped per source\n  in `game._casualty_cast_hooks`, gated to the controller's instants/sorceries.\n- **Printed label, not enum**: \"Casualty\" goes in `printed_keywords`; never add\n  it to the `Keyword` enum (frozen at 16).\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
