{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01WDZvABr41SRW1caT6qGREF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012cjeoGxU8nan8AgTAdVS4D","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"- Engine: `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` gained an additive `ignore_timing: bool = False` parameter. When True it bypasses the sorcery-speed timing gate (`is_sorcery_speed`/`can_cast_at_instant_speed`) — used ONLY by the miracle draw-cast so a granted SORCERY can be cast at draw time (its own casting window per CR 702.94a, not bound by sorcery-speed). Defaults False so all existing callers are unaffected. Convention: alternative casting windows that grant their own timing permission opt into `ignore_timing=True`; never weaken normal enforcement for ordinary casts. The miracle draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s in a way that hides real failures.","new_string":"- Engine: `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` gained an additive `ignore_timing: bool = False` parameter. When True it bypasses the sorcery-speed timing gate (`is_sorcery_speed`/`can_cast_at_instant_speed`) — used ONLY by the miracle draw-cast so a granted SORCERY can be cast at draw time (its own casting window per CR 702.94a, not bound by sorcery-speed). Defaults False so all existing callers are unaffected. Convention: alternative casting windows that grant their own timing permission opt into `ignore_timing=True`; never weaken normal enforcement for ordinary casts. The miracle draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s in a way that hides real failures.\n## Engine: Casualty framework (from sos_226)\n- New additive module `engine/casualty.py` (modelled on `engine/miracle.py`) implements Casualty N (CR 702.153): a queryable grant + an optional-additional-cost sacrifice + copy-on-payment. No engine-symbol renames; `Keyword` stays at 16; \"Casualty\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, never an enum member.\n- Public API:\n  - Grant surface: `CASUALTY_ONE: int = 1`; `is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`; `get_casualty_value(card)` / `set_casualty_value(card, value|None)` / `has_casualty(card)` (read/write a `card.casualty` int attr); `grant_casualty_to_hand(game, source, controller, value=CASUALTY_ONE)` — continuous static body writing `casualty` onto every instant/sorcery in the controller's hand, refreshes per call, clears stale grants (lazy per-game registry `game._casualty_grants` keyed by `id(source)`); `clear_casualty_grants(game, source)`.\n  - Payment (702.153a): `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice(creature, value)` (power boundary: power 0 illegal, power >= N legal); `legal_casualty_sacrifices(game, player, value)`; `pay_casualty(game, player, spell, creature, value=None)` — validates threshold + control, sacrifices via `engine.game.sacrifice` (to graveyard), records `mark_casualty_paid(spell)` → `spell.casualty_paid = True`; `was_casualty_paid(spell)`.\n  - Copy (702.153c): `copy_spell_on_casualty(game, player, spell, new_targets=None)` REUSES the existing `engine.stack.copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` primitive (also used by fdn_248 Thousand-Year Storm) — no new copy primitive added. `offer_casualty(game, player, spell, value=None)` bundles the optional flow (yes/no → choose legal sacrifice → pay → copy with optional new targets). The copy is independent (new targets don't mutate the original).\n- Card-side: expose `get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) -> int|None` (value only when source is on the battlefield, `spell` is instant/sorcery, and spell is the controller's). Wire `grant_casualty_to_hand` in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects`, and register the cast hook as a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger deduped per source in lazy `game._casualty_cast_hooks`, gated to the controller's instants/sorceries. Note: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` exists in `engine/events.py` but `cast_spell` does not fire it — the hook is exercised by firing the event (same as fdn_248's storm trigger)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3249,"cache_read_input_tokens":61953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3249},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"6632d3f7-85c0-4f94-ae34-6c700f2d443b","request_id":"req_011CbeDVmUjx3yfL9nj6JT4C"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012cjeoGxU8nan8AgTAdVS4D","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"58166469-7c07-4f37-b1c5-a5068c5eb0b0","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:43:43.193Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- Engine: `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` gained an additive `ignore_timing: bool = False` parameter. When True it bypasses the sorcery-speed timing gate (`is_sorcery_speed`/`can_cast_at_instant_speed`) — used ONLY by the miracle draw-cast so a granted SORCERY can be cast at draw time (its own casting window per CR 702.94a, not bound by sorcery-speed). Defaults False so all existing callers are unaffected. Convention: alternative casting windows that grant their own timing permission opt into `ignore_timing=True`; never weaken normal enforcement for ordinary casts. The miracle draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s in a way that hides real failures.","newString":"- Engine: `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` gained an additive `ignore_timing: bool = False` parameter. When True it bypasses the sorcery-speed timing gate (`is_sorcery_speed`/`can_cast_at_instant_speed`) — used ONLY by the miracle draw-cast so a granted SORCERY can be cast at draw time (its own casting window per CR 702.94a, not bound by sorcery-speed). Defaults False so all existing callers are unaffected. Convention: alternative casting windows that grant their own timing permission opt into `ignore_timing=True`; never weaken normal enforcement for ordinary casts. The miracle draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s in a way that hides real failures.\n## Engine: Casualty framework (from sos_226)\n- New additive module `engine/casualty.py` (modelled on `engine/miracle.py`) implements Casualty N (CR 702.153): a queryable grant + an optional-additional-cost sacrifice + copy-on-payment. No engine-symbol renames; `Keyword` stays at 16; \"Casualty\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, never an enum member.\n- Public API:\n  - Grant surface: `CASUALTY_ONE: int = 1`; `is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`; `get_casualty_value(card)` / `set_casualty_value(card, value|None)` / `has_casualty(card)` (read/write a `card.casualty` int attr); `grant_casualty_to_hand(game, source, controller, value=CASUALTY_ONE)` — continuous static body writing `casualty` onto every instant/sorcery in the controller's hand, refreshes per call, clears stale grants (lazy per-game registry `game._casualty_grants` keyed by `id(source)`); `clear_casualty_grants(game, source)`.\n  - Payment (702.153a): `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice(creature, value)` (power boundary: power 0 illegal, power >= N legal); `legal_casualty_sacrifices(game, player, value)`; `pay_casualty(game, player, spell, creature, value=None)` — validates threshold + control, sacrifices via `engine.game.sacrifice` (to graveyard), records `mark_casualty_paid(spell)` → `spell.casualty_paid = True`; `was_casualty_paid(spell)`.\n  - Copy (702.153c): `copy_spell_on_casualty(game, player, spell, new_targets=None)` REUSES the existing `engine.stack.copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` primitive (also used by fdn_248 Thousand-Year Storm) — no new copy primitive added. `offer_casualty(game, player, spell, value=None)` bundles the optional flow (yes/no → choose legal sacrifice → pay → copy with optional new targets). The copy is independent (new targets don't mutate the original).\n- Card-side: expose `get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) -> int|None` (value only when source is on the battlefield, `spell` is instant/sorcery, and spell is the controller's). Wire `grant_casualty_to_hand` in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects`, and register the cast hook as a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger deduped per source in lazy `game._casualty_cast_hooks`, gated to the controller's instants/sorceries. Note: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` exists in `engine/events.py` but `cast_spell` does not fire it — the hook is exercised by firing the event (same as fdn_248's storm trigger).","originalFile":"# Key Decisions\n\nPersistent, append-only log of conventions and design decisions across runs.\n\n## Engine: stack->graveyard exile redirect (from sos_1)\n- For \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" free-cast effects:\n  `engine.casting` now has an additive per-game redirect registry:\n  - `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card, destination)` — one-shot, identity-keyed by `id(card)`.\n  - `clear_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card)`.\n  - `_redirect_registry(game)` lazily attaches `game._stack_to_graveyard_redirects` (no GameState.__init__ change).\n  - `_resolve_spell` pops any registered redirect for a non-permanent spell and routes it there instead of the graveyard; with no redirect registered, behavior is unchanged (defaults to GRAVEYARD).\n- Usage in a card: call `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, chosen_card, \"exile\")` before `cast_spell_free(...)`. Clear it if the cast raises.\n- Rationale: `engine.zones.move_to_zone` only consults replacement effects when `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`, so STACK->GRAVEYARD resolution would otherwise bypass an exile-instead replacement.\n\n## Convention: cost_reduction counts (from sos_1)\n- Card `cost_reduction` returns the raw count (e.g. instants+sorceries in controller's graveyard); the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the generic portion of the cost. Mirrors fdn_167 (Tolarian Terror). Count only the controller's graveyard unless the card says otherwise.\n## Convention: Converge / colors_spent (from sos_4)\n- Converge X = number of distinct colors of mana spent to cast. Already wired in engine:\n  `engine.casting.cast_spell` sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (distinct, colorless-excluded, sorted list of `engine.types.Color`).\n- Card-side: default `self.colors_spent = []` in `__init__`; compute `X = len(self.colors_spent)`. No engine change needed for Converge.\n- Player-vs-creature target detection idiom: `hasattr(obj, \"life\")` is True only for `engine.player.Player` (established FDN idiom, e.g. fdn_192).\n## Engine: Preparation Card framework (from sos_13)\n- New additive module `engine/preparation.py` implements the \"Prepared\" designation mechanic (CR 722). Public API:\n  - `is_prepared(permanent) -> bool`\n  - `mark_prepared(game, permanent) -> copy|None` — sets designation and creates a copy of the prepare spell in the controller's exile, keyed by `id(permanent)` in lazy per-game registry `game._prepared_copies`; idempotent.\n  - `unprepare(game, permanent)` — clears designation, removes exile copy.\n  - `get_prepared_copy(game, permanent)` / `get_prepared_source(game, copy)`.\n  - `cast_prepared_copy(game, player, copy)` — casts the exiled copy via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`, then (only on cast success, CR 722.3c) clears the source's prepared designation and detaches the registry entry. On cast failure the source stays prepared and the copy stays in exile.\n- Conventions for future Preparation cards:\n  - \"Prepared\" is a DESIGNATION, NOT a `Keyword` enum member. Do NOT add it to `Keyword` — `engine_tests/test_types.py::test_exactly_sixteen_members` hard-asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`. Track via `is_prepared`/`prepared` boolean attrs; store the printed label in `printed_keywords` if needed.\n  - The card exposes its prepare half via `make_prepare_spell()` factory; cost surface via `prepare_mana_cost`/`back_mana_cost`.\n- Card-spec note: when a split/preparation card's `card_spec.json` omits the back-face oracle text, implement the canonical effect implied by the back-face name (sos_13's back half \"Swords to Plowshares\" = \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\"). Logged as a coordinator ruling in RUN_DECISIONS.\n## Engine: delayed one-shot triggers + main-phase event + mana_spent (from sos_57)\n- `engine/events.py`: new `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)` with fields `player` (active player) and `precombat: bool`. Fired from `engine/turn.py` `run_turn` at the start of each main phase (`step is None` at PRECOMBAT_MAIN / POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) — additive `elif`, does not disturb untap/upkeep/draw/combat/cleanup.\n- `engine/triggers.py`:\n  - `TriggerRegistration` gained additive field `one_shot: bool = False` (defaulted — existing call sites unaffected).\n  - `TriggerManager.register_delayed(event_type, effect, source, controller, condition=None) -> TriggerRegistration` registers a one-shot delayed trigger.\n  - `fire_event` removes matched `one_shot` triggers at fire time (using a pre-built match list, no mutation-during-iteration), so a delayed trigger fires EXACTLY ONCE then is removed.\n  - Note: `fire_event` pushes the delayed effect as a `StackObject` rather than executing inline — tests must resolve the stack after firing.\n- `engine/casting.py`: now sets `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (total mana paid after cost reduction) after payment, cleared at the start of each cast alongside `colors_spent`. For \"amount of mana spent\" effects, read `card.mana_spent`, falling back to `mana_cost.cmc` for spells staged directly on the stack (unpaid). Known limitation: equals mana value (no special X/alt-cost handling) — accepted.\n- Use `register_delayed(..., condition=lambda g,e: e.player is controller)` for \"at the beginning of your next main phase\" deferred effects controlled by \"you\".\n## Engine: coin-flip RNG + skip-turn mechanism (from sos_97)\n- Coin flips (`engine/game.py`, all additive):\n  - `get_rng(game) -> random.Random` — lazily attaches/returns `game._rng`.\n  - `seed_rng(game, seed)` — seeds for deterministic flips (tests use this).\n  - `flip_coin(game) -> bool` (True=heads); `flip_coins(game, n) -> int` (number of heads).\n  - Unseeded = fair coin. Test pattern: `seed_rng(game, s); flip_coins(game, 5)` is reproducible.\n- Skip-turn mechanism (additive):\n  - `engine/player.py`: new field `Player.skipped_turns: int = 0`.\n  - `engine/game.py`: `add_skipped_turns(game, player, amount=1)`.\n  - `engine/game_state.py`: rotation factored into `_next_active_index_raw()` (preserves existing `extra_turns` FIFO semantics) + `_pick_next_active_index()` which consumes `skipped_turns` (if the next player would be active and has skipped_turns>0, decrement and pass to the next player; bounded loop). `advance_phase` calls `_pick_next_active_index`.\n  - Defaults to 0 so existing turn/extra-turn tests are unaffected. Extra turns and skips compose.\n- Test pattern for skips: `add_skipped_turns(game, opp, N)` then drive turns via `game.phase=Phase.ENDING; game.step=Step.CLEANUP; game.advance_phase()` and read `game.active_player_index` / `opp.skipped_turns`.\n## Engine: Paradigm framework (from sos_120)\n- New additive module `engine/paradigm.py` (modelled on engine/preparation.py) for the \"Paradigm\" keyword (CR 702.192): \"Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.\"\n- Public API:\n  - `mark_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool` / `has_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool` — per-game first-resolution gate, keyed by `(id(player), name)` in lazy `game._paradigm_resolved`. `mark` returns True only on the FIRST resolution.\n  - `register_paradigm(game, source, controller, factory, name)` — marks first resolution and installs (deduped per `(controller, name)` via lazy `game._paradigm_registered`) ONE RECURRING trigger on `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` via `TriggerManager.register` (NOT `register_delayed`, which is one-shot). Condition: `event.player is controller AND event.precombat AND has_paradigm_resolved(...)`.\n  - `offer_paradigm_copy(game, controller, factory, name)` — builds a copy in the controller's exile, asks `choose_yes_no`, casts free via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)` on yes (leaves in exile on decline).\n  - Helpers `is_paradigm_copy(card)`, `is_castable_spell(card)` (lands aren't spells).\n- Card-side: `make_paradigm_copy()` factory (mirrors `make_prepare_spell`); \"Paradigm\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, NOT a Keyword enum member (frozen at 16).\n- Reuse pattern: recurring main-phase effects use `TriggerManager.register` (persistent); one-shot deferred effects use `register_delayed` (sos_57). \"Then exile this spell\" reuses sos_1's `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, self, \"exile\")`.\n## Engine: Miracle framework + cast_spell ignore_timing (from sos_201)\n- New additive module `engine/miracle.py` implements Miracle (CR 702.94) as a queryable grant + draw-time cast hook (no true layered-effect pipeline in the engine):\n  - Grant surface: `MIRACLE_TWO: ManaCost` ({2}); `is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`; `get_miracle_cost(card)` / `set_miracle_cost(card, cost|None)` / `has_miracle(card)` (read/write a `card.miracle_cost` attribute); `grant_miracle_to_hand(game, source, controller, cost=MIRACLE_TWO)` — continuous static body that writes `miracle_cost` onto every instant/sorcery in the controller's hand, refreshes per call, clears stale grants (lazy per-game registry `game._miracle_grants` keyed by `id(source)`); `clear_miracle_grants(game, source)`.\n  - Draw-time cast hook: `is_first_draw_of_turn(player)` (`player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`); `offer_miracle_cast(game, player, card)`; `register_miracle_draw_hook(game, source, controller, cost_resolver=None)` — deduped per source via `game._miracle_draw_hooks`, registers a `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger gated to the first draw. `draw_card` increments `cards_drawn_this_turn` BEFORE firing the event, so the first draw sees count==1 at trigger time.\n- Card-side: the granting card exposes a `get_miracle_cost(self, game, card) -> ManaCost|None` query (returns the grant only when the source is on the battlefield, `card` is instant/sorcery, and `card` is in the source's controller's hand). Wire `grant_miracle_to_hand` + `register_miracle_draw_hook(..., cost_resolver=self.get_miracle_cost)` in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects`. \"Miracle\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, NOT a Keyword enum member (frozen at 16).\n- Engine: `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` gained an additive `ignore_timing: bool = False` parameter. When True it bypasses the sorcery-speed timing gate (`is_sorcery_speed`/`can_cast_at_instant_speed`) — used ONLY by the miracle draw-cast so a granted SORCERY can be cast at draw time (its own casting window per CR 702.94a, not bound by sorcery-speed). Defaults False so all existing callers are unaffected. Convention: alternative casting windows that grant their own timing permission opt into `ignore_timing=True`; never weaken normal enforcement for ordinary casts. The miracle draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s in a way that hides real failures.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":66,"oldLines":3,"newStart":66,"newLines":10,"lines":["   - Draw-time cast hook: `is_first_draw_of_turn(player)` (`player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`); `offer_miracle_cast(game, player, card)`; `register_miracle_draw_hook(game, source, controller, cost_resolver=None)` — deduped per source via `game._miracle_draw_hooks`, registers a `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger gated to the first draw. `draw_card` increments `cards_drawn_this_turn` BEFORE firing the event, so the first draw sees count==1 at trigger time."," - Card-side: the granting card exposes a `get_miracle_cost(self, game, card) -> ManaCost|None` query (returns the grant only when the source is on the battlefield, `card` is instant/sorcery, and `card` is in the source's controller's hand). Wire `grant_miracle_to_hand` + `register_miracle_draw_hook(..., cost_resolver=self.get_miracle_cost)` in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects`. \"Miracle\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, NOT a Keyword enum member (frozen at 16)."," - Engine: `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` gained an additive `ignore_timing: bool = False` parameter. When True it bypasses the sorcery-speed timing gate (`is_sorcery_speed`/`can_cast_at_instant_speed`) — used ONLY by the miracle draw-cast so a granted SORCERY can be cast at draw time (its own casting window per CR 702.94a, not bound by sorcery-speed). Defaults False so all existing callers are unaffected. Convention: alternative casting windows that grant their own timing permission opt into `ignore_timing=True`; never weaken normal enforcement for ordinary casts. The miracle draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s in a way that hides real failures.","+## Engine: Casualty framework (from sos_226)","+- New additive module `engine/casualty.py` (modelled on `engine/miracle.py`) implements Casualty N (CR 702.153): a queryable grant + an optional-additional-cost sacrifice + copy-on-payment. No engine-symbol renames; `Keyword` stays at 16; \"Casualty\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, never an enum member.","+- Public API:","+  - Grant surface: `CASUALTY_ONE: int = 1`; `is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`; `get_casualty_value(card)` / `set_casualty_value(card, value|None)` / `has_casualty(card)` (read/write a `card.casualty` int attr); `grant_casualty_to_hand(game, source, controller, value=CASUALTY_ONE)` — continuous static body writing `casualty` onto every instant/sorcery in the controller's hand, refreshes per call, clears stale grants (lazy per-game registry `game._casualty_grants` keyed by `id(source)`); `clear_casualty_grants(game, source)`.","+  - Payment (702.153a): `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice(creature, value)` (power boundary: power 0 illegal, power >= N legal); `legal_casualty_sacrifices(game, player, value)`; `pay_casualty(game, player, spell, creature, value=None)` — validates threshold + control, sacrifices via `engine.game.sacrifice` (to graveyard), records `mark_casualty_paid(spell)` → `spell.casualty_paid = True`; `was_casualty_paid(spell)`.","+  - Copy (702.153c): `copy_spell_on_casualty(game, player, spell, new_targets=None)` REUSES the existing `engine.stack.copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` primitive (also used by fdn_248 Thousand-Year Storm) — no new copy primitive added. `offer_casualty(game, player, spell, value=None)` bundles the optional flow (yes/no → choose legal sacrifice → pay → copy with optional new targets). The copy is independent (new targets don't mutate the original).","+- Card-side: expose `get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) -> int|None` (value only when source is on the battlefield, `spell` is instant/sorcery, and spell is the controller's). Wire `grant_casualty_to_hand` in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects`, and register the cast hook as a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger deduped per source in lazy `game._casualty_cast_hooks`, gated to the controller's instants/sorceries. Note: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` exists in `engine/events.py` but `cast_spell` does not fire it — the hook is exercised by firing the event (same as fdn_248's storm trigger)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01FysNTRmiGysqLXtL7hi2Q6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0149Hciw1V9KwwGRmkmGhHwA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md <<'EOF'\n## Untestable items: sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant (Casualty mechanic, 3 items)\n- Medium-tier {2}{W}{B} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4, Flying+Vigilance. \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1.\" (CR 702.153)\n- Tester wrote 18 tests (statics + a non-skipping grant anchor fail; 7 tolerant casualty-grant probes skip pending a queryable surface). 3 deferred items: (1) optional additional cost = sacrifice a power>=1 creature as you cast + record payment; (2) the power-1-or-greater legality threshold; (3) \"when you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets\" — no engine casualty/additional-cost/spell-copy-on-payment pipeline.\n- **Decision (a)**: directed Implementer to build an additive `engine/casualty.py` (mirroring engine/miracle.py): queryable grant surface + lazy per-game registry + cast hook; pay-by-sacrifice validating power>=N and recording `spell.casualty_paid`; copy-on-payment REUSING the existing `engine.stack.copy_spell` primitive (no new copy primitive). Make all 18 tests pass.\n- After Implementer built it, re-invoked Tester ONCE: added 18 real casualty-resolution tests (pay/copy/decline/power-boundary/scope). Total 36 tests, all pass; full suite 1430. No implementation bug found. Convention promoted to KEY_DECISIONS.md.\nEOF\ngit add KEY_DECISIONS.md RUN_DECISIONS.md && git commit -q --amend --no-edit && git log --oneline -1","description":"Append run note, amend sos_226 commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1698,"cache_read_input_tokens":65202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1698},"ou