{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012LqAbHsYfVQQm9y7fjAtbH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AGENTS.md — Workspace Orientation\n2\t\n3\t## Task\n4\t\n5\tYou are implementing SOS card implementations. Each card's implementation class\n6\tmust be placed in its assigned file:\n7\t\n8\t```\n9\tcards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py\n10\t```\n11\t\n12\t## Hard Rules\n13\t\n14\t1. **Card location invariant** — Each card's canonical implementation class must\n15\t   remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Do not move or rename card\n16\t   directories.\n17\t\n18\t2. **Staged-test integrity** — Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only: do not\n19\t   modify, add to, or delete files in it. Likewise do not modify or delete any\n20\t   existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (you may read\n21\t   them as examples, but never edit them). These tests are for your local\n22\t   verification and learning only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies\n23\t   for grading. Editing them — including adding new files — will not change\n24\t   your score, it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are\n25\t   correct. Your own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n26\t\n27\t3. **Additive-only engine modifications** — You may add new methods, classes,\n28\t   helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing\n29\t   functions to implement card behavior. You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete\n30\t   anything that already exists in `engine/` — no renaming, no refactoring.\n31\t   Restructuring the engine will break the grader's imports and zero your score.\n32\t\n33\tThese rules are derived from the project's Workspace Contract decisions\n34\t(maintained outside this workspace). They ensure deterministic grading.\n35\t\n36\t## Test Commands\n37\t\n38\tRun from the workspace root:\n39\t\n40\t```bash\n41\tpytest\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\tThis discovers:\n45\t- Engine regression tests at `engine_tests/test_*.py`.\n46\t- Per-card FDN reference tests at `cards/fdn/fdn_{collector_number}/tests.py`.\n47\t  Only a handful of FDN cards ship with a `tests.py` — see `PROJECT_MAP.md`\n48\t  for the canonical list, and use them as illustrative per-card test examples.\n49\t- Per-card SOS tests you write at `cards/sos/sos_{collector_number}/tests.py`.\n50\t\n51\tThe workspace `pytest.ini` configures `python_files = test_*.py tests.py` for\n52\tdiscovery of all three patterns and sets a per-test timeout (5 minutes).\n53\t\n54\tStandard imports inside per-card tests:\n55\t\n56\t```python\n57\tfrom cards.sos.sos_<N>.card_impl import <ClassName>\n58\tfrom engine.card import Creature, Instant                  # or whichever base\n59\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone\n60\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t## Engine Extension Scope\n64\t\n65\t- **May**: Add files, methods, classes, and helpers inside `engine/`.\n66\t- **May**: Modify the bodies of existing functions in `engine/`.\n67\t- **Must NOT**: Rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/`.\n68\t\n69\t## Rules questions → grep RULEBOOK.txt\n70\t\n71\t`RULEBOOK.txt` (workspace root) is the Magic: The Gathering Comprehensive Rules — the authoritative source for any rules question. **Whenever you're unsure how a mechanic works (keyword behavior, timing, replacement vs trigger ordering, state-based actions, etc.), check the rulebook before guessing in a `card_impl.py` or an `engine/` change.**\n72\t\n73\tThe file is large — don't `cat` or `Read` it whole. See the workspace skill at [`skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`](skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md) for grep recipes, the file's structure (numbered rules + glossary), and best practices.\n74\t\n75\t## Tools\n76\t\n77\tGit is available. The workspace is initialized as a git repository at stage time.\n78\t\n79\t## Navigation\n80\t\n81\tSee `PROJECT_MAP.md` for the directory layout.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01P7xZZQySF9L4KiVzkCHLvW","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"25fbe00a-6167-462b-a5d0-8fef33c9a3f3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:44:33.909Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_245"}
