ue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 101459\ntool_uses: 30\nduration_ms: 211805</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"c93986ce-9ce2-4fbf-8e7c-f7ac5334106c","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:48:02.102Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Write pytest tests (TDD red phase) for card sos_245 \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\".\n\nCard spec: `cards/sos/sos_245/card_spec.json`. Read it. Summary: {6}{B}{G} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, colors B+G, keywords Deathtouch + Flying + Affinity. Oracle:\n\"Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control.)\nFlying, deathtouch\nInstant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n\nWhere to learn conventions (read these):\n- Test conventions + fixtures: `engine_tests/` and an example like `engine_tests/test_casting.py`. Tests run from `/workspace`; workspace root on sys.path, so imports are bare (e.g. `from cards.sos.sos_245.card_impl import ...`, `from engine.card import Creature`, `from engine.types import Color, Keyword`).\n- FDN reference cards at `cards/fdn/fdn_{N}/` (PROJECT_MAP.md lists which ship with tests.py).\n- **IMPORTANT — read `KEY_DECISIONS.md`**: it documents the cost-reduction convention from sos_1/fdn_167 (Tolarian Terror): a card exposes `cost_reduction` returning a raw count which the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps to the generic portion of the cost. Affinity for creatures = {1} less per creature you control = exactly this cost-reduction shape (the count is \"number of creatures the controller controls\"). Also note the frozen-`Keyword`-enum convention (16 members) — but FIRST CHECK whether \"Affinity\" is already one of the 16 existing `Keyword` enum members (read `engine/types.py` / `engine_tests/test_types.py`); if it is, use it; if not, it is a printed label in `printed_keywords`. Also read `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT_MAP.md`, `FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n\nWhat the tests must cover (derive concrete assertions from the spec):\n1. Static data: a Creature named \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\", cost {6}{B}{G} (mana value 8), base P/T 5/5, supertype LEGENDARY, subtypes {Dragon, Elder}, keywords Deathtouch + Flying (+ Affinity however it's modeled — enum member or printed label, whichever is correct), colors B+G.\n2. **Affinity for creatures on Witherbloom itself**: the {6}{B}{G} spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature its controller controls. Test the cost-reduction value the card reports (e.g. `cost_reduction` count == number of creatures controlled), and ideally drive an effective-cost computation through the engine's `get_cost_reduction` to confirm the generic cost drops by the creature count (clamped to the generic portion). Use the sos_1/fdn_167 convention.\n3. **Granted affinity for creatures on the controller's instant/sorcery spells**: a continuous static ability granting affinity-for-creatures to the controller's instant and sorcery spells. Probe the grant surface TOLERANTLY (a query method on the Witherbloom card and/or an attribute on the affected spell, mirroring sos_201/sos_226 grant tests), and `pytest.skip` only if no recognised surface exists yet, with one non-skipping anchor so the contract fails loudly on the empty stub. Scope: only the CONTROLLER's instants/sorceries (not creature spells, not opponents' spells, nothing while Witherbloom is off the battlefield).\n   - If driving the granted reduction through the actual cast/cost pipeline isn't expressible yet, record it in `untestable.json` with what would unblock it (the coordinator will arbitrate building engine support, then re-invoke you once).\n\nMake tests FAIL against the current empty stub (genuine behavioral assertions, not import errors) — TDD red. Statics + Witherbloom's own affinity should be concrete passes once implemented; the granted-affinity surface is the harder part.\n\nOutputs:\n- Test file at `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md` — behaviour contract + per-test rationale + what you deferred and why.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-files.txt` — list of test file paths.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/untestable.json` — JSON array of requirements you could NOT test yet + what would unblock each (empty `[]` if none).\n\nReturn a short status summary:\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_count: <N>\nred_confirmed: <yes/no — how many fail vs skip against the stub>\nuntestable_count: <N>\ntest_files_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-files.txt","agentId":"a09592f3c6a3e7877","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All outputs are in place and validated. The tests are in the correct TDD red state.\n\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_count: 27\nred_confirmed: yes — 17 fail (genuine behavioral contracts: statics, positive cost-reduction counts, and the non-skipping grant-surface anchor), 7 skip (5 granted-affinity scope probes with no surface on the stub, plus 2 optional-static surface probes), 3 pass (zero-expecting cost-reduction scope tests; `CardImpl.cost_reduction` returns 0 so the opponent/non-creature exclusion assertions are already satisfied — same shape as sos_1's empty-graveyard test, and anchored by the positive-count tests that fail red)\nuntestable_count: 1\ntest_files_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-files.txt\n\nNotes:\n- Test file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` (27 cases, under the 30 cap).\n- Static data, Witherbloom's own affinity-for-creatures cost reduction (raw `cost_reduction` count + engine `get_cost_reduction` clamp to the `{6}` generic), and the granted-affinity grant surface are all covered. \"Affinity\" is asserted to be a printed-keyword label, never a `Keyword` enum member (the enum is frozen at 16; no AFFINITY).\n- The granted affinity is probed tolerantly (mirroring sos_226/sos_201). The non-skipping anchor `TestWitherbloomGrantWiring::test_card_exposes_an_affinity_grant_surface` fails loudly on the empty stub so the grant contract is never silently green.\n- One requirement deferred to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/untestable.json`: driving the GRANTED per-spell reduction through the live cast/cost pipeline — no engine affinity pipeline exists; the unblock is an additive granted-cost-reduction hook in `cast_spell`/`get_cost_reduction` (registry like `engine.casualty`/`engine.miracle`)."}],"totalDurationMs":211805,"totalTokens":101459,"totalToolUseCount":30,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":100380,"output_tokens":702,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":375},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":100380,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":375,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":16,"searchCount":4,"bashCount":6,"editFileCount":4,"linesAdded":675,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
