{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01FVXzmzofcx5nMQi72M9q1Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B4X9GxSDLX7Bgynhzjs8JW","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator Directives — sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n\nCard: **Witherbloom, the Balancer** — `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon — 5/5 —\nFlying, Deathtouch (complex tier).\nOracle:\n> Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control.)\n> Flying, deathtouch\n> Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\n\nThe Tester wrote 27 tests: statics + Witherbloom's OWN affinity-for-creatures cost reduction +\na non-skipping grant-surface anchor all FAIL on the empty stub; 7 tolerant granted-affinity\nprobes SKIP pending a queryable surface; 3 zero-count scope tests pass vacuously (anchored by\nthe failing positive-count tests). One item is deferred in\n`/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/untestable.json`: driving the GRANTED per-spell reduction through\nthe live cast/cost pipeline.\n\nADDITIVE per AGENTS.md: add new methods/classes/helpers/fields/modules; modify existing\nfunction BODIES; NEVER rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. The `Keyword` enum MUST stay\nat 16 members — confirm whether \"Affinity\" is already one of the 16 existing members; if NOT,\nit is a printed label in `printed_keywords` (do not add to the enum). Reuse prior-card\nconventions in KEY_DECISIONS.md (the sos_1/fdn_167 cost-reduction convention; the\nsos_201/sos_226 grant-surface + lazy-registry pattern).\n\n## Statics + Witherbloom's OWN affinity (make these pass first)\n- Creature \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\", `{6}{B}{G}` (mv 8), 5/5, LEGENDARY, subtypes\n  {Dragon, Elder}, keywords Deathtouch + Flying (+ Affinity, modeled as the Tester expects —\n  printed label unless Affinity is an existing enum member), colors B+G.\n- **Affinity for creatures on Witherbloom itself**: it costs {1} less to cast per creature its\n  controller controls. Implement via the established `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` hook\n  (sos_1 / fdn_167 Tolarian Terror): return the number of creatures the controller controls;\n  the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the spell's generic portion. Make the\n  positive-count tests AND the engine-clamp tests pass.\n\n## Build an additive granted-cost-reduction hook (the deferred item)\n\"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\" Two pieces:\n1. **The grant surface (queryable).** Expose, mirroring sos_201/sos_226, a query method on the\n   Witherbloom card (e.g. `get_affinity_grant(self, game, spell)` / `grants_affinity(...)` —\n   read `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` to see EXACTLY which method/attribute names the tolerant\n   probe recognises and satisfy them) AND/OR an attribute the grant writes onto affected\n   spells. Scope: only the CONTROLLER's instants/sorceries (not creature spells, not opponents'\n   spells, nothing while Witherbloom is off the battlefield). Make the 7 skipped probes + the\n   non-skipping anchor become real PASSES.\n2. **Drive the granted reduction through the cast/cost pipeline.** Add an additive hook so that\n   when the controller casts a granted instant/sorcery, its generic cost drops by the number of\n   creatures the controller controls (clamped to the spell's generic), EXACTLY like affinity.\n   The unblock (from untestable.json): a registry mirroring `engine.casualty`/`engine.miracle`\n   that, when `cast_spell`/`get_cost_reduction` computes a spell's effective cost, ADDS any\n   granted reduction registered for that controller's instants/sorceries. Extend\n   `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (modify its BODY additively) to consult the granted-\n   reduction registry in addition to the cast card's own `cost_reduction(game)` hook — both\n   contributions sum, then clamp to the spell's generic. Do NOT break existing cost-reduction\n   behavior (sos_1, fdn_167) — when no grant is registered, behavior is unchanged.\n   Suggested: a new `engine/affinity.py` (or fold into the cost-reduction path) with a lazy\n   per-game registry `game._affinity_grants` keyed by `id(source)`; the card registers its\n   grant in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects` and clears it on leave-play.\n\n## Make ALL 27 tests pass (no avoidable skips)\nRead `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`; satisfy every assertion + grant probe. Do NOT modify any\ntest file. If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible, return DISPUTE.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` → all pass.\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (report totals). Pay special attention that\n  sos_1 and fdn_167 cost-reduction tests still pass after you touch `get_cost_reduction`.\n\nAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to add end-to-end granted-\nreduction tests (cast a granted instant while controlling N creatures → generic paid drops by\nmin(N, generic); scoping driven through the pipeline). Build the hook so those are real.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":799,"cache_read_input_tokens":70978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":799},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"d775b5e0-f293-4193-ad1c-6e7dac003ae7","request_id":"req_011CbeDrKAYNGQD95zoEmx9p"}
