{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Aybdcuni5NQjyiRgS3UaxR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011ZQCTY2TPiZpW5s2RVhLVB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement sos_245 + affinity grant hook","subagent_type":"Implementer","prompt":"Card: sos_245 \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\". Implement the card AND build an additive engine hook so a granting permanent can contribute a per-spell cost reduction (granted affinity-for-creatures) recognised by the cast/cost pipeline.\n\nRead these first (in order):\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/coordinator-directives.md` — your full task. READ THE WHOLE FILE.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md` — the Tester's behaviour contract and exactly which grant-surface method/attribute names the tolerant probes recognise.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/untestable.json` — the deferred item you must make testable (driving the granted reduction through the live cast/cost pipeline).\n- `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` — the 27 tests you must make pass. You MUST NOT modify this file (the only entry in `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-files.txt`).\n\nWorkspace context:\n- `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`, `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md`, `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n- The cost-reduction convention is documented in KEY_DECISIONS.md (from sos_1 / fdn_167 Tolarian Terror): a card exposes `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` (raw count), and `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the spell's generic portion. READ `engine/casting.py` to see `get_cost_reduction` / `cast_spell` and how effective cost is computed.\n- The grant-surface + lazy-per-game-registry pattern is in `engine/miracle.py` (sos_201) and `engine/casualty.py` (sos_226) — mirror it.\n- FDN reference: `cards/fdn/fdn_167/card_impl.py` (Tolarian Terror) for the own-affinity cost_reduction shape.\n\nTHE TASK: implement `cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` (`WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)`: statics {6}{B}{G}/5-5/LEGENDARY/Dragon+Elder/Flying+Deathtouch+Affinity/colors B+G; its OWN affinity-for-creatures via `cost_reduction` = number of creatures controller controls; a queryable granted-affinity surface for the controller's instants/sorceries). AND extend the engine ADDITIVELY so the granted reduction actually applies through `cast_spell`/`get_cost_reduction`: add a granted-reduction registry (e.g. new `engine/affinity.py` with lazy `game._affinity_grants` keyed by `id(source)`, mirroring engine.casualty), and modify the BODY of `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` so it sums the cast card's own `cost_reduction(game)` with any granted reduction registered for that controller's instants/sorceries, then clamps to the spell's generic. When no grant is registered, behavior MUST be unchanged (sos_1, fdn_167 still pass). See the directives file for exact surfaces and scope rules.\n\nConstraints:\n- ADDITIVE engine changes only: add new methods/classes/helpers/fields/modules, modify existing function BODIES, but never rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. The `Keyword` enum MUST stay at exactly 16 members (confirm \"Affinity\" is either an existing member or a printed label — do NOT grow the enum).\n- Use a lazy per-game registry (no GameState.__init__ change).\n- You MUST NOT modify any test file. If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible, return DISPUTE.\n\nVerification you must run:\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` → all 27 pass.\n- `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (report totals). Confirm sos_1 and fdn_167 cost-reduction tests still pass.\n\nOutputs (write all):\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl.diff` — full git diff of implementation + engine changes (NOT test files).\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md` — rationale: own-affinity, the granted-affinity grant surface, the granted-reduction registry + how get_cost_reduction was extended (and why existing reductions are unaffected), what you reuse