{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KDJJWCGGK7ZFkgpjU44DkX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives — sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Witherbloom, the Balancer** — `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon — 5/5 —\n4\tFlying, Deathtouch (complex tier).\n5\tOracle:\n6\t> Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control.)\n7\t> Flying, deathtouch\n8\t> Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\n9\t\n10\tThe Tester wrote 27 tests: statics + Witherbloom's OWN affinity-for-creatures cost reduction +\n11\ta non-skipping grant-surface anchor all FAIL on the empty stub; 7 tolerant granted-affinity\n12\tprobes SKIP pending a queryable surface; 3 zero-count scope tests pass vacuously (anchored by\n13\tthe failing positive-count tests). One item is deferred in\n14\t`/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/untestable.json`: driving the GRANTED per-spell reduction through\n15\tthe live cast/cost pipeline.\n16\t\n17\tADDITIVE per AGENTS.md: add new methods/classes/helpers/fields/modules; modify existing\n18\tfunction BODIES; NEVER rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. The `Keyword` enum MUST stay\n19\tat 16 members — confirm whether \"Affinity\" is already one of the 16 existing members; if NOT,\n20\tit is a printed label in `printed_keywords` (do not add to the enum). Reuse prior-card\n21\tconventions in KEY_DECISIONS.md (the sos_1/fdn_167 cost-reduction convention; the\n22\tsos_201/sos_226 grant-surface + lazy-registry pattern).\n23\t\n24\t## Statics + Witherbloom's OWN affinity (make these pass first)\n25\t- Creature \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\", `{6}{B}{G}` (mv 8), 5/5, LEGENDARY, subtypes\n26\t  {Dragon, Elder}, keywords Deathtouch + Flying (+ Affinity, modeled as the Tester expects —\n27\t  printed label unless Affinity is an existing enum member), colors B+G.\n28\t- **Affinity for creatures on Witherbloom itself**: it costs {1} less to cast per creature its\n29\t  controller controls. Implement via the established `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` hook\n30\t  (sos_1 / fdn_167 Tolarian Terror): return the number of creatures the controller controls;\n31\t  the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the spell's generic portion. Make the\n32\t  positive-count tests AND the engine-clamp tests pass.\n33\t\n34\t## Build an additive granted-cost-reduction hook (the deferred item)\n35\t\"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\" Two pieces:\n36\t1. **The grant surface (queryable).** Expose, mirroring sos_201/sos_226, a query method on the\n37\t   Witherbloom card (e.g. `get_affinity_grant(self, game, spell)` / `grants_affinity(...)` —\n38\t   read `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` to see EXACTLY which method/attribute names the tolerant\n39\t   probe recognises and satisfy them) AND/OR an attribute the grant writes onto affected\n40\t   spells. Scope: only the CONTROLLER's instants/sorceries (not creature spells, not opponents'\n41\t   spells, nothing while Witherbloom is off the battlefield). Make the 7 skipped probes + the\n42\t   non-skipping anchor become real PASSES.\n43\t2. **Drive the granted reduction through the cast/cost pipeline.** Add an additive hook so that\n44\t   when the controller casts a granted instant/sorcery, its generic cost drops by the number of\n45\t   creatures the controller controls (clamped to the spell's generic), EXACTLY like affinity.\n46\t   The unblock (from untestable.json): a registry mirroring `engine.casualty`/`engine.miracle`\n47\t   that, when `cast_spell`/`get_cost_reduction` computes a spell's effective cost, ADDS any\n48\t   granted reduction registered for that controller's instants/sorceries. Extend\n49\t   `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (modify its BODY additively) to consult the granted-\n50\t   reduction registry in addition to the cast card's own `cost_reduction(game)` hook — both\n51\t   contributions sum, then clamp to the spell's generic. Do NOT break existing cost-reduction\n52\t   behavior (sos_1, fdn_167) — when no grant is registered, behavior is unchanged.\n53\t   Suggested: a new `engine/affinity.py` (or fold into the cost-reduction path) with a lazy\n54\t   per-game registry `game._affinity_grants` keyed by `id(source)`; the card registers its\n55\t   grant in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects` and clears it on leave-play.\n56\t\n57\t## Make ALL 27 tests pass (no avoidable skips)\n58\tRead `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`; satisfy every assertion + grant probe. Do NOT modify any\n59\ttest file. If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible, return DISPUTE.\n60\t\n61\t## Verification\n62\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` → all pass.\n63\t- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (report totals). Pay special attention that\n64\t  sos_1 and fdn_167 cost-reduction tests still pass after you touch `get_cost_reduction`.\n65\t\n66\tAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to add end-to-end granted-\n67\treduction tests (cast a granted instant while controlling N creatures → generic paid drops by\n68\tmin(N, generic); scoping driven through the pipeline). Build the hook so those are real.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011ZQCTY2TPiZpW5s2RVhLVB","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"e5a86219-4892-448c-ac7c-1eb9e7d13f43","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:48:54.081Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245 + affinity grant hook"}
