{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MknLHRCEfgL343befxCXyG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Tests for SOS 245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer.\n2\t\n3\tOracle text (from card_spec.json):\n4\t\n5\t    Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature\n6\t    you control.)\n7\t    Flying, deathtouch\n8\t    Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\n9\t\n10\tBehaviour contract derived from that text:\n11\t\n12\t* Static: Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, {6}{B}{G} (mana value 8), 5/5,\n13\t  black+green, with Flying and Deathtouch. \"Affinity\" is NOT an evergreen\n14\t  ``engine.types.Keyword`` enum member (that enum is frozen at 16 members and\n15\t  ``engine_tests/test_types.py::test_exactly_sixteen_members`` hard-asserts\n16\t  that), so it must be recorded as a printed-keyword label, never an enum\n17\t  member.\n18\t\n19\t* Witherbloom's OWN affinity for creatures: the {6}{B}{G} spell costs {1} less\n20\t  to cast for each creature its controller controls. This is exactly the\n21\t  sos_1 / fdn_167 cost-reduction shape — the card's ``cost_reduction(game)``\n22\t  hook returns the raw count (number of creatures the controller controls), and\n23\t  the engine's ``get_cost_reduction`` clamps that count to the generic portion\n24\t  ({6}) of the cost. Only creatures the CONTROLLER controls count (an\n25\t  opponent's creatures do not); only creatures count (other permanents do not).\n26\t\n27\t* Granted affinity for creatures: a continuous static ability that grants\n28\t  affinity for creatures to each instant and sorcery SPELL its controller\n29\t  casts. There is no engine-level affinity pipeline yet, so the implementation\n30\t  must expose some observable surface that reports the grant for the\n31\t  controller's instants/sorceries (and grants it to no other card types, no\n32\t  other players, and not while Witherbloom is off the battlefield). These tests\n33\t  probe that surface TOLERANTLY — they accept any of the conventional spellings\n34\t  the implementer is likely to use (a query method on the Witherbloom card\n35\t  and/or an attribute written onto the affected spell), and skip-with-reason\n36\t  only if NO recognised surface exists (anchored on one non-skipping positive\n37\t  case so the contract fails loudly on an empty stub).\n38\t\n39\t  Driving the GRANTED reduction through the actual cast/cost pipeline (so that\n40\t  casting a granted instant while controlling N creatures really pays {N} less)\n41\t  is recorded in untestable.json: there is no engine affinity pipeline wiring a\n42\t  granted, per-spell cost reduction into ``cast_spell`` yet.\n43\t\n44\tThese tests are written for the TDD red phase: they must FAIL against the empty\n45\tstub and PASS once the card is implemented correctly.\n46\t\"\"\"\n47\t\n48\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n49\t\n50\tfrom typing import Any\n51\t\n52\timport pytest\n53\t\n54\tfrom cards.sos.sos_245.card_impl import WitherbloomTheBalancer\n55\tfrom engine.card import Creature, Instant, Sorcery\n56\tfrom engine.casting import get_cost_reduction\n57\tfrom engine.types import Color, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Supertype\n58\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n59\t\n60\t\n61\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n62\t# Test helper cards\n63\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n64\t\n65\t\n66\tdef _vanilla_instant(name: str = \"Test Instant\") -> Instant:\n67\t    return Instant(name=name, mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{R}\"))\n68\t\n69\t\n70\tdef _vanilla_sorcery(name: str = \"Test Sorcery\") -> Sorcery:\n71\t    return Sorcery(name=name, mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{2}{R}\"))\n72\t\n73\t\n74\tdef _vanilla_creature(name: str = \"Test Bear\") -> Creature:\n75\t    return Creature(\n76\t        name=name,\n77\t        mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{G}\"),\n78\t        base_power=2,\n79\t        base_toughness=2,\n80\t    )\n81\t\n82\t\n83\tdef _affinity_grant_for(card_obj: Any, game: Any, spell: Any) -> Any:\n84\t    \"\"\"Best-effort probe for the granted affinity-for-creatures of *spell*.\n85\t\n86\t    The affinity grant has no engine pipeline, so the implementation is free to\n87\t    surface it in a number of conventional ways. This helper tries each in turn\n88\t    and returns the reported value, or raises ``pytest.skip`` if no recognised\n89\t    surface exists (so the contract is not silently green).\n90\t    \"\"\"\n91\t    val = _probe_affinity_silent(card_obj, game, spell)\n92\t    if val is _MISSING:\n93\t        pytest.skip(\n94\t            \"No observable surface for the granted affinity for creatures — \"\n95\t            \"the implementation must expose a query method on the card \"\n96\t            \"(e.g. has_affinity_for_creatures(...)/get_affinity(...)/\"\n97\t            \"grants_affinity_to(...)) or an attribute on the affected spell \"\n98\t            \"(e.g. affinity_for_creatures / affinity / granted_affinity).\"\n99\t        )\n100\t    return val\n101\t\n102\t\n103\t_MISSING = object()\n104\t\n105\t\n106\tdef _probe_affinity_silent(card_obj: Any, game: Any, spell: Any) -> Any:\n107\t    \"\"\"Like ``_affinity_grant_for`` but returns the sentinel ``_MISSING`` when no\n108\t    recognised surface reports a value for *spell* (used for exclusion-side\n109\t    assertions, always anchored on a positive case so the test is never\n110\t    vacuous).\"\"\"\n111\t    # 1. A method on the Witherbloom card that reports whether/what affinity it\n112\t    #    grants to a given spell.\n113\t    for meth_name in (\n114\t        \"has_affinity_for_creatures\",\n115\t        \"grants_affinity_for_creatures\",\n116\t        \"grants_affinity_to\",\n117\t        \"affinity_for_creatures_for\",\n118\t        \"get_affinity_for_creatures\",\n119\t        \"affinity_for\",\n120\t        \"get_affinity\",\n121\t        \"affinity_value_for\",\n122\t        \"get_affinity_value\",\n123\t    ):\n124\t        meth = getattr(card_obj, meth_name, None)\n125\t        if callable(meth):\n126\t            try:\n127\t                return meth(game, spell)\n128\t            except TypeError:\n129\t                try:\n130\t                    return meth(spell)\n131\t                except TypeError:\n132\t                    continue\n133\t    # 2. The grant written directly onto the spell.\n134\t    for attr_name in (\n135\t        \"affinity_for_creatures\",\n136\t        \"has_affinity_for_creatures\",\n137\t        \"granted_affinity_for_creatures\",\n138\t        \"affinity\",\n139\t        \"granted_affinity\",\n140\t    ):\n141\t        if hasattr(spell, attr_name):\n142\t            val = getattr(spell, attr_name)\n143\t            if val is not None:\n144\t                return val\n145\t    return _MISSING\n146\t\n147\t\n148\tdef _is_granted(value: Any) -> bool:\n149\t    \"\"\"Return True if *value* represents an active affinity-for-creatures grant.\n150\t\n151\t    Accepts a truthy flag (``True``), a string like ``\"creatures\"`` /\n152\t    ``\"affinity for creatures\"``, or anything exposing a ``.kind``/``.type``\n153\t    naming creatures. A bare ``None``/``False``/``0`` means \"not granted\".\n154\t    \"\"\"\n155\t    if value is _MISSING or value is None or value is False:\n156\t        return False\n157\t    if value is True:\n158\t        return True\n159\t    if isinstance(value, str):\n160\t        low = value.lower()\n161\t        return \"creature\" in low or \"affinity\" in low\n162\t    if isinstance(value, int):\n163\t        return value != 0\n164\t    for attr in (\"kind\", \"type\", \"value\", \"name\"):\n165\t        v = getattr(value, attr, None)\n166\t        if isinstance(v, str) and \"creature\" in v.lower():\n167\t            return True\n168\t    # An object that exists and is not a recognised \"off\" sentinel: treat as a\n169\t    # grant (the implementation chose to return some grant descriptor).\n170\t    return True\n171\t\n172\t\n173\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n174\t# Static card data\n175\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n176\t\n177\t\n178\tclass TestWitherbloomProperties:\n179\t    \"\"\"Static characteristics must match the SOS 245 spec.\"\"\"\n180\t\n181\t    def test_is_creature(self) -> None:\n182\t        assert isinstance(WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None), Creature)\n183\t\n184\t    def test_name(self) -> None:\n185\t        assert (\n186\t            WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None).name == \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\"\n187\t        )\n188\t\n189\t    def test_mana_cost(self) -> None:\n190\t        assert WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None).mana_cost == ManaCost.parse(\n191\t            \"{6}{B}{G}\"\n192\t        )\n193\t\n194\t    def test_mana_value_is_eight(self) -> None:\n195\t        assert WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None).mana_cost.cmc == 8\n196\t\n197\t    def test_generic_portion_is_six(self) -> None:\n198\t        \"\"\"The generic portion is {6}; affinity reduces only this part.\"\"\"\n199\t        assert WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None).mana_cost.generic == 6\n200\t\n201\t    def test_power_toughness(self) -> None:\n202\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None)\n203\t        assert card.base_power == 5\n204\t        assert card.base_toughness == 5\n205\t\n206\t    def test_is_legendary(self) -> None:\n207\t        assert (\n208\t            Supertype.LEGENDARY in WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None).supertypes\n209\t        )\n210\t\n211\t    def test_is_elder_dragon(self) -> None:\n212\t        subtypes = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None).subtypes\n213\t        assert \"Dragon\" in subtypes\n214\t        assert \"Elder\" in subtypes\n215\t\n216\t    def test_has_flying(self) -> None:\n217\t        assert Keyword.FLYING in WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None).keywords\n218\t\n219\t    def test_has_deathtouch(self) -> None:\n220\t        assert Keyword.DEATHTOUCH in WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None).keywords\n221\t\n222\t    def test_is_black_green(self) -> None:\n223\t        \"\"\"{6}{B}{G} has exactly one black and one green pip and no others.\"\"\"\n224\t        cost = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None).mana_cost\n225\t        assert cost.pips.get(ManaType.BLACK, 0) == 1\n226\t        assert cost.pips.get(ManaType.GREEN, 0) == 1\n227\t        assert cost.pips.get(ManaType.WHITE, 0) == 0\n228\t        assert cost.pips.get(ManaType.BLUE, 0) == 0\n229\t        assert cost.pips.get(ManaType.RED, 0) == 0\n230\t\n231\t    def test_colors_are_black_and_green(self) -> None:\n232\t        \"\"\"If the implementation exposes a ``colors`` surface it must be exactly\n233\t        {B, G}. If it does not, the pip-based ``test_is_black_green`` above\n234\t        already pins the colours, so this is skipped rather than failing.\"\"\"\n235\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None)\n236\t        colors = getattr(card, \"colors\", None)\n237\t        if not colors:\n238\t            pytest.skip(\"no explicit colors attribute; pip test covers colours\")\n239\t        assert set(colors) == {Color.BLACK, Color.GREEN}\n240\t\n241\t    def test_affinity_is_printed_keyword_label_not_enum(self) -> None:\n242\t        \"\"\"'Affinity' is a printed-keyword label (the Keyword enum is frozen at\n243\t        16 evergreen members), so it must NOT appear as a Keyword enum member.\n244\t        If the implementation records printed labels, \"Affinity\" should be among\n245\t        them; if it exposes no such surface this is skipped (the cost-reduction\n246\t        and grant tests below are the real affinity contract).\"\"\"\n247\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=None)\n248\t        # Affinity must not have been smuggled into the evergreen Keyword enum.\n249\t        assert not hasattr(Keyword, \"AFFINITY\")\n250\t        labels = getattr(card, \"printed_keywords\", None)\n251\t        if labels is None:\n252\t            pytest.skip(\"no printed_keywords surface to assert the Affinity label\")\n253\t        assert any(\"affinity\" in str(label).lower() for label in labels)\n254\t\n255\t\n256\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n257\t# Witherbloom's own affinity for creatures — cost reduction\n258\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n259\t\n260\t\n261\tclass TestWitherbloomOwnAffinityCostReduction:\n262\t    \"\"\"Affinity for creatures: {6}{B}{G} costs {1} less to cast for each creature\n263\t    YOU control (the sos_1 / fdn_167 cost-reduction convention).\"\"\"\n264\t\n265\t    def test_no_reduction_with_no_creatures(self) -> None:\n266\t        game = create_game()\n267\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n268\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n269\t        assert card.cost_reduction(game) == 0\n270\t\n271\t    def test_one_creature_reduces_by_one(self) -> None:\n272\t        game = create_game()\n273\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n274\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n275\t        set_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=[_vanilla_creature(\"Bear\")])\n276\t        assert card.cost_reduction(game) == 1\n277\t\n278\t    def test_three_creatures_reduce_by_three(self) -> None:\n279\t        game = create_game()\n280\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n281\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n282\t        set_board_state(\n283\t            game,\n284\t            0,\n285\t            battlefield=[\n286\t                _vanilla_creature(\"Bear A\"),\n287\t                _vanilla_creature(\"Bear B\"),\n288\t                _vanilla_creature(\"Bear C\"),\n289\t            ],\n290\t        )\n291\t        assert card.cost_reduction(game) == 3\n292\t\n293\t    def test_non_creature_permanents_do_not_count(self) -> None:\n294\t        \"\"\"Affinity for CREATURES counts only creatures; an instant/sorcery card\n295\t        on the battlefield-side zones is not a creature and must not reduce the\n296\t        cost. (We use non-creature cards placed in the controller's graveyard to\n297\t        confirm they never get counted as battlefield creatures.)\"\"\"\n298\t        game = create_game()\n299\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n300\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n301\t        set_board_state(\n302\t            game,\n303\t            0,\n304\t            battlefield=[],\n305\t            graveyard=[_vanilla_instant(\"Gy Bolt\"), _vanilla_sorcery(\"Gy Ritual\")],\n306\t        )\n307\t        assert card.cost_reduction(game) == 0\n308\t\n309\t    def test_only_creatures_you_control_count(self) -> None:\n310\t        \"\"\"An opponent's creatures must not reduce the cost — only creatures\n311\t        YOU control count. Controller has zero creatures; opponent has three.\"\"\"\n312\t        game = create_game()\n313\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n314\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n315\t        set_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=[])\n316\t        set_board_state(\n317\t            game,\n318\t            1,\n319\t            battlefield=[\n320\t                _vanilla_creature(\"Opp A\"),\n321\t                _vanilla_creature(\"Opp B\"),\n322\t                _vanilla_creature(\"Opp C\"),\n323\t            ],\n324\t        )\n325\t        assert card.cost_reduction(game) == 0\n326\t\n327\t    def test_witherbloom_itself_does_not_count_while_on_stack(self) -> None:\n328\t        \"\"\"When Witherbloom is being cast it is on the stack, not the\n329\t        battlefield, so it does not count itself. Controlling exactly one OTHER\n330\t        creature reduces the cost by exactly 1 (not 2).\"\"\"\n331\t        game = create_game()\n332\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n333\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n334\t        # Only a single other creature is on the battlefield; Witherbloom is not.\n335\t        set_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=[_vanilla_creature(\"Lone Bear\")])\n336\t        assert card.cost_reduction(game) == 1\n337\t\n338\t    def test_effective_reduction_through_engine_partial(self) -> None:\n339\t        \"\"\"Driving the count through the engine's clamp helper: four creatures\n340\t        reduce the {6} generic by exactly 4.\"\"\"\n341\t        game = create_game()\n342\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n343\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n344\t        set_board_state(\n345\t            game,\n346\t            0,\n347\t            battlefield=[\n348\t                _vanilla_creature(\"A\"),\n349\t                _vanilla_creature(\"B\"),\n350\t                _vanilla_creature(\"C\"),\n351\t                _vanilla_creature(\"D\"),\n352\t            ],\n353\t        )\n354\t        assert get_cost_reduction(game, card, p1) == 4\n355\t\n356\t    def test_effective_reduction_clamped_to_generic_six(self) -> None:\n357\t        \"\"\"The engine clamps the reduction to the generic portion ({6}), so\n358\t        controlling more than six creatures cannot push generic below 0 — the\n359\t        clamped effective reduction is 6 even with nine creatures.\"\"\"\n360\t        game = create_game()\n361\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n362\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n363\t        creatures = [_vanilla_creature(f\"C{i}\") for i in range(9)]\n364\t        set_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=creatures)\n365\t        # The raw hook may report 9, but the clamped effective reduction is 6.\n366\t        assert get_cost_reduction(game, card, p1) == 6\n367\t\n368\t\n369\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n370\t# Granted affinity for creatures — controller's instant/sorcery spells\n371\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n372\t\n373\t\n374\tclass TestWitherbloomGrantsAffinityToSpells:\n375\t    \"\"\"While on the battlefield, Witherbloom grants affinity for creatures to\n376\t    each instant and sorcery SPELL its controller casts (and to nothing else).\"\"\"\n377\t\n378\t    def _setup(\n379\t        self,\n380\t        controller_spells: list[Any],\n381\t        opp_spells: list[Any] | None = None,\n382\t        *,\n383\t        on_battlefield: bool = True,\n384\t    ):\n385\t        game = create_game()\n386\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n387\t        p2 = game.players[1]\n388\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n389\t        if on_battlefield:\n390\t            set_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=[card], hand=controller_spells)\n391\t        else:\n392\t            # Witherbloom in hand, not on the battlefield: the grant must be off.\n393\t            set_board_state(game, 0, hand=[card] + controller_spells)\n394\t        if opp_spells is not None:\n395\t            set_board_state(game, 1, hand=opp_spells)\n396\t        # Apply continuous effects / triggers if the engine maintains them, so a\n397\t        # registry-based implementation has a chance to write its grant.\n398\t        try:\n399\t            card.register_replacement_effects(game)\n400\t            card.register_triggers(game)\n401\t        except Exception:\n402\t            pass\n403\t        if hasattr(game, \"effect_manager\"):\n404\t            try:\n405\t                game.effect_manager.apply_all(game)\n406\t            except Exception:\n407\t                pass\n408\t        return game, p1, p2, card\n409\t\n410\t    def test_instant_gets_affinity(self) -> None:\n411\t        \"\"\"A controller's instant is granted affinity for creatures.\"\"\"\n412\t        spell = _vanilla_instant(\"My Bolt\")\n413\t        game, p1, p2, card = self._setup([spell])\n414\t        assert _is_granted(_affinity_grant_for(card, game, spell))\n415\t\n416\t    def test_sorcery_gets_affinity(self) -> None:\n417\t        \"\"\"A controller's sorcery is granted affinity for creatures.\"\"\"\n418\t        spell = _vanilla_sorcery(\"My Ritual\")\n419\t        game, p1, p2, card = self._setup([spell])\n420\t        assert _is_granted(_affinity_grant_for(card, game, spell))\n421\t\n422\t    def test_creature_spell_does_not_get_affinity(self) -> None:\n423\t        \"\"\"The grant is only for instant/sorcery spells. A creature spell is\n424\t        neither, so it must not be granted affinity. Anchored on a real instant\n425\t        first (via the probe, which skips if no surface exists) so this fails on\n426\t        an empty stub rather than passing vacuously.\"\"\"\n427\t        anchor = _vanilla_instant(\"Anchor Bolt\")\n428\t        bear = _vanilla_creature(\"Hand Bear\")\n429\t        game, p1, p2, card = self._setup([anchor, bear])\n430\t        # Anchor: confirm the grant surface exists and grants the instant.\n431\t        assert _is_granted(_affinity_grant_for(card, game, anchor))\n432\t        # The creature spell must NOT be granted affinity.\n433\t        assert not _is_granted(_probe_affinity_silent(card, game, bear))\n434\t\n435\t    def test_opponents_instant_does_not_get_affinity(self) -> None:\n436\t        \"\"\"Only spells YOU cast get affinity — an opponent's instant is\n437\t        unaffected. Anchored on a controller-side instant so the test fails on an\n438\t        empty stub rather than passing vacuously.\"\"\"\n439\t        my_spell = _vanilla_instant(\"My Instant\")\n440\t        opp_spell = _vanilla_instant(\"Opp Instant\")\n441\t        game, p1, p2, card = self._setup([my_spell], opp_spells=[opp_spell])\n442\t        # Anchor: my own instant gets affinity (skips if no surface exists).\n443\t        assert _is_granted(_affinity_grant_for(card, game, my_spell))\n444\t        # The opponent's instant must NOT be granted affinity.\n445\t        assert not _is_granted(_probe_affinity_silent(card, game, opp_spell))\n446\t\n447\t    def test_no_grant_while_off_battlefield(self) -> None:\n448\t        \"\"\"A static ability of a permanent functions only while that permanent\n449\t        is on the battlefield (CR 113.6 / 604.x). With Witherbloom in hand (not\n450\t        on the battlefield), an instant must NOT be granted affinity.\n451\t\n452\t        Anchored on the positive on-battlefield case (which skips if no surface\n453\t        exists), so a stub that always returns a grant is caught while\n454\t        genuinely-absent surfaces skip rather than pass.\"\"\"\n455\t        # Positive anchor: a parallel on-battlefield setup must grant affinity.\n456\t        anchor_spell = _vanilla_instant(\"Anchor While On Field\")\n457\t        a_game, _, _, a_card = self._setup([anchor_spell])\n458\t        assert _is_granted(_affinity_grant_for(a_card, a_game, anchor_spell))\n459\t\n460\t        # Now Witherbloom is in hand, not on the battlefield: no grant.\n461\t        spell = _vanilla_instant(\"Off Field Instant\")\n462\t        game, p1, p2, card = self._setup([spell], on_battlefield=False)\n463\t        assert not _is_granted(_probe_affinity_silent(card, game, spell))\n464\t\n465\t\n466\tclass TestWitherbloomGrantWiring:\n467\t    \"\"\"The affinity grant is a continuous static ability, so the card must wire\n468\t    it through one of the engine's continuous/effect/trigger hooks rather than\n469\t    doing nothing. We assert the card actually installs something observable.\"\"\"\n470\t\n471\t    def test_card_exposes_an_affinity_grant_surface(self) -> None:\n472\t        \"\"\"The implementation must expose at least one recognised affinity-grant\n473\t        surface (a query method on the card, or an attribute it writes onto an\n474\t        affected spell). An empty stub exposes none and fails here.\"\"\"\n475\t        game = create_game()\n476\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n477\t        card = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n478\t        spell = _vanilla_instant(\"Probe Instant\")\n479\t        set_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=[card], hand=[spell])\n480\t        try:\n481\t            card.register_replacement_effects(game)\n482\t            card.register_triggers(game)\n483\t        except Exception:\n484\t            pass\n485\t        if hasattr(game, \"effect_manager\"):\n486\t            try:\n487\t                game.effect_manager.apply_all(game)\n488\t            except Exception:\n489\t                pass\n490\t\n491\t        has_method = any(\n492\t            callable(getattr(card, m, None))\n493\t            for m in (\n494\t                \"has_affinity_for_creatures\",\n495\t                \"grants_affinity_for_creatures\",\n496\t                \"grants_affinity_to\",\n497\t                \"affinity_for_creatures_for\",\n498\t                \"get_affinity_for_creatures\",\n499\t                \"affinity_for\",\n500\t                \"get_affinity\",\n501\t                \"affinity_value_for\",\n502\t                \"get_affinity_value\",\n503\t            )\n504\t        )\n505\t        has_attr = any(\n506\t            getattr(spell, a, None) is not None\n507\t            for a in (\n508\t                \"affinity_for_creatures\",\n509\t                \"has_affinity_for_creatures\",\n510\t                \"granted_affinity_for_creatures\",\n511\t                \"affinity\",\n512\t                \"granted_affinity\",\n513\t            )\n514\t        )\n515\t        assert has_method or has_attr, (\n516\t            \"Witherbloom must expose an observable affinity-grant surface \"\n517\t            \"(a query method on the card or an attribute on the affected spell).\"\n518\t        )\n519\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011ZQCTY2TPiZpW5s2RVhLVB","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"58f5dadb-6f96-4777-91df-40ecd7e1d473","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:48:55.086Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245 + affinity grant hook"}
