{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QVHVcV8UVhGrS1GKMxc1GV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X2hrJKkoBQxHxMjg4eJ8Ho","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_245 \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\"\n\n## Static data\n`WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)`: name \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\", cost\n`{6}{B}{G}` (mv 8, generic 6), base P/T 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes\n`{Dragon, Elder}`, keywords `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`, explicit\n`self.colors = [Color.BLACK, Color.GREEN]`. \"Affinity\" is recorded as a printed\nlabel in `self.printed_keywords = [\"Affinity\"]` — it is **not** added to the\n`Keyword` enum, which stays frozen at 16 members (confirmed\n`engine_tests/test_types.py` and `not hasattr(Keyword, \"AFFINITY\")` both pass).\nThis follows the Casualty/Miracle/Paradigm printed-label convention.\n\n## Witherbloom's OWN affinity for creatures (`cost_reduction`)\nImplemented with the established `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` hook\n(sos_1 / fdn_167 Tolarian Terror shape): it returns the raw count of creatures\nthe controller controls (`CardType.CREATURE` on the controller's battlefield)\nand the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the spell's generic (`{6}`).\nScope is naturally correct: only the controller's battlefield is scanned, only\n`CardType.CREATURE` counts (instants/sorceries in the graveyard never count),\nand an opponent's creatures are not on the controller's battlefield so they do\nnot count. Witherbloom-on-the-stack does not count itself because the stack is\nnot the battlefield.\n\n## The granted-affinity grant surface (queryable)\nThe tolerant probe in `tests.py` recognises a method named\n`has_affinity_for_creatures(game, spell)` on the card (it is first in the\nmethod-name list and is called as `meth(game, spell)`). I implemented exactly\nthat. It returns `True` only when:\n* Witherbloom is on the battlefield (`_is_on_battlefield`),\n* `spell` is an instant or sorcery (`engine.affinity.is_instant_or_sorcery`), and\n* `spell` is the controller's (spell.controller is the controller, or the card\n  is in the controller's hand — the observable proxy; a card found in another\n  player's hand is explicitly *not* granted).\n\nBelt-and-suspenders, the continuous grant also writes the recognised attribute\n`affinity_for_creatures = True` onto every instant/sorcery in the controller's\nhand (via `engine.affinity.grant_affinity_to_hand`), so the second probe\nsurface (an attribute on the affected spell) is also satisfied and the\n`test_card_exposes_an_affinity_grant_surface` anchor passes via both method and\nattribute. This mirrors the Miracle/Casualty grant-surface pattern.\n\n## The granted-reduction registry + how `get_cost_reduction` was extended\nNew additive module `engine/affinity.py` mirrors `engine/casualty.py` and\n`engine/miracle.py`:\n* **Flag registry** — lazy per-game `game._affinity_flags` keyed by `id(source)`\n  tracks which hand cards a source flagged so refreshes can clear stale flags\n  (`grant_affinity_to_hand`, `clear_affinity_flags`).\n* **Granted-reduction registry** — lazy per-game `game._affinity_grants` keyed by\n  `id(source)`. Each record holds `{controller, applies, resolver}`:\n  * `applies(game, spell, controller) -> bool` — gate (source on battlefield,\n    the controller's spell, instant/sorcery, not the source itself).\n  * `resolver(game, spell, controller) -> int` — the {1}-less count (for affinity\n    for creatures: number of creatures the controller controls).\n  * `register_affinity_grant` / `clear_affinity_grant` install/remove a source's\n    record; `get_granted_reduction(game, spell, controller)` sums the\n    contributions of every applicable grant.\n\n`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` was modified **additively in its body only**:\nafter querying the cast card's own `card.cost_reduction(game)`, it adds\n`engine.affinity.get_granted_reduction(game, card, controller)` to `raw`, then\nclamps to the spell's generic exactly as before. The function signature, the\nclamp, and the own-reduction query are all unchanged.\n\n### Why existing reductions are unaffected\n`get_granted_reduction` returns `0` whenever `game._affinity_grants` is absent or\nempty (the common case — no Witherbloom in play), so for sos_1, fdn_167, and\nevery engine cost-reduction test the added term is `0` and the result is\nbyte-for-byte the prior clamped own-reduction. Confirmed: full suite\n1457 passed; `engine_tests/test_cost_reduction.py`, `test_casting.py`,\n`test_types.py` (197) and sos_1 (26) all green.\n\n## Wiring\n`register_triggers` and `register_replacement_effects` both call\n`_apply_affinity_grant` (flag the controller's hand instants/sorceries, or clear\nwhen off-battlefield) and `_register_affinity_reduction` (install/refresh the\ngranted-reduction record, or clear when off-battlefield). Re-registering the same\nsource overwrites its record (idempotent per `id(source)`), so repeated effect\nrecomputation does not stack duplicate reductions. When Witherbloom leaves the\nbattlefield, both the flags and the granted-reduction record are cleared, so the\ngrant stops contributing.\n\n## Reused\n* `engine.casualty` / `engine.miracle` lazy-per-game-registry + grant-surface\n  pattern (new `engine/affinity.py` mirrors them).\n* The sos_1 / fdn_167 `cost_reduction` convention for Witherbloom's own affinity.\n* `get_cost_reduction`'s existing clamp-to-generic logic (only the summed input\n  changed).\n\n## Spec deviations\nNone material. The card-spec model (own affinity via `cost_reduction`; granted\naffinity via a queryable surface plus a pipeline-driven reduction) is implemented\nas specified. The granted reduction now flows through the real\n`cast_spell`/`get_cost_reduction` pipeline, unblocking the deferred item in\n`untestable.json` so the coordinator's follow-up end-to-end tests are real.\n\n## Conventions for future Affinity / granted-cost-reduction cards\n* **A card's OWN affinity** uses the `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` hook\n  returning the raw count of the relevant quality; the engine clamps to generic.\n  \"Affinity\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, never a `Keyword` member.\n* **A permanent that GRANTS a per-spell cost reduction** to the controller's\n  spells should:\n  1. Expose a queryable surface (`has_affinity_for_creatures(game, spell)` /\n     analogous) AND/OR flag affected hand spells via\n     `engine.affinity.grant_affinity_to_hand`.\n  2. Register a granted reduction with\n     `engine.affinity.register_affinity_grant(game, source, controller,\n     resolver, applies)` in `register_triggers` / `register_replacement_effects`,\n     and `clear_affinity_grant(game, source)` when off-battlefield / on leave.\n* `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` already sums all registered granted\n  reductions with the cast card's own hook before clamping — a generic granting\n  cost-reduction permanent only needs to register a `(resolver, applies)` pair;\n  no further engine change is required. `applies` MUST gate on source-on-\n  battlefield, controller-only, and the correct spell types so opponents' and\n  off-battlefield spells contribute nothing.\n* `get_granted_reduction` swallows resolver/predicate exceptions and ignores\n  non-positive contributions, so a buggy grant can never raise during a cast or\n  push generic below 0.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":223,"cache_read_input_tokens":94844,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":223,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011ZQCTY2TPiZpW5s2RVhLVB","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"58052cf3-65b4-4d04-bbad-82d88f8e5f8e","request_id":"req_011CbeE9zJiqrmr4dARP2Syb","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245 + affinity grant hook"}
