{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01NBiLofd78ugQXwon4CgfUQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012PdTiWwLx9D8hXiCZBgRzy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17884,"cache_read_input_tokens":13066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":17884,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GmEQaTZxgS4sSGe8wEJ5BR","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"063bd044-fa80-483b-ae96-82e281fa2678","request_id":"req_011CbeEHAijmRn1kMA59Fttn","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_245 affinity tests"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012PdTiWwLx9D8hXiCZBgRzy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_245 \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\"\n2\t\n3\tCard: `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, colors B+G.\n4\tOracle text:\n5\t\n6\t> Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control.)\n7\t> Flying, deathtouch\n8\t> Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\n9\t\n10\t## Behaviour contract\n11\t\n12\t1. **Static data** — a `Creature` named \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\", cost\n13\t   `{6}{B}{G}` (mana value 8, generic 6), base P/T 5/5, supertype LEGENDARY,\n14\t   subtypes `{Dragon, Elder}`, evergreen keywords `Deathtouch` + `Flying`,\n15\t   colors B+G. \"Affinity\" is **not** an `engine.types.Keyword` enum member —\n16\t   that enum is frozen at 16 members (`engine_tests/test_types.py::\n17\t   test_exactly_sixteen_members`) and contains no AFFINITY — so it must be a\n18\t   printed-keyword label (`printed_keywords`), mirroring the\n19\t   Casualty/Miracle/Paradigm convention in KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n20\t\n21\t2. **Witherbloom's own affinity for creatures** — the `{6}{B}{G}` spell costs\n22\t   `{1}` less to cast for each creature its controller controls. This is the\n23\t   sos_1 / fdn_167 cost-reduction shape: the card's `cost_reduction(game)` hook\n24\t   returns the raw count (number of creatures the controller controls), and the\n25\t   engine's `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` clamps that to the generic\n26\t   portion (`{6}`). Only creatures the controller controls count; other\n27\t   permanents and opponents' creatures do not.\n28\t\n29\t3. **Granted affinity for creatures** — a continuous static ability granting\n30\t   affinity for creatures to the controller's instant and sorcery spells. There\n31\t   is no engine affinity pipeline, so the grant is probed through a TOLERANT\n32\t   surface (a query method on the card and/or an attribute on the affected\n33\t   spell), with one non-skipping anchor (`test_card_exposes_an_affinity_grant_\n34\t   surface`) so the contract fails loudly on the empty stub. Scope is restricted\n35\t   to the CONTROLLER's instants/sorceries (not creature spells, not opponents'\n36\t   spells, and not while Witherbloom is off the battlefield). Driving the\n37\t   granted reduction through the real cast/cost pipeline is deferred — see\n38\t   `untestable.json`.\n39\t\n40\t## Test file\n41\t\n42\t`cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` — 27 test cases (under the 30-per-card cap).\n43\t\n44\t### `TestWitherbloomProperties` (static data — 13 tests)\n45\t\n46\t- `test_is_creature` — instance of `engine.card.Creature`.\n47\t- `test_name` — name is \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\".\n48\t- `test_mana_cost` — cost equals `ManaCost.parse(\"{6}{B}{G}\")`.\n49\t- `test_mana_value_is_eight` — `mana_cost.cmc == 8`.\n50\t- `test_generic_portion_is_six` — `mana_cost.generic == 6` (the part affinity\n51\t  reduces).\n52\t- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T 5/5.\n53\t- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` present.\n54\t- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes contain both \"Dragon\" and \"Elder\".\n55\t- `test_has_flying` — `Keyword.FLYING` in keywords.\n56\t- `test_has_deathtouch` — `Keyword.DEATHTOUCH` in keywords.\n57\t- `test_is_black_green` — pip-based colour check: exactly one B and one G pip,\n58\t  zero W/U/R. Pins colours independent of any `colors` attribute.\n59\t- `test_colors_are_black_and_green` — if a `colors` surface exists it must be\n60\t  exactly `{B, G}`; skips (the pip test already covers colours) if absent.\n61\t- `test_affinity_is_printed_keyword_label_not_enum` — asserts `Keyword` has no\n62\t  AFFINITY member; if `printed_keywords` exists, \"Affinity\" must be among the\n63\t  labels. Skips only the label-presence half if no `printed_keywords` surface\n64\t  exists (the enum-exclusion assertion always runs).\n65\t\n66\t### `TestWitherbloomOwnAffinityCostReduction` (own affinity — 8 tests)\n67\t\n68\t- `test_no_reduction_with_no_creatures` — 0 creatures ⇒ `cost_reduction == 0`.\n69\t- `test_one_creature_reduces_by_one` — 1 creature ⇒ 1.\n70\t- `test_three_creatures_reduce_by_three` — 3 creatures ⇒ 3.\n71\t- `test_non_creature_permanents_do_not_count` — instants/sorceries (here in the\n72\t  graveyard) are not creatures and never count ⇒ 0.\n73\t- `test_only_creatures_you_control_count` — opponent's three creatures do not\n74\t  reduce the controller's cost ⇒ 0.\n75\t- `test_witherbloom_itself_does_not_count_while_on_stack` — with Witherbloom on\n76\t  the stack (not the battlefield) and exactly one other creature out, the\n77\t  reduction is 1, not 2 (the spell does not count itself).\n78\t- `test_effective_reduction_through_engine_partial` — four creatures reduce the\n79\t  `{6}` generic by exactly 4 via `get_cost_reduction`.\n80\t- `test_effective_reduction_clamped_to_generic_six` — nine creatures clamp to 6\n81\t  (generic never goes below 0) via `get_cost_reduction`.\n82\t\n83\t### `TestWitherbloomGrantsAffinityToSpells` (granted affinity scope — 5 tests)\n84\t\n85\tTolerant probes (`_affinity_grant_for` skips when no surface exists;\n86\t`_probe_affinity_silent` returns a sentinel for exclusion checks). Every\n87\texclusion test is anchored on a positive case so it never passes vacuously.\n88\t\n89\t- `test_instant_gets_affinity` — a controller's instant is granted.\n90\t- `test_sorcery_gets_affinity` — a controller's sorcery is granted.\n91\t- `test_creature_spell_does_not_get_affinity` — a creature spell is not granted\n92\t  (anchored on a real instant).\n93\t- `test_opponents_instant_does_not_get_affinity` — an opponent's instant is not\n94\t  granted (anchored on the controller's instant).\n95\t- `test_no_grant_while_off_battlefield` — Witherbloom in hand grants nothing\n96\t  (anchored on a parallel on-battlefield positive case).\n97\t\n98\t### `TestWitherbloomGrantWiring` (grant-surface anchor — 1 test)\n99\t\n100\t- `test_card_exposes_an_affinity_grant_surface` — the **non-skipping anchor**:\n101\t  the implementation must expose at least one recognised affinity-grant surface\n102\t  (a query method on the card or an attribute on the affected spell). An empty\n103\t  stub exposes none, so this fails loudly even though the scope probes above\n104\t  skip — guaranteeing the granted-affinity contract is never silently green.\n105\t\n106\t## Red-phase confirmation (against the empty stub)\n107\t\n108\t`pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`: **17 failed, 3 passed, 7 skipped**.\n109\t\n110\t- The 17 failures are the genuine red-phase contracts (statics + positive\n111\t  cost-reduction counts + the grant-surface anchor).\n112\t- The 3 \"passes\" are the **zero-expecting** cost-reduction tests\n113\t  (`test_no_reduction_with_no_creatures`,\n114\t  `test_non_creature_permanents_do_not_count`,\n115\t  `test_only_creatures_you_control_count`). The base `CardImpl.cost_reduction`\n116\t  returns `0`, so these scope/exclusion assertions are already satisfied by the\n117\t  stub — exactly as sos_1's `test_no_reduction_with_empty_graveyard` behaves.\n118\t  They are not vacuous: each pins a real scoping rule (opponents' creatures and\n119\t  non-creatures must not count) and is anchored by the positive-count tests that\n120\t  DO fail red.\n121\t- The 7 skips are: 2 conditional static probes (the optional `colors` /\n122\t  `printed_keywords` surfaces) and the 5 granted-affinity scope probes (no\n123\t  surface on the stub). All five are covered by the non-skipping\n124\t  `test_card_exposes_an_affinity_grant_surface` anchor, which fails red.\n125\t\n126\t## Deferred (see `untestable.json`)\n127\t\n128\tDriving the granted reduction through the live cast/cost pipeline (casting a\n129\tgranted instant while controlling N creatures actually paying `{N}` less) is\n130\tdeferred: the engine's `get_cost_reduction` only consults the cast card's own\n131\t`cost_reduction` hook, with no mechanism to apply a per-spell reduction granted\n132\tby another permanent. Recorded with the unblock requirement so the Coordinator\n133\tcan decide whether to ask the Implementer to add engine support and re-invoke.\n134\t\n135\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n136\t\n137\t- **Flying/Deathtouch combat behaviour** — engine evergreen keyword mechanics\n138\t  are exercised by `engine_tests/`; testing them here would re-test the engine,\n139\t  not the card.\n140\t- **Legend rule / state-based actions for the legendary supertype** — engine\n141\t  responsibility, out of scope for this card.\n142\t- **Affinity interaction with `{X}` / alternative costs** — Witherbloom has no\n143\t  `{X}` and the affinity only ever reduces the fixed `{6}` generic, so no extra\n144\t  cases are warranted beyond the clamp test.\n145\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GmEQaTZxgS4sSGe8wEJ5BR","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"0bde0641-57a3-4026-ab84-326c6719fd83","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:53:45.358Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_245 affinity tests"}
