{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01W3A269UzV1YPaEtj6iUMpv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KZiAp1eeW4Spx49nz2YczG","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2777,"cache_read_input_tokens":8113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2777,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01STkDpC5UkMTwGuV6iPmCqF","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"5edbb713-c822-4572-936e-e50bd2670914","request_id":"req_011CbeEm9vtkoQE4DKH86mef","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_245 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KZiAp1eeW4Spx49nz2YczG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_245 \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\"\n2\t\n3\t## Static data\n4\t`WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)`: name \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\", cost\n5\t`{6}{B}{G}` (mv 8, generic 6), base P/T 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes\n6\t`{Dragon, Elder}`, keywords `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`, explicit\n7\t`self.colors = [Color.BLACK, Color.GREEN]`. \"Affinity\" is recorded as a printed\n8\tlabel in `self.printed_keywords = [\"Affinity\"]` — it is **not** added to the\n9\t`Keyword` enum, which stays frozen at 16 members (confirmed\n10\t`engine_tests/test_types.py` and `not hasattr(Keyword, \"AFFINITY\")` both pass).\n11\tThis follows the Casualty/Miracle/Paradigm printed-label convention.\n12\t\n13\t## Witherbloom's OWN affinity for creatures (`cost_reduction`)\n14\tImplemented with the established `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` hook\n15\t(sos_1 / fdn_167 Tolarian Terror shape): it returns the raw count of creatures\n16\tthe controller controls (`CardType.CREATURE` on the controller's battlefield)\n17\tand the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the spell's generic (`{6}`).\n18\tScope is naturally correct: only the controller's battlefield is scanned, only\n19\t`CardType.CREATURE` counts (instants/sorceries in the graveyard never count),\n20\tand an opponent's creatures are not on the controller's battlefield so they do\n21\tnot count. Witherbloom-on-the-stack does not count itself because the stack is\n22\tnot the battlefield.\n23\t\n24\t## The granted-affinity grant surface (queryable)\n25\tThe tolerant probe in `tests.py` recognises a method named\n26\t`has_affinity_for_creatures(game, spell)` on the card (it is first in the\n27\tmethod-name list and is called as `meth(game, spell)`). I implemented exactly\n28\tthat. It returns `True` only when:\n29\t* Witherbloom is on the battlefield (`_is_on_battlefield`),\n30\t* `spell` is an instant or sorcery (`engine.affinity.is_instant_or_sorcery`), and\n31\t* `spell` is the controller's (spell.controller is the controller, or the card\n32\t  is in the controller's hand — the observable proxy; a card found in another\n33\t  player's hand is explicitly *not* granted).\n34\t\n35\tBelt-and-suspenders, the continuous grant also writes the recognised attribute\n36\t`affinity_for_creatures = True` onto every instant/sorcery in the controller's\n37\thand (via `engine.affinity.grant_affinity_to_hand`), so the second probe\n38\tsurface (an attribute on the affected spell) is also satisfied and the\n39\t`test_card_exposes_an_affinity_grant_surface` anchor passes via both method and\n40\tattribute. This mirrors the Miracle/Casualty grant-surface pattern.\n41\t\n42\t## The granted-reduction registry + how `get_cost_reduction` was extended\n43\tNew additive module `engine/affinity.py` mirrors `engine/casualty.py` and\n44\t`engine/miracle.py`:\n45\t* **Flag registry** — lazy per-game `game._affinity_flags` keyed by `id(source)`\n46\t  tracks which hand cards a source flagged so refreshes can clear stale flags\n47\t  (`grant_affinity_to_hand`, `clear_affinity_flags`).\n48\t* **Granted-reduction registry** — lazy per-game `game._affinity_grants` keyed by\n49\t  `id(source)`. Each record holds `{controller, applies, resolver}`:\n50\t  * `applies(game, spell, controller) -> bool` — gate (source on battlefield,\n51\t    the controller's spell, instant/sorcery, not the source itself).\n52\t  * `resolver(game, spell, controller) -> int` — the {1}-less count (for affinity\n53\t    for creatures: number of creatures the controller controls).\n54\t  * `register_affinity_grant` / `clear_affinity_grant` install/remove a source's\n55\t    record; `get_granted_reduction(game, spell, controller)` sums the\n56\t    contributions of every applicable grant.\n57\t\n58\t`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` was modified **additively in its body only**:\n59\tafter querying the cast card's own `card.cost_reduction(game)`, it adds\n60\t`engine.affinity.get_granted_reduction(game, card, controller)` to `raw`, then\n61\tclamps to the spell's generic exactly as before. The function signature, the\n62\tclamp, and the own-reduction query are all unchanged.\n63\t\n64\t### Why existing reductions are unaffected\n65\t`get_granted_reduction` returns `0` whenever `game._affinity_grants` is absent or\n66\tempty (the common case — no Witherbloom in play), so for sos_1, fdn_167, and\n67\tevery engine cost-reduction test the added term is `0` and the result is\n68\tbyte-for-byte the prior clamped own-reduction. Confirmed: full suite\n69\t1457 passed; `engine_tests/test_cost_reduction.py`, `test_casting.py`,\n70\t`test_types.py` (197) and sos_1 (26) all green.\n71\t\n72\t## Wiring\n73\t`register_triggers` and `register_replacement_effects` both call\n74\t`_apply_affinity_grant` (flag the controller's hand instants/sorceries, or clear\n75\twhen off-battlefield) and `_register_affinity_reduction` (install/refresh the\n76\tgranted-reduction record, or clear when off-battlefield). Re-registering the same\n77\tsource overwrites its record (idempotent per `id(source)`), so repeated effect\n78\trecomputation does not stack duplicate reductions. When Witherbloom leaves the\n79\tbattlefield, both the flags and the granted-reduction record are cleared, so the\n80\tgrant stops contributing.\n81\t\n82\t## Reused\n83\t* `engine.casualty` / `engine.miracle` lazy-per-game-registry + grant-surface\n84\t  pattern (new `engine/affinity.py` mirrors them).\n85\t* The sos_1 / fdn_167 `cost_reduction` convention for Witherbloom's own affinity.\n86\t* `get_cost_reduction`'s existing clamp-to-generic logic (only the summed input\n87\t  changed).\n88\t\n89\t## Spec deviations\n90\tNone material. The card-spec model (own affinity via `cost_reduction`; granted\n91\taffinity via a queryable surface plus a pipeline-driven reduction) is implemented\n92\tas specified. The granted reduction now flows through the real\n93\t`cast_spell`/`get_cost_reduction` pipeline, unblocking the deferred item in\n94\t`untestable.json` so the coordinator's follow-up end-to-end tests are real.\n95\t\n96\t## Conventions for future Affinity / granted-cost-reduction cards\n97\t* **A card's OWN affinity** uses the `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` hook\n98\t  returning the raw count of the relevant quality; the engine clamps to generic.\n99\t  \"Affinity\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, never a `Keyword` member.\n100\t* **A permanent that GRANTS a per-spell cost reduction** to the controller's\n101\t  spells should:\n102\t  1. Expose a queryable surface (`has_affinity_for_creatures(game, spell)` /\n103\t     analogous) AND/OR flag affected hand spells via\n104\t     `engine.affinity.grant_affinity_to_hand`.\n105\t  2. Register a granted reduction with\n106\t     `engine.affinity.register_affinity_grant(game, source, controller,\n107\t     resolver, applies)` in `register_triggers` / `register_replacement_effects`,\n108\t     and `clear_affinity_grant(game, source)` when off-battlefield / on leave.\n109\t* `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` already sums all registered granted\n110\t  reductions with the cast card's own hook before clamping — a generic granting\n111\t  cost-reduction permanent only needs to register a `(resolver, applies)` pair;\n112\t  no further engine change is required. `applies` MUST gate on source-on-\n113\t  battlefield, controller-only, and the correct spell types so opponents' and\n114\t  off-battlefield spells contribute nothing.\n115\t* `get_granted_reduction` swallows resolver/predicate exceptions and ignores\n116\t  non-positive contributions, so a buggy grant can never raise during a cast or\n117\t  push generic below 0.\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01STkDpC5UkMTwGuV6iPmCqF","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"c8e10b69-bfa2-4ab8-b090-b2c69f24581f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:00:04.635Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_245 implementation"}
