{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01STkDpC5UkMTwGuV6iPmCqF","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 1\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/review.json\n\nSummary of what I verified (no strict issues found):\n\n- Statics correct: `{6}{B}{G}` (mv 8, generic 6), 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{Dragon, Elder}`, `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`, `self.colors = [Color.BLACK, Color.GREEN]`, and \"Affinity\" recorded in `printed_keywords` (not the enum). `engine/types.py` is untouched, so `Keyword` stays at exactly 16 members.\n- Witherbloom's own affinity via `cost_reduction(game)` correctly counts only `CardType.CREATURE` on the controller's battlefield (opponents/non-creatures excluded; Witherbloom-on-stack does not count itself); engine clamp handles the rest.\n- Granted affinity is correctly scoped: controller's instants/sorceries only, source-on-battlefield gated, opponent spells and the source's own creature spell excluded (`_applies`: `spell is source` → False, `ctrl is not grant_controller` → False).\n- The load-bearing change in `engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction` is body-only/additive (signature, own-reduction query, and `max(0, min(raw, generic))` clamp all preserved). `get_granted_reduction` returns 0 when `game._affinity_grants` is absent/empty, so sos_1/fdn_167 and engine cost-reduction tests are unchanged. No double-counting (registry keyed by `id(source)`, idempotent re-register), and contributions are filtered to `> 0`.\n- Additive-only discipline holds: new `engine/affinity.py` mirrors the established `engine/casualty.py` pattern (lazy per-game registries `game._affinity_flags` / `game._affinity_grants`, no `GameState.__init__` change); no engine symbol renamed/moved/deleted; no edits to `engine_tests/` or `cards/fdn/*/tests.py`. Card class lives at `cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`.\n\nRelevant file paths:\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_