{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01VFUq1DapXx2sS91RUdVLqY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fp3AzjiYzgUfH32KvB29eL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_257 \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"\n\n## Behaviour contract\n\nGreat Hall of the Biblioplex is a colorless, nonbasic **Land** with three abilities:\n\n1. `{T}: Add {C}.`\n2. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.`\n3. `{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.`\n\nTests follow the established per-card convention (fdn_272 Plains, fdn_267 Secluded Courtyard, sos_57): read the public ability surface (`get_mana_abilities` / `get_activated_abilities`) and invoke the cost/effect callables directly, asserting observable state (mana pool, life, card types/subtypes, P/T, registered triggers).\n\nEngine reference points confirmed by reading source:\n- `engine/card.py` — `Land`, `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)`, `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)`, `get_mana_abilities()`, `get_activated_abilities()`; `can_cast()` returns `False` for lands.\n- `engine/mana.py` — `ManaPool` is a flat `dict[ManaType,int]`; **no restricted-mana tagging**.\n- `engine/continuous_effects.py` — a layer system exists (`Layer.TYPE`, `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`) but **no becomes-a-creature animation helper**.\n- `cards/fdn/fdn_267/card_impl.py` — same `{T}: Add {C}` + restricted any-color shape, with an in-code \"ENGINE LIMITATION\" note that restrictions are unenforced.\n\n## File: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`\n\n26 test cases across 6 classes. Helper functions tolerate the two legal ability-closure shapes (1-arg `cost(game)` per fdn_272 vs 2-arg `cost(game, source)` per fdn_267, and `mana_produced` either returning a `{ManaType:int}` dict or mutating the pool).\n\n### TestGreatHallProperties (static data) — 9 cases\n- `test_name` — name is \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\". (Concrete; fails on stub.)\n- `test_is_a_land` — instance of `Land`, `CardType.LAND` present. The strongest positive identity anchor. (Fails on stub.)\n- `test_not_a_creature_while_unanimated` — `CardType.CREATURE` absent before {5}. Genuine property an implementation must preserve. (Passes on stub — a valid negative property, not misleading.)\n- `test_has_no_mana_cost` — `mana_cost == ManaCost()` (lands are played, not cast). Valid negative property.\n- `test_cannot_be_cast` — `can_cast()` is `False`. (Fails on stub — base `CardImpl.can_cast` returns True; only `Land` returns False.)\n- `test_has_no_colors` — `protection.get_colors` returns empty set. Valid negative property.\n- `test_is_not_a_basic_land` — no `Supertype.BASIC`. Valid negative property.\n- `test_has_no_basic_land_subtype` — subtypes disjoint from the five basics. Valid negative property.\n- `test_power_toughness_unset_while_not_a_creature` — `power`/`toughness` absent or `None` while a plain land. Valid negative property.\n\nThe six negative-property tests pass against the empty stub because the stub is a bare `CardImpl` — but every one asserts a property the finished card MUST keep true (colorless, nonbasic, no mana cost, no P/T before animation). They are not vacuous self-equalities; they are real regression guards. The positive identity contract (`name`, `is_a_land`, `cannot_be_cast`) all fail in red, so the static surface is genuinely exercised.\n\n### TestGreatHallColorlessManaAbility — Ability 1 `{T}: Add {C}` — 4 cases (all concrete, all red)\n- `test_exposes_at_least_two_mana_abilities` — the card prints ≥2 `ManaAbility`s.\n- `test_colorless_ability_taps_the_land` — running the {C} ability's cost sets `is_tapped`.\n- `test_colorless_ability_adds_one_colorless_mana` — exactly one `COLORLESS` mana lands in the controller's pool (`total() == 1`).\n- `test_colorless_ability_cost_fails_when_already_tapped` — a tapped land cannot re-pay `{T}`.\n\nThese are the concrete core required by the spec; they fail loudly against the stub (no mana abilities yet).\n\n### TestGreatHallAnyColorManaAbility — Ability 2 — 6 cases\n- `test_any_color_ability_taps_the_land` — second ability taps the land. (Concrete.)\n- `test_any_color_ability_pays_one_life` — controller's life drops by exactly 1. (Concrete.)\n- `test_any_color_ability_adds_one_mana_of_chosen_color` — scripted blue → 1 blue mana, `total()==1`. (Concrete.)\n- `test_any_color_ability_can_produce_a_different_color` — scripted green → 1 green mana (\"any color\"). (Concrete.)\n- `test_any_color_mana_is_marked_restricted_to_instants_sorceries` — **tolerant probe** for the spend restriction. Asserts that *some* restriction surface exists (card-level `mana_spend_restriction`/`produces_restricted_mana`, ability-level `restriction`/`spend_restriction`, or a pool-level `restrictions`). Fails loudly today; the restriction clause is recorded in `untestable.json`.\n\nColor choices are driven deterministically via `create_game(scripts=([Color.X], []))` so the any-color picker is reproducible regardless of how the implementer wires `controller.choose`.\n\n### TestGreatHallAnimationAbilitySurface — Ability 3 surface — 1 case\n- `test_exposes_an_activated_ability` — `{5}` is a non-mana `ActivatedAbility`. (Fails on stub.)\n\n### TestGreatHallAnimationEffect — Ability 3 animation — 5 cases (tolerant probes)\n- `test_becomes_a_creature` — after activating {5}, `CardType.CREATURE` is added.\n- `test_is_still_a_land_after_animation` — `CardType.LAND` retained (\"It's still a land\").\n- `test_becomes_a_wizard` — `\"Wizard\"` subtype added.\n- `test_becomes_two_four` — `power==2`, `toughness==4` after `effect_manager.apply_all`.\n- `test_animation_no_op_when_already_a_creature` — re-activating while already a creature changes neither the 2/4 body nor the trigger count (\"If this land isn't a creature\").\n\nThese assert the observable end state the spec demands. The engine has no animation pipeline, so they fail loudly now; the deep surface is recorded in `untestable.json`.\n\n### TestGreatHallGrantedPumpTrigger — Ability 3 granted trigger — 2 cases (tolerant probes)\n- `test_animation_registers_a_pump_trigger` — animating registers a new trigger (the granted \"whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell\" ability).\n- `test_pump_trigger_adds_plus_one_zero_until_end_of_turn` — firing the granted trigger's effect once yields a 3/4 body (2/4 + 1/0) after recomputing the layer system.\n\nBoth fail loudly absent a grant-on-animation pipeline; the until-end-of-turn duration and per-cast scaling are recorded in `untestable.json`.\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- Already-tapped land cannot re-pay `{T}` (ability 1).\n- Two distinct colors honoured by the any-color ability (\"any color\", not a fixed color).\n- Exact life delta (`-1`, not 0 or 2) for the pay-1-life cost.\n- \"If this land isn't a creature\" — second animation is a no-op (no double-grant, body unchanged).\n- \"It's still a land\" — LAND type explicitly asserted to survive animation.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (out of scope / no engine surface)\n- Enforcing that the restricted any-color mana *cannot* pay for a creature spell but *can* pay for an instant/sorcery — no restricted-mana mechanism (see `untestable.json` #1).\n- Full layered animation P/T under the real layer pipeline, granted-ability registration on resolution, and the EOT pump expiry at cleanup — no becomes-a-creature / grant-on-animation surface (see `untestable.json` #2, #3). Probes fail loudly instead.\n- Summoning sickness / haste interactions of the animated land's attack — out of scope for this card's printed text and dependent on the missing animation pipeline.\n\n## Red-phase confirmation\n`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → **20 failed, 6 passed** against the empty stub. No import/collection errors (26 collected). The 6 passers are valid negative-property regression guards (colorless, nonbasic, no mana cost, no P/T pre-animation, no creature type) that the finished card must keep true; every positive behavioral assertion (identity, both mana abilities, life payment, animation, granted pump) fails in red.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2009,"cache_read_input_tokens":91991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2009,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":52,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QNA4ces9AkbzirNP9xC9rV","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"24293ad7-4f80-4f9d-88d3-63c57dd74ef6","request_id":"req_011CbeFCWmUHwovQeKaiMyH7","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_257"}
