a Land (no mana cost, no colors, no keywords). Oracle:\n\"{T}: Add {C}.\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\n{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\\" It's still a land.\"\n\nWhere to learn conventions (read these):\n- Test conventions + fixtures: `engine_tests/` and examples. Tests run from `/workspace`; workspace root on sys.path → bare imports (e.g. `from cards.sos.sos_257.card_impl import ...`, `from engine.card import Land`, `from engine.types import Color, CardType, Subtype`).\n- **IMPORTANT — find an existing LAND / mana-ability / activated-ability reference**: look in `cards/fdn/` for a Land card and for cards with activated mana abilities, and read `engine/card.py` (Land class, activated/mana abilities), `engine/abilities.py`, `engine/mana.py` (mana pool, restricted mana / \"spend only to cast\" tags), and `engine/continuous_effects.py` (becomes-creature / animation). Discover how the engine models: (a) a basic `{T}: Add {C}` mana ability, (b) restricted mana that can only pay for instants/sorceries, and (c) a land \"becomes a 2/4 creature but is still a land\" animation with a granted triggered ability.\n- Read `KEY_DECISIONS.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT_MAP.md`, `FILES_MODIFIED.json`. The `Keyword` enum is frozen at 16.\n\nWhat the tests must cover (derive concrete assertions from the spec):\n1. Static data: is a `Land` named \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\", type line \"Land\", no colors, no mana cost (it's a land, cast for free / put into play), and it is NOT a basic land (no basic land subtype). Power/toughness are null while it's not animated.\n2. **Ability 1 — `{T}: Add {C}`**: activating taps the land and adds one colorless mana to the controller's mana pool. Use whatever the engine's mana-ability API is (mirror an existing FDN land).\n3. **Ability 2 — `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color, spendable only on instants/sorceries`**: activating taps the land, pays 1 life (controller's life drops by 1), and adds one mana of a chosen color that is RESTRICTED to casting instant/sorcery spells. If the engine has a restricted-mana mechanism, assert the restriction (the mana can pay for an instant/sorcery but not, e.g., a creature). If the engine lacks restricted-mana tagging, record that piece in `untestable.json` with what would unblock it.\n4. **Ability 3 — `{5}`: animate into a 2/4 Wizard creature that is still a Land**, with the granted triggered ability \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" Test: paying {5} (only if it isn't already a creature) makes it a 2/4 with CardType.CREATURE added, Subtype WIZARD, while RETAINING CardType.LAND; and the granted pump trigger gives +1/+0 (until end of turn) per instant/sorcery cast. If the engine lacks a becomes-creature/animation pipeline or the \"until end of turn\" pump, record those pieces in `untestable.json` with concrete unblock notes (the coordinator will arbitrate building engine support, then re-invoke you once).\n\nMake tests FAIL against the current empty stub (genuine behavioral assertions, not import errors) — TDD red. Statics + the basic `{T}: Add {C}` should be concrete; the restricted mana and the animation are the hard parts — anchor any tolerant probe so it fails loudly rather than passing vacuously, and defer to `untestable.json` what truly has no engine surface yet.\n\nOutputs:\n- Test file at `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md` — behaviour contract + per-test rationale + what you deferred and why.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-files.txt` — list of test file paths.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json` — JSON array of requirements you could NOT test yet + what would unblock each (empty `[]` if none).\n\nReturn a short status summary:\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_count: <N>\nred_confirmed: <yes/no — how many fail vs skip against the stub>\nuntestable_count: <N>\ntest_files_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-files.txt","agentId":"ac31354ec6a7cad1c","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All outputs are in place and the red phase is confirmed.\n\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_count: 26\nred_confirmed: yes — 20 fail, 6 pass against the empty stub (no import/collection errors; the 6 passers are valid negative-property regression guards — colorless, nonbasic, no mana cost, no P/T pre-animation, no creature type — that the finished card must keep true; every positive behavioral assertion fails red)\nuntestable_count: 3\ntest_files_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-files.txt\n\nnotes: Concrete coverage of statics, `{T}: Add {C}`, and the `{T}, Pay 1 life: any color` ability (tap + 1-life payment + chosen-color production). Deferred to untestable.json: (1) the instant/sorcery-only mana spend restriction (no restricted-mana surface in ManaPool — same gap fdn_267 documents), (2) the {5} becomes-a-2/4-Wizard-still-a-land animation, and (3) the granted \"+1/+0 until end of turn per I/S cast\" trigger (no animation/grant pipeline). The animation and restriction assertions are tolerant probes anchored to fail loudly rather than pass vacuously.\n\nOutput files (all absolute):\n- /workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-files.txt\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json"}],"totalDurationMs":259957,"totalTokens":98460,"totalToolUseCount":43,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":514,"cache_read_input_tokens":97417,"output_tokens":527,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":514},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":527,"cache_read_i