{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011XGsi6UnSk55AmFYJLryBP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n4\t    \"requirement\": \"{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\",\n5\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The 'spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell' restriction has no engine surface. engine/mana.py ManaPool stores only a flat dict[ManaType, int] with no per-mana spend-restriction tagging, and engine.casting/engine.mana provide no way to mark mana as restricted or to enforce/query that a payment honoured such a restriction. The FDN analog fdn_267 (Secluded Courtyard) documents the identical gap in-code ('ENGINE LIMITATION: The engine does not support conditional mana spending restrictions'). The tap, the 1-life payment, and the any-color production ARE fully tested; only the restriction clause is deferred. A tolerant probe (test_any_color_mana_is_marked_restricted_to_instants_sorceries) fails loudly so this is not silently green.\",\n6\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Add a restricted-mana mechanism: e.g. a restriction tag carried alongside mana in ManaPool (a parallel list/record keyed by ManaType) plus a card-/ability-level query such as `produces_restricted_mana`/`mana_spend_restriction`, and have engine.casting.cast_spell consult it so the restricted mana can pay for an instant/sorcery but is rejected when paying for a creature/other spell. Once a public surface exists to (a) tag the produced mana and (b) observe that an instant/sorcery payment consumed it while a creature payment could not, the probe and a positive/negative spend test can be made concrete.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n10\t    \"requirement\": \"{5}: ... it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature ... It's still a land. (the becomes-a-creature animation)\",\n11\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The engine has no land-animation / becomes-a-creature pipeline. engine/continuous_effects.py exposes a layer system (Layer.TYPE for type changes, Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, DURATION_PERMANENT) and CardImpl._reset_characteristics, but there is no helper to animate a Land into a 2/4 creature that retains CardType.LAND, no helper to add a Creature subtype/base P/T to a non-Creature CardImpl, and a plain Land has no power/toughness properties (only engine.card.Creature does). The activated-ability surface ({5} via get_activated_abilities) and the observable end state (CREATURE added, LAND retained, Wizard subtype, 2/4) are written as tolerant probes that fail loudly; they will go green once the Implementer/Coordinator adds an animation surface, but cannot be asserted against the current engine without inventing the mechanism inside the card.\",\n12\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Add an additive becomes-a-creature animation helper in engine/continuous_effects.py (or a new engine module) that, when {5} resolves, layers CardType.CREATURE onto the land (keeping LAND), grants the Wizard subtype, and sets a 2/4 body discoverable via card.power/card.toughness after effect_manager.apply_all — modelled on the existing Layer.TYPE / Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS sublayers. The 'if this land isn't a creature' guard and the durable (until the source leaves) duration also need a home. Once a non-creature CardImpl can report power/toughness under an active animation effect, the test_becomes_* probes become concrete assertions.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n16\t    \"requirement\": \"the animated creature has \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn\\\" (granted trigger + until-end-of-turn pump)\",\n17\t    \"why_untestable\": \"Two gaps: (1) there is no pipeline to GRANT a triggered ability to a permanent when it is animated (the only trigger path is a card's own register_triggers, called at a fixed time, not a grant attached by a resolving activated ability); and (2) the '+1/+0 until end of turn' pump needs a DURATION_END_OF_TURN continuous P/T effect (Layer 7c) targeting an animated land that has no Creature P/T base today (see the animation entry above). The per-cast scaling ('Whenever you cast' — once per instant/sorcery) and the cleanup-time expiry of the pump cannot be asserted until the animated land has an observable, modifiable power/toughness and a registered cast trigger. Tolerant probes (test_animation_registers_a_pump_trigger, test_pump_trigger_adds_plus_one_zero_until_end_of_turn) fail loudly so the gap is explicit.\",\n18\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Provide (a) a way for the {5} resolution to register a SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger controlled by the land's controller, gated to the controller's own instant/sorcery casts, that (b) adds a Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS (sublayer 7c) +1/+0 ContinuousEffect with duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN to the now-animated land, observable via card.power after effect_manager.apply_all and swept by remove_expired at cleanup. This depends on the becomes-a-creature animation surface above; once both exist, firing the trigger N times and asserting +N/+0 (then EOT reset) becomes concrete.\"\n19\t  }\n20\t]\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b37a361f-ec69-44ec-8f43-1c8509e702ce","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:06:35.406Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n    \"requirement\": \"{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"The 'spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell' restriction has no engine surface. engine/mana.py ManaPool stores only a flat dict[ManaType, int] with no per-mana spend-restriction tagging, and engine.casting/engine.mana provide no way to mark mana as restricted or to enforce/query that a payment honoured such a restriction. The FDN analog fdn_267 (Secluded Courtyard) documents the identical gap in-code ('ENGINE LIMITATION: The engine does not support conditional mana spending restrictions'). The tap, the 1-life payment, and the any-color production ARE fully tested; only the restriction clause is deferred. A tolerant probe (test_any_color_mana_is_marked_restricted_to_instants_sorceries) fails loudly so this is not silently green.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Add a restricted-mana mechanism: e.g. a restriction tag carried alongside mana in ManaPool (a parallel list/record keyed by ManaType) plus a card-/ability-level query such as `produces_restricted_mana`/`mana_spend_restriction`, and have engine.casting.cast_spell consult it so the restricted mana can pay for an instant/sorcery but is rejected when paying for a creature/other spell. Once a public surface exists to (a) tag the produced mana and (b) observe that an instant/sorcery payment consumed it while a creature payment could not, the probe and a positive/negative spend test can be made concrete.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n    \"requirement\": \"{5}: ... it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature ... It's still a land. (the becomes-a-creature animation)\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"The engine has no land-animation / becomes-a-creature pipeline. engine/continuous_effects.py exposes a layer system (Layer.TYPE for type changes, Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, DURATION_PERMANENT) and CardImpl._reset_characteristics, but there is no helper to animate a Land into a 2/4 creature that retains CardType.LAND, no helper to add a Creature subtype/base P/T to a non-Creature CardImpl, and a plain Land has no power/toughness properties (only engine.card.Creature does). The activated-ability surface ({5} via get_activated_abilities) and the observable end state (CREATURE added, LAND retained, Wizard subtype, 2/4) are written as tolerant probes that fail loudly; they will go green once the Implementer/Coordinator adds an animation surface, but cannot be asserted against the current engine without inventing the mechanism inside the card.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Add an additive becomes-a-creature animation helper in engine/continuous_effects.py (or a new engine module) that, when {5} resolves, layers CardType.CREATURE onto the land (keeping LAND), grants the Wizard subtype, and sets a 2/4 body discoverable via card.power/card.toughness after effect_manager.apply_all — modelled on the existing Layer.TYPE / Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS sublayers. The 'if this land isn't a creature' guard and the durable (until the source leaves) duration also need a home. Once a non-creature CardImpl can report power/toughness under an active animation effect, the test_becomes_* probes become concrete assertions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_257\",\n    \"requirement\": \"the animated creature has \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn\\\" (granted trigger + until-end-of-turn pump)\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"Two gaps: (1) there is no pipeline to GRANT a triggered ability to a permanent when it is animated (the only trigger path is a card's own register_triggers, called at a fixed time, not a grant attached by a resolving activated ability); and (2) the '+1/+0 until end of turn' pump needs a DURATION_END_OF_TURN continuous P/T effect (Layer 7c) targeting an animated land that has no Creature P/T base today (see the animation entry above). The per-cast scaling ('Whenever you cast' — once per instant/sorcery) and the cleanup-time expiry of the pump cannot be asserted until the animated land has an observable, modifiable power/toughness and a registered cast trigger. Tolerant probes (test_animation_registers_a_pump_trigger, test_pump_trigger_adds_plus_one_zero_until_end_of_turn) fail loudly so the gap is explicit.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Provide (a) a way for the {5} resolution to register a SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger controlled by the land's controller, gated to the controller's own instant/sorcery casts, that (b) adds a Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS (sublayer 7c) +1/+0 ContinuousEffect with duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN to the now-animated land, observable via card.power after effect_manager.apply_all and swept by remove_expired at cleanup. This depends on the becomes-a-creature animation surface above; once both exist, firing the trigger N times and asserting +N/+0 (then EOT reset) becomes concrete.\"\n  }\n]\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
