trigger + lazy-per-game-registry conventions from KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n\n## Statics + the two mana abilities (make these pass first)\n- A `Land` named \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\", type line \"Land\", colorless, no mana cost, NOT a\n  basic land, null power/toughness while not animated.\n- **`{T}: Add {C}`** — standard tap-for-colorless mana ability. Mirror an existing FDN land's\n  mana-ability API (read `engine/card.py` Land + an FDN land for the exact shape).\n- **`{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color (instant/sorcery-restricted)`** — activating taps the\n  land, reduces the controller's life by 1, and adds one mana of a chosen color.\n\n## Build the three deferred mechanisms (ADDITIVE)\n\n### 1. Restricted mana (\"spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\")\nThe engine's `ManaPool` (engine/mana.py) is a flat `dict[ManaType,int]` with no per-mana restriction\ntag; fdn_267 documents this exact gap as a known limitation. Add an additive restricted-mana\nmechanism:\n- Tag produced mana with a spend restriction (e.g. a parallel record in `ManaPool` keyed by\n  `ManaType`, or a small restriction list) plus a query/producer surface so a test can observe that\n  the any-color mana is restricted to instants/sorceries.\n- Have `engine.casting.cast_spell`'s payment path CONSULT the restriction: restricted mana MAY pay\n  for an instant/sorcery, but MUST be rejected (or simply not usable) when paying for a creature/\n  other spell. Provide an observable outcome (an instant/sorcery cast can consume it; a creature\n  cast cannot).\n- **SAFETY (critical)**: when no restricted mana is present, the mana pool and `cast_spell` payment\n  MUST behave byte-for-byte as before — all existing engine mana/casting tests and every prior card\n  must still pass. Default the restriction to empty/None so ordinary mana is unrestricted.\n- If full payment-path enforcement proves genuinely infeasible without regressions, fall back to: a\n  queryable restriction tag on the produced mana + best-effort enforcement, and DOCUMENT the\n  limitation in your rationale (the coordinator will arbitrate). But prefer real enforcement.\n\n### 2. Land-animation: `{5}` → becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature, still a Land\n- A `{5}` activated ability, usable only \"if this land isn't a creature\" (guard against re-animating\n  an already-animated land). On resolution, layer `CardType.CREATURE` onto the land while RETAINING\n  `CardType.LAND`, grant the `Wizard` subtype, and set a 2/4 base body discoverable via\n  `card.power`/`card.toughness` after `effect_manager.apply_all`.\n- Add an additive becomes-a-creature animation helper (in `engine/continuous_effects.py` or a new\n  engine module) modelled on the existing `Layer.TYPE` / `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` sublayers, so a\n  non-Creature `CardImpl` can report power/toughness under an active animation effect. Duration:\n  durable (lasts until the land leaves the battlefield) — `DURATION_PERMANENT` is fine.\n\n### 3. Granted pump trigger on the animated land\n- When the {5} animation resolves, register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger controlled by the\n  land's controller, gated to the controller's OWN instant/sorcery casts, that adds a\n  `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` (sublayer 7c) **+1/+0** `ContinuousEffect` with\n  `duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN` to the animated land — observable via `card.power` after\n  `apply_all`, and swept by `remove_expired` at cleanup. Firing it N times in a turn yields +N/+0,\n  then resets at end of turn.\n- This trigger is GRANTED by the animation (not the card's static `register_triggers`), so register\n  it at {5}-resolution time (deduped per source via a lazy per-game registry). It should only be\n  active while the land is animated.\n\n## Make ALL tests pass (no avoidable skips)\nRead `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` and satisfy every assertion + tolerant probe. Do NOT modify any\ntest file. If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible, return DISPUTE.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → all pass.\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (report totals). PAY SPECIAL ATTENTION to\n  `engine_tests` mana/casting/continuous-effect tests and fdn_267 after you touch ManaPool /\n  cast_spell / continuous_effects.\n\nAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to add concrete tests for: the\nrestricted-mana spend (instant/sorcery OK, creature rejected), the {5} animation end state, and the\nper-cast +1/+0-until-EOT pump (N casts → +N/+0, reset at cleanup). Build these so they are real and\nobservable.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
