{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WmVF1bj1RqZGfzQx4q2AfL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives — sos_257 (Great Hall of the Biblioplex)\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Great Hall of the Biblioplex** — a Land (complex tier).\n4\tOracle:\n5\t> {T}: Add {C}.\n6\t> {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\n7\t> {5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an\n8\t> instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.\n9\t\n10\tThe Tester wrote 26 tests: statics, `{T}: Add {C}`, and the `{T}, Pay 1 life: any color` tap+life+\n11\tcolor production are concrete and FAIL on the empty stub; 6 negative-property guards pass. THREE\n12\titems are deferred in `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json` for lack of engine surface:\n13\t(1) the \"spend only on instant/sorcery\" mana restriction, (2) the {5} becomes-a-2/4-Wizard-still-a-\n14\tland animation, (3) the granted \"Whenever you cast an instant/sorcery, +1/+0 until end of turn\"\n15\ttrigger on the animated land. Build all three ADDITIVELY.\n16\t\n17\tADDITIVE per AGENTS.md: add new methods/classes/helpers/fields/modules; modify existing function\n18\tBODIES; NEVER rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. The `Keyword` enum stays at 16. Reuse the\n19\tlayer system in `engine/continuous_effects.py` (`Layer.TYPE`, `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`/7c,\n20\t`DURATION_PERMANENT`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`, `effect_manager.apply_all`, `remove_expired`) and the\n21\t`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger + lazy-per-game-registry conventions from KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n22\t\n23\t## Statics + the two mana abilities (make these pass first)\n24\t- A `Land` named \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\", type line \"Land\", colorless, no mana cost, NOT a\n25\t  basic land, null power/toughness while not animated.\n26\t- **`{T}: Add {C}`** — standard tap-for-colorless mana ability. Mirror an existing FDN land's\n27\t  mana-ability API (read `engine/card.py` Land + an FDN land for the exact shape).\n28\t- **`{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color (instant/sorcery-restricted)`** — activating taps the\n29\t  land, reduces the controller's life by 1, and adds one mana of a chosen color.\n30\t\n31\t## Build the three deferred mechanisms (ADDITIVE)\n32\t\n33\t### 1. Restricted mana (\"spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\")\n34\tThe engine's `ManaPool` (engine/mana.py) is a flat `dict[ManaType,int]` with no per-mana restriction\n35\ttag; fdn_267 documents this exact gap as a known limitation. Add an additive restricted-mana\n36\tmechanism:\n37\t- Tag produced mana with a spend restriction (e.g. a parallel record in `ManaPool` keyed by\n38\t  `ManaType`, or a small restriction list) plus a query/producer surface so a test can observe that\n39\t  the any-color mana is restricted to instants/sorceries.\n40\t- Have `engine.casting.cast_spell`'s payment path CONSULT the restriction: restricted mana MAY pay\n41\t  for an instant/sorcery, but MUST be rejected (or simply not usable) when paying for a creature/\n42\t  other spell. Provide an observable outcome (an instant/sorcery cast can consume it; a creature\n43\t  cast cannot).\n44\t- **SAFETY (critical)**: when no restricted mana is present, the mana pool and `cast_spell` payment\n45\t  MUST behave byte-for-byte as before — all existing engine mana/casting tests and every prior card\n46\t  must still pass. Default the restriction to empty/None so ordinary mana is unrestricted.\n47\t- If full payment-path enforcement proves genuinely infeasible without regressions, fall back to: a\n48\t  queryable restriction tag on the produced mana + best-effort enforcement, and DOCUMENT the\n49\t  limitation in your rationale (the coordinator will arbitrate). But prefer real enforcement.\n50\t\n51\t### 2. Land-animation: `{5}` → becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature, still a Land\n52\t- A `{5}` activated ability, usable only \"if this land isn't a creature\" (guard against re-animating\n53\t  an already-animated land). On resolution, layer `CardType.CREATURE` onto the land while RETAINING\n54\t  `CardType.LAND`, grant the `Wizard` subtype, and set a 2/4 base body discoverable via\n55\t  `card.power`/`card.toughness` after `effect_manager.apply_all`.\n56\t- Add an additive becomes-a-creature animation helper (in `engine/continuous_effects.py` or a new\n57\t  engine module) modelled on the existing `Layer.TYPE` / `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` sublayers, so a\n58\t  non-Creature `CardImpl` can report power/toughness under an active animation effect. Duration:\n59\t  durable (lasts until the land leaves the battlefield) — `DURATION_PERMANENT` is fine.\n60\t\n61\t### 3. Granted pump trigger on the animated land\n62\t- When the {5} animation resolves, register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger controlled by the\n63\t  land's controller, gated to the controller's OWN instant/sorcery casts, that adds a\n64\t  `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` (sublayer 7c) **+1/+0** `ContinuousEffect` with\n65\t  `duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN` to the animated land — observable via `card.power` after\n66\t  `apply_all`, and swept by `remove_expired` at cleanup. Firing it N times in a turn yields +N/+0,\n67\t  then resets at end of turn.\n68\t- This trigger is GRANTED by the animation (not the card's static `register_triggers`), so register\n69\t  it at {5}-resolution time (deduped per source via a lazy per-game registry). It should only be\n70\t  active while the land is animated.\n71\t\n72\t## Make ALL tests pass (no avoidable skips)\n73\tRead `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` and satisfy every assertion + tolerant probe. Do NOT modify any\n74\ttest file. If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible, return DISPUTE.\n75\t\n76\t## Verification\n77\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → all pass.\n78\t- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (report totals). PAY SPECIAL ATTENTION to\n79\t  `engine_tests` mana/casting/continuous-effect tests and fdn_267 after you touch ManaPool /\n80\t  cast_spell / continuous_effects.\n81\t\n82\tAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to add concrete tests for: the\n83\trestricted-mana spend (instant/sorcery OK, creature rejected), the {5} animation end state, and the\n84\tper-cast +1/+0-until-EOT pump (N casts → +N/+0, reset at cleanup). Build these so they are real and\n85\tobservable.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013DvBFWmxzpqf1jHj4XNC9b","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"c7bec9bc-a61d-4072-ad57-b1bd3a2075c9","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:07:48.130Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_257 + 3 engine mechanisms"}
