{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ohp2gT5kDryEwHTw7jSra","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_257 \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"\n2\t\n3\t## Behaviour contract\n4\t\n5\tGreat Hall of the Biblioplex is a colorless, nonbasic **Land** with three abilities:\n6\t\n7\t1. `{T}: Add {C}.`\n8\t2. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.`\n9\t3. `{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.`\n10\t\n11\tTests follow the established per-card convention (fdn_272 Plains, fdn_267 Secluded Courtyard, sos_57): read the public ability surface (`get_mana_abilities` / `get_activated_abilities`) and invoke the cost/effect callables directly, asserting observable state (mana pool, life, card types/subtypes, P/T, registered triggers).\n12\t\n13\tEngine reference points confirmed by reading source:\n14\t- `engine/card.py` — `Land`, `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)`, `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)`, `get_mana_abilities()`, `get_activated_abilities()`; `can_cast()` returns `False` for lands.\n15\t- `engine/mana.py` — `ManaPool` is a flat `dict[ManaType,int]`; **no restricted-mana tagging**.\n16\t- `engine/continuous_effects.py` — a layer system exists (`Layer.TYPE`, `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`) but **no becomes-a-creature animation helper**.\n17\t- `cards/fdn/fdn_267/card_impl.py` — same `{T}: Add {C}` + restricted any-color shape, with an in-code \"ENGINE LIMITATION\" note that restrictions are unenforced.\n18\t\n19\t## File: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`\n20\t\n21\t26 test cases across 6 classes. Helper functions tolerate the two legal ability-closure shapes (1-arg `cost(game)` per fdn_272 vs 2-arg `cost(game, source)` per fdn_267, and `mana_produced` either returning a `{ManaType:int}` dict or mutating the pool).\n22\t\n23\t### TestGreatHallProperties (static data) — 9 cases\n24\t- `test_name` — name is \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\". (Concrete; fails on stub.)\n25\t- `test_is_a_land` — instance of `Land`, `CardType.LAND` present. The strongest positive identity anchor. (Fails on stub.)\n26\t- `test_not_a_creature_while_unanimated` — `CardType.CREATURE` absent before {5}. Genuine property an implementation must preserve. (Passes on stub — a valid negative property, not misleading.)\n27\t- `test_has_no_mana_cost` — `mana_cost == ManaCost()` (lands are played, not cast). Valid negative property.\n28\t- `test_cannot_be_cast` — `can_cast()` is `False`. (Fails on stub — base `CardImpl.can_cast` returns True; only `Land` returns False.)\n29\t- `test_has_no_colors` — `protection.get_colors` returns empty set. Valid negative property.\n30\t- `test_is_not_a_basic_land` — no `Supertype.BASIC`. Valid negative property.\n31\t- `test_has_no_basic_land_subtype` — subtypes disjoint from the five basics. Valid negative property.\n32\t- `test_power_toughness_unset_while_not_a_creature` — `power`/`toughness` absent or `None` while a plain land. Valid negative property.\n33\t\n34\tThe six negative-property tests pass against the empty stub because the stub is a bare `CardImpl` — but every one asserts a property the finished card MUST keep true (colorless, nonbasic, no mana cost, no P/T before animation). They are not vacuous self-equalities; they are real regression guards. The positive identity contract (`name`, `is_a_land`, `cannot_be_cast`) all fail in red, so the static surface is genuinely exercised.\n35\t\n36\t### TestGreatHallColorlessManaAbility — Ability 1 `{T}: Add {C}` — 4 cases (all concrete, all red)\n37\t- `test_exposes_at_least_two_mana_abilities` — the card prints ≥2 `ManaAbility`s.\n38\t- `test_colorless_ability_taps_the_land` — running the {C} ability's cost sets `is_tapped`.\n39\t- `test_colorless_ability_adds_one_colorless_mana` — exactly one `COLORLESS` mana lands in the controller's pool (`total() == 1`).\n40\t- `test_colorless_ability_cost_fails_when_already_tapped` — a tapped land cannot re-pay `{T}`.\n41\t\n42\tThese are the concrete core required by the spec; they fail loudly against the stub (no mana abilities yet).\n43\t\n44\t### TestGreatHallAnyColorManaAbility — Ability 2 — 6 cases\n45\t- `test_any_color_ability_taps_the_land` — second ability taps the land. (Concrete.)\n46\t- `test_any_color_ability_pays_one_life` — controller's life drops by exactly 1. (Concrete.)\n47\t- `test_any_color_ability_adds_one_mana_of_chosen_color` — scripted blue → 1 blue mana, `total()==1`. (Concrete.)\n48\t- `test_any_color_ability_can_produce_a_different_color` — scripted green → 1 green mana (\"any color\"). (Concrete.)\n49\t- `test_any_color_mana_is_marked_restricted_to_instants_sorceries` — **tolerant probe** for the spend restriction. Asserts that *some* restriction surface exists (card-level `mana_spend_restriction`/`produces_restricted_mana`, ability-level `restriction`/`spend_restriction`, or a pool-level `restrictions`). Fails loudly today; the restriction clause is recorded in `untestable.json`.\n50\t\n51\tColor choices are driven deterministically via `create_game(scripts=([Color.X], []))` so the any-color picker is reproducible regardless of how the implementer wires `controller.choose`.\n52\t\n53\t### TestGreatHallAnimationAbilitySurface — Ability 3 surface — 1 case\n54\t- `test_exposes_an_activated_ability` — `{5}` is a non-mana `ActivatedAbility`. (Fails on stub.)\n55\t\n56\t### TestGreatHallAnimationEffect — Ability 3 animation — 5 cases (tolerant probes)\n57\t- `test_becomes_a_creature` — after activating {5}, `CardType.CREATURE` is added.\n58\t- `test_is_still_a_land_after_animation` — `CardType.LAND` retained (\"It's still a land\").\n59\t- `test_becomes_a_wizard` — `\"Wizard\"` subtype added.\n60\t- `test_becomes_two_four` — `power==2`, `toughness==4` after `effect_manager.apply_all`.\n61\t- `test_animation_no_op_when_already_a_creature` — re-activating while already a creature changes neither the 2/4 body nor the trigger count (\"If this land isn't a creature\").\n62\t\n63\tThese assert the observable end state the spec demands. The engine has no animation pipeline, so they fail loudly now; the deep surface is recorded in `untestable.json`.\n64\t\n65\t### TestGreatHallGrantedPumpTrigger — Ability 3 granted trigger — 2 cases (tolerant probes)\n66\t- `test_animation_registers_a_pump_trigger` — animating registers a new trigger (the granted \"whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell\" ability).\n67\t- `test_pump_trigger_adds_plus_one_zero_until_end_of_turn` — firing the granted trigger's effect once yields a 3/4 body (2/4 + 1/0) after recomputing the layer system.\n68\t\n69\tBoth fail loudly absent a grant-on-animation pipeline; the until-end-of-turn duration and per-cast scaling are recorded in `untestable.json`.\n70\t\n71\t## Edge cases covered\n72\t- Already-tapped land cannot re-pay `{T}` (ability 1).\n73\t- Two distinct colors honoured by the any-color ability (\"any color\", not a fixed color).\n74\t- Exact life delta (`-1`, not 0 or 2) for the pay-1-life cost.\n75\t- \"If this land isn't a creature\" — second animation is a no-op (no double-grant, body unchanged).\n76\t- \"It's still a land\" — LAND type explicitly asserted to survive animation.\n77\t\n78\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (out of scope / no engine surface)\n79\t- Enforcing that the restricted any-color mana *cannot* pay for a creature spell but *can* pay for an instant/sorcery — no restricted-mana mechanism (see `untestable.json` #1).\n80\t- Full layered animation P/T under the real layer pipeline, granted-ability registration on resolution, and the EOT pump expiry at cleanup — no becomes-a-creature / grant-on-animation surface (see `untestable.json` #2, #3). Probes fail loudly instead.\n81\t- Summoning sickness / haste interactions of the animated land's attack — out of scope for this card's printed text and dependent on the missing animation pipeline.\n82\t\n83\t## Red-phase confirmation\n84\t`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → **20 failed, 6 passed** against the empty stub. No import/collection errors (26 collected). The 6 passers are valid negative-property regression guards (colorless, nonbasic, no mana cost, no P/T pre-animation, no creature type) that the finished card must keep true; every positive behavioral assertion (identity, both mana abilities, life payment, animation, granted pump) fails in red.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013DvBFWmxzpqf1jHj4XNC9b","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"565982c6-7b4c-4297-ad32-2743d1911c43","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:07:48.640Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_257 + 3 engine mechanisms"}
