{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"aa3dc3e7b05aa86e1","tool_use_id":"toolu_013DvBFWmxzpqf1jHj4XNC9b","description":"Writing engine/animation.py","subagent_type":"Implementer","usage":{"total_tokens":134569,"tool_uses":40,"duration_ms":208224},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"b3528767-b5b2-4e78-a104-cd5f69cf1835","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014aNRRuD48AN3X5DvazBhGv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018UTZKoNya7Z6nVC9nxYgRR","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/animation.py","content":"\"\"\"Land-animation (\"becomes a creature\") framework.\n\nSeveral lands turn themselves into creatures while remaining lands — e.g.\nGreat Hall of the Biblioplex:\n\n    {5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with\n    \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0\n    until end of turn.\"  It's still a land.\n\nThe engine's :mod:`engine.continuous_effects` layer system already models type\nchanges (Layer 4) and P/T effects (Layer 7), but it had no helper to *animate*\na non-Creature :class:`~engine.card.CardImpl` into a creature that retains its\nland type, exposes a base power/toughness, and gains a creature subtype.  This\nmodule adds that helper *additively* — no existing engine symbol is renamed,\nmoved, or deleted.  It mirrors the lazy per-game-registry + grant conventions of\n:mod:`engine.miracle` / :mod:`engine.casualty` / :mod:`engine.affinity`.\n\nTwo observable mechanisms live here:\n\n1. **Animation** (:func:`animate_land`).  Layers ``CardType.CREATURE`` onto the\n   land while keeping ``CardType.LAND``, grants a creature subtype, and sets a\n   base body.  The body is observable via ``card.power`` / ``card.toughness``\n   once the card reports those characteristics under the active animation (a\n   :class:`~engine.card.Land` ordinarily has no power/toughness — the animating\n   card is expected to expose ``power``/``toughness`` properties that read the\n   animation state set here; see ``cards/sos/sos_257``).  The animation is\n   durable (``DURATION_PERMANENT`` — it lasts until the land leaves play), and\n   is *idempotent* per land via a lazy per-game registry, so \"if this land isn't\n   a creature\" re-activation is a true no-op.\n\n2. **The granted pump trigger** (:func:`register_instant_sorcery_pump`).  The\n   animation grants the land a triggered ability — \"Whenever you cast an instant\n   or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn\" — registered as\n   a :class:`~engine.events.SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger controlled by the\n   land's controller and gated to that controller's own instant/sorcery casts.\n   Firing it adds a Layer 7c (``MODIFY_PT``) +1/+0 :class:`ContinuousEffect`\n   with ``DURATION_END_OF_TURN`` to the land, so N casts in a turn yield +N/+0,\n   swept back at cleanup by ``EffectManager.remove_expired``.  The trigger is\n   deduped per source so animating once registers exactly one trigger.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n\nfrom engine.continuous_effects import (\n    DURATION_END_OF_TURN,\n    DURATION_PERMANENT,\n    ContinuousEffect,\n    Layer,\n    SubLayer,\n)\nfrom engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\nfrom engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\nfrom engine.types import CardType\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Per-game registry of animated permanents (idempotency / \"isn't a creature\")\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _animation_registry(game: GameState) -> dict[int, dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the per-game land-animation registry.\n\n    Maps ``id(land)`` to a record describing the active animation.  Stored\n    lazily on the game object so no ``GameState.__init__`` change is needed.\n    \"\"\"\n    registry = getattr(game, \"_land_animations\", None)\n    if registry is None:\n        registry = {}\n        game._land_animations = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    return registry\n\n\ndef is_animated(game: GameState, land: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *land* is currently animated into a creature.\n\n    Checks both the per-game registry and the land's own card types, so a card\n    that became a creature by any means reports correctly.\n    \"\"\"\n    if id(land) in _animation_registry(game):\n        return True\n    return CardType.CREATURE in getattr(land, \"card_types\", set())\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Animation — becomes a creature, still a land\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef animate_land(\n    game: GameState,\n    land: Any,\n    base_power: int,\n    base_toughness: int,\n    subtype: str | None = None,\n    controller: Any = None,\n) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Animate *land* into a ``base_power``/``base_toughness`` creature.\n\n    Implements \"it becomes a [P]/[T] [subtype] creature ... It's still a land\":\n\n    * adds ``CardType.CREATURE`` to the land's card types while RETAINING\n      ``CardType.LAND``;\n    * grants *subtype* (e.g. ``\"Wizard\"``) to its subtypes;\n    * records a base body the animating card can surface via ``power`` /\n      ``toughness`` (this writes ``land._animated``, ``land._anim_base_power``,\n      ``land._anim_base_toughness``, and seeds ``modified_power`` /\n      ``modified_toughness``);\n    * installs a durable (``DURATION_PERMANENT``) Layer-4 type effect and a\n      Layer 7b ``SET_PT`` base-body effect through the engine layer system so\n      the change survives ``EffectManager.apply_all``'s reset-and-reapply.\n\n    The change is applied *immediately* (so ``CardType.CREATURE`` is observable\n    without first calling ``apply_all``) AND registered as a continuous effect\n    (so it persists across recomputation).\n\n    Guarded by \"if this land isn't a creature\": if *land* is already animated\n    (or already a creature), this is a no-op and returns ``False``.  Otherwise\n    it animates and returns ``True``.\n    \"\"\"\n    if is_animated(game, land):\n        return False\n\n    if controller is None:\n        controller = getattr(land, \"controller\", None)\n\n    # --- Immediate mutation so the new characteristics are observable now. ---\n    land.card_types = set(getattr(land, \"card_types\", set())) | {CardType.CREATURE}\n    if subtype is not None:\n        subtypes = getattr(land, \"subtypes\", None)\n        if subtypes is None:\n            subtypes = set()\n            land.subtypes = subtypes\n        subtypes.add(subtype)\n\n    land._animated = True  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    land._anim_base_power = base_power  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    land._anim_base_toughness = base_toughness  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    land._anim_subtype = subtype  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    land.modified_power = base_power  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    land.modified_toughness = base_toughness  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n\n    # --- Durable layer effects so the animation survives apply_all resets. ---\n    def _apply_type(g: GameState) -> None:\n        land.card_types = set(getattr(land, \"card_types\", set())) | {\n            CardType.CREATURE\n        }\n        land.card_types.add(CardType.LAND)\n        if subtype is not None:\n            land.subtypes.add(subtype)\n\n    def _apply_base_body(g: GameState) -> None:\n        land.modified_power = base_power  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n        land.modified_toughness = base_toughness  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n\n    type_effect = ContinuousEffect(\n        source=land,\n        layer=Layer.TYPE,\n        apply=_apply_type,\n        duration=DURATION_PERMANENT,\n    )\n    body_effect = ContinuousEffect(\n        source=land,\n        layer=Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS,\n        sublayer=SubLayer.SET_PT,\n        apply=_apply_base_body,\n        duration=DURATION_PERMANENT,\n    )\n    game.effect_manager.add(type_effect)\n    game.effect_manager.add(body_effect)\n\n    _animation_registry(game)[id(land)] = {\n        \"controller\": controller,\n        \"base_power\": base_power,\n        \"base_toughness\": base_toughness,\n        \"subtype\": subtype,\n        \"type_effect\": type_effect,\n        \"body_effect\": body_effect,\n    }\n    return True\n\n\ndef deanimate_land(game: GameState, land: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Remove *land*'s animation (e.g. when it leaves the battlefield).\n\n    Drops the registry record and the durable layer effects, clears the\n    animation flags, and removes the granted pump trigger.  This is the\n    \"until it leaves play\" cleanup; it is safe to call when *land* is not\n    animated (no-op).\n    \"\"\"\n    registry = _animation_registry(game)\n    record = registry.pop(id(land), None)\n    if record is None:\n        return\n    for key in (\"type_effect\", \"body_effect\"):\n        effect = record.get(key)\n        if effect is not None:\n            game.effect_manager.remove(effect)\n    game.trigger_manager.unregister(land)\n    land._animated = False  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    land.card_types = set(getattr(land, \"card_types\", set())) - {CardType.CREATURE}\n    subtype = record.get(\"subtype\")\n    if subtype is not None and subtype in getattr(land, \"subtypes\", set()):\n        land.subtypes.discard(subtype)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# The granted pump trigger\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef add_pump_until_end_of_turn(\n    game: GameState,\n    land: Any,\n    power_bonus: int = 1,\n    toughness_bonus: int = 0,\n) -> ContinuousEffect:\n    \"\"\"Give *land* +``power_bonus``/+``toughness_bonus`` until end of turn.\n\n    Adds a Layer 7c (``MODIFY_PT``) :class:`ContinuousEffect` with\n    ``DURATION_END_OF_TURN`` to the engine layer system.  After\n    ``EffectManager.apply_all`` the bonus is visible via ``land.power`` /\n    ``land.toughness``; firing this N times in a turn stacks to +N/+0, and\n    ``EffectManager.remove_expired`` (run at cleanup) sweeps every such effect\n    away so the body resets at end of turn.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _apply(g: GameState) -> None:\n        if getattr(land, \"modified_power\", None) is not None:\n            land.modified_power += power_bonus  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n        if getattr(land, \"modified_toughness\", None) is not None:\n            land.modified_toughness += toughness_bonus  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n\n    effect = ContinuousEffect(\n        source=land,\n        layer=Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS,\n        sublayer=SubLayer.MODIFY_PT,\n        apply=_apply,\n        duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN,\n    )\n    return game.effect_manager.add(effect)\n\n\ndef _pump_trigger_registry(game: GameState) -> set[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return (creating if necessary) the per-game pump-trigger dedup set.\"\"\"\n    registry = getattr(game, \"_animation_pump_triggers\", None)\n    if registry is None:\n        registry = set()\n        game._animation_pump_triggers = registry  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    return registry\n\n\ndef register_instant_sorcery_pump(\n    game: GameState,\n    land: Any,\n    controller: Any,\n    power_bonus: int = 1,\n    toughness_bonus: int = 0,\n) -> TriggerRegistration | None:\n    \"\"\"Grant *land* \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery, +1/+0 until EOT\".\n\n    Registers (deduped per source via a lazy per-game registry) a\n    :class:`~engine.events.SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger controlled by\n    *controller* and gated to *controller*'s own instant/sorcery casts.  When it\n    fires, :func:`add_pump_until_end_of_turn` gives *land*\n    +``power_bonus``/+``toughness_bonus`` until end of turn.\n\n    Returns the created :class:`~engine.triggers.TriggerRegistration`, or\n    ``None`` if a pump trigger was already registered for this source (so a\n    second animation does not stack a second grant).\n    \"\"\"\n    registry = _pump_trigger_registry(game)\n    if id(land) in registry:\n        return None\n\n    def _condition(g: GameState, event: SpellCastTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n        caster = getattr(event, \"player\", None) or getattr(event, \"controller\", None)\n        if caster is not controller:\n            return False\n        spell = getattr(event, \"spell\", None) or getattr(event, \"card\", None)\n        card_types = getattr(spell, \"card_types\", set())\n        return CardType.INSTANT in card_types or CardType.SORCERY in card_types\n\n    def _effect(g: GameState) -> None:\n        add_pump_until_end_of_turn(g, land, power_bonus, toughness_bonus)\n\n    trigger = TriggerRegistration(\n        event_type=SpellCastTriggeredEvent,\n        condition=_condition,\n        effect=_effect,\n        source=land,\n        controller=controller,\n    )\n    game.trigger_manager.register(trigger)\n    registry.add(id(land))\n    return trigger\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":709,"cache_read_input_tokens":133446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":709,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013DvBFWmxzpqf1jHj4XNC9b","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"589f1ffb-cb39-485e-b1d7-1406c14c6a61","request_id":"req_011CbeFXvxYJ1D1wGhRyjN7L","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_257 + 3 engine mechanisms"}
