{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Ke4ZWLu5WQAXzFm6EHtiR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Tests for SOS 226 — Silverquill, the Disputant.\n2\t\n3\tOracle text (from card_spec.json):\n4\t\n5\t    Flying, vigilance\n6\t    Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you cast that\n7\t    spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When you do,\n8\t    copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\n9\t\n10\tBehaviour contract derived from that text:\n11\t\n12\t* Static: Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, {2}{W}{B}, 4/4, black+white, with\n13\t  Flying and Vigilance.\n14\t* Casualty-granting static ability: while Silverquill is on the battlefield,\n15\t  every instant and sorcery SPELL its controller casts \"has casualty 1\"\n16\t  (CR 702.153). Casualty 1 means: as an additional cost you MAY sacrifice a\n17\t  creature with power 1 or greater; when you do, copy the spell and may choose\n18\t  new targets for the copy.\n19\t\n20\t  There is no engine-level casualty pipeline, so the implementation must expose\n21\t  some observable surface that reports the casualty value (1) for an\n22\t  instant/sorcery the controller casts (and grants it to no other card types /\n23\t  no other players). These tests probe that surface TOLERANTLY: they accept any\n24\t  of the conventional spellings the implementer is likely to use (a query method\n25\t  on the Silverquill card and/or an attribute written onto the affected spell),\n26\t  and skip-with-reason only if NO recognised surface exists (so the contract is\n27\t  never silently green).\n28\t\n29\t  The copy/sacrifice RESOLUTION mechanic (paying the casualty cost by\n30\t  sacrificing a power>=1 creature, then producing a copy with optional new\n31\t  targets) is recorded in untestable.json: no engine casualty pipeline exists to\n32\t  assert it against yet.\n33\t\n34\tThese tests are written for the TDD red phase: they must FAIL against the empty\n35\tstub and PASS once the card is implemented correctly.\n36\t\"\"\"\n37\t\n38\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n39\t\n40\tfrom typing import Any\n41\t\n42\timport pytest\n43\t\n44\tfrom cards.sos.sos_226.card_impl import SilverquillTheDisputant\n45\tfrom engine.card import Creature, Instant, Sorcery\n46\tfrom engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n47\tfrom engine.stack import StackObject\n48\tfrom engine.types import Color, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Supertype, Zone\n49\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n50\t\n51\t\n52\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n53\t# Test helper cards\n54\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n55\t\n56\t\n57\tdef _vanilla_instant(name: str = \"Test Instant\") -> Instant:\n58\t    return Instant(name=name, mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{R}\"))\n59\t\n60\t\n61\tdef _vanilla_sorcery(name: str = \"Test Sorcery\") -> Sorcery:\n62\t    return Sorcery(name=name, mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{2}{G}\"))\n63\t\n64\t\n65\tdef _vanilla_creature(name: str = \"Test Bear\") -> Creature:\n66\t    return Creature(\n67\t        name=name,\n68\t        mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{G}\"),\n69\t        base_power=2,\n70\t        base_toughness=2,\n71\t    )\n72\t\n73\t\n74\tdef _casualty_value_for(card_obj: Any, game: Any, spell: Any) -> Any:\n75\t    \"\"\"Best-effort probe for the granted casualty value of *spell*.\n76\t\n77\t    The casualty mechanic has no engine pipeline, so the implementation is free\n78\t    to surface the grant in a number of conventional ways. This helper tries\n79\t    each in turn and returns the reported value, or raises ``pytest.skip`` if no\n80\t    recognised surface exists (so the contract is not silently green).\n81\t    \"\"\"\n82\t    # 1. A method on the Silverquill card that reports the casualty value it\n83\t    #    grants to a given spell.\n84\t    for meth_name in (\n85\t        \"casualty_value_for\",\n86\t        \"get_casualty_value\",\n87\t        \"casualty_for\",\n88\t        \"get_casualty\",\n89\t        \"casualty_value\",\n90\t    ):\n91\t        meth = getattr(card_obj, meth_name, None)\n92\t        if callable(meth):\n93\t            try:\n94\t                return meth(game, spell)\n95\t            except TypeError:\n96\t                try:\n97\t                    return meth(spell)\n98\t                except TypeError:\n99\t                    continue\n100\t    # 2. The grant written directly onto the spell.\n101\t    for attr_name in (\"casualty_value\", \"casualty\", \"granted_casualty\"):\n102\t        val = getattr(spell, attr_name, None)\n103\t        if val is not None:\n104\t            return val\n105\t    pytest.skip(\n106\t        \"No observable surface for the granted casualty value — implementation \"\n107\t        \"must expose casualty_value_for(...)/get_casualty_value(...) on the \"\n108\t        \"card or a casualty_value attribute on the affected spell.\"\n109\t    )\n110\t\n111\t\n112\tdef _probe_casualty_silent(card_obj: Any, game: Any, spell: Any) -> Any:\n113\t    \"\"\"Like ``_casualty_value_for`` but returns None instead of skipping when no\n114\t    recognised surface reports a value for *spell* (used for the exclusion-side\n115\t    assertions, anchored on a positive case so the test is never vacuous).\"\"\"\n116\t    for meth_name in (\n117\t        \"casualty_value_for\",\n118\t        \"get_casualty_value\",\n119\t        \"casualty_for\",\n120\t        \"get_casualty\",\n121\t        \"casualty_value\",\n122\t    ):\n123\t        meth = getattr(card_obj, meth_name, None)\n124\t        if callable(meth):\n125\t            try:\n126\t                return meth(game, spell)\n127\t            except TypeError:\n128\t                try:\n129\t                    return meth(spell)\n130\t                except TypeError:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CbsKBgtu5hXmsenTvvH1UM","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"6f93d5e5-235e-4789-a1a0-62f5b4031590","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:19:54.944Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_257 tests"}
