{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01PBwyUSdXEy79Ekdcwj3hzX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UFgEXXwL1nKYHW9eXaXMT4","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md","old_string":"## Red-phase confirmation\n`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → **20 failed, 6 passed** against the empty stub. No import/collection errors (26 collected). The 6 passers are valid negative-property regression guards (colorless, nonbasic, no mana cost, no P/T pre-animation, no creature type) that the finished card must keep true; every positive behavioral assertion (identity, both mana abilities, life payment, animation, granted pump) fails in red.","new_string":"## Red-phase confirmation\n`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → **20 failed, 6 passed** against the empty stub. No import/collection errors (26 collected). The 6 passers are valid negative-property regression guards (colorless, nonbasic, no mana cost, no P/T pre-animation, no creature type) that the finished card must keep true; every positive behavioral assertion (identity, both mana abilities, life payment, animation, granted pump) fails in red.\n\n---\n\n# Extended coverage (post-implementation green phase)\n\nThe Implementer built the three formerly-deferred mechanisms **additively**:\n\n1. **Restricted mana** — `engine/mana.py`: `ManaPool.add_restricted(...)` records a `ManaRestriction` (`RESTRICT_INSTANT_SORCERY`) in a parallel `pool.restrictions` list; `can_pay_for_spell(cost, spell)` excludes restricted mana that doesn't permit the spell type; `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` now calls `can_pay_for_spell` instead of `can_pay`.\n2. **Land animation** — new `engine/animation.py`: `animate_land(game, land, p, t, subtype, controller)` adds `CardType.CREATURE` (keeping `LAND`), grants the subtype, seeds a 2/4 base body surfaced via the card's `power`/`toughness` properties, and registers durable (`DURATION_PERMANENT`) Layer.TYPE + Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS/SET_PT effects. Guarded by `is_animated` so re-animation is a true no-op.\n3. **Granted pump trigger** — `engine/animation.py::register_instant_sorcery_pump(...)`: deduped-per-source `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` `TriggerRegistration` gated to the controller's instant/sorcery casts; firing calls `add_pump_until_end_of_turn`, adding a Layer 7c (`MODIFY_PT`) +1/+0 `ContinuousEffect` with `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`.\n\nI confirmed each API by reading the source and by standalone probes, then added **20 concrete tests** (total now **46**, all passing). The original 26 tests (including the three tolerant probes) are unchanged — those probes now pass because the surfaces they look for exist.\n\nThese tests drive the REAL engine, not mocks: restricted mana is produced (often via the card's own ability) and spent through `cast_spell`; the {5} cost is paid out of the controller's pool; the pump is triggered via the established `trigger_manager.fire_event(SpellCastTriggeredEvent(...))` pattern (cf. sos_226) and resolved off the stack before P/T is read.\n\n### TestGreatHallRestrictedManaSpend — 7 cases\n- `test_card_produced_mana_is_tagged_restricted` — activating the card's `{T}, Pay 1 life` any-color ability deposits BLUE that the pool reports as `has_restricted_mana()` / `restricted_amount() == 1` (drives the card, not a hand-built record).\n- `test_instant_can_be_cast_with_restricted_mana` — an `Instant` for `{U}` casts through the real `cast_spell` consuming the card-produced restricted mana (stack non-empty, pool drained, `restricted_amount()==0`).\n- `test_sorcery_can_be_cast_with_restricted_mana` — a `Sorcery` for `{G}` is equally a permitted target.\n- `test_creature_cannot_be_cast_with_restricted_mana` — **negative**: a `Creature` for `{G}` raises `CastingError` (\"insufficient mana\"); the spell is rolled back to hand and the restricted mana is left untouched.\n- `test_creature_can_be_cast_with_unrestricted_mana` — **anchor**: the identical creature for `{G}` casts fine when the green is ordinary, proving the rejection above is about the restriction, not the cost.\n- `test_restricted_mana_does_not_taint_an_unrestricted_pool` — **regression anchor**: with no restricted mana present, a `{1}{G}` creature still casts (the restriction machinery never blocks ordinary mana — the documented fast path).\n\n### TestGreatHallAnimationEndState — 6 cases\n- `test_five_cost_is_paid_from_the_pool` — activating `{5}` consumes exactly 5 generic mana (6 → 1).\n- `test_animated_gains_creature_but_keeps_land` — `CREATURE` added, `LAND` retained (\"It's still a land\").\n- `test_animated_gains_wizard_subtype` — `\"Wizard\"` subtype present.\n- `test_animated_body_is_two_four` — `power==2`, `toughness==4` after `apply_all`.\n- `test_body_survives_recomputation` — three repeated `apply_all` cycles keep the 2/4 body and CREATURE+LAND types (the durable layer effects survive reset-and-reapply).\n- `test_reanimation_is_a_noop_no_second_body_or_grant` — the guard: a second `{5}` (cost paid again from a 10-mana pool) does NOT register a second trigger, does NOT add extra layer effects, and the body stays 2/4 (not stacked).\n\n### TestGreatHallGrantedPumpBehaviour — 7 cases\n- `test_animation_registers_exactly_one_pump_trigger` — exactly one `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger after animation.\n- `test_one_instant_cast_pumps_plus_one_zero` — one instant cast → power 3, toughness 4.\n- `test_sorcery_cast_also_pumps` — a sorcery is an equally valid trigger.\n- `test_multiple_casts_stack_plus_n_zero` — N=3 casts → power `2 + N`, toughness 4 (the per-cast scaling).\n- `test_pump_resets_at_end_of_turn` — two casts (power 4 mid-turn), then `remove_expired` + `apply_all` sweeps the `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` effects → back to 2/4.\n- `test_animation_type_effect_survives_eot_sweep` — the cleanup sweep removes the pump but NOT the permanent animation (still a 2/4 Wizard creature-land after EOT reset).\n- `test_opponents_cast_does_not_pump` — gating: an opponent's instant pushes no trigger and leaves the land at 2/4.\n- `test_controllers_creature_cast_does_not_pump` — gating: the controller casting a CREATURE (neither instant nor sorcery) pushes no trigger; land stays 2/4.\n\n### Bugs found\nNone. Every mechanism behaves exactly as the implementation rationale describes:\nrestricted mana pays instants/sorceries but is rejected for creatures and never\ntaints an unrestricted pool; the {5} animation yields a 2/4 creature-land with\nthe Wizard subtype and is idempotent under the \"isn't a creature\" guard; the\ngranted pump stacks +1/+0 per controller instant/sorcery cast, is correctly\ngated against opponents and creature casts, and resets at cleanup while the\npermanent animation persists. All 46 tests pass.\n\n### Extended-coverage edge cases\n- Card-produced restricted mana (not just a hand-built `ManaRestriction`) — the production path is exercised end to end via `get_mana_abilities()`.\n- Rollback-to-hand on the rejected creature cast, with the restricted mana preserved.\n- Durability of the animation across repeated `apply_all` and across the EOT sweep (permanent vs end-of-turn duration distinction).\n- Both gating axes for the pump (wrong player AND wrong spell type).\n\n### Extended-coverage edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n- Summoning-sickness/haste of the animated land in combat — out of scope for the printed text and orthogonal to the three built mechanisms.\n- `deanimate_land` leave-play cleanup — not part of the card's printed behavior (it has no \"until end of turn\" animation clause); the animation is permanent, so de-animation only matters on zone change, which is engine territory covered elsewhere.\n- Mixed restricted + unrestricted payment optimisation (e.g. paying a `{1}{U}` instant partly with restricted, partly with ordinary mana) — the spec's clause is a binary permit/deny that the covered tests already exercise; finer payment-ordering is engine behavior, not card contract."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3735,"cache_read_input_tokens":95054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3735,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CbsKBgtu5hXmsenTvvH1UM","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b296f105-c306-4a5a-aec6-d60f24ac0085","request_id":"req_011CbeGUxGwvUXbdoXJLx1FS","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_257 tests"}
