{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CbsKBgtu5hXmsenTvvH1UM","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 46 pass. The test-files.txt is already accurate (single file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`), untestable.json is now `[]`, and the rationale has its \"Extended coverage\" section.\n\nTESTS_EXTENDED\ntotal_test_count: 46\nnew_tests: 20\nall_passing: yes\nuntestable_remaining: 0\n\nSummary of what I added to `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` (preserving all 26 existing tests; only added imports and three new test classes):\n\n- **TestGreatHallRestrictedManaSpend (7)** — drives `ManaPool.add_restricted` + `can_pay_for_spell` through the real `cast_spell`: card-produced restricted mana is tagged; an Instant and a Sorcery can be cast with it; a Creature is rejected with `CastingError` (rolled back to hand, restricted mana untouched); anchored by the same creature casting fine on unrestricted mana, plus a regression anchor that an unrestricted pool is never tainted.\n- **TestGreatHallAnimationEndState (6)** — pays the real `{5}` from the pool; asserts CREATURE added while LAND retained, Wizard subtype, a 2/4 body after `apply_all`, durability across repeated recomputation, and the \"if this land isn't a creature\" guard (second activation grants no second trigger, adds no extra layer effects, body stays 2/4).\n- **TestGreatHallGrantedPumpBehaviour (7)** — fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (the established pattern) and resolves the stacked trigger: one instant → 3/4; sorcery also pumps; N=3 casts → power `2+N`; `remove_expired` at cleanup resets to 2/4 while the permanent animation survives; gated so an opponent's cast and a controller's creature cast do not pump.\n\nNo implementation bugs found — every mechanism behaves exactly as the rationale documents. I verified each engine API by reading `engine/mana.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/animation.py`, `engine/continuous_effects.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, and `engine/events.py`, and confirmed behavior via standalone probes before committing the assertions.\n\nOutputs updated:\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` (46 tests, all passing)\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md` (added \"Extended coverage\" section, \"Bugs found: None\")\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json` → `[]`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-files.txt` (already accurate — single file)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a185b8e2ba9e6d5b6 (use SendMessage with to: 'a185b8e2ba9e6d5b6' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 103448\ntool_uses: 38\nduration_ms: 261654</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"d13c55cd-a247-474d-8212-76902ecbe6f8","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:23:31.497Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Follow-up on card sos_257 \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\" (a man-land). You previously wrote 26 tests and deferred 3 items to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json`: (1) the \"spend only on instant/sorcery\" mana restriction, (2) the {5} becomes-a-2/4-Wizard-still-a-land animation, (3) the granted \"+1/+0 until end of turn per instant/sorcery cast\" pump trigger. The Implementer has now built all three additively. Extend `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` with REAL tests.\n\nRead first:\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json` — the 3 deferred items.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-rationale.md` — the Implementer's description of: the restricted-mana mechanism (the surface/tag in `engine/mana.py` and how `engine.casting.cast_spell` enforces it), the land-animation helper (new `engine/animation.py`), and the granted pump trigger. Use the EXACT function/attribute/module names it documents.\n- `engine/mana.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/animation.py` — confirm the actual APIs (signatures, restriction-tag names, animation helper names, how power/toughness become observable, the trigger registration).\n- `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` — your existing file; ADD to it, do not remove existing tests.\n\nNew coverage to add — drive the real mechanisms:\n1. **Restricted mana spend**: activate `{T}, Pay 1 life` to produce one mana of a chosen color tagged \"instant/sorcery only\". Assert an INSTANT (and a SORCERY) can be cast consuming that restricted mana, but a CREATURE cast canNOT use it (the restricted mana is rejected / cannot pay). Drive through `cast_spell` and the real ManaPool, asserting the observable outcome.\n2. **{5} animation end state**: pay {5} on the un-animated land → it gains CardType.CREATURE while RETAINING CardType.LAND, gains Subtype.WIZARD, and is a 2/4 (card.power == 2, card.toughness == 4 after the effect manager applies). Assert the \"if this land isn't a creature\" guard: activating {5} again while already a creature does NOT re-animate / stack a second body.\n3. **Granted pump trigger**: once animated, casting (or firing the SpellCastTriggeredEvent for) the controller's instant/sorcery gives +1/+0 until end of turn. Fire it N times → power == 2 + N (toughness stays 4). Assert the pump RESETS at cleanup/end of turn (remove_expired sweeps the DURATION_END_OF_TURN effects → power back to 2). Assert it's gated to the CONTROLLER's instant/sorcery casts (an opponent's cast, or a creature cast, does not pump).\n\nConstraints:\n- REAL passing tests against the now-built engine (not skips). Anchor any tolerant probe so a missing surface fails loudly.\n- Do NOT weaken or delete the existing 26 tests.\n- Tests run from `/workspace`; bare imports.\n\nRun `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` and confirm the full count passes. If you find a genuine implementation bug (restriction not enforced, wrong animation end state, guard missing, pump doesn't reset, wrong gating), write the failing test anyway and describe the bug clearly — do NOT paper over it.\n\nOutputs:\n- Update `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`.\n- Update `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md` with