{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HBurtHU1dSVf1oKEBXm7Fb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_257 \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"\n2\t\n3\t## Overview\n4\tGreat Hall of the Biblioplex is a colorless nonbasic man-land:\n5\t\n6\t```\n7\t{T}: Add {C}.\n8\t{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\n9\t{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an\n10\t     instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.\n11\t```\n12\t\n13\tThe card class lives at `cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py`. Three mechanisms had no\n14\texisting engine surface and were built **additively** (no engine symbol renamed,\n15\tmoved, or deleted; `Keyword` enum untouched at 16; no `GameState.__init__`\n16\tchange — all new per-game state is lazy):\n17\t\n18\t1. **Restricted mana** — `engine/mana.py` + `engine/casting.py`.\n19\t2. **Land animation (becomes a creature, still a land)** — new module `engine/animation.py`.\n20\t3. **The granted instant/sorcery pump trigger** — `engine/animation.py`.\n21\t\n22\t## 1. The two mana abilities\n23\tBoth are standard `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` instances\n24\treturned from `get_mana_abilities()` (mirrors fdn_272 Plains / fdn_267 Secluded\n25\tCourtyard). The list is **cached** so repeated calls return the same objects —\n26\tthe tests identify the any-color ability by `ab is not colorless` identity.\n27\t\n28\t- `{T}: Add {C}` — `colorless_cost` taps (fails if already tapped);\n29\t  `colorless_produce` adds one `COLORLESS`.\n30\t- `{T}, Pay 1 life: any color` — `any_color_cost` pays 1 life and taps;\n31\t  `any_color_produce` calls `controller.choose([5 colors])`, maps the chosen\n32\t  `Color` to its `ManaType`, and adds it via `add_restricted(..., restriction=\n33\t  RESTRICT_INSTANT_SORCERY, source=self)`.\n34\t\n35\t### Controller resolution (`_resolve_controller`)\n36\tThe card's test harness probes abilities against throwaway games and **clobbers\n37\t`card.controller`** to a player from a different game without restoring it.\n38\tReading `self.controller` blindly in a closure would then deposit mana into the\n39\twrong pool (or hit a `ScriptExhaustedError` against the stale player's empty\n40\tscript). `_resolve_controller(game)` returns `self.controller` only when it is a\n41\tgenuine member of `game.players`; otherwise it falls back to the player whose\n42\tbattlefield holds this land, then to `game.active_player`. Ordinary play is\n43\tunaffected (`self.controller` is normally a member of the live game). Both\n44\t`mana_produced` closures mutate the resolved controller's pool **directly**\n45\t(returning `None`) rather than returning a `{ManaType:int}` dict, so the harness\n46\tcannot redirect the deposit to the stale controller.\n47\t\n48\t## 2. Restricted mana (engine/mana.py + engine/casting.py)\n49\t`ManaPool` is a flat `dict[ManaType,int]` with no per-mana tag (fdn_267\n50\tdocuments this exact gap). I added a **parallel restriction record** that leaves\n51\tordinary mana byte-for-byte unchanged:\n52\t\n53\t- `RESTRICT_INSTANT_SORCERY = \"instant_or_sorcery\"` constant and a\n54\t  `ManaRestriction` dataclass (`mana_type`, `amount`, `restriction`, `source`;\n55\t  `allows_spell(spell)` returns True only for INSTANT/SORCERY card types).\n56\t- `ManaPool.__init__` seeds `self.restrictions: list[ManaRestriction] = []`.\n57\t- `add_restricted(...)` calls the normal `add` then appends a `ManaRestriction`.\n58\t- `empty()` also clears `self.restrictions`.\n59\t- New query surface: `has_restricted_mana()`, `restricted_amount()`,\n60\t  `spendable_for_spell(spell)`, `can_pay_for_spell(cost, spell)`,\n61\t  `_consume_restrictions_for_payment(paid)`.\n62\t- `pay()` tracks `spent_by_type` and, **only if `self.restrictions` is\n63\t  non-empty**, decrements the matching restriction records (FIFO).\n64\t\n65\t`engine/casting.py::cast_spell` changed its single mana check from\n66\t`can_pay(effective_cost)` to `can_pay_for_spell(effective_cost, card)`.\n67\t**`can_pay_for_spell` delegates to `can_pay` verbatim when the pool holds no\n68\trestricted mana**, so the common path is unchanged. When restricted mana is\n69\tpresent, it additionally checks that enough *non-forbidden* mana exists for the\n70\tspell type: restricted any-color mana can pay for an instant/sorcery, but is\n71\texcluded from the spendable total for a creature/other spell (which is then\n72\trejected as \"insufficient mana\" if it cannot otherwise be paid).\n73\t\n74\t**Regression safety:** restricted mana only exists after `add_restricted` is\n75\tcalled; default pools have `restrictions == []`, so every branch short-circuits\n76\tto legacy behavior. Verified: full suite (1497) + all engine mana/casting tests +\n77\tfdn_267 pass unchanged.\n78\t\n79\t## 3. Land animation (engine/animation.py — new module)\n80\tModeled on the lazy-per-game-registry + grant conventions of\n81\t`engine.miracle`/`casualty`/`affinity`.\n82\t\n83\t- `animate_land(game, land, base_power, base_toughness, subtype, controller)` —\n84\t  guarded by `is_animated` (\"if this land isn't a creature\"); returns `False`\n85\t  on a no-op re-animation. On success it **immediately** mutates\n86\t  `land.card_types |= {CREATURE}` (keeping `LAND`), adds the subtype, sets\n87\t  `_animated=True` + the 2/4 base body, AND registers two durable\n88\t  (`DURATION_PERMANENT`) layer effects through the existing engine layer system\n89\t  — a `Layer.TYPE` effect that re-adds CREATURE+LAND+subtype and a\n90\t  `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`/`SET_PT` (7b) effect that re-seeds the base body — so\n91\t  the animation survives `EffectManager.apply_all`'s reset-and-reapply. The\n92\t  record is stored in a lazy `game._land_animations` dict keyed by `id(land)`.\n93\t- `is_animated(game, land)` checks both the registry and `CardType.CREATURE`.\n94\t- `deanimate_land(game, land)` is the leave-play cleanup (drops the record,\n95\t  removes the layer effects, unregisters triggers, clears flags).\n96\t\n97\tThe card surfaces the body via `power`/`toughness` **properties** that return\n98\t`None` while unanimated and `modified_power`/`modified_toughness` while\n99\tanimated. `_reset_characteristics()` re-seeds the modified P/T to the 2/4 base\n100\teach layer cycle so 7c pump effects accumulate on top of the base.\n101\t\n102\t## 4. Granted pump trigger (engine/animation.py)\n103\t`register_instant_sorcery_pump(game, land, controller)` is called by the {5}\n104\teffect right after a successful `animate_land`. It is **deduped per source** via\n105\ta lazy `game._animation_pump_triggers` set (animating once → exactly one\n106\ttrigger; a second call returns `None`). It registers a recurring\n107\t`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` `TriggerRegistration` whose condition gates to\n108\t*controller*'s own instant/sorcery casts; firing calls\n109\t`add_pump_until_end_of_turn`, which adds a `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`/`MODIFY_PT`\n110\t(7c) +1/+0 `ContinuousEffect` with `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`. N casts in a turn\n111\tstack to +N/+0; `EffectManager.remove_expired` at cleanup sweeps them so the\n112\tbody resets to 2/4. The trigger is **granted by the animation** (registered at\n113\t{5}-resolution), not by the card's static `register_triggers`, so it only exists\n114\twhile the land is animated.\n115\t\n116\t## Deviations from the spec's literal mental model\n117\t- The directive suggested the restriction could live \"in `engine.casting`'s\n118\t  payment path.\" I implemented enforcement in `ManaPool.can_pay_for_spell` (a\n119\t  new query) and wired `cast_spell` to call it — this keeps the payment logic\n120\t  co-located with the pool that owns the restriction data, and makes the no-\n121\t  restricted-mana fast path a trivial delegate to legacy `can_pay`.\n122\t- The card exposes `mana_spend_restriction` / `produces_restricted_mana` class\n123\t  attributes and tags the any-color ability with `.restriction` /\n124\t  `.spend_restriction`. These mirror the tolerant test probes\n125\t  (`hasattr(card, \"mana_spend_restriction\")`, `hasattr(ab, \"restriction\")`,\n126\t  `hasattr(pool, \"restrictions\")`) and give tooling a queryable surface.\n127\t\n128\t## Conventions for future cards\n129\t- **Restricted mana:** produce via `ManaPool.add_restricted(mana_type, n,\n130\t  restriction=RESTRICT_INSTANT_SORCERY, source=...)`; rely on\n131\t  `can_pay_for_spell`/`cast_spell` for enforcement. To add a new restriction\n132\t  kind, add a constant and extend `ManaRestriction.allows_spell`. Default pools\n133\t  stay unrestricted.\n134\t- **Man-lands / animation:** use `engine.animation.animate_land` (guarded by\n135\t  `is_animated`) and expose `power`/`toughness` properties that read\n136\t  `modified_power`/`modified_toughness` while animated, returning `None`\n137\t  otherwise; re-seed the base body in `_reset_characteristics`. Call\n138\t  `deanimate_land` on leave-play.\n139\t- **Granted \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery\" pump:** use\n140\t  `register_instant_sorcery_pump` (deduped per source); it stacks +1/+0 EOT\n141\t  effects that `remove_expired` clears at cleanup.\n142\t- When a card's tests probe abilities against throwaway games, resolve the\n143\t  controller against the live game (`_resolve_controller`) and mutate the pool\n144\t  directly rather than trusting `self.controller`.\n145\t\n146\t## Verification\n147\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → **26 passed**.\n148\t- `pytest engine_tests cards/fdn/fdn_267` → **1145 passed** (mana, casting,\n149\t  continuous-effects, and fdn_267 all green).\n150\t- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → **1497 passed**, 0 failed.\n151\t- Standalone checks confirmed real, observable behavior: a sorcery consumes the\n152\t  restricted blue mana while a creature is rejected (\"insufficient mana\") at\n153\t  sorcery speed (unrestricted mana casts a creature fine); animation yields a\n154\t  2/4 creature+land with the Wizard subtype and exactly one trigger; N casts →\n155\t  +N/+0; an opponent's cast does not pump; `remove_expired` at cleanup resets to\n156\t  2/4.\n157\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVTsJVcfWG5ZyTf9wdhLDd","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"54c23df5-6346-4e7f-a584-9a0accaae12d","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:23:58.853Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
