{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WB2nrdRjZK88qKxrDptCcX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent, append-only log of conventions and design decisions across runs.\n4\t\n5\t## Engine: stack->graveyard exile redirect (from sos_1)\n6\t- For \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" free-cast effects:\n7\t  `engine.casting` now has an additive per-game redirect registry:\n8\t  - `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card, destination)` — one-shot, identity-keyed by `id(card)`.\n9\t  - `clear_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, card)`.\n10\t  - `_redirect_registry(game)` lazily attaches `game._stack_to_graveyard_redirects` (no GameState.__init__ change).\n11\t  - `_resolve_spell` pops any registered redirect for a non-permanent spell and routes it there instead of the graveyard; with no redirect registered, behavior is unchanged (defaults to GRAVEYARD).\n12\t- Usage in a card: call `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, chosen_card, \"exile\")` before `cast_spell_free(...)`. Clear it if the cast raises.\n13\t- Rationale: `engine.zones.move_to_zone` only consults replacement effects when `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`, so STACK->GRAVEYARD resolution would otherwise bypass an exile-instead replacement.\n14\t\n15\t## Convention: cost_reduction counts (from sos_1)\n16\t- Card `cost_reduction` returns the raw count (e.g. instants+sorceries in controller's graveyard); the engine's `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the generic portion of the cost. Mirrors fdn_167 (Tolarian Terror). Count only the controller's graveyard unless the card says otherwise.\n17\t## Convention: Converge / colors_spent (from sos_4)\n18\t- Converge X = number of distinct colors of mana spent to cast. Already wired in engine:\n19\t  `engine.casting.cast_spell` sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (distinct, colorless-excluded, sorted list of `engine.types.Color`).\n20\t- Card-side: default `self.colors_spent = []` in `__init__`; compute `X = len(self.colors_spent)`. No engine change needed for Converge.\n21\t- Player-vs-creature target detection idiom: `hasattr(obj, \"life\")` is True only for `engine.player.Player` (established FDN idiom, e.g. fdn_192).\n22\t## Engine: Preparation Card framework (from sos_13)\n23\t- New additive module `engine/preparation.py` implements the \"Prepared\" designation mechanic (CR 722). Public API:\n24\t  - `is_prepared(permanent) -> bool`\n25\t  - `mark_prepared(game, permanent) -> copy|None` — sets designation and creates a copy of the prepare spell in the controller's exile, keyed by `id(permanent)` in lazy per-game registry `game._prepared_copies`; idempotent.\n26\t  - `unprepare(game, permanent)` — clears designation, removes exile copy.\n27\t  - `get_prepared_copy(game, permanent)` / `get_prepared_source(game, copy)`.\n28\t  - `cast_prepared_copy(game, player, copy)` — casts the exiled copy via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`, then (only on cast success, CR 722.3c) clears the source's prepared designation and detaches the registry entry. On cast failure the source stays prepared and the copy stays in exile.\n29\t- Conventions for future Preparation cards:\n30\t  - \"Prepared\" is a DESIGNATION, NOT a `Keyword` enum member. Do NOT add it to `Keyword` — `engine_tests/test_types.py::test_exactly_sixteen_members` hard-asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`. Track via `is_prepared`/`prepared` boolean attrs; store the printed label in `printed_keywords` if needed.\n31\t  - The card exposes its prepare half via `make_prepare_spell()` factory; cost surface via `prepare_mana_cost`/`back_mana_cost`.\n32\t- Card-spec note: when a split/preparation card's `card_spec.json` omits the back-face oracle text, implement the canonical effect implied by the back-face name (sos_13's back half \"Swords to Plowshares\" = \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\"). Logged as a coordinator ruling in RUN_DECISIONS.\n33\t## Engine: delayed one-shot triggers + main-phase event + mana_spent (from sos_57)\n34\t- `engine/events.py`: new `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)` with fields `player` (active player) and `precombat: bool`. Fired from `engine/turn.py` `run_turn` at the start of each main phase (`step is None` at PRECOMBAT_MAIN / POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) — additive `elif`, does not disturb untap/upkeep/draw/combat/cleanup.\n35\t- `engine/triggers.py`:\n36\t  - `TriggerRegistration` gained additive field `one_shot: bool = False` (defaulted — existing call sites unaffected).\n37\t  - `TriggerManager.register_delayed(event_type, effect, source, controller, condition=None) -> TriggerRegistration` registers a one-shot delayed trigger.\n38\t  - `fire_event` removes matched `one_shot` triggers at fire time (using a pre-built match list, no mutation-during-iteration), so a delayed trigger fires EXACTLY ONCE then is removed.\n39\t  - Note: `fire_event` pushes the delayed effect as a `StackObject` rather than executing inline — tests must resolve the stack after firing.\n40\t- `engine/casting.py`: now sets `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (total mana paid after cost reduction) after payment, cleared at the start of each cast alongside `colors_spent`. For \"amount of mana spent\" effects, read `card.mana_spent`, falling back to `mana_cost.cmc` for spells staged directly on the stack (unpaid). Known limitation: equals mana value (no special X/alt-cost handling) — accepted.\n41\t- Use `register_delayed(..., condition=lambda g,e: e.player is controller)` for \"at the beginning of your next main phase\" deferred effects controlled by \"you\".\n42\t## Engine: coin-flip RNG + skip-turn mechanism (from sos_97)\n43\t- Coin flips (`engine/game.py`, all additive):\n44\t  - `get_rng(game) -> random.Random` — lazily attaches/returns `game._rng`.\n45\t  - `seed_rng(game, seed)` — seeds for deterministic flips (tests use this).\n46\t  - `flip_coin(game) -> bool` (True=heads); `flip_coins(game, n) -> int` (number of heads).\n47\t  - Unseeded = fair coin. Test pattern: `seed_rng(game, s); flip_coins(game, 5)` is reproducible.\n48\t- Skip-turn mechanism (additive):\n49\t  - `engine/player.py`: new field `Player.skipped_turns: int = 0`.\n50\t  - `engine/game.py`: `add_skipped_turns(game, player, amount=1)`.\n51\t  - `engine/game_state.py`: rotation factored into `_next_active_index_raw()` (preserves existing `extra_turns` FIFO semantics) + `_pick_next_active_index()` which consumes `skipped_turns` (if the next player would be active and has skipped_turns>0, decrement and pass to the next player; bounded loop). `advance_phase` calls `_pick_next_active_index`.\n52\t  - Defaults to 0 so existing turn/extra-turn tests are unaffected. Extra turns and skips compose.\n53\t- Test pattern for skips: `add_skipped_turns(game, opp, N)` then drive turns via `game.phase=Phase.ENDING; game.step=Step.CLEANUP; game.advance_phase()` and read `game.active_player_index` / `opp.skipped_turns`.\n54\t## Engine: Paradigm framework (from sos_120)\n55\t- New additive module `engine/paradigm.py` (modelled on engine/preparation.py) for the \"Paradigm\" keyword (CR 702.192): \"Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.\"\n56\t- Public API:\n57\t  - `mark_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool` / `has_paradigm_resolved(game, player, name) -> bool` — per-game first-resolution gate, keyed by `(id(player), name)` in lazy `game._paradigm_resolved`. `mark` returns True only on the FIRST resolution.\n58\t  - `register_paradigm(game, source, controller, factory, name)` — marks first resolution and installs (deduped per `(controller, name)` via lazy `game._paradigm_registered`) ONE RECURRING trigger on `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` via `TriggerManager.register` (NOT `register_delayed`, which is one-shot). Condition: `event.player is controller AND event.precombat AND has_paradigm_resolved(...)`.\n59\t  - `offer_paradigm_copy(game, controller, factory, name)` — builds a copy in the controller's exile, asks `choose_yes_no`, casts free via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)` on yes (leaves in exile on decline).\n60\t  - Helpers `is_paradigm_copy(card)`, `is_castable_spell(card)` (lands aren't spells).\n61\t- Card-side: `make_paradigm_copy()` factory (mirrors `make_prepare_spell`); \"Paradigm\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, NOT a Keyword enum member (frozen at 16).\n62\t- Reuse pattern: recurring main-phase effects use `TriggerManager.register` (persistent); one-shot deferred effects use `register_delayed` (sos_57). \"Then exile this spell\" reuses sos_1's `register_stack_to_graveyard_redirect(game, self, \"exile\")`.\n63\t## Engine: Miracle framework + cast_spell ignore_timing (from sos_201)\n64\t- New additive module `engine/miracle.py` implements Miracle (CR 702.94) as a queryable grant + draw-time cast hook (no true layered-effect pipeline in the engine):\n65\t  - Grant surface: `MIRACLE_TWO: ManaCost` ({2}); `is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`; `get_miracle_cost(card)` / `set_miracle_cost(card, cost|None)` / `has_miracle(card)` (read/write a `card.miracle_cost` attribute); `grant_miracle_to_hand(game, source, controller, cost=MIRACLE_TWO)` — continuous static body that writes `miracle_cost` onto every instant/sorcery in the controller's hand, refreshes per call, clears stale grants (lazy per-game registry `game._miracle_grants` keyed by `id(source)`); `clear_miracle_grants(game, source)`.\n66\t  - Draw-time cast hook: `is_first_draw_of_turn(player)` (`player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`); `offer_miracle_cast(game, player, card)`; `register_miracle_draw_hook(game, source, controller, cost_resolver=None)` — deduped per source via `game._miracle_draw_hooks`, registers a `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger gated to the first draw. `draw_card` increments `cards_drawn_this_turn` BEFORE firing the event, so the first draw sees count==1 at trigger time.\n67\t- Card-side: the granting card exposes a `get_miracle_cost(self, game, card) -> ManaCost|None` query (returns the grant only when the source is on the battlefield, `card` is instant/sorcery, and `card` is in the source's controller's hand). Wire `grant_miracle_to_hand` + `register_miracle_draw_hook(..., cost_resolver=self.get_miracle_cost)` in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects`. \"Miracle\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, NOT a Keyword enum member (frozen at 16).\n68\t- Engine: `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` gained an additive `ignore_timing: bool = False` parameter. When True it bypasses the sorcery-speed timing gate (`is_sorcery_speed`/`can_cast_at_instant_speed`) — used ONLY by the miracle draw-cast so a granted SORCERY can be cast at draw time (its own casting window per CR 702.94a, not bound by sorcery-speed). Defaults False so all existing callers are unaffected. Convention: alternative casting windows that grant their own timing permission opt into `ignore_timing=True`; never weaken normal enforcement for ordinary casts. The miracle draw-cast no longer swallows genuine `CastingError`s in a way that hides real failures.\n69\t## Engine: Casualty framework (from sos_226)\n70\t- New additive module `engine/casualty.py` (modelled on `engine/miracle.py`) implements Casualty N (CR 702.153): a queryable grant + an optional-additional-cost sacrifice + copy-on-payment. No engine-symbol renames; `Keyword` stays at 16; \"Casualty\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, never an enum member.\n71\t- Public API:\n72\t  - Grant surface: `CASUALTY_ONE: int = 1`; `is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`; `get_casualty_value(card)` / `set_casualty_value(card, value|None)` / `has_casualty(card)` (read/write a `card.casualty` int attr); `grant_casualty_to_hand(game, source, controller, value=CASUALTY_ONE)` — continuous static body writing `casualty` onto every instant/sorcery in the controller's hand, refreshes per call, clears stale grants (lazy per-game registry `game._casualty_grants` keyed by `id(source)`); `clear_casualty_grants(game, source)`.\n73\t  - Payment (702.153a): `is_legal_casualty_sacrifice(creature, value)` (power boundary: power 0 illegal, power >= N legal); `legal_casualty_sacrifices(game, player, value)`; `pay_casualty(game, player, spell, creature, value=None)` — validates threshold + control, sacrifices via `engine.game.sacrifice` (to graveyard), records `mark_casualty_paid(spell)` → `spell.casualty_paid = True`; `was_casualty_paid(spell)`.\n74\t  - Copy (702.153c): `copy_spell_on_casualty(game, player, spell, new_targets=None)` REUSES the existing `engine.stack.copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` primitive (also used by fdn_248 Thousand-Year Storm) — no new copy primitive added. `offer_casualty(game, player, spell, value=None)` bundles the optional flow (yes/no → choose legal sacrifice → pay → copy with optional new targets). The copy is independent (new targets don't mutate the original).\n75\t- Card-side: expose `get_casualty_value(self, game, spell) -> int|None` (value only when source is on the battlefield, `spell` is instant/sorcery, and spell is the controller's). Wire `grant_casualty_to_hand` in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects`, and register the cast hook as a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger deduped per source in lazy `game._casualty_cast_hooks`, gated to the controller's instants/sorceries. Note: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` exists in `engine/events.py` but `cast_spell` does not fire it — the hook is exercised by firing the event (same as fdn_248's storm trigger).\n76\t## Engine: Affinity + granted-cost-reduction framework (from sos_245)\n77\t- A card's OWN affinity (e.g. \"affinity for creatures\" = {1} less per creature you control) uses the established `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` hook (sos_1/fdn_167 convention): return the raw count; `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` clamps to the spell's generic. \"Affinity\" is a printed label in `printed_keywords`, NOT a `Keyword` enum member (frozen at 16; confirmed `not hasattr(Keyword, \"AFFINITY\")`).\n78\t- New additive module `engine/affinity.py` lets a permanent GRANT a per-spell cost reduction to the controller's spells (mirrors `engine/casualty.py`/`engine/miracle.py`):\n79\t  - Flag surface: `grant_affinity_to_hand(game, source, controller)` writes `affinity_for_creatures = True` onto the controller's hand instants/sorceries (lazy `game._affinity_flags` keyed by `id(source)`); `clear_affinity_flags`. Plus the granting card exposes a query `has_affinity_for_creatures(self, game, spell) -> bool` (True only when source on battlefield, spell is instant/sorcery, spell is the controller's).\n80\t  - Granted-reduction registry: lazy `game._affinity_grants` keyed by `id(source)`, each record `{controller, applies, resolver}`. `register_affinity_grant(game, source, controller, resolver, applies)` / `clear_affinity_grant(game, source)`; `get_granted_reduction(game, spell, controller)` sums contributions of every applicable grant. `applies(game, spell, controller)` MUST gate on source-on-battlefield + controller-only + correct spell types; `resolver(game, spell, controller)` returns the {1}-less count.\n81\t- **Load-bearing engine change**: `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` BODY now adds `engine.affinity.get_granted_reduction(game, card, controller)` to the cast card's own `cost_reduction(game)` BEFORE the existing clamp-to-generic. Signature, clamp, and own-reduction query unchanged. `get_granted_reduction` returns 0 when `game._affinity_grants` is absent/empty, so all prior reductions (sos_1, fdn_167, engine cost-reduction tests) are byte-for-byte unchanged. It swallows resolver/predicate exceptions and ignores non-positive contributions (a buggy grant can never raise during a cast or push generic below 0).\n82\t- Card-side wiring: in `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects`, flag hand spells AND `register_affinity_grant(...)`; clear both when off-battlefield/on leave. Re-registering the same `id(source)` overwrites its record (idempotent — no duplicate stacking). A future granting permanent only needs to register a `(resolver, applies)` pair — no further engine change required.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVTsJVcfWG5ZyTf9wdhLDd","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"6b2ea638-f60f-40cf-b930-72218c02ec5b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:23:59.467Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a5bdbc2dadc390b89","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVTsJVcfWG5ZyTf9wdhLDd","description":"Reading engine/mana.py","subagent_type":"Reviewer","usage":{"total_tokens":42908,"tool_uses":5,"duration_ms":6390},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"68f9ca3b-17bf-467f-b32a-9486869e2d40","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01EnXEfDzkcXj5pookgkcQ5i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KWnVedpXE6P75d4PVfjZms","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/mana.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31801,"cache_read_input_tokens":11090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":31801,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVTsJVcfWG5ZyTf9wdhLDd","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"6ac64b9f-1651-4496-b866-66bd2d09a156","request_id":"req_011CbeGbAhUvPGE8nJ98DeUK","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KWnVedpXE6P75d4PVfjZms","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Mana pool and cost payment logic.\"\"\"\n2\t\n3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n4\t\n5\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n6\tfrom typing import Any\n7\t\n8\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Color, HybridManaSymbol, ManaCost, ManaType\n9\t\n10\t# Map colored ManaTypes to their corresponding Color enum values.\n11\t_MANA_TO_COLOR: dict[ManaType, Color] = {\n12\t    ManaType.WHITE: Color.WHITE,\n13\t    ManaType.BLUE: Color.BLUE,\n14\t    ManaType.BLACK: Color.BLACK,\n15\t    ManaType.RED: Color.RED,\n16\t    ManaType.GREEN: Color.GREEN,\n17\t}\n18\t\n19\t\n20\t#: Restriction tag meaning \"spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery\n21\t#: spell\" (Great Hall of the Biblioplex's any-color mana).\n22\tRESTRICT_INSTANT_SORCERY = \"instant_or_sorcery\"\n23\t\n24\t\n25\t@dataclass\n26\tclass ManaRestriction:\n27\t    \"\"\"An outstanding chunk of restricted mana in a :class:`ManaPool`.\n28\t\n29\t    Attributes:\n30\t        mana_type: The kind of mana produced (e.g. the chosen color).\n31\t        amount: How many mana of this chunk remain unspent.\n32\t        restriction: A tag describing what the mana may be spent on.  The\n33\t            only built-in tag is :data:`RESTRICT_INSTANT_SORCERY` (\"spend\n34\t            this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\").  An\n35\t            unrecognised tag is treated conservatively (no spell qualifies),\n36\t            so a future restriction never silently behaves as unrestricted.\n37\t        source: Optional back-reference to the permanent/ability that\n38\t            produced the restricted mana (advisory only).\n39\t    \"\"\"\n40\t\n41\t    mana_type: ManaType\n42\t    amount: int\n43\t    restriction: str\n44\t    source: Any = None\n45\t\n46\t    def allows_spell(self, spell: Any) -> bool:\n47\t        \"\"\"Return ``True`` if this restricted mana may pay for *spell*.\n48\t\n49\t        Only the instant/sorcery restriction is understood; any other tag\n50\t        is treated as \"no spell qualifies\" so the restriction is never\n51\t        accidentally bypassed.\n52\t        \"\"\"\n53\t        if self.restriction == RESTRICT_INSTANT_SORCERY:\n54\t            card_types = getattr(spell, \"card_types\", set())\n55\t            return CardType.INSTANT in card_types or CardType.SORCERY in card_types\n56\t        return False\n57\t\n58\t\n59\tclass ManaPool:\n60\t    \"\"\"Tracks available mana for a player.\n61\t\n62\t    Internal storage uses a ``dict[ManaType, int]`` mapping each mana type\n63\t    to its current count.\n64\t\n65\t    Restricted mana\n66\t    ---------------\n67\t    Some effects produce mana that may only be spent in a limited way\n68\t    (e.g. Great Hall of the Biblioplex: \"Spend this mana only to cast an\n69\t    instant or sorcery spell\").  The base pool has no notion of a spend\n70\t    restriction; to support such mana *additively* (without changing the\n71\t    flat ``dict[ManaType, int]`` model or any existing payment behaviour),\n72\t    the pool carries a small parallel record:\n73\t\n74\t    * :attr:`restrictions` — a list of :class:`ManaRestriction` records, one\n75\t      per outstanding chunk of restricted mana that has not yet been spent.\n76\t\n77\t    Unrestricted mana is never recorded here, so when no effect produces\n78\t    restricted mana the list stays empty and every existing operation\n79\t    (:meth:`add`, :meth:`pay`, :meth:`can_pay`, :meth:`empty`, ...) behaves\n80\t    byte-for-byte as before.  The restriction record is purely advisory at\n81\t    the pool level — enforcement lives in :func:`engine.casting.cast_spell`,\n82\t    which consults :meth:`restricted_amount` / :meth:`spendable_for_spell`\n83\t    so restricted mana can pay a permitted spell but is rejected for a\n84\t    disallowed one.\n85\t    \"\"\"\n86\t\n87\t    def __init__(self) -> None:\n88\t        self._pool: dict[ManaType, int] = {mt: 0 for mt in ManaType}\n89\t        self._last_payment_colors: list[Color] = []\n90\t        # Parallel record of outstanding restricted-mana chunks.  Empty for\n91\t        # ordinary mana, so all existing behaviour is unchanged by default.\n92\t        self.restrictions: list[ManaRestriction] = []\n93\t\n94\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n95\t    # Basic operations\n96\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n97\t\n98\t    def add(self, mana_type: ManaType, amount: int = 1) -> None:\n99\t        \"\"\"Add *amount* mana of the given type to the pool.\n100\t\n101\t        Parameters:\n102\t            mana_type: The type of mana to add.\n103\t            amount: How many mana to add (must be non-negative).\n104\t        \"\"\"\n105\t        if amount < 0:\n106\t            raise ValueError(f\"Cannot add negative mana: {amount}\")\n107\t        self._pool[mana_type] = self._pool.get(mana_type, 0) + amount\n108\t\n109\t    def add_restricted(\n110\t        self,\n111\t        mana_type: ManaType,\n112\t        amount: int = 1,\n113\t        restriction: str = RESTRICT_INSTANT_SORCERY,\n114\t        source: Any = None,\n115\t    ) -> None:\n116\t        \"\"\"Add *amount* mana of *mana_type* tagged with a spend *restriction*.\n117\t\n118\t        The mana lands in the flat pool exactly like ordinary mana (so it is\n119\t        countable via :meth:`get` / :meth:`total` and payable by the unchanged\n120\t        :meth:`pay`), and a parallel :class:`ManaRestriction` record is kept in\n121\t        :attr:`restrictions` so the casting pipeline can tell that this much of\n122\t        the pool may only be spent on a permitted spell.\n123\t\n124\t        Use this instead of :meth:`add` when an effect produces mana with a\n125\t        spend restriction (e.g. \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or\n126\t        sorcery spell\").  Producing ordinary mana via :meth:`add` records no\n127\t        restriction, leaving existing behaviour unchanged.\n128\t        \"\"\"\n129\t        self.add(mana_type, amount)\n130\t        if amount > 0:\n131\t            self.restrictions.append(\n132\t                ManaRestriction(\n133\t                    mana_type=mana_type,\n134\t                    amount=amount,\n135\t                    restriction=restriction,\n136\t                    source=source,\n137\t                )\n138\t            )\n139\t\n140\t    def empty(self) -> None:\n141\t        \"\"\"Clear the pool — happens at phase/step transitions.\"\"\"\n142\t        for mt in self._pool:\n143\t            self._pool[mt] = 0\n144\t        # Restricted mana empties with the rest of the pool.\n145\t        self.restrictions = []\n146\t\n147\t    def total(self) -> int:\n148\t        \"\"\"Return the total amount of mana in the pool across all types.\"\"\"\n149\t        return sum(self._pool.values())\n150\t\n151\t    def get(self, mana_type: ManaType) -> int:\n152\t        \"\"\"Return the amount of a specific mana type in the pool.\"\"\"\n153\t        return self._pool.get(mana_type, 0)\n154\t\n155\t    @property\n156\t    def last_payment_colors(self) -> list[Color]:\n157\t        \"\"\"Return the distinct colors of mana spent in the last :meth:`pay` call.\n158\t\n159\t        Colorless mana is not a color and is excluded.  The list is sorted\n160\t        by Color enum order for determinism.  Empty if no payment has been\n161\t        made or if all mana spent was colorless.\n162\t        \"\"\"\n163\t        return list(self._last_payment_colors)\n164\t\n165\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n166\t    # Restricted-mana queries / bookkeeping\n167\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n168\t\n169\t    def has_restricted_mana(self) -> bool:\n170\t        \"\"\"Return ``True`` if the pool holds any outstanding restricted mana.\"\"\"\n171\t        return any(r.amount > 0 for r in self.restrictions)\n172\t\n173\t    def restricted_amount(self) -> int:\n174\t        \"\"\"Return the total amount of currently-restricted mana in the pool.\"\"\"\n175\t        return sum(r.amount for r in self.restrictions if r.amount > 0)\n176\t\n177\t    def spendable_for_spell(self, spell: Any) -> int:\n178\t        \"\"\"Return how much of the pool may legally help pay for *spell*.\n179\t\n180\t        Restricted mana that does not permit *spell* is excluded; all\n181\t        unrestricted mana (the pool total minus the restricted portion) plus\n182\t        any restricted mana whose restriction permits *spell* is included.\n183\t        With no restricted mana present this is simply :meth:`total`.\n184\t        \"\"\"\n185\t        forbidden = sum(\n186\t            r.amount\n187\t            for r in self.restrictions\n188\t            if r.amount > 0 and not r.allows_spell(spell)\n189\t        )\n190\t        return self.total() - forbidden\n191\t\n192\t    def can_pay_for_spell(self, cost: ManaCost, spell: Any) -> bool:\n193\t        \"\"\"Like :meth:`can_pay`, but honouring restricted-mana spend rules.\n194\t\n195\t        Returns ``True`` only if the cost can be paid *and* no restricted mana\n196\t        that disallows *spell* is forced into the payment.  When the pool holds\n197\t        no restricted mana this delegates straight to :meth:`can_pay`, so\n198\t        ordinary casts are entirely unaffected.\n199\t        \"\"\"\n200\t        if not self.has_restricted_mana():\n201\t            return self.can_pay(cost)\n202\t        if not self.can_pay(cost):\n203\t            return False\n204\t        # The spell's total cost cannot exceed the mana that may legally pay it.\n205\t        needed = cost.generic + sum(cost.pips.values()) + len(cost.hybrid)\n206\t        return self.spendable_for_spell(spell) >= needed\n207\t\n208\t    def _consume_restrictions_for_payment(self, paid: dict[ManaType, int]) -> None:\n209\t        \"\"\"Decrement restriction records to mirror a committed *paid* deduction.\n210\t\n211\t        *paid* maps each :class:`ManaType` to how many of it the payment spent.\n212\t        Restricted records of the matching type are drawn down first so the\n213\t        outstanding restricted amount never overstates what remains in the pool.\n214\t        Records that reach zero are dropped.\n215\t        \"\"\"\n216\t        for mana_type, spent in paid.items():\n217\t            remaining = spent\n218\t            for record in self.restrictions:\n219\t                if remaining <= 0:\n220\t                    break\n221\t                if record.mana_type is not mana_type or record.amount <= 0:\n222\t                    continue\n223\t                take = min(record.amount, remaining)\n224\t                record.amount -= take\n225\t                remaining -= take\n226\t        self.restrictions = [r for r in self.restrictions if r.amount > 0]\n227\t\n228\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n229\t    # Cost payment\n230\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n231\t\n232\t    def can_pay(self, cost: ManaCost) -> bool:\n233\t        \"\"\"Check whether the pool can satisfy *cost*.\n234\t\n235\t        Generic mana can be paid by any type.  X is treated as 0 for\n236\t        ``can_pay`` unless explicitly set in the cost's generic component.\n237\t        Hybrid symbols can be paid with either option; this method uses\n238\t        backtracking to find a valid assignment.\n239\t\n240\t        Returns:\n241\t            True if the pool has enough mana to pay the cost.\n242\t        \"\"\"\n243\t        remaining: dict[ManaType, int] = dict(self._pool)\n244\t\n245\t        # Pay colored/colorless pips first.\n246\t        for mana_type, count in cost.pips.items():\n247\t            if remaining.get(mana_type, 0) < count:\n248\t                return False\n249\t            remaining[mana_type] = remaining.get(mana_type, 0) - count\n250\t\n251\t        # Solve hybrid symbols with backtracking.\n252\t        if cost.hybrid:\n253\t            if not self._can_pay_hybrid(remaining, list(cost.hybrid), 0, cost.generic):\n254\t                return False\n255\t            return True\n256\t\n257\t        # Then check generic — sum of all remaining mana must cover it.\n258\t        return sum(remaining.values()) >= cost.generic\n259\t\n260\t    def pay(self, cost: ManaCost, choices: dict[ManaType, int] | None = None) -> bool:\n261\t        \"\"\"Deduct mana from the pool to pay *cost*.\n262\t\n263\t        Parameters:\n264\t            cost: The mana cost to pay.\n265\t            choices: How to split the generic portion across mana types.\n266\t                If ``None``, auto-pay greedily: pay colored pips first,\n267\t                then hybrid symbols, then generic using colorless first,\n268\t                then excess colored.\n269\t\n270\t        Returns:\n271\t            True if payment succeeded, False if the pool has insufficient mana.\n272\t        \"\"\"\n273\t        if not self.can_pay(cost):\n274\t            return False\n275\t\n276\t        # Work on a copy so we can roll back on failure.\n277\t        working: dict[ManaType, int] = dict(self._pool)\n278\t\n279\t        # 1. Pay colored/colorless pips.\n280\t        for mana_type, count in cost.pips.items():\n281\t            working[mana_type] -= count\n282\t\n283\t        # 2. When explicit generic choices are provided, reserve that mana\n284\t        #    *before* solving hybrids so the solver doesn't steal it.\n285\t        generic_remaining = cost.generic\n286\t        if generic_remaining > 0 and choices is not None:\n287\t            # Reject negative choice amounts — they would create mana.\n288\t            if any(v < 0 for v in choices.values()):\n289\t                return False\n290\t            # Validate choices sum to generic cost.\n291\t            if sum(choices.values()) != generic_remaining:\n292\t                return False\n293\t            for mana_type, amount in choices.items():\n294\t                if working.get(mana_type, 0) < amount:\n295\t                    return False\n296\t                working[mana_type] -= amount\n297\t\n298\t        # 3. Pay hybrid symbols using backtracking to find a valid assignment.\n299\t        #    Generic choices (if any) have already been reserved above,\n300\t        #    so _solve_hybrid sees only the genuinely available mana.\n301\t        if cost.hybrid:\n302\t            generic_for_solver = generic_remaining if choices is None else 0\n303\t            hybrid_assignment = self._solve_hybrid(\n304\t                working, list(cost.hybrid), 0, generic_for_solver,\n305\t            )\n306\t            if hybrid_assignment is None:\n307\t                return False  # pragma: no cover – should not happen after can_pay\n308\t            for mt in hybrid_assignment:\n309\t                working[mt] = working.get(mt, 0) - 1\n310\t\n311\t        # 4. Pay generic cost (auto-pay path — choices already deducted above).\n312\t        if generic_remaining > 0 and choices is None:\n313\t            generic_remaining = self._auto_pay_generic(working, generic_remaining)\n314\t            if generic_remaining > 0:\n315\t                return False  # pragma: no cover – should not happen after can_pay\n316\t\n317\t        # Commit the payment.\n318\t        # Compute colors of mana spent by comparing old pool to new working pool.\n319\t        colors_spent: set[Color] = set()\n320\t        spent_by_type: dict[ManaType, int] = {}\n321\t        for mt, old_amount in self._pool.items():\n322\t            new_amount = working.get(mt, 0)\n323\t            if new_amount < old_amount:\n324\t                spent_by_type[mt] = old_amount - new_amount\n325\t                if mt in _MANA_TO_COLOR:\n326\t                    colors_spent.add(_MANA_TO_COLOR[mt])\n327\t        self._last_payment_colors = sorted(colors_spent, key=lambda c: c.value)\n328\t        self._pool = working\n329\t        # Keep restriction bookkeeping in sync with the deduction.  Skipped\n330\t        # entirely when no restricted mana is outstanding, so ordinary payments\n331\t        # are byte-for-byte unchanged.\n332\t        if self.restrictions and spent_by_type:\n333\t            self._consume_restrictions_for_payment(spent_by_type)\n334\t        return True\n335\t\n336\t    @staticmethod\n337\t    def _can_pay_hybrid(\n338\t        remaining: dict[ManaType, int],\n339\t        hybrids: list[HybridManaSymbol],\n340\t        idx: int,\n341\t        generic: int,\n342\t    ) -> bool:\n343\t        \"\"\"Recursively check if hybrid symbols + generic can be satisfied.\n344\t\n345\t        Uses backtracking: for each hybrid symbol, try option_a then option_b.\n346\t        After all hybrids are assigned, check that remaining mana covers generic.\n347\t        \"\"\"\n348\t        if idx >= len(hybrids):\n349\t            return sum(remaining.values()) >= generic\n350\t\n351\t        sym = hybrids[idx]\n352\t        for option in (sym.option_a, sym.option_b):\n353\t            if remaining.get(option, 0) > 0:\n354\t                remaining[option] -= 1\n355\t                if ManaPool._can_pay_hybrid(remaining, hybrids, idx + 1, generic):\n356\t                    remaining[option] += 1\n357\t                    return True\n358\t                remaining[option] += 1\n359\t        return False\n360\t\n361\t    @staticmethod\n362\t    def _solve_hybrid(\n363\t        remaining: dict[ManaType, int],\n364\t        hybrids: list[HybridManaSymbol],\n365\t        idx: int,\n366\t        generic: int,\n367\t    ) -> list[ManaType] | None:\n368\t        \"\"\"Find a valid assignment for hybrid symbols.\n369\t\n370\t        Returns a list of ManaType choices (one per hybrid symbol) or None\n371\t        if no valid assignment exists.\n372\t        \"\"\"\n373\t        if idx >= len(hybrids):\n374\t            if sum(remaining.values()) >= generic:\n375\t                return []\n376\t            return None\n377\t\n378\t        sym = hybrids[idx]\n379\t        for option in (sym.option_a, sym.option_b):\n380\t            if remaining.get(option, 0) > 0:\n381\t                remaining[option] -= 1\n382\t                result = ManaPool._solve_hybrid(remaining, hybrids, idx + 1, generic)\n383\t                if result is not None:\n384\t                    remaining[option] += 1\n385\t                    return [option] + result\n386\t                remaining[option] += 1\n387\t        return None\n388\t\n389\t    @staticmethod\n390\t    def _auto_pay_generic(working: dict[ManaType, int], amount: int) -> int:\n391\t        \"\"\"Deduct *amount* generic mana from *working*, preferring colorless.\n392\t\n393\t        Returns the remaining unpaid generic amount (0 on success).\n394\t        \"\"\"\n395\t        # Pay with colorless first.\n396\t        if working.get(ManaType.COLORLESS, 0) > 0:\n397\t            take = min(working[ManaType.COLORLESS], amount)\n398\t            working[ManaType.COLORLESS] -= take\n399\t            amount -= take\n400\t\n401\t        # Then pay with each colored type in enum order.\n402\t        for mt in ManaType:\n403\t            if mt is ManaType.COLORLESS:\n404\t                continue\n405\t            if amount <= 0:\n406\t                break\n407\t            if working.get(mt, 0) > 0:\n408\t                take = min(working[mt], amount)\n409\t                working[mt] -= take\n410\t                amount -= take\n411\t\n412\t        return amount\n413\t\n414\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n415\t    # Dunder helpers\n416\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n417\t\n418\t    def __repr__(self) -> str:\n419\t        non_zero = {mt.name: v for mt, v in self._pool.items() if v > 0}\n420\t        return f\"ManaPool({non_zero})\"\n421\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVTsJVcfWG5ZyTf9wdhLDd","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"c8ab3b98-be84-48e5-a57b-e81b3d02b3d8","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:24:02.424Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
