{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DVTsJVcfWG5ZyTf9wdhLDd","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. I verified the diff against the actual engine signatures (`ContinuousEffect` from `engine.continuous_effects`, `TriggerRegistration`, `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, `ManaCost`, `Land`/`ManaAbility`/`ActivatedAbility`, `effect_manager`/`trigger_manager` accessors) and traced the restricted-mana payment paths.\n\nKey findings:\n\n- The additive-only discipline holds: no engine symbol renamed/moved/deleted, `engine/animation.py` is new, the `cast_spell` change is a single call-site swap that delegates to legacy `can_pay` when no restricted mana is present, and the default-unrestricted fast path keeps all other cards byte-for-byte unchanged. Statics, animation (CREATURE+LAND retained, 2/4 Wizard, re-animation guard), and the deduped controller-gated pump trigger all match spec intent.\n- One genuine correctness bug (`strict`) in new engine code: `ManaPool.can_pay_for_spell` only does a count-based spendability check and does not enforce colored-pip legality, allowing this card's any-color restricted mana to illegally pay a colored pip for a disallowed (e.g. creature) spell under a specific pool composition. Currently unexercised by the arbitrated tests, but a real spend-restriction bypass.\n- One `advisory`: `deanimate_land` leaks its `_animation_pump_triggers` entry, breaking re-animation of the same object (dormant for this card, which never calls deanimate).\n\nI did not flag the `_resolve_controller` indirection, direct-pool mutation, null P/T-while-unanimated properties, or the FIFO restriction consumption — those conform to engine conventions (`basic_lands.py`, KEY_DECISIONS man-land/grant patterns) and are intent-correct.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 1\nadvisory_count: 1\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a5bdbc2dadc390b89 (use SendMessage with 