nforcement in cast_spell. VERIFY: restricted mana can pay for instants/sorceries but is rejected for creatures; AND — critically — when NO restricted mana is present, ManaPool and cast_spell behave EXACTLY as before (default unrestricted, no behavior change for all other cards). Look for: payment ordering bugs (does restricted mana get preferred/avoided correctly?), rollback correctness on a failed cast, and any path where ordinary mana could accidentally be treated as restricted.\n- ANIMATION: {5} adds CardType.CREATURE while RETAINING CardType.LAND, grants Subtype.WIZARD, 2/4 body observable via card.power/toughness after apply_all; the \"if this land isn't a creature\" guard prevents re-animation/stacking; durable until leaves play.\n- GRANTED PUMP TRIGGER: registered at {5}-resolution (deduped per source, lazy registry), gated to the CONTROLLER's own instant/sorcery casts, adds +1/+0 with DURATION_END_OF_TURN, resets at cleanup; opponent/creature casts don't pump.\n- Additive-only discipline: no rename/move/delete of existing engine symbols; `Keyword` stays at 16; lazy per-game registries (no GameState.__init__ change).\n\nConstraints:\n- Do NOT demand test rewrites — tests were already arbitrated. Test-quality concerns are `advisory` only.\n- Do NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards or conventions in KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n\nWrite `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json` as a JSON array of `{\"severity\": \"strict\"|\"advisory\", \"file\", \"line\", \"comment\"}`. Empty `[]` if no comments. Reserve `strict` for genuine correctness/regression bugs.\n\nReturn:\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json","agentId":"a5bdbc2dadc390b89","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. I verified the diff against the actual engine signatures (`ContinuousEffect` from `engine.continuous_effects`, `TriggerRegistration`, `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, `ManaCost`, `Land`/`ManaAbility`/`ActivatedAbility`, `effect_manager`/`trigger_manager` accessors) and traced the restricted-mana payment paths.\n\nKey findings:\n\n- The additive-only discipline holds: no engine symbol renamed/moved/deleted, `engine/animation.py` is new, the `cast_spell` change is a single call-site swap that delegates to legacy `can_pay` when no restricted mana is present, and the default-unrestricted fast path keeps all other cards byte-for-byte unchanged. Statics, animation (CREATURE+LAND retained, 2/4 Wizard, re-animation guard), and the deduped controller-gated pump trigger all match spec intent.\n- One genuine correctness bug (`strict`) in new engine code: `ManaPool.can_pay_for_spell` only does a count-based spendability check and does not enforce colored-pip legality, allowing this card's any-color restricted mana to illegally pay a colored pip for a disallowed (e.g. creature) spell under a specific pool composition. Currently unexercised by the arbitrated tests, but a real spend-restriction bypass.\n- One `advisory`: `deanimate_land` leaks its `_animation_pump_triggers` entry, breaking re-animation of the same object (dormant for this card, which never calls deanimate).\n\nI did not flag the `_resolve_controller` indirection, direct-pool mutation, null P/T-while-unanimated properties, or the FIFO restriction consumption — those conform to engine conventions (`basic_lands.py`, KEY_DECISIONS man-land/grant patterns) and are intent-correct.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 1\nadvisory_count: 1\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json"}],"totalDurationMs":135943,"totalTokens":79974,"totalToolUseCount":19,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1789,"cache_read_input_tokens":77500,"output_tokens":683,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1789},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_token