{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M1a17HxGn9b17MxHXQ21Nh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"engine/mana.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 192,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"can_pay_for_spell only does a COUNT check (spendable_for_spell(spell) >= cmc), which does not verify that the legally-spendable (non-forbidden) mana can satisfy the spell's COLORED PIPS. Exploit reachable via this card's any-color restricted mana: pool = 1 restricted BLUE (instant/sorcery only) + 3 unrestricted COLORLESS, cast a CREATURE costing {U}. can_pay({U}) is True (blue pip met by the blue), needed=1, spendable_for_spell(creature)=total(4)-forbidden(1)=3 >= 1 -> returns True. The cast is then allowed and pay() is forced to spend the restricted blue on the {U} pip — a spend-restriction bypass for a disallowed (creature) spell. The existing tests don't catch this because they only test pools where the restricted mana is the ONLY mana of the needed type with no surplus. To be correct, the spendability check must exclude forbidden mana from the per-pip/backtracking solve (e.g. compute can_pay over a pool with the forbidden restricted mana removed), not just compare totals.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"engine/animation.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 188,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"deanimate_land() unregisters triggers and pops the _land_animations record but does NOT remove id(land) from the _animation_pump_triggers dedup set. If a land is deanimated (the documented \\\"until it leaves play\\\" cleanup) and later re-animated as the same Python object, register_instant_sorcery_pump returns None and silently fails to re-grant the pump trigger. Harmless for sos_257 as shipped (the card never calls deanimate_land and never re-animates within a game), but the framework's own leave-play/re-enter contract is broken — clear the pump-registry entry in deanimate_land for symmetry.\"\n13\t  }\n14\t]\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"7954125b-d7b6-4441-83f5-2d2025d8002a","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:26:15.991Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"engine/mana.py\",\n    \"line\": 192,\n    \"comment\": \"can_pay_for_spell only does a COUNT check (spendable_for_spell(spell) >= cmc), which does not verify that the legally-spendable (non-forbidden) mana can satisfy the spell's COLORED PIPS. Exploit reachable via this card's any-color restricted mana: pool = 1 restricted BLUE (instant/sorcery only) + 3 unrestricted COLORLESS, cast a CREATURE costing {U}. can_pay({U}) is True (blue pip met by the blue), needed=1, spendable_for_spell(creature)=total(4)-forbidden(1)=3 >= 1 -> returns True. The cast is then allowed and pay() is forced to spend the restricted blue on the {U} pip — a spend-restriction bypass for a disallowed (creature) spell. The existing tests don't catch this because they only test pools where the restricted mana is the ONLY mana of the needed type with no surplus. To be correct, the spendability check must exclude forbidden mana from the per-pip/backtracking solve (e.g. compute can_pay over a pool with the forbidden restricted mana removed), not just compare totals.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"engine/animation.py\",\n    \"line\": 188,\n    \"comment\": \"deanimate_land() unregisters triggers and pops the _land_animations record but does NOT remove id(land) from the _animation_pump_triggers dedup set. If a land is deanimated (the documented \\\"until it leaves play\\\" cleanup) and later re-animated as the same Python object, register_instant_sorcery_pump returns None and silently fails to re-grant the pump trigger. Harmless for sos_257 as shipped (the card never calls deanimate_land and never re-animates within a game), but the framework's own leave-play/re-enter contract is broken — clear the pump-registry entry in deanimate_land for symmetry.\"\n  }\n]\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}}}
