{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CEC9yRFvx7pmVEn3WnEG7u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019WKdPJ7AhbwAo5ff5Hkzdm","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Revise sos_257 restricted-mana fix","subagent_type":"Implementer","prompt":"Revision round for card sos_257 \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\". The Reviewer found ONE strict correctness bug in the restricted-mana code you wrote. Fix it. (Plus one optional advisory.)\n\nRead first:\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json` — the review comments. There is 1 strict and 1 advisory.\n- Your prior diff `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl.diff` and rationale `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-rationale.md`.\n- `engine/mana.py` (the `can_pay_for_spell` / `spendable_for_spell` / `pay` methods you added) and `engine/casting.py` (the cast_spell payment path) and `engine/animation.py`.\n- `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` — the 46 tests. You MUST NOT modify any test file.\n\nSTRICT bug to fix (review.json index 0, engine/mana.py ~line 192):\n`can_pay_for_spell` only does a COUNT check (`spendable_for_spell(spell) >= cmc`), which does NOT verify that the legally-spendable (non-forbidden) mana can satisfy the spell's COLORED PIPS. Exploit: pool = 1 restricted BLUE (instant/sorcery only) + 3 unrestricted COLORLESS; casting a CREATURE costing {U} wrongly returns payable because the count check passes and the blue pip is \"met\" by the restricted blue — forcing the restricted blue to illegally pay a creature's colored pip. FIX: the spendability check for a given spell must run the real per-pip / backtracking `can_pay` solve over a pool with the FORBIDDEN restricted mana REMOVED (i.e. only the mana legally spendable on this spell), not a totals comparison. After the fix: restricted any-color mana must be rejected for a creature even when surplus unrestricted mana of other types exists; instants/sorceries still pay fine; and — critically — when NO restricted mana is present, behavior is byte-for-byte unchanged (the default fast path must still delegate to the legacy `can_pay`).\n\nADVISORY (review.json index 1, engine/animation.py ~line 188) — OPTIONAL but preferred since it's a cheap correctness fix to the framework's own leave-play contract: `deanimate_land()` does not remove `id(land)` from the `_animation_pump_triggers` dedup set, so a deanimated-then-reanimated same object silently fails to re-grant the pump trigger. Clear that registry entry in `deanimate_land` for symmetry. If you apply it, confirm no test regresses; if you choose not to, record it in disagreements.json with justification.\n\nConstraints:\n- ADDITIVE only; never rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; `Keyword` stays at 16; do NOT modify any test file.\n- All 46 sos_257 tests must still pass, AND the fix must not regress the full suite.\n\nVerification:\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → all 46 pass.\n- `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (report totals); explicitly confirm engine mana/casting tests + fdn_267 pass.\n\nOutputs:\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised.diff` — full git diff after the fix (NOT test files).\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised-rationale.md` — what you changed and why the colored-pip solve is now correct + the no-restricted-mana fast path unchanged.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/disagreements.json` — JSON array of `{review_comment_index, reviewer_comment, implementer_justification}` for any strict comment you do NOT fully apply (empty `[]` if you applied everything).\n- Update `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-files.txt` and upsert the sos_257 entry in `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n\nReturn:\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: <N>\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/disagreements.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cac