{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01BuTbvm5LmrrASxk8Uben28","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0136UVgDiR4Vh2hUv1qJkV3q","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revision rationale — sos_257 \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"\n\nAddresses the Reviewer's findings in `review.json`: one strict correctness bug\nin the restricted-mana payability check (`engine/mana.py`), plus the optional\nadvisory in `engine/animation.py`. Both applied. No test files modified.\n\n## STRICT (review index 0) — colored-pip solve over the filtered pool\n\n### The bug\n`can_pay_for_spell` previously verified restricted-mana legality with a *count*\ncomparison only:\n\n```python\nneeded = cost.generic + sum(cost.pips.values()) + len(cost.hybrid)\nreturn self.spendable_for_spell(spell) >= needed   # totals only\n```\n\nA totals check cannot see *which* mana satisfies *which* colored pip. Exploit:\npool = 1 restricted BLUE (instant/sorcery only) + 3 unrestricted COLORLESS, cast\na CREATURE costing `{U}`. `can_pay({U})` is True (the blue pip is met by the\nblue), `needed == 1`, and `spendable_for_spell(creature) == total(4) -\nforbidden(1) == 3 >= 1`, so the old check returned True. The cast was then\nallowed and `pay()` was forced to spend the restricted blue on the creature's\n`{U}` pip — a spend-restriction bypass for a disallowed spell type.\n\n### The fix\nThe spendability check now runs the *real* per-pip / hybrid / generic\nbacktracking solve over a pool from which the FORBIDDEN restricted mana has been\nremoved **per mana type**, not a totals comparison:\n\n- New `_spendable_pool_for_spell(spell)` returns a copy of the flat `_pool` with\n  each `ManaRestriction` that does NOT permit `spell` subtracted from its own\n  mana type (`max(0, current - amount)`). Restricted mana that *does* permit the\n  spell stays in place and spends like ordinary mana of its type.\n- `can_pay_for_spell` now does:\n  ```python\n  if not self.has_restricted_mana():\n      return self.can_pay(cost)          # fast path — unchanged\n  spendable = self._spendable_pool_for_spell(spell)\n  return self._can_pay_pool(spendable, cost)\n  ```\n\n`_can_pay_pool(remaining, cost)` is a new **static** helper extracted verbatim\nfrom the body of `can_pay`: it pays the colored/colorless pips, backtracks over\nhybrids, then checks generic against the sum of what's left. `can_pay` itself now\ndelegates to `_can_pay_pool(dict(self._pool), cost)`, so `can_pay` is\nbehaviourally identical to before (same solver, same copy-of-pool semantics).\nBecause `can_pay_for_spell` runs that *same* solver, the colored `{U}` pip on the\ncreature can only be satisfied by mana that legally remains after the forbidden\nblue is removed — i.e. it now correctly fails (the 3 colorless cannot pay a\ncolored pip), while it still passes for an instant/sorcery (the blue is kept) and\nstill passes for a generic `{1}` creature cost (paid by the colorless).\n\n### Why the no-restricted-mana fast path is byte-for-byte unchanged\nWhen `has_restricted_mana()` is False (every default pool, all ordinary play),\n`can_pay_for_spell` returns `self.can_pay(cost)` exactly as before. `can_pay`'s\nexternally observable result is unchanged by the extraction (it forwards a copy\nof the real pool into the identical solve that previously lived inline). Verified\ndirectly: across a sample of costs (`{G}`, `{1}{G}`, `{2}`, `{G}{G}`, `{C}`)\n`can_pay_for_spell == can_pay` for a pool with no restrictions.\n\n## ADVISORY (review index 1) — applied\n\n`deanimate_land` now calls `_pump_trigger_registry(game).discard(id(land))` so\nthe per-source pump-trigger dedup set is cleared on leave-play. Without it, a\ndeanimated-then-reanimated *same Python object* would hit\n`register_instant_sorcery_pump`'s `id(land) in registry` guard and silently fail\nto re-grant the pump trigger. `_pump_trigger_registry` is a module-level function\nresolved at call time, so referencing it from the earlier-defined\n`deanimate_land` is fine. Harmless for sos_257 as shipped (the card never\ndeanimates), but restores the framework's leave-play / re-enter symmetry. No test\nregressed.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → **46 passed**.\n- Engine mana/casting/cast tests (`engine_tests -k \"mana or casting or cast\"`) →\n  **335 passed**.\n- fdn_267 has no `tests.py` (reference card; only `card_impl.py`); it imports\n  cleanly under the full run.\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → **1517 passed**, 0 failed (no regressions).\n- Direct exploit check: creature `{U}` with `[restricted BLUE + 3 COLORLESS]`\n  now returns False; instant `{U}` returns True; creature `{1}` returns True.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nAdditive only — no engine symbol renamed/moved/deleted; `_can_pay_pool` and\n`_spendable_pool_for_spell` are new helpers, `can_pay`'s signature is unchanged.\n`Keyword` enum untouched. No test file modified.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":64573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":547,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019WKdPJ7AhbwAo5ff5Hkzdm","session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"5dbd38fb-e565-43b1-b8c4-dec655cdaa7f","request_id":"req_011CbeGuUoAJF1Pv1fpstNWQ","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_257 restricted-mana fix"}
