{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019WKdPJ7AhbwAo5ff5Hkzdm","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clean. The only changes are the 4 implementation files plus `FILES_MODIFIED.json` (and the pre-existing `run_manifest.json` / untracked `tests.py` which I did not touch).\n\nAll work is complete and verified.\n\nSummary of what changed:\n\nSTRICT fix (`engine/mana.py`): Replaced the count-only legality check in `can_pay_for_spell` with the real backtracking solve over a filtered pool. Added `_spendable_pool_for_spell(spell)` (copies `_pool` and subtracts forbidden restricted mana per mana type) and extracted the shared solver `_can_pay_pool(remaining, cost)` from `can_pay`. `can_pay` now delegates to `_can_pay_pool(dict(self._pool), cost)` (behaviorally identical), and `can_pay_for_spell` runs the same solver over the filtered pool when restricted mana is present, otherwise delegates straight to `can_pay`. This makes a forbidden restricted colored mana unable to satisfy a disallowed spell's colored pip. Verified: creature `{U}` with `[restricted BLUE + 3 COLORLESS]` now returns False; instant `{U}` True; creature `{1}` True; no-restricted fast path matches `can_pay` exactly.\n\nADVISORY fix (`engine/animation.py`): `deanimate_land` now calls `_pump_trigger_registry(game).discard(id(land))` so a deanimated-then-reanimated same object can re-grant its pump trigger. No test regressed; `disagreements.json` is `[]`.\n\nVerification: `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` -> 46 passed; engine mana/casting tests -> 335 passed; full `pytest` -> 1517 passed, 0 failed (no regressions). fdn_267 has no `tests.py` (reference card; `card_impl.py` only) and imports cleanly under the full run.\n\nRelevant file paths (all absolute):\n- /workspace/engine/mana.py\n- /workspace/engine/animation.py\n- /workspace/engine/casting.py\n- /workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\n- /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised.diff\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised-rationale.md\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/disagreements.json\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-files.txt\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/disagreements.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a7a6a048416c6587c (use SendMessage with to: 'a7a6a048416c6587c' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 77656\ntool_uses: 27\nduration_ms: 178586</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"a56716ec-6e3c-4d93-96c3-1705e03c2d00","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:29:35.182Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Revision round for card sos_257 \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\". The Reviewer found ONE strict correctness bug in the restricted-mana code you wrote. Fix it. (Plus one optional advisory.)\n\nRead first:\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json` — the review comments. There is 1 strict and 1 advisory.\n- Your prior diff `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl.diff` and rationale `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-rationale.md`.\n- `engine/mana.py` (the `can_pay_for_spell` / `spendable_for_spell` / `pay` methods you added) and `engine/casting.py` (the cast_spell payment path) and `engine/animation.py`.\n- `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` — the 46 tests. You MUST NOT modify any test file.\n\nSTRICT bug to fix (review.json index 0, engine/mana.py ~line 192):\n`can_pay_for_spell` only does a COUNT check (`spendable_for_spell(spell) >= cmc`), which does NOT verify that the legally-spendable (non-forbidden) mana can satisfy the spell's COLORED PIPS. Exploit: pool = 1 restricted BLUE (instant/sorcery only) + 3 unrestricted COLORLESS; casting a CREATURE costing {U} wrongly returns payable because the count check passes and the blue pip is \"met\" by the restricted blue — forcing the restricted blue to illegally pay a creature's colored pip. FIX: the spendability check for a given spell must run the real per-pip / backtracking `can_pay` solve over a pool with the FORBIDDEN restricted mana REMOVED (i.e. only the mana legally spendable on this spell), not a totals comparison. After the fix: restricted any-color mana must be rejected for a creature even when surplus unrestricted mana of other types exists; instants/sorceries still pay fine; and — critically — when NO restricted mana is present, behavior is byte-for-byte unchanged (the default fast path must still delegate to the legacy `can_pay`).\n\nADVISORY (review.json index 1, engine/animation.py ~line 188) — OPTIONAL but preferred since it's a cheap correctness fix to the framework's own leave-play contract: `deanimate_land()` does not remove `id(land)` from the `_animation_pump_triggers` dedup set, so a deanimated-then-reanimated same object silently fails to re-grant the pump trigger. Clear that registry entry in `deanimate_land` for symmetry. If you apply it, confirm no test regresses; if you choose not to, record it in disagreements.json with justification.\n\nConstraints:\n- ADDITIVE only; never rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; `Keyword` stays at 16; do NOT modify any test file.\n- All 46 sos_257 tests must still pass, AND the fix must not regress the full suite.\n\nVerification:\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → all 46 pass.\n- `pytest` from `/workspace` → no regressions (report totals); explicitly confirm engine mana/casting tests + fdn_267 pass.\n\nOutputs:\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised.diff` — full git diff after the fix (NOT test files).\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised-rationale.md` — what you changed and why the colored-pip solve is now correct + the no-restricted-mana fast path unchanged.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/disagreements.json` — JSON array of `{review_comment_index, reviewer_comment, implementer_justification}` for any strict comment you do NOT fully apply (empty `[]` if you