{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012AdnbqnDUzKLrspy6dNxXh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Revision rationale — sos_257 \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"\n2\t\n3\tAddresses the Reviewer's findings in `review.json`: one strict correctness bug\n4\tin the restricted-mana payability check (`engine/mana.py`), plus the optional\n5\tadvisory in `engine/animation.py`. Both applied. No test files modified.\n6\t\n7\t## STRICT (review index 0) — colored-pip solve over the filtered pool\n8\t\n9\t### The bug\n10\t`can_pay_for_spell` previously verified restricted-mana legality with a *count*\n11\tcomparison only:\n12\t\n13\t```python\n14\tneeded = cost.generic + sum(cost.pips.values()) + len(cost.hybrid)\n15\treturn self.spendable_for_spell(spell) >= needed   # totals only\n16\t```\n17\t\n18\tA totals check cannot see *which* mana satisfies *which* colored pip. Exploit:\n19\tpool = 1 restricted BLUE (instant/sorcery only) + 3 unrestricted COLORLESS, cast\n20\ta CREATURE costing `{U}`. `can_pay({U})` is True (the blue pip is met by the\n21\tblue), `needed == 1`, and `spendable_for_spell(creature) == total(4) -\n22\tforbidden(1) == 3 >= 1`, so the old check returned True. The cast was then\n23\tallowed and `pay()` was forced to spend the restricted blue on the creature's\n24\t`{U}` pip — a spend-restriction bypass for a disallowed spell type.\n25\t\n26\t### The fix\n27\tThe spendability check now runs the *real* per-pip / hybrid / generic\n28\tbacktracking solve over a pool from which the FORBIDDEN restricted mana has been\n29\tremoved **per mana type**, not a totals comparison:\n30\t\n31\t- New `_spendable_pool_for_spell(spell)` returns a copy of the flat `_pool` with\n32\t  each `ManaRestriction` that does NOT permit `spell` subtracted from its own\n33\t  mana type (`max(0, current - amount)`). Restricted mana that *does* permit the\n34\t  spell stays in place and spends like ordinary mana of its type.\n35\t- `can_pay_for_spell` now does:\n36\t  ```python\n37\t  if not self.has_restricted_mana():\n38\t      return self.can_pay(cost)          # fast path — unchanged\n39\t  spendable = self._spendable_pool_for_spell(spell)\n40\t  return self._can_pay_pool(spendable, cost)\n41\t  ```\n42\t\n43\t`_can_pay_pool(remaining, cost)` is a new **static** helper extracted verbatim\n44\tfrom the body of `can_pay`: it pays the colored/colorless pips, backtracks over\n45\thybrids, then checks generic against the sum of what's left. `can_pay` itself now\n46\tdelegates to `_can_pay_pool(dict(self._pool), cost)`, so `can_pay` is\n47\tbehaviourally identical to before (same solver, same copy-of-pool semantics).\n48\tBecause `can_pay_for_spell` runs that *same* solver, the colored `{U}` pip on the\n49\tcreature can only be satisfied by mana that legally remains after the forbidden\n50\tblue is removed — i.e. it now correctly fails (the 3 colorless cannot pay a\n51\tcolored pip), while it still passes for an instant/sorcery (the blue is kept) and\n52\tstill passes for a generic `{1}` creature cost (paid by the colorless).\n53\t\n54\t### Why the no-restricted-mana fast path is byte-for-byte unchanged\n55\tWhen `has_restricted_mana()` is False (every default pool, all ordinary play),\n56\t`can_pay_for_spell` returns `self.can_pay(cost)` exactly as before. `can_pay`'s\n57\texternally observable result is unchanged by the extraction (it forwards a copy\n58\tof the real pool into the identical solve that previously lived inline). Verified\n59\tdirectly: across a sample of costs (`{G}`, `{1}{G}`, `{2}`, `{G}{G}`, `{C}`)\n60\t`can_pay_for_spell == can_pay` for a pool with no restrictions.\n61\t\n62\t## ADVISORY (review index 1) — applied\n63\t\n64\t`deanimate_land` now calls `_pump_trigger_registry(game).discard(id(land))` so\n65\tthe per-source pump-trigger dedup set is cleared on leave-play. Without it, a\n66\tdeanimated-then-reanimated *same Python object* would hit\n67\t`register_instant_sorcery_pump`'s `id(land) in registry` guard and silently fail\n68\tto re-grant the pump trigger. `_pump_trigger_registry` is a module-level function\n69\tresolved at call time, so referencing it from the earlier-defined\n70\t`deanimate_land` is fine. Harmless for sos_257 as shipped (the card never\n71\tdeanimates), but restores the framework's leave-play / re-enter symmetry. No test\n72\tregressed.\n73\t\n74\t## Verification\n75\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → **46 passed**.\n76\t- Engine mana/casting/cast tests (`engine_tests -k \"mana or casting or cast\"`) →\n77\t  **335 passed**.\n78\t- fdn_267 has no `tests.py` (reference card; only `card_impl.py`); it imports\n79\t  cleanly under the full run.\n80\t- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → **1517 passed**, 0 failed (no regressions).\n81\t- Direct exploit check: creature `{U}` with `[restricted BLUE + 3 COLORLESS]`\n82\t  now returns False; instant `{U}` returns True; creature `{1}` returns True.\n83\t\n84\t## Constraints honoured\n85\tAdditive only — no engine symbol renamed/moved/deleted; `_can_pay_pool` and\n86\t`_spendable_pool_for_spell` are new helpers, `can_pay`'s signature is unchanged.\n87\t`Keyword` enum untouched. No test file modified.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c150b5-c49a-4f71-a445-032aa09f64bc","uuid":"b15a1ac0-5687-4f63-97d7-951288d8f248","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:29:52.043Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revision rationale — sos_257 \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"\n\nAddresses the Reviewer's findings in `review.json`: one strict correctness bug\nin the restricted-mana payability check (`engine/mana.py`), plus the optional\nadvisory in `engine/animation.py`. Both applied. No test files modified.\n\n## STRICT (review index 0) — colored-pip solve over the filtered pool\n\n### The bug\n`can_pay_for_spell` previously verified restricted-mana legality with a *count*\ncomparison only:\n\n```python\nneeded = cost.generic + sum(cost.pips.values()) + len(cost.hybrid)\nreturn self.spendable_for_spell(spell) >= needed   # totals only\n```\n\nA totals check cannot see *which* mana satisfies *which* colored pip. Exploit:\npool = 1 restricted BLUE (instant/sorcery only) + 3 unrestricted COLORLESS, cast\na CREATURE costing `{U}`. `can_pay({U})` is True (the blue pip is met by the\nblue), `needed == 1`, and `spendable_for_spell(creature) == total(4) -\nforbidden(1) == 3 >= 1`, so the old check returned True. The cast was then\nallowed and `pay()` was forced to spend the restricted blue on the creature's\n`{U}` pip — a spend-restriction bypass for a disallowed spell type.\n\n### The fix\nThe spendability check now runs the *real* per-pip / hybrid / generic\nbacktracking solve over a pool from which the FORBIDDEN restricted mana has been\nremoved **per mana type**, not a totals comparison:\n\n- New `_spendable_pool_for_spell(spell)` returns a copy of the flat `_pool` with\n  each `ManaRestriction` that does NOT permit `spell` subtracted from its own\n  mana type (`max(0, current - amount)`). Restricted mana that *does* permit the\n  spell stays in place and spends like ordinary mana of its type.\n- `can_pay_for_spell` now does:\n  ```python\n  if not self.has_restricted_mana():\n      return self.can_pay(cost)          # fast path — unchanged\n  spendable = self._spendable_pool_for_spell(spell)\n  return self._can_pay_pool(spendable, cost)\n  ```\n\n`_can_pay_pool(remaining, cost)` is a new **static** helper extracted verbatim\nfrom the body of `can_pay`: it pays the colored/colorless pips, backtracks over\nhybrids, then checks generic against the sum of what's left. `can_pay` itself now\ndelegates to `_can_pay_pool(dict(self._pool), cost)`, so `can_pay` is\nbehaviourally identical to before (same solver, same copy-of-pool semantics).\nBecause `can_pay_for_spell` runs that *same* solver, the colored `{U}` pip on the\ncreature can only be satisfied by mana that legally remains after the forbidden\nblue is removed — i.e. it now correctly fails (the 3 colorless cannot pay a\ncolored pip), while it still passes for an instant/sorcery (the blue is kept) and\nstill passes for a generic `{1}` creature cost (paid by the colorless).\n\n### Why the no-restricted-mana fast path is byte-for-byte unchanged\nWhen `has_restricted_mana()` is False (every default pool, all ordinary play),\n`can_pay_for_spell` returns `self.can_pay(cost)` exactly as before. `can_pay`'s\nexternally observable result is unchanged by the extraction (it forwards a copy\nof the real pool into the identical solve that previously lived inline). Verified\ndirectly: across a sample of costs (`{G}`, `{1}{G}`, `{2}`, `{G}{G}`, `{C}`)\n`can_pay_for_spell == can_pay` for a pool with no restrictions.\n\n## ADVISORY (review index 1) — applied\n\n`deanimate_land` now calls `_pump_trigger_registry(game).discard(id(land))` so\nthe per-source pump-trigger dedup set is cleared on leave-play. Without it, a\ndeanimated-then-reanimated *same Python object* would hit\n`register_instant_sorcery_pump`'s `id(land) in registry` guard and silently fail\nto re-grant the pump trigger. `_pump_trigger_registry` is a module-level function\nresolved at call time, so referencing it from the earlier-defined\n`deanimate_land` is fine. Harmless for sos_257 as shipped (the card never\ndeanimates), but restores the framework's leave-play / re-enter symmetry. No test\nregressed.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` → **46 passed**.\n- Engine mana/casting/cast tests (`engine_tests -k \"mana or casting or cast\"`) →\n  **335 passed**.\n- fdn_267 has no `tests.py` (reference card; only `card_impl.py`); it imports\n  cleanly under the full run.\n- Full `pytest` from `/workspace` → **1517 passed**, 0 failed (no regressions).\n- Direct exploit check: creature `{U}` with `[restricted BLUE + 3 COLORLESS]`\n  now returns False; instant `{U}` returns True; creature `{1}` returns True.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nAdditive only — no engine symbol renamed/moved/deleted; `_can_pay_pool` and\n`_spendable_pool_for_spell` are new helpers, `can_pay`'s signature is unchanged.\n`Keyword` enum untouched. No test file modified.\n","numLines":88,"startLine":1,"totalLines":88}}}
